{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e","id":841149,"title":"Changeling Kiths (2E)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-02T22:58:07-08:00","id":841149,"title":"Changeling Kiths (2E)","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Here are some conversions of several kiths from both the 1E Changeling supplements (like Winter Masques and Night Horrors: Grim Fears) and the homebrew that's lying around at different parts of the net (such as the Goblin Chronicles). Critique is appreciated, and expect more additions to be made in the days to come. Credit goes to those whose own custom kiths are among these conversions.<br /> <br /> I'm also adding in the House Rules I have for the canon 2E Kiths. Again, critique is appreciated.</span></span></span> <hr /><br /> <b>HOUSE RULED KITHS</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><u>Author</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Author can read and interpret anything in a mortal language, and never fails to tell or write a story, or carry out other wordy endeavors. She adds her Wyrd to such rolls, and automatically receives one success in addition to the roll results. If she is making a vocal Expression, Persuasion, or Subterfuge roll, she can spend Glamour to inflict the False Memories Condition on a number of people equal to her Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Brewer</u></b>\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The changeling gains three dots in the Witch's Brew Merit, and may spend a point of Glamour while touching up to Wyrd liters of a liquid to change it either into a potent alcohol or a poison. If it is an alcohol, it gains a Potency (see p. XX) equal to her Wyrd plus successes rolled on a Wits + Crafts roll. If it is a poison, its Potency is half that, rounded up.<br /> <br /> <sub>Note: The Witch's Brew Merit can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841832-homebrew-changeling-merits#post841832\">here</a>.</sub><br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Chimera</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> She gains half her Wyrd to all social rolls when interacting with creatures from the Hedge. Also, she may spend a point of Glamour to apply the rote quality on a roll to resist or otherwise avoid any Contract or other supernatural effect targeting her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Larcenist</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Larcenist gains the Pusher Merit for free, and needs only three successes to score an exceptional success in a Larceny, Persuasion, or Subterfuge roll. If he spends a point of Glamour, he may add half his Wyrd to all such rolls for the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Minstrel</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Minstrel gains the three-dot version of Enchanting Performance, and opens additional doors equal to his Wyrd when he spends Glamour to activate Siren. Additionally, if he's making Expression rolls which involve singing or playing a musical instrument, he gains an Exceptional Success at three successes instead of five.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>HOMEBREW KITHS</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1elqCKhNJweqnLuUy8Rbh2PiZSsnccnXQWrNy8cPf5o4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Proceed here.</a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 10-15-2016, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T06:17:20-08:00","id":841254,"title":"","content":"The Romancer is still in, its just called Dearheart now. But your verison is cool too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T08:21:01-08:00","id":841307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=841254#post841254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Romancer is still in, its just called Dearheart now. But your verison is cool too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that the Dearheart was for the Apsara and Incubus/Succubus kith. But still, glad to know you like my take on the Romancer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T15:24:42-08:00","id":841531,"title":"","content":"Take a look at the Wizened discription of the Dearheart, its the Romancer.<br /> <br /> And the Apsara appears to be absent, but I personally would dump the Ogre description and replace with Apsara Elemental discription.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T15:57:30-08:00","id":841547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=841531#post841531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take a look at the Wizened discription of the Dearheart, its the Romancer.<br /> <br /> And the Apsara appears to be absent, but I personally would dump the Ogre description and replace with Apsara Elemental discription.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Noted.<br /> Still, I'll probably keep my take on the Romancer to work as a kith for spies, thieves, and very sociable characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T16:32:12-08:00","id":841566,"title":"","content":"I'd replace Bar Fly merit with Many Mask in your Romancer, it will better achieve effect your going for appearance wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T16:38:51-08:00","id":841571,"title":"","content":"Noted <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Will revise accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T04:23:33-08:00","id":841815,"title":"","content":"Wizened berserker with a heart pping adrenaline instead of blood!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T04:41:46-08:00","id":841821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=841815#post841815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wizened berserker with a heart pping adrenaline instead of blood!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, that's an awesome idea. How about this for a description?<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Wizened:</b> A steampunk construct whose hydraulic heart pumps adrenaline for blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T06:39:39-08:00","id":841864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=841821#post841821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, that's an awesome idea. How about this for a description?<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Wizened:</b> A steampunk construct whose hydraulic heart pumps adrenaline for blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yaaa\u00e0aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T15:00:59-08:00","id":842176,"title":"","content":"Added in the Hearthweaver kith, and made some revisions to the Romancer. Critique is welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T00:10:02-08:00","id":842438,"title":"","content":"Need someone reliable to browse through the Goblin Market? Or perhaps you're in the mood for a character who can catch even other Lost with a sealed pledge. I got a couple of additions to the list which need both critique and some sample descriptions for a few of the Seemings. <hr /><br /> <u><b>Barrister</b></u><br /> Arcadia runs on rules and laws, though these esoteric systems are created from whole cloth and known only to the True Fae. An inkling of this knowledge flows into the Barristers, who navigate the bizarre legalities of life in and beyond the Hedge with inhuman aplomb. As mortals, they may have defined their lives by a set of rules, or even possessed a knack for maneuvering through the system to get what they wanted.. Either way, it was only by knowing and exploiting the rules of Faerie that they survived long enough to flee via a loophole.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Barristers gain the Bureaucratic Navigator Merit, and can perform Sealings on non-changelings at no cost. If he performs a Sealing on a fae creature, he may initiate a Clash of Wills to bind them without their knowledge. Both roll Wits + Wyrd, and the Huckster secretly places the seal if he scores more successes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Huckster</b></u><br /> Everything has a price, and that goes doubly so in the lands beyond the Thorns. Some Changelings were taken for their talent im bartering, buying, and more importantly, selling. They may have worked the goblin markets at their Master's behest, managed the appraisal and purchase of slaves, or just bargained every sunrise for another day of life. Those who manage to escape did so by cunning and guile, trapping their Keepers in bad deals or exploiting the fine print to force an opening.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>Hucksters are skilled brokers and businessmen, able to land good bargains (and weed out bad ones) with ruthless efficiency. They gain the Market Sense Merit for free, and may apply the latter to deals and transactions made outside the Goblin Market. They may also perform Bargains without shedding the Mask, and double the benefits gained from making one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T05:49:47-08:00","id":842501,"title":"","content":"New Kith<br /> <br /> Villian: You were chosen to play the &quot;bad guy&quot;, to the Gentry's&quot;good guy&quot;, for every hero needs a villian to defeat. Upon returning to Earth most Villians subvert the trope they were based on as a way of rejecting their Keeper. A few instead embrace their role, but on their terms.<br /> <br /> Wizened: Mustach twirling bastard, that always seems to attract the service of thugs eagar to obey his orders.<br /> Beast: The devil, with massive horns, red skin and hooved feet, to their Keepers God, the souls of the damned ready to answer his call.<br /> Ogre: A muscle bound Alien horror with far too many teeth and the gleam of an dark intellect behind her eyes, her brood sack ready to give birth to fresh minions.<br /> Darkling: a necromancer in a skull mask he never seems to remove, and wiggling magical tatoos of blasphemist nature. Zombies come bidden at his unholy chanting.<br /> Elemental: Pure Evil, his Mein is more emotional then visual, evil radiates off him like heat from a fire, evil as aphysical presence instead of merely a concept, reminding those around him of all that they find vile and morally unforgivable. People with evil urges come to him as moths drawn to a flame, happy to obey.<br /> Fairest: The dark Queen, regal, whose evil beauty taints her clothes and those around her,enhancing their beauty, but in a way that matches her own tainted gorgeous, yet unnatural appearance. Servants and Guardsman jump at her every order.<br /> <br /> Blessing: Free small unit tactics merit and the staff: 1 (minions) merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T06:35:21-08:00","id":842524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=842501#post842501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Kith<br /> <br /> Villian: You were chosen to play the &amp;quot;bad guy&amp;quot;, to the Gentry's&amp;quot;good guy&amp;quot;, for every hero needs a villian to defeat. Upon returning to Earth most Villians subvert the trope they were based on as a way of rejecting their Keeper. A few instead embrace their role, but on their terms.<br /> <br /> Wizened: Mustach twirling bastard, that always seems to attract the service of thugs eagar to obey his orders.<br /> Beast: The devil, with massive horns, red skin and hooved feet, to their Keepers God, the souls of the damned ready to answer his call.<br /> Ogre: A muscle bound Alien horror with far too many teeth and the gleam of an dark intellect behind her eyes, her brood sack ready to give birth to fresh minions.<br /> Darkling: a necromancer in a skull mask he never seems to remove, and wiggling magical tatoos of blasphemist nature. Zombies come bidden at his unholy chanting.<br /> Elemental: Pure Evil, his Mein is more emotional then visual, evil radiates off him like heat from a fire, evil as aphysical presence instead of merely a concept, reminding those around him of all that they find vile and morally unforgivable. People with evil urges come to him as moths drawn to a flame, happy to obey.<br /> Fairest: The dark Queen, regal, whose evil beauty taints her clothes and those around her,enhancing their beauty, but in a way that matches her own tainted gorgeous, yet unnatural appearance. Servants and Guardsman jump at her every order.<br /> <br /> Blessing: Free small unit tactics merit and the staff: 1 (minions) merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting write-up. Though maybe remove the Staff Merit as part of the kith blessing and replace it with something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T10:44:24-08:00","id":842638,"title":"","content":"What would you suggest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T17:42:20-08:00","id":842805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=842638#post842638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you suggest?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Maybe not limit it to just villains? I can see this kith being expanded to include authority figures. But yeah, here's what I got as a suggestion for the kith's blessing. <hr /><br /> <b>Blessing: </b>The changeling gains the Small Unit Tactics Merit, as well as a dot of Presence that can take him above the limits imposed by his Wyrd. If he spends a point of glamour, he can invoke the benefits of the three-dot version of the Mind Control Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T18:51:59-08:00","id":843233,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea, but we already have Kiths that focus on social manipulation, Dearheart, Flowering, Nix, Flamesiren, Illes, Larencist, and to a lesser extent Shadowsoul.<br /> <br /> The goal of the Kith's minions isn't social manipulation, its that many of the great villians have minor disposable minions to throught at their enemies. <br /> <br /> That why I choose the staff merits its perfect way to show faceless minions, without clogging up gameplay. They do their one auto success and then they're gone, driven off or killed by the &quot;good&quot; guy.<br /> <br /> And I see the minions actually being part of the Villians mien, not true individuals, semi automous at best, and killing them off as being no damaging tothe Villian then cutting his/her finger nails. Its also allows the minions to look more fantastical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T19:12:04-08:00","id":843243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=843233#post843233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting idea, but we already have Kiths that focus on social manipulation, Dearheart, Flowering, Nix, Flamesiren, Illes, Larencist, and to a lesser extent Shadowsoul.<br /> <br /> The goal of the Kith's minions isn't social manipulation, its that many of the great villians have minor disposable minions to throught at their enemies.<br /> <br /> That why I choose the staff merits its perfect way to show faceless minions, without clogging up gameplay. They do their one auto success and then they're gone, driven off or killed by the &quot;good&quot; guy.<br /> <br /> And I see the minions actually being part of the Villians mien, not true individuals, semi automous at best, and killing them off as being no damaging tothe Villian then cutting his/her finger nails. Its also allows the minions to look more fantastical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted. Though I guess it's just a matter of working out how the disposable minions work, mechanics-wise. Maybe you could rework it as a power that needs to require a point of Glamour to activate? Alternatively, or perhaps additionally, you could simply have a changeling who develops this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833785-contracts-2e-conversions#post833785\">homebrew Wizened trick</a> for the Control Elements Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T19:21:54-08:00","id":843247,"title":"","content":"Looking for someone more explosive than an Ifrit? Hotter to handle than a Flamesiren? The Vulcanalis kith (based on the creature of the same name in Grimm) is finally on the main post. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Vulcanalis</u></b><br /> The Earth is not just enduring, it is forceful, reminding all of its presence and power; the changelings of this Kith embody that sense of power, parallelling gods and spirits of volcanos. As mortals, they may have been hot-tempered, quick to explode upon provocation. Or they may have seemed mild-mannered, yet seethed with pent up rage deep inside. And once they were taken, they were cast into rivers of lava and lakes of magma, where the crushing pressure forced their anger and fury to finally erupt in all their glory.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> A salamander with charcoal scales, whose body lights up in fiery patterns when angered.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> A figure sculpted from boiling rock, veins of magma visible on the surface.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> He appears to have skin reddened from prolonged exposure to the sun, and his body is adorned with crimson tattoos.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Vulcanalis inflict lethal damage with their unarmed attacks, and gain an additional dot in Presence that can take them above the usual limitations imposed by their Wyrd. Furthermore, they can spend glamour to inflict the Inferno Tilt up to a radius of three meters. Each point of glamour spent causes the Tilt's effects to last a number of turns equal to the Vulcanalis' Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-06-2016, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T07:09:53-08:00","id":843408,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Architect</b></u><br /> The human architeture always have enchanted the Fae, but the secret passages, tunnels and crazy houses is one of the most iconic features in the fantastic architeture. Some Gentry like to gather humans to design and construct ellegant houses with complex systems of vaults, tunnels and secret entries.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> A strange humanoid amount of bricks who can move and merge with the walls.<br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> A half-man half-ox monster, holding a gigantic axe. <i>(Thanks Omegaphallic</i>)<br /> \u2022 <b>Wizened:</b> A worker with a safety helment and mechanical arms attached to his body who can lift good amounts of cement.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The architect can achieve an expectional sucess with three sucesses instead of five on Investigation and Craft rolls related to buildings. He can also spend a point of Glamour and mark the perimeter of an area to create a temporary Safe Place Merit. The level of the Merit is equal to half the changeling\u2019s Wyrd (round up) and the effect lasts for 24 hours from creation or until she leaves, whichever is longer. The area can manifest secret passages and/or tunnels that increase the difficulty for finding the Architet as per Safe Place. Sometimes, a new tunnel or secret passage is created without the knowledge of the architet.<br /> <br /> The effect manifest underground and above ground in different ways:<br /> Above ground: You need the materials to construct the Safe Place(cement, bricks, etc). Or you can modify houses that haven't had any owners for at least a year and a day.<br /> Underground: You can create tunnels with rocks and earth, but you still need materials for doors, locks, etc.<br /> <br /> You can turn the effect of the merit permanent with Experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 03-18-2016, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T07:26:49-08:00","id":843418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=843408#post843408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Architect</b></u></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting concept, and it doesn't overlap (much) with the Troll or the Hearthweaver.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Consider this added.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T07:45:22-08:00","id":843428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=843418#post843418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting concept, and it doesn't overlap (much) with the Troll or the Hearthweaver.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Consider this added.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. To be fair, it was inspired on the Troll kith. I'll check the Hearthweaver to see if I can make it more interesting and try to not overlap much these two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T07:51:16-08:00","id":843432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=843428#post843428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. To be fair, it was inspired on the Troll kith. I'll check the Hearthweaver to see if I can make it more interesting and try to not overlap much these two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go ahead. So far, though, they're all distinct from one another. I have to ask, though. Isn't Unseen Sense supposed to apply to supernatural entities? If so, maybe Unseen Sense (Secret Passages) should be swapped with something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T09:33:15-08:00","id":844007,"title":"","content":"Thank you for starting this thread. I've been working on several kiths of my own, and I've been reluctant to share them out of fear of stepping on someone else's toes, but this is one that I've been toying with that I'd like some feedback on, so I hope you don't mind me sharing it here.<br /> <br /> <b>Doppelganger</b> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">No, sir. I've been here all night. Ask anyone.</span><br /> <br /> Sometimes the Gentry need a servant that can be in more than one place at a time. Towards this end, the Gentry look for people who are known for their obedience or who work well with others, and make them into doppelgangers. Some were taken to function as living armies, with each doppelganger functioning as an independent unit in the greater legion. Other doppelgangers were taken to act as part of a traveling Gentry's entourage, quietly following behind while their twins slip off to spy on another Keeper. A doppelganger's escape forces him back into a single body, but the sensation of existing in separate bodies never truly leaves him.<br /> <br /> <b>-Beast:</b> Pack creatures, such as a wolf whose voice echoes with the howls of many others.<br /> <b>-Darkling:</b> A ghostly figure that casts three dark shadows regardless of ambient lighting.<br /> <b>-Wizened:</b> Glowing eyes stare out of the depths of an ancient Greek helmet, and each armored footstep sounds like the tread of an entire army.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> By spending a point of Glamour, a doppelganger is able to create a duplicate of himself. Each duplicate has a number of Health levels equal to the changeling's Wyrd, and will persist for the duration of the scene. Duplicates act instinctively to assist the changeling, functioning as secondary actors in teamwork actions for any action involving a Physical Skill. The doppelganger may also take full control of a single duplicate by spending another point of Glamour. While controlling the duplicate, the doppelganger cannot engage in any strenuous activities with his own body, and will suffer a -3 distraction penalty on all other actions. The doppelganger may only control one duplicate in this manner at a time. The doppelganger may only have a number of duplicates equal to half his Wyrd, rounded up, and each duplicate after the first incurs a -1 distraction penalty on all actions. This is cumulative with the distraction penalty of taking full control of one of the duplicates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T15:21:13-08:00","id":844174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=844007#post844007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for starting this thread. I've been working on several kiths of my own, and I've been reluctant to share them out of fear of stepping on someone else's toes, but this is one that I've been toying with that I'd like some feedback on, so I hope you don't mind me sharing it here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this was a nice write-up I got to find this morning. The Doppelganger is a rather intimidating kith, especially if you combine it with Dual Kith and/or Potent Kith. Then, you have a literal one-man army that won't (often) fall with just one hit.<br /> <br /> Nicely done <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm adding this to my main post when I got time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T01:34:47-08:00","id":844973,"title":"","content":"Anyone mind critiquing this new kith, for me? Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr /><br /> <b><u>Logician</u></b> <br /> Some changelings were shaped to be the living beings of pure reason and thought. These Lost served as calculated advisors to their faerie master, while others were given tasks of great magnitude and order. Their heightened thought processes, however, led them to the solution to their plight, and thus made their escape possible. <br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> An animal well-known for its intellect, like a dolphin or an octopus.<br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling:</b> A hardhearted demon with inhuman intellect and an absence of emotion. <br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> Shifting fractals of light that cluster together in the shape of a man. <br /> \u2022 <b>Wizened:</b> A human computer, with circuit lines and fiber wires running throughout his body, and a crystalline processor for a brain. <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Logician gains a dot of Intelligence, which can take him above the usual limitations imposed by his Wyrd. He also does not suffer from any penalties to rolls which use either the Intelligence Attribute or Mental Skills. If a Logician spends a point of glamour, he benefits from the advanced action quality and a dice bonus equal to his Wyrd on such rolls for a scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T04:39:44-08:00","id":845014,"title":"","content":"I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T20:43:05-08:00","id":845420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=845014#post845014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I wasn't sure if it was too powerful or not. But I'm glad you like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:16:54-08:00","id":845735,"title":"","content":"Since this thread is being used to consolidate the kiths people are creating, I thought I'd copy my Dreamstalker kith from the Moar Kiths thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dreamstalker</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">She was just standing there when I woke up. She leaned down, kissed me on the forehead, and whispered &quot;I told you I knew where you slept.&quot; Then she was gone. I swear, I'm never sleeping again.</span><br /> <br /> Dreamstalkers are unusual for changelings, as most of them spent little time in their Keepers' lands. A dreamstalker is invariable tasked with haunting mortal dreamscapes, collecting information or bestowing blessings and curses on the Gentry's behalf. Some are used to delight mortals, plying them with dreams of wonders just out of reach, calling them slowly but surely into their Keepers' arms. Others visit nightmares upon those who have commit some transgression against the Gentry, making each night another battle for the mortal's sanity. While an escaping dreamstalker may think freedom to be only a mortal dream away, she finds that no matter how far she runs, every night pulls her dangerously close to where she started.<br /> <br /> -<b>Beast:</b> They are made up of creatures omnipresent in a nightmare, such as a humanoid figure composed of countless crawling spiders or a tangled mass of branch and wire filled with staring red-eyed crows.<br /> <b>-Elemental:</b> Constantly shifting features and colors, never the same twice, yet somehow always recognizable as the same entity.<br /> <b>-Fairest:</b> Beautiful dream lovers, too perfect to be human, beckoning seductively.<br /> <b>-Wizened:</b> Little imps with constantly twitching fingers and glowing symbols forming from the multi-colored sands pouring from cracks in their skin.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Dreamstalkers gain the Dreamsteps Contract for free, and gain an exceptional success on 3 successes instead of 5 when rolling for the Contract's activation. Additionally, a dreamstalker may spend a point of Glamour when touching a mortal to mark them. A dreamstalker instantly knows whenever a marked mortal has fallen asleep, and by spending another point of Glamour, this mortal is treated as though they were nearby for the purposes of the Dreamsteps Contract, allowing the dreamstalker to travel through their dreams from a distance. A dreamstalker may only have a number of mortals equal to their Wyrd marked in this manner, although they can erase a mark at any time by spending another point of Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T12:18:42-08:00","id":845763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=845735#post845735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since this thread is being used to consolidate the kiths people are creating, I thought I'd copy my Dreamstalker kith from the Moar Kiths thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nicely done on the Dreamstalker kith <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Will be adding it in, when I have time.<br /> <br /> Also, on a sidenote, may make slight tweaks to the Logician blessing as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T13:01:20-08:00","id":845795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=845763#post845763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nicely done on the Dreamstalker kith <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank y