path.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T07:10:55-07:00","id":852404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852307#post852307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homebrewing content is kind of addicting once I get into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah. It <i>does</i> get addicting, after a while. Looking forward to those next two kiths.<br /> :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T10:37:25-07:00","id":852478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852404#post852404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, yeah. It <i>does</i> get addicting, after a while. Looking forward to those next two kiths.<br /> :3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Here they are!</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">----------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Toon</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Aww, anybody can do that, Doc. This is Loony Toon Land!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Many among the True Fae find entertainment in the pain of others. Changelings who became Toons were used to provide their Keepers with slapstick humor for hours at a time, their bodies subjected to injuries that would cripple or even kill ordinary people, only to resume work hours later in good health! It was this pseudo-immortality that lead to their escape from their Keeper's realm.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A brightly colored, anthropomorphic animal who looks like they walked out of a children's entertainment program.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> An inanimate object brought to life, complete with human appendages and facial features.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A character from a 1980's action cartoon who is known for their witty one liners and popular catch phrases.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A violent anime character who's series displayed grand, over the top battles to satisfy the adrenaline fueled audience.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> An adult cartoon known for its gritty atmosphere and serious undertones.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A cartoon version of their original human form, changed in order to assimilate to the Keeper's realm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Like they say, it is almost impossible to kill a Toon. The Changeling automatically gains the Quick Healer Merit for free at character creation. Additionally, they may reflexively spend a point of Glamour to ignore Wyrd x3 Bashing damage or Wyrd x1 Lethal damage when they suffer injury.<br /> <br /> <i>Note:</i> Any damage that the Toon ignores will appear to heal itself instantly in cartoonish fashion such as reattaching lost limbs, inflating crushed body parts or even just returning to perfect health when you take your eyes off them.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Executioner</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I could make this painless for you... but you pissed me off.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Although the True Fae are functionally immortal within their own realms, even they are not strangers to the hand of death. Changelings who became Executioners were created to dispose of those who their Keepers no longer wanted around. Sometimes the executions were public spectacles, and other times they needed to be as discrete as possible. Maybe their Keeper shouldn't have taught them so many ways to kill Fae...<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A lithe figure dressed in shinobi robes and carrying hidden weapons under their clothing.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A magically animated suit of armor, uninhibited by human emotions on the battlefield.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A lumbering man who never removes his black cowl in public and spends his free time sharpening his weapon of choice.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A pit fighting animal who was only released for gladiator matches. They still wear the shattered restraints once used to keep them locked up.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A beautiful angel of death who beckons you into their sweet embrace with promises to ease your suffering.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A cyborg monstrosity who's body was remade into an engine of war.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Masters of death and destruction, the Executioner gains the benefit of the 8 Again rule when attempting to use any weapon type they are have specialized in. Additionally, they may spend a point of Glamour to upgrade their weapon's base damage type for one attack each.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-25-2016, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T21:38:32-07:00","id":852791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852478#post852478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Here they are!</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">----------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Toon</b><br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;Aww, anybody can do that, Doc. This is Loony Toon Land!&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> Many among the True Fae find entertainment in the pain of others. Changelings who became Toons were used to provide their Keepers with slapstick humor for hours at a time, their bodies subjected to injuries that would cripple or even kill ordinary people, only to resume work hours later in good health! It was this pseudo-immortality that lead to their escape from their Keeper's realm.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A brightly colored, anthropomorphic animal who looks like they walked out of a children's entertainment program.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> An inanimate object brought to life, complete with human appendages and facial features.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A character from a 1980's action cartoon who is known for their witty one liners and popular catch phrases.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A violent anime character who's series displayed grand, over the top battles to satisfy the adrenaline fueled audience.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> An adult cartoon known for its gritty atmosphere and serious undertones.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A cartoon version of their original human form, changed in order to assimilate to the Keeper's realm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Like they say, it is almost impossible to kill a Toon. The Changeling automatically gains the Quick Healer Merit for free at character creation. Additionally, they may spend a point of Glamour to ignore Wyrd x3 Bashing damage or Wyrd x1 Lethal damage when suffering injury.<br /> <br /> <i>Note:</i> Any damage that the Toon ignores will appear to heal itself instantly in cartoonish fashion such as reattaching lost limbs, inflating crushed body parts or even just returning to perfect health when you take your eyes off them.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Executioner</b><br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;I could make this painless for you... but you pissed me off.&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> Although the True Fae are functionally immortal within their own realms, even they are not strangers to the hand of death. Changelings who became Executioners were created to dispose of those who their Keepers no longer wanted around. Sometimes the executions were public spectacles, and other times they needed to be as discrete as possible. Maybe their Keeper shouldn't have taught them so many ways to kill Fae...<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A lithe figure dressed in shinobi robes and carrying hidden weapons under their clothing.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A magically animated suit of armor, uninhibited by human emotions on the battlefield.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A lumbering man who never removes his black cowl in public and spends his free time sharpening his weapon of choice.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A pit fighting animal who was only released for gladiator matches. They still wear the shattered restraints once used to keep them locked up.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A beautiful angel of death who beckons you into their sweet embrace with promises to ease your suffering.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A cyborg monstrosity who's body was remade into an engine of war.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Masters of death and destruction, the Executioner gains the benefit of the 8 Again rule when attempting to use any weapon they are trained in. Additionally, they may spend a point of Glamour to upgrade their weapon's base damage type for one attack each.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I am liking this, especially the Executioner. Though it and the Toon may need more elaboration on their Blessings. For the former, I assume the 8-again is for all Weaponry rolls? Or for any kind of weapon, in general, including firearms, bows, and throwing knives?<br /> <br /> For the latter, is the glamour effect per turn? Or scene long?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T21:47:51-07:00","id":852794,"title":"","content":"No, the Executioner gets a bonus to any weapon they are trained in. Meaning they have a skill point in it. Like say if they had skill in Melee (Knife), they would get 8 again on attempts to use knives, but not swords unless they also had skill in swords.<br /> <br /> As for the Glamour, yes, it is per turn. I felt it may be a little bit too OP if you could turn a lethal weapon into an aggravated one for the rest of the scene. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T21:56:21-07:00","id":852796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852794#post852794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the Executioner gets a bonus to any weapon they are trained in. Meaning they have a skill point in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The system does not go that granular. You're conflating Skill dots with Skill Specialties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T22:01:31-07:00","id":852799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852794#post852794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the Executioner gets a bonus to any weapon they are trained in. Meaning they have a skill point in it. Like say if they had skill in Melee (Knife), they would get 8 again on attempts to use knives, but not swords unless they also had skill in swords.<br /> <br /> As for the Glamour, yes, it is per turn. I felt it may be a little bit too OP if you could turn a lethal weapon into an aggravated one for the rest of the scene. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm with Satchel on that. I suppose you could just clarify that they must have a Specialty in the desired weapon to avail of the Executioner blessing.<br /> <br /> Also, how about the Toon's glamour-based power? I dont think a duration was specified for it, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T22:04:58-07:00","id":852802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852799#post852799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I'm with Satchel on that. I suppose you could just clarify that they must have a Specialty in the desired weapon to avail of the Executioner blessing.<br /> <br /> Also, how about the Toon's glamour-based power? I dont think a duration was specified for it, either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was also a a 1 for 1 basis. Meaning they spend the Glamour to decrease the effectiveness of the next attack coming their way. But alright, I'll edit the Executioner to include specialties instead. Also, edited the Toon Blessing to be more descriptive of its effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-25-2016, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T22:37:10-07:00","id":852813,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to think of a shaman-style Kith that is to spirits as Gravewright is to ghosts. Something that would be good for interacting with the Uratha and even the Shadow. My first idea is to mimic the Gravewright blessing word for word but apply it to spirits, and complement that with the right Tokens and Contracts. The blessing could also mimic some of the Merits from the Book Of Spirits. Extra Kiths that would go well with this one include Hunterheart, Witchtooth, Farwalker and Woodwalker.<br /> <br /> How does that sound? I'm having a hard time coming up with a name, so I might just call them Shamans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T22:56:25-07:00","id":852822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852813#post852813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does that sound? I'm having a hard time coming up with a name, so I might just call them Shamans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Shaman King!<br /> <br /> But no, seriously.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>What about<b></b>:</b><br /> <br /> Spiritwalker<br /> <br /> Druid<br /> <br /> Forest Folk<br /> <br /> Kami","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T23:04:50-07:00","id":852826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852813#post852813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to think of a shaman-style Kith that is to spirits as Gravewright is to ghosts. Something that would be good for interacting with the Uratha and even the Shadow. My first idea is to mimic the Gravewright blessing word for word but apply it to spirits, and complement that with the right Tokens and Contracts. The blessing could also mimic some of the Merits from the Book Of Spirits. Extra Kiths that would go well with this one include Hunterheart, Witchtooth, Farwalker and Woodwalker.<br /> <br /> How does that sound? I'm having a hard time coming up with a name, so I might just call them Shamans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with Spiritwalker, as Nyrufa suggested. Or maybe Spiritseer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T23:41:00-07:00","id":852844,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Nyrufa and Deionscribe. I'll go with Spiritseer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T23:45:26-07:00","id":852845,"title":"","content":"You're welcome. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T00:46:04-07:00","id":852853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852845#post852845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're welcome. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>Added in the Executioner and Toon to the main post :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T01:17:10-07:00","id":852854,"title":"","content":"Here's a full write-up of that kith which uses Dark Passenger. Enjoy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr /><br /> <u><b>Twoface</b></u><br /> <i>&quot;You're sure he's hiding something?&quot;<br /> &quot;Absolutely. You ought to pay more attention to the details, like how unusually polite he's being with you.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Alluding to folktales on creatures like the Futakuchi-onna, as well as how people think of their conscience as voices in their head, Twofaces were taken by Gentry who desired advisors and confidantes, or perhaps someone who could gauge the intentions of their rivals. Their minds were painfully divided, with one half enchanted to glean greater insights to its surroundings. Such a split, however, was a blessing in disguise, as the separate personalities worked together to discover a way out.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Darkling:</b> A fiendish creature that possesses a face on both sides of its head.<br /> <b>\u2022 Elemental:</b> A living whirlwind that periodically assumes a human form, with a head that shifts between two faces.<br /> <b>\u2022 Fairest:</b> A delicate, yet graceful woman, whose long dark hair conceals the monstrous mouth behind her head.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The changeling gains the Dark Passenger Merit for free, and can ask a number of questions equal to Wyrd + 1 when using it. Furthermore, she only needs to feed the mouth after a number of hours equal to her Wyrd, and can do so through either food or a point of Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T06:08:51-07:00","id":852919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, she only needs to feed the mouth after a number of hours equal to her Wyrd </div> </div> </div>So no sleeping ever again then....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T07:29:25-07:00","id":852962,"title":"","content":"<b>Portender</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Yes its a bag of salt, I keep it in case of emergencies. Now hold your breath, we're driving past a graveyard!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Despite all the pomp and bluster, the True Fae are not as omniscient as they would have you believe. Portenders were used to forewarn their masters of tragedy before it struck, or sometimes they were the cause of such tragedy. One day they managed to escape when they refused to warn their master appropriately!<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A ghostly woman who prowls the streets, wailing away into the night. Her cries signal that somebody will die before the next sunrise.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A foreboding animal such as a raven, black cat, or large dog. Its gaze constantly follows the ill fated.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> An oracle who's flesh has been embedded with round scrying crystals allowing them to read the patterns of fate.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Brought on board her Keeper's ship before it was attacked at sea, this woman managed to conceal her identity by dressing like the enemy and stealing some weapons to defend herself.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A nightmarish, horrifying creature, merely seeing them in person is said to condemn a man to death!<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A gestalt entity formed out of broken down, rusty and faulty technology. They are literally an accident waiting to happen.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Portenders were strongly tied to luck and fortune during their time in Arcadia, and retain that connection to a lesser extent once they escape. They gain the Changeling Fate Contract for free, but do not suffer from its Ban and need only spend 1 Glamour point to activate it. Furthermore, they add their Wyrd as a dice bonus on all rolls made to detect an impending ambush.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":".  Edited Name and Blessing 04-03-2016, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T08:20:50-07:00","id":852977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852919#post852919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no sleeping ever again then....</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, shouldn't it <i>allow</i> for more chance to sleep, seeing as the default version requires the mouth to be fed every hour?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T08:24:44-07:00","id":852980,"title":"","content":"Maybe make it 1 + [Wyrd] hours?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T08:34:39-07:00","id":852986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852962#post852962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Omen</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Interesting. Though Danger Sense seems kinda weak as a benefit, in my opinion. Hmm. Perhaps giving them a free Contract, with additional benefits made for activating it could work? On a semi-related note, maybe changing the name from Omen would be a good idea. Perhaps something along the lines of Doomseer?<br /> <br /> Here's a suggestion for a revised blessing, which could be in addition to or in lieu of Danger Sense.<br /> <hr /><b>Blessing:</b> The Changeling gains three dots in the Changeling Fate Contract, and needs only spend a single point of Glamour to activate it. Furthermore, they may invoke the Contract on a single target once a day per dot of Wyrd he possesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T08:37:40-07:00","id":852987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852980#post852980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe make it 1 + [Wyrd] hours?</div> </div> </div> </div>How's this, then? <hr /><br /> <u><b>Twoface</b></u><br /> <i>&quot;You're sure he's hiding something?&quot;<br /> &quot;Absolutely. You ought to pay more attention to the details, like how unusually polite he's being with you.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Alluding to folktales on creatures like the Futakuchi-onna, as well as how people think of their conscience as voices in their head, Twofaces were taken by Gentry who desired advisors and confidantes, or perhaps someone who could gauge the intentions of their rivals. Their minds were painfully divided, with one half enchanted to glean greater insights to its surroundings. Such a split, however, was a blessing in disguise, as the separate personalities worked together to discover a way out.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Darkling:</b> A fiendish creature that possesses a face on both sides of its head.<br /> <b>\u2022 Elemental:</b> A living whirlwind that periodically assumes a human form, with a head that shifts between two faces.<br /> <b>\u2022 Fairest:</b> A delicate, yet graceful woman, whose long dark hair conceals the monstrous mouth behind her head.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The changeling gains the Dark Passenger Merit for free, and can ask a number of questions equal to Wyrd + 1 when using it. Furthermore, she only needs to feed the mouth after a number of hours equal to her Wyrd + 1, and can do so through either food or a point of Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:48:19-07:00","id":853091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852986#post852986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. Interesting. Though Danger Sense seems kinda weak as a benefit, in my opinion. Hmm. Perhaps giving them a free Contract, with additional benefits made for activating it could work? On a semi-related note, maybe changing the name from Omen would be a good idea. Perhaps something along the lines of Doomseer?<br /> <br /> Here's a suggestion for a revised blessing, which could be in addition to or in lieu of Danger Sense.<br /> <hr /><b>Blessing:</b> The Changeling gains three dots in the Changeling Fate Contract, and needs only spend a single point of Glamour to activate it. Furthermore, they may invoke the Contract on a single target once a day per dot of Wyrd he possesses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, I wanted to give them the Precognitive Merit, but I'm not sure if Psychics are a different template entirely. I'm also not sure what the new contracts are for 2nd E. If you have a link to them, I'd appreciate it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I was originally going to call them Banshees, but felt that was too limiting for their Seemings. There's all kinds of omens, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T12:23:43-07:00","id":853110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Orig