g-the-lost/832066-2e-playtest-compilation-now-with-pledges-and-huntsmen\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832066-2e-playtest-compilation-now-with-pledges-and-huntsmen\"> 2E Playtest Compilation (now with Pledges and Huntsmen) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832066-2e-playtest-compilation-now-with-pledges-and-huntsmen\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832066-2e-playtest-compilation-now-with-pledges-and-huntsmen </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The version I put up yesterday missed the Huntsmen, and then Dave shared pledges, so I've added those. Changeling the Lost 2E Playtest Compilation </div> </div> </div><br /> Here you go.<br /> :3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T17:25:13-07:00","id":853239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852977#post852977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, shouldn't it <i>allow</i> for more chance to sleep, seeing as the default version requires the mouth to be fed every hour?</div> </div> </div> </div>Starting changelings would have still needed to feed the mouth every hour so would have to not sleep until they get to wyrd 2 or 3.... and I'd imagine that'd die from exhaustion long before they get their wyrd that high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T12:40:13-07:00","id":853619,"title":"","content":"Here's one I've been working on for a couple weeks. Feedback would certainly be welcome, as I worry that I may have made it too powerful.<br /> <br /> <b>Wonderwell</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">I can make your fondest wish come true. There's just one tiny little favor you need to do for me in exchange.</span><br /> <br /> Arcadia is a place of beauty as well as terror, and all too often a desperate or greedy mortal is seduced into the waiting arms of the Gentry by the promise of untold power and riches. Some Keepers delight in the corruption of mortal wishes, while others feel that granting wishes is a fair bargain for a mortal's freedom. Wonderwells are often chosen to lure such mortals, granting their hearts' desires while slowly drawing them deeper into the Gentry's influence. Her close interactions with humanity makes it difficult for a wonderwell to forget her previous life, leading many to perpetual sorrow. Mortals who are moved to pity for their plight should be wary, though, as a wish for a wonderwell's freedom often comes at the price of their own.<br /> <br /> <b>-Beast:</b> They are covered in shimmering fish scales, with small fins at their joints.<br /> <b>-Darkling:</b> Attractive yet sinister figures, with small horns upon their heads and warm smiles upon their lips as their offer hangs in the air.<br /> <b>-Elemental:</b> Skin composed of gray bricks, with water pouring out from between the stones, and eyes that gleam like two silver coins.<br /> <b>-Fairest:</b> Beautiful men and women, clothed in nothing but beautiful jewels and sheer fabrics, with legs fading into mist.<br /> <b>-Ogre:</b> Huge and intimidating figures composed of smokeless fire, their colorful eyes promising reward and punishment alike.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Wonderwells are skilled at granting the desires of others. By spending a point of Glamour when entering into a bargain, both the subject and the changeling will temporarily gain the benefit of a Goblin Vow (as the Merit) for the duration of their agreement. The subject does not need to be informed of the granted boon, but will still be capable of using the Merit if he makes the attempt. If the subject breaks a personal use of the Goblin Vow, the consequences of the violation will fall on both the wonderwell and the subject. The duration or severity of these consequences are considered one degree higher for breaking a Goblin Vow that the wonderwell does not already possess as a Merit. A wonderwell can only have a number of these transient Goblin Vows equal to her Wyrd at any given time, and removing an existing one requires that the subject break a sealing or bargain that he has entered into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T13:47:09-07:00","id":853656,"title":"","content":"And that's when the Keeper becomes the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3OcGSi3FobA\" target=\"_blank\">God Hand!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T15:37:18-07:00","id":853711,"title":"","content":"<b>Reanimator</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Don't be silly, of course I can die! I just don't stay dead for very long.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> In the chaotic, ever changing realm of the Fae, survival is less about the fittest and more about blind luck. Not all slaves are blessed with the luck required to survive their Keeper's realm and come to meet tragic fates. To compensate for this, the god-like Fae restored them to life, and then they did so again, and again, and again, and again! A thousand times the Reanimator died, and a thousand times they were brought back to life, being refused death by their sadistic Keepers. Eventually, they turned this curse into a blessing and managed to escape when their Keeper was unable to threaten them anymore!<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A multi headed serpent who's central head is immortal.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A genocidal monster who's body adapts itself with every death it experiences.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A splendorous bird of flame who is reborn from the ashes of its own cremation.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Cursing the heavens for its lot in life, this tortured individual defies even death itself from stopping their vengeance.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> Having escaped from a recycling plant, it's body is made out of renewable resources.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> An amalgamation of fresh body parts held together by a road map of stitches, leather straps and steel bolts.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Reanimator has crossed the line between death and life more times than they can remember, and now it has become second nature to them. Each turn, the Changeling regenerates a number of health boxes equal to half of their Wyrd (rounded up) starting with the lowest type of damage. Additionally, they may spend a point of Glamour as a reflexive action to resurrect themselves from death once per day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-26-2016, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T18:48:17-07:00","id":853795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=853619#post853619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's one I've been working on for a couple weeks. Feedback would certainly be welcome, as I worry that I may have made it too powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting write-up. Heh, I can see this fitting well with that Rumplestiltskin's Bargain hack I saw lying around here in the forums. Not to mention 1E pledgecrafting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=853711#post853711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Reanimator</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. You know, I happen to have a 2E conversion of the Death Clause in my Contract Conversion thread. Perhaps it could fit well with the Reanimator's kith blessing, or perhaps be part of it with a unique advantage? Either way, great work.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-26-2016, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T20:30:05-07:00","id":853846,"title":"","content":"Was trying to give them regenerative powers like Werewolves, without it being super OP. The way I heard it, Werewolves are going to be damn near unkillable via mundane attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T20:44:07-07:00","id":853851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=853846#post853846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was trying to give them regenerative powers like Werewolves, without it being super OP. The way I heard it, Werewolves are going to be damn near unkillable via mundane attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the 2E book for werewolves, so yeah. That's true. Hmm. Perhaps lowering it to half their Wyrd (rounded up) could work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T20:47:27-07:00","id":853853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=853851#post853851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I got the 2E book for werewolves, so yeah. That's true. Hmm. Perhaps lowering it to half their Wyrd (rounded up) could work?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> edited it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the way, in case nobody got the reference, the Ogre is inspired by Doomsday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T21:24:01-07:00","id":853875,"title":"","content":"Here is another one I've been working on. My goal with it was to create a music-based kith that didn't trample the toes of the ones that we've already got. <br /> <br /> <b>Revelrouser</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">You've got to come with me tonight! I've heard the guy they've got playing before, and this rave is going to be like nothing you've ever experienced before!</span><br /> <br /> The revels of the Gentry are legendary, and mortals are known to lose all inhibitions at the first note of faery music that they hear. Chosen from mortals with a talent for music and a lust for life, the revelrousers are utilized as entertainers by Keepers seeking an evening of unbridled debauchery. A Durance of endless revelry can strain the sanity of even the most dedicated performers, however, and a revelrouser may discover that escape is his only chance for respite.<br /> <br /> <b>-Beast:</b> A rugged man with the horns and legs of a goat and a set of pipes hanging around his neck.<br /> <b>-Elemental:</b> Neon light outlines her every rippling feature as she raises the silver flute to her sparkling lips.<br /> <b>-Ogre:</b> A cracked but functional electric guitar clutched in the roughly callused hands of a two-headed giant singing in harmony.<br /> <b>-Wizened:</b> Glowing eyes pulse with each beat emitted from the turntable embedded within his chest.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Revelrousers gain the rote quality on all rolls to perform music. By spending a point of Glamour while performing, the changeling may roll Presence + Expression vs. Composure + Wyrd to induce hedonistic behavior in his audience, inflicting the Swooning or Wanton Condition on all affected members of the audience. The Condition persists for a number of hours equal to the revelrouser's Wyrd. A character suffering from either Condition who partakes in alcohol or drug use will also gain the Intoxicated Condition for the same duration. Without spending Glamour, the changeling may still seek to inflict one of these Conditions on his listeners, but the Condition only affects those with lower Composure than the changeling's Wyrd, and the effects will only persist for the duration of the revelrouser's performance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T21:37:31-07:00","id":853883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=853875#post853875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is another one I've been working on. My goal with it was to create a music-based kith that didn't trample the toes of the ones that we've already got. <br /> <br /> <b>Revelrouser</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">You've got to come with me tonight! I've heard the guy they've got playing before, and this rave is going to be like nothing you've ever experienced before!</span><br /> <br /> The revels of the Gentry are legendary, and mortals are known to lose all inhibitions at the first note of faery music that they hear. Chosen from mortals with a talent for music and a lust for life, the revelrousers are utilized as entertainers by Keepers seeking an evening of unbridled debauchery. A Durance of endless revelry can strain the sanity of even the most dedicated performers, however, and a revelrouser may discover that escape is his only chance for respite.<br /> <br /> <b>-Beast:</b> A rugged man with the horns and legs of a goat and a set of pipes hanging around his neck.<br /> <b>-Elemental:</b> Neon light outlines her every rippling feature as she raises the silver flute to her sparkling lips.<br /> <b>-Ogre:</b> A cracked but functional electric guitar clutched in the roughly callused hands of a two-headed giant singing in harmony.<br /> <b>-Wizened:</b> Glowing eyes pulse with each beat emitted from the turntable embedded within his chest.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Revelrousers gain the rote quality on all rolls to perform music. By spending a point of Glamour while performing, the changeling may roll Presence + Expression vs. Composure + Wyrd to induce hedonistic behavior in his audience, inflicting the Swooning or Wanton Condition on all affected members of the audience. The Condition persists for a number of hours equal to the revelrouser's Wyrd. A character suffering from either Condition who partakes in alcohol or drug use will also gain the Intoxicated Condition for the same duration. Without spending Glamour, the changeling may still seek to inflict one of these Conditions on his listeners, but the Condition only affects those with lower Composure than the changeling's Wyrd, and the effects will only persist for the duration of the revelrouser's performance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nicely done.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Now, we have the potential for a musical quartet of Lost. Hehe, onto a more serious note, may I suggest Dionysian as an alternative name? There was this Dionysian kith I found online that I was meaning to convert, but I never quite figured out how to alter the blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T23:00:15-07:00","id":853913,"title":"","content":"I'm glad that you like the kith. I will keep them with their current name, though, as Dionysian has a bit more of a religious overtone to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T09:41:28-07:00","id":854086,"title":"","content":"This is a good one, I think. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Babelfish</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I am fluent in over six million forms of communication!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> The alien world of the Fae is home to infinite forms of dialect, many of which are physically impossible for human mouths to speak. Changelings who became Babelfish were used as some form of universal translator, bridging the gap between those who would have otherwise been incapable of communication. Eventually, the magic of Arcadia blended the languages together for them, so now all dialect sounds the same to the Babelfish. One day, they managed to outsmart their Keepers by luring them to a place where they couldn't understand the people around them!<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A sophisticated trout wearing scholarly glasses, a top hat and wet scarf wrapped around his gills.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A political android who accompanies Court ambassadors on foreign missions.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A blood stained interrogator who laughs at the idea of language barriers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> When speaking to a Babelfish, you may as well be talking in their native language as far as they're concerned. At character creation, the Babelfish is automatically fluent in all forms of spoken language, even if it is the first time hearing it. By spending a point of Glamour, they can share this knowledge with others for the rest of the scene, allowing perfect communication between untrained parties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-27-2016, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:05:21-07:00","id":854128,"title":"","content":"I've got a kith idea I'm mulling over. I think the appropriate name would be something like &quot;Tweedleduo.&quot; Basic idea is that two people are abducted to be a pair of identical twins for humorous and/or creepy effect. Not sure if it should be done as having two separate characters, a PC and NPC, or a single &quot;person&quot; with two bodies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T14:28:14-07:00","id":854215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=854128#post854128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a kith idea I'm mulling over. I think the appropriate name would be something like &quot;Tweedleduo.&quot; Basic idea is that two people are abducted to be a pair of identical twins for humorous and/or creepy effect. Not sure if it should be done as having two separate characters, a PC and NPC, or a single &quot;person&quot; with two bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Might I suggest giving them an automatic split personality? Their mask looks like one crazy person, but their Mien being the twins always within arms reach of one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T17:55:16-07:00","id":854276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=854086#post854086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Babelfish</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Without saying more than I'm sure I can: This isn't going to have a terribly strong niche in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T17:58:38-07:00","id":854278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=854276#post854276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without saying more than I'm sure I can: This isn't going to have a terribly strong niche in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to agree here. Maybe make them be able to read and write in any language automatically, like Authors? And perhaps let them spend Glamour to extend that gift to others a la the Swimmerskin with their ability to give air to others?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T18:04:50-07:00","id":854284,"title":"","content":"I suppose the Babelfish would be at its best in a setting that involves a nomadic freehold or an extremely cosmopolitan city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T19:27:26-07:00","id":854319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=854278#post854278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm inclined to agree here. Maybe make them be able to read and write in any language automatically, like Authors? And perhaps let them spend Glamour to extend that gift to others a la the Swimmerskin with their ability to give air to others?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright, I edited it as suggested.<br /> <br /> I wanted it to be spoken language instead of written. The term &quot;Babelfish&quot; is a commonly used film trope in which the characters are actually speaking in their native language; but for convenience sake, the audience hears it in whatever language the film happens to be translated in. Kind of like wearing a green lantern power ring. This explains why so many alien races happen to speak perfect English. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That was the inspiration behind the Kith, and I felt it was something the Fae might actually come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-27-2016, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T19:53:00-07:00","id":854330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=854319#post854319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Alright, I edited it as suggested.<br /> <br /> I wanted it to be spoken language instead of written. The term &amp;quot;Babelfish&amp;quot; is a commonly used film trope in which the characters are actually speaking in their native language; but for convenience sake, the audience hears it in whatever language the film happens to be translated in. Kind of like wearing a green lantern power ring. This explains why so many alien races happen to speak perfect English. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That was the inspiration behind the Kith, and I felt it was something the Fae might actually come up with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I see. Now, I understand it a little better. And in that case, maybe you can limit it to spoken languages, then? I don't know. I'm trying to figure out how to further distinguish it from the Author.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T20:00:29-07:00","id":854331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=854330#post854330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And in that case, maybe you can limit it to spoken languages</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that's how I had it set up the first time. :P Changed it back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T20:15:11-07:00","id":854337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=854278#post854278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm inclined to agree here. Maybe make them be able to read and write in any language automatically, like Authors? And perhaps let them spend Glamour to extend that gift to others a la the Swimmerskin with their ability to give air to others?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not going to have a niche because there's a merit that more or less allows this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https:/