s://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T21:02:37-07:00","id":854350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=854348#post854348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noooooooooooooooope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol. Alright, will just keep managing this thread while I wait patiently for all the 2E stuff to come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T00:40:44-07:00","id":854383,"title":"","content":"<b>Burrower</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I swear, if you call me a Dwarf one more time, I will take this axe and split your skull open!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> From goblin hordes, to bearded men, to Lovecraftian cultists, there are many stories of those who tunnel beneath the surface. While in Arcadia, those who became Burrowers served in massive subterranean kingdoms. The first time they saw daylight was most likely when they escaped to the surface and fled into the Hedge. Sometimes the Burrowers were used to work the mines, digging out precious resources to fuel their Keeper's needs or desires. Other times they were construction workers tasked with expanding the Keeper's realm of influence. And if they were really unfortunate, they were just given a compulsive urge to dig with no real explanation!<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A stout, broad shouldered man holding a pick axe in one hand and his waist length beard in the other. He's known around the Freehold for being an alcoholic.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A giant mole who walks upright like a man and wears comically thick lense glasses.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A dark robed cultist who can be found muttering about entities locked away eons ago.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> One of their hands was replaced with a trow after it was crushed by falling rocks. A mining helmet is strapped tightly around their head, flameless torches hang from their twin bandoleers while telescopic spectacles adorn their face.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> Spending time as a human sink hole, their body is comprised of loose, shifting mud that threatens to swallow prisoners down into the earth.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> With rosy cheeks, a pot belly and hair covering the tops of their feet, they lived under the hills of Arcadia for a time. Eventually, the call of adventure prompted them to abandon their shire homes.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Having been forced to work underground for so long, Burrowers are now exceptionally skilled excavators. Burrowers will never become lost underground regardless of the structural layout they find themselves in, and they can see without the need for a light source unless their vision is supernaturally impaired. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, the Burrower is capable of digging a 6x6 foot space equal to half their Wyrd rounded up in only a single turn, provided that their tools are capable of penetrating the material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":".  Grammatical errors corrected. 03-31-2016, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T06:04:59-07:00","id":855641,"title":"","content":"<b>Wyrdo:</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Look, it's very simple. That cloud insulted this scorpion That's why you got chocolate pudding instead of vanilla!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> In the homeworld of the True Fae, things rarely make sense to human perspectives. But once in a while you get that special brand of craziness that leaves even the True Fae scratching their heads in confusion. Changelings who became Wyrdos were taken from those who already teetered on the brink of insanity and were constantly transformed and recreated during their stay. Unsure of what they were supposed to be, their whimsical madness would eventually allow them to disorient even the True Fae themselves, and thus escape back to the stable reality of Earth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A human sized spleen that crawls around with a giant thumb and a single knee cap.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> An old man with an octopus for a face who often lives underground, his hobbies include sailing and oneiromancy.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened: </b> A private investigator who's own body functions like a magic satchel, containing all the gadgets he needs to complete his mission.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Due to their experience in Arcadia, Wyrdos have grown accustomed to madness and can deal with it much easier than other people. They gain the benefit of the 8 again rule when attempting to resist Clarity breaks. Additionally, they can share this with other Changelings by spending a point of Glamour and explaining their alien rationality. The effects of this last until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> The Wyrdo's explanation doesn't have to make logical sense. There is also no word count and can be anywhere from brief quips to full on lectures. Players are encouraged to have fun with it, either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T06:12:58-07:00","id":855643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=855641#post855641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wyrdo:</b><br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;Look, it's very simple. That cloud insulted this scorpion That's why you got chocolate pudding instead of vanilla!&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> In the homeworld of the True Fae, things rarely make sense to human perspectives. But once in a while you get that special brand of craziness that leaves even the True Fae scratching their heads in confusion. Changelings who became Wyrdos were taken from those who already teetered on the brink of insanity and were constantly transformed and recreated during their stay. Unsure of what they were supposed to be, their whimsical madness would eventually allow them to disorient even the True Fae themselves, and thus escape back to the stable reality of Earth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A human sized spleen that crawls around with a giant thumb and a single knee cap.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> An old man with an octopus for a face who often lives underground, his hobbies include sailing and oneiromancy.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened: </b> A private investigator who's own body functions like a magic satchel, containing all the gadgets he needs to complete his mission.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Due to their experience in Arcadia, Wyrdos have grown accustomed to madness and can deal with it much easier than other people. They gain the benefit of the 8 again rule when attempting to resist Clarity breaks. Additionally, they can share this with other Changelings by spending a point of Glamour and explaining their alien rationality. The effects of this last until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> The Wyrdo's explanation doesn't have to make logical sense. There is also no word count and can be anywhere from brief quips to full on lectures. Players are encouraged to have fun with it, either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>O_o<br /> Wow. This is kinda creepy. Changelings whose madness confounds even the Gentry? Hello, fae Malkavians. I shudder to imagine how much mayhem a Chimera/Wyrdo could cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T06:32:19-07:00","id":855652,"title":"","content":"I recall that someone on one of the threads had been looking for a 'wizardly' kith. This one was my attempt to create such a kith. I worry that I may have made it too potent, though. I'm thinking about getting rid of the Seeming affinity and replacing it with a free use of the other part of their blessing once per scene. Any feedback would be welcome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Runeskin</b><br /> <br /> The old lady who lives in that house is a witch. My big brother told me so. He said that she seems nice enough, but he once saw her turn into a toad. You can go up there if you want to, but I'm sure not about to ring her doorbell!<br /> <br /> The Gentry take people with an unhealthy fascination with the occult to make into runeskins. These changelings served as familiars or apprentices to sorcerous Keepers, and learned first hand the extent of the magic that the Gentry wield. Although the runeskins may utilize their knowledge to escape their Keeper, the constant flow of Arcadian magic never truly leaves them.<br /> <br /> <b>-Beast:</b> An animal that appears to be a witch's familiar, such as a black cat with glowing sigils in her eyes, or a toad with warts forming arcane patterns.<br /> <b>-Darkling:</b> Inky black symbols shift from one shape to another as they slowly drift across her pale skin.<br /> <b>-Elemental:</b> An androgynous figure made up of translucent blue light, with glyphs of brighter light floating within the shining form.<br /> <b>-Wizened:</b> He is tall and lanky, with a long white beard and dexterous wooden hands engraved with intricate runes.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Runeskins are especially adept at acquiring and wielding the magic of Arcadia. Each runeskin has an affinity for a second Seeming, and will gain the favored effect for that Seeming as well as their own when acquiring new Contracts. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, the next Contract that the runeskin activates within the scene will have its target number lowered from 8 to 7. The changeling may use this blessing multiple times, but each use applies to a different Contract, and the runeskin may only improve a number of Contracts in a given scene equal to their Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T06:53:01-07:00","id":855661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=855652#post855652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Runeskin</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting concept. But the Blessing could use some polishing. Maybe even a little revision. <br /> <br /> If I may? <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Runeskins are especially adept at acquiring and wielding the magic of Arcadia. Upon learning a new Contract, they may gain the clause of another Seeming, which can be in addition to the clause they may have an affinity for. Furthermore, they may reflexively use a given Contract a number of times equal to their Wyrd + 1 in a scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-30-2016, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T07:19:21-07:00","id":855678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=855652#post855652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall that someone on one of the threads had been looking for a 'wizardly' kith.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do they know about Witchtooth yet? They're a Kith who specializes in the occult and are able to curse people.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mZpz1PhV2jzc2ihda1IwHZc_WTrWTv5qbNv4vzcU2-4/preview?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a link to some already existing Kiths.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:49:17-07:00","id":856250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=855661#post855661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting concept. But the Blessing could use some polishing. Maybe even a little revision.<br /> <br /> If I may?<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Runeskins are especially adept at acquiring and wielding the magic of Arcadia. Upon learning a new Contract, they may gain the clause of another Seeming, which can be in addition to the clause they may have an affinity for. Furthermore, they may reflexively use a given Contract a number of times equal to their Wyrd + 1 in a scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the feedback. Interestingly enough, your suggestion for a revision to the favored effect part of the Contract was exactly what I had originally thought of when I was first working on them. The kith's blessing has gone through several iterations over the course of creating them, and I decided to limit it to a single Seeming so that they didn't get what amounted to a bonus Experience every time they purchased a new Contract. I had actually worried that even with that limitation, it might be too much of an experience break. I had had some other ideas for it that ultimately I removed, such as a monthly ritual for a Glamour infusion or other dice effects for Contracts (9-Again, bonus dice equal to Wyrd, etc.). I settled on the target number reduction as a way of giving them a bonus to Contract activation that would still benefit those with Dual Kith to one of the kiths that have a bonus to activate a single Contract. Your idea of giving them reflexive Contract activation rather than an easier time wielding them is an interesting one, and one that I had never even considered previously. I'll need to give that one some thought after looking through the Contracts again. Thank you again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=855678#post855678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do they know about Witchtooth yet? They're a Kith who specializes in the occult and are able to curse people.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They had, but it wasn't quite what they were looking for. I tracked down the original post about it, and ultimately, my kith wouldn't have fit what they were looking for either. They were hoping for one that could learn mortal supernatural Merits at a discounted cost or something like that.<br /> <br /> Also, kudos on the Burrowers. They were very well done. You saved me a lot of effort there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T00:14:41-07:00","id":856319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=856250#post856250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the feedback. Interestingly enough, your suggestion for a revision to the favored effect part of the Contract was exactly what I had originally thought of when I was first working on them. The kith's blessing has gone through several iterations over the course of creating them, and I decided to limit it to a single Seeming so that they didn't get what amounted to a bonus Experience every time they purchased a new Contract. I had actually worried that even with that limitation, it might be too much of an experience break. I had had some other ideas for it that ultimately I removed, such as a monthly ritual for a Glamour infusion or other dice effects for Contracts (9-Again, bonus dice equal to Wyrd, etc.). I settled on the target number reduction as a way of giving them a bonus to Contract activation that would still benefit those with Dual Kith to one of the kiths that have a bonus to activate a single Contract. Your idea of giving them reflexive Contract activation rather than an easier time wielding them is an interesting one, and one that I had never even considered previously. I'll need to give that one some thought after looking through the Contracts again. Thank you again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad I could help. And now that you mentioned them, letting them have Contract affinity with one other Seeming does make more sense if you want to avoid giving them free passes with new powers. The reflexive Contract use were derived from the Contract mechanics in the 2E playtest draft, which (I think) allowed you to reflexively activate a Contract once in a scene/chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T00:16:57-07:00","id":856321,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Tradesman</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I assure you, she'll be a valued slave for your collection. And I'm offering her for the low, low price of my continued freedom!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> In the world of the Fae, everything is conducted through bargaining and contracts. But making deals is dangerous, even for the Gentry. Changelings who became Tradesmen were used to conduct business proposals in their Keeper's stead, while allowing their master to reap the profits of their dealings. They bargained with Hedge Markets, Loyalists and even the True Fae themselves, until eventually they became experienced enough to cut a deal that resulted in their escape.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A merchant prince dressed head to toe in extravagant jewelry and top of the line clothing.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A raccoon-dog who carries their wares in a large, fur covered bag slung over their shoulder.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A shifty street peddler who sells stolen merchandise in dark alleyways.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Their time spent in Arcadia has instilled the Tradesman with a supernatural talent for business sense. They gain +3 on attempts to barter with others. Additionally, they may spend a point of Glamour to add their Wyrd on attempts to appraise items. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T02:27:08-07:00","id":856349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=856321#post856321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Tradesman</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Do compare it to my version of the Huckster kith. I'm not sure if the Tradesman is eclipsed by it in terms of Blessings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:01:13-07:00","id":856387,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Apollonian</u></b> <br /> These changelings come to embody the physical ideal of perfection rather than the aesthetic, like the heroic athletes of legend. Often fiercely competitive or highly ambitious as mortals, they were taken to excel at all manner of physical contests for their Keepers, whether it's cleaving a block of stone in two with a single blow, running for days on end without so much as losing their breath, or skittering catlike through the most deadly obstacles.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> A man whose features are of an animal that embodies sportsmanship<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> A golden Colossus endowed with the strength of ten men.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> An attractive, short-haired woman who can outrun most people with ease.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> An Apollonian gains an extra dot in Strength or Dexterity, which can take her above the usual limitations imposed by her Wyrd. She also benefits from the 8-again rule on all Athletics, Brawl, and Weaponry rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T22:03:15-07:00","id":856949,"title":"","content":"Okay, here is another one I've been working on. I'm pretty proud of it, but I'm worried that it might be a bit underpowered. Any feedback would be welcome.<br /> <br /> <b>Faerysue</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Don't worry, I can handle this. I've done something just like it once before.</span><br /> <br /> Most of the time, when one of the Gentry takes a mortal, they intend to change them into something very specific. Then there are those who wish for a single changeling that can excel at a large variety of tasks, either because the Keeper has an extremely varied list of tasks that must be accomplished or because the Keeper wishes to have a servant that can quickly adapt to any situation that arises. Towards this end, the Gentry choose mortals of great skill, adaptability, or potential to become their faerysues. The trouble with such an adaptable servant, though, is that there is generally nothing that can be done to stop her when she finally decides that she is ready to return home.<br /> <br /> <b>-Fairest:</b> A beautiful and inspiring figure, inevitably with some unusual trait that it quite striking. The faerysue is such an impressive changeling that they inevitably inspire others to follow them, often beginning a mass exodus of a given Keeper's changelings. Because of this, all faerysues end up as Fairest, regardless of their actual plan to escape. Some may show some hint of what they might have become if they'd been a member of a lesser kith, however, such as a pair of adorable cat ears for one that might have otherwise become a Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A faerysue is intended to excel at everything they do, and their Blessing reflects this. A faerysue gains the 8-Again effect on all Skill rolls, and achieves an exceptional success on 3 successes instead of 5. For any Skill roll involving one of her Specialties, she receives the rote quality. Additionally, the Wyrd is so impressed by her awesomeness that it lends the faerysue a little more power than other changelings receive. By spending a point of Glamour, a faerysue can gain access to a Contract or Merit that she doesn't possess for the duration of the scene. The faerysue is only able to gain a number of these additional traits equal to her Wyrd in a given scene, and the Glamour spent on acquiring a new Contract does not count towards the cost of activating the Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T05:59:17-07:00","id":857081,"title":"","content":"While I like the name, I don't quite agree with them being limited to Fairest seeming. Having Kiths exclusive to a Seeming was something that 1E had, which was frustrating and limited (at least to me.)<br /> <br /> Changeling 2E included the option for any Seeming to be of any Kith, which was a nice change and added for more imagination.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's a few other possible ideas you could have for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> The new girl in the town who inexplicably was welcomed by everybody despite her bland personality and generic backstory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ogre: </b>A champion among men, the Authors have written fact books depicting his many accomplishments, like catching bullets with their pecks, or sawing down trees with their eyelashes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> An extremely well trained animal capable of performing stunts they would never have attempted in nature, such as jumping through fire, riding on a ball, or dancing in a conga line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T06:09:15-07:00","id":857084,"title":"","content":"Having a bit of trouble wrapping my head around this kith, given the trope it embodies. I suppose it's a matter of preference, though, seeing as I find this kith somewhat overpowered rather than under. Excellent work, regardless, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T06:58:16-07:00","id":857104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=857084#post857084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a bit of trouble wrapping my head around this kith, given the trope it embodies. I suppose it's a matter of preference, though, seeing as I find this kith somewhat overpowered rather than under. Excellent work, regardless, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Check the date.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T08:14:32-07:00","id":857136,"title":"","content":"<b>Orc</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Yeah, I drink the blood of elves, whatever. Now piss off before I start feeling thirsty!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> As terrible as warfare is in the human world, it still can't compare to the glorious nightmare that is a war between rival Fae armies. Changelings who became Orcs did not simply participate in war, they lived for it! Chosen from the ranks of the blood thirsty and the adrenaline junkies, Orcs were commonly male, although there were occasional females seen among their number. The only opinions Orcs considered valid were those of the strong. Cowards and weaklings were not worthy of consideration, which is why they abandoned the army once they felt their Keeper was no longer worthy of their allegiance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> The head of a boar on the body of a man or woman. Their pot belly serves well to mask the brutish strength coursing through their limbs.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A green skinned humanoid with porcine tusks and hulking muscles. Even the women of their clan were more than a match for human soldiers.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Gray skinned, pointy ears and a hoard of battle scars, this barbarian raided enemy settlements at night and returned to base before sunrise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Orcs lived and breathed combat during their time in Arcadia, turning them into savage warriors. Orcs gain the benefit of the 8 again rule on all contests involving Strength and Stamina. Additionally, they may spend a point of Glamour to add +3 damage on melee attacks (weapon or fists) on its next attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-02-2016, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T08:42:52-07:00","id":857149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=857104#post857104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Check the date.</div> </div> </div> </div> ......<br /> ...... Damn. April Fools strikes again.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> On a more serious note.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=857136#post857136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Orc</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Nicely done on the Orc kith, man <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It'll probably make me consider revisiting the Blessing for my Apollonian conversion. But all the same, great work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T06:50:11-07:00","id":857675,"title":"","content":"<b>Damsel</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;If you expect me to put out just because you saved me, I'll show you what happened to the last guy who made assumptions about me.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Some Fae like to play the hero in their realm, defeating the forces of evil and saving the people while being showered with praise. Unfortunately their alien mindset is unable to distinguish genuine acts of heroism from a common PR stunt. Changelings who became Damsels were taken from women who lead abusive or dangerous lives for the soul purpose of being rescued over and over again. During their time in Arcadia, they were constantly kidnapped, threatened, assaulted, or imprisoned from the world, only to have their Keeper come to their rescue. After being celebrated for their heroic deed, the Keeper would take the Damsel to his bed and the cycle would repeat again. One day, they decided to save themselves instead of waiting around for others to do it for them!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Her perfect beauty attracted the scorn of those vying for her Keeper's affections. One day, she took advantage of her position and staged a preemptive strike on the evil queen, denying the Keeper his chance to save the day.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> She was told that only true love's kiss would break the spell that turned her into a hideous monster. But now she's done looking for romance, she just wants revenge on the one who cursed her.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A beautiful nature spirit kidnapped by evil wizards who desired her power for their own. One day, she decided to show them what happens when you antagonize mother nature.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Isolated from social contact, she often found that animals were her only companions in life. One day she used her connection to them and became the savage princess of the wild that she is now.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Her Keeper trapped her in a continuous loop of watching her friends and family slaughtered by a tyrant who claimed her as his bride, only to have the Keeper avenge their deaths and free her from the unwanted marriage. That kind of trauma can do terrible things to a young girl's soul, like giving her the strength to murder her husband who was still exhausted from sex.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A life sized toy brought to life, she was the key piece of a play set orchestrated by her Keeper. Before her escape, she showed the puppet master why men often have a psychological fear of dolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Damsels were made to be rescued until they learned how to rescue themselves. Their blessing gives them the Rote quality on attempts to persuade others that they are weak or foolish. They also add half their Wyrd rounded up on attempts to maintain their Wits during unprovoked confrontations, even if they pretend to have done otherwise. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, they can add +3 to Subterfuge rolls for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> As the name implies, Damsels are stereotypically female characters. However, there have cases where eccentric or female oriented Keepers have chosen male Damsels as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":".  Edited the Blessing 04-03-2016, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T12:39:36-07:00","id":857858,"title":"","content":"I like the concept, though I suppose some fae would produce a male damsel in an attempt to be original, or so that they could play warrior princess themselves and subvert the familiar trope, even if it's just a shallow inversion. Another male version I can think of is the unlucky sidekick who exists for the supervillain to abduct so the superhero Gentry can rescue him. ...Up until the sidekick gets clever enough to make his own escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T13:31:19-07:00","id":857887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=856319#post856319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Glad I could help. And now that you mentioned them, letting them have Contract affinity with one other Seeming does make more sense if you want to avoid giving them free passes with new powers. The reflexive Contract use were derived from the Contract mechanics in the 2E playtest draft, which (I think) allowed you to reflexively activate a Contract once in a scene/chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I looked over the draft, and it is actually something that can be done by spending Glamour anyway when fulfilling a Contract's Catch. It is actually something that can be done multiple times per scene anyway, as the limit is based on how much Glamour you can spend and how many Catches you can activate. I've been working on a different version of the blessing, though, and here it is:<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Runeskins are especially adept at acquiring and wielding the magic of Arcadia. Each runeskin has an affinity for a second Seeming, and will gain the favored effect for that Seeming as well as their own when acquiring new Contracts. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, the next Contract that the runeskin activates within the scene will benefit from the 8-Again effect. The changeling may only use this blessing a number of times in a scene equal to their Wyrd, and the Glamour cost to utilize the blessing is not obviated by enacting a Contract's Catch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T13:39:41-07:00","id":857894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=857081#post857081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I like the name, I don't quite agree with them being limited to Fairest seeming. Having Kiths exclusive to a Seeming was something that 1E had, which was frustrating and limited (at least to me.)<br /> <br /> Changeling 2E included the option for any Seeming to be of any Kith, which was a nice change and added for more imagination.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's a few other possible ideas you could have for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> The new girl in the town who inexplicably was welcomed by everybody despite her bland personality and generic backstory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ogre: </b>A champion among men, the Authors have written fact books depicting his many accomplishments, like catching bullets with their pecks, or sawing down trees with their eyelashes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> An extremely well trained animal capable of performing stunts they would never have attempted in nature, such as jumping through fire, riding on a ball, or dancing in a conga line.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like what you came up with here, especially the Darkling one. It was intended to be part of the gag when I'd gone Fairest only for them, but you do make a good point about the added potential of allowing the other Seemings to be faerysues as well. <br /> <br /> I do hope everyone enjoyed my little joke. I'm slowly working on a more serious 'jack-of-all-trades' flavored kith that would be a bit better balanced than the faerysues.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T13:47:00-07:00","id":857898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=857675#post857675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Damsel</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Having been exposed to danger countless times, the Damsel is less like Princess Peach and more like Princess Leia. They add half their Wyrd rounded down on attempts to maintain their Wits and Composure in unprovoked confrontations. Additionally, they may spend a point of Glamour to add +3 to their Subterfuge for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> As the name implies, Damsels are intended to be female characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with BronzeDog that you shouldn't limit the Damsels to female characters, even if they are the most common.<br /> <br /> I think that for the blessing, you should round their Wyrd up rather than down, as it would mean that even Wyrd 1 changelings would be able to benefit from it. I could also see some capability of being able to get a message to someone in times of great need as part of their blessing, such as spending a point of Glamour to instantly send a message consisting of a number of sentences equal to their Wyrd when they are in physical danger or magically imprisoned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T15:30:58-07:00","id":857963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=857898#post857898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with BronzeDog that you shouldn't limit the Damsels to female characters, even if they are the most common.<br /> <br /> I think that for the blessing, you should round their Wyrd up rather than down, as it would mean that even Wyrd 1 changelings would be able to benefit from it. I could also see some capability of being able to get a message to someone in times of great need as part of their blessing, such as spending a point of Glamour to instantly send a message consisting of a number of sentences equal to their Wyrd when they are in physical danger or magically imprisoned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Idealy, I was going to give them free Telepathy at character creation, since there are many stories of princesses having prophetic dreams or sending visions to those who would be their heroes. But the point of the Kith was that they learned how to save themselves, instead of waiting for others to come get them. So I designed their blessing to be more self reliant.<br /> <br /> But I thought the rounded down option would have allowed Wyrd 1 characters, or did I misunderstand that?<br /> <br /> Anyways, went back and edited it, also included the possibility of males in the Note.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-02-2016, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T15:59:52-07:00","id":857973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=856387#post856387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Apollonian</u></b><br /> These changelings come to embody the physical ideal of perfection rather than the aesthetic, like the heroic athletes of legend. Often fiercely competitive or highly ambitious as mortals, they were taken to excel at all manner of physical contests for their Keepers, whether it's cleaving a block of stone in two with a single blow, running for days on end without so much as losing their breath, or skittering catlike through the most deadly obstacles.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> A man whose features are of an animal that embodies sportsmanship<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> A golden Colossus endowed with the strength of ten men.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> An attractive, short-haired woman who can outrun most people with ease.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> An Apollonian gains an extra dot in Strength or Dexterity, which can take her above the usual limitations imposed by her Wyrd. She also benefits from the 8-again rule on all Athletics, Brawl, and Weaponry rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is an update of the Kith from 1d4chan, right? You should link to the source.<br /> <br /> As it stands, I'd restrict their Blessing a little bit. For example, I don't think that Weaponry rolls for silently assassinating someone in the dark fits their concept very much. My suggestion is to give the 8 Again for duels, competitions, self-defense or just showing off. Actually brutalizing, maiming and killing should be done by Bloodbrutes, Razorhands, Soldiers and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:13:54-07:00","id":857983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=857136#post857136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Orc</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Yeah, I drink the blood of elves, whatever. Now piss off before I start feeling thirsty!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> As terrible as warfare is in the human world, it still can't compare to the glorious nightmare that is a war between rival Fae armies. Changelings who became Orcs did not simply participate in war, they lived for it! Chosen from the ranks of the blood thirsty and the adrenaline junkies, Orcs were commonly male, although there were occasional females seen among their number. The only opinions Orcs considered valid were those of the strong. Cowards and weaklings were not worthy of consideration, which is why they abandoned the army once they felt their Keeper was no longer worthy of their allegiance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> The head of a boar on the body of a man or woman. Their pot belly serves well to mask the brutish strength coursing through their limbs.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A green skinned humanoid with porcine tusks and hulking muscles. Even the women of their clan were more than a match for human soldiers.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Gray skinned, pointy ears and a hoard of battle scars, this barbarian raided enemy settlements at night and returned to base before sunrise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Orcs lived and breathed combat during their time in Arcadia, turning them into savage warriors. Orcs gain the benefit of the 8 again rule on all contests involving Strength and Stamina. Additionally, they may spend a point of Glamour to add +3 damage on melee attacks (weapon or fists) for the rest of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div> While I like the quote and the description, this seems like it could be fused with the Bloodbrute and/or Soldier Kiths. I mean, isn't an Ogre Soldier already pretty Orc-like? Also, that scene-long bonus to damage is really powerful, even more so if it stacks with normal Damage Bonuses. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:36:22-07:00","id":858002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=857973#post857973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is an update of the Kith from 1d4chan, right? You should link to the source.<br /> <br /> As it stands, I'd restrict their Blessing a little bit. For example, I don't think that Weaponry rolls for silently assassinating someone in the dark fits their concept very much. My suggestion is to give the 8 Again for duels, competitions, self-defense or just showing off. Actually brutalizing, maiming and killing should be done by Bloodbrutes, Razorhands, Soldiers and such.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe it only works when there's at least [11 - Wyrd] nonparticipants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:51:35-07:00","id":858009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858002#post858002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe it only works when there's at least [11 - Wyrd] nonparticipants?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's too specific and unnecessarily restrictive. If it looks and feels like a duel, challenge, bet, performance, tournament or championship of some kind, apply the 8 Again. Just go with the narrative flow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:53:34-07:00","id":858011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858009#post858009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's too specific and unnecessarily restrictive. If it looks and feels like a duel, challenge, bet, performance, tournament or championship of some kind, apply the 8 Again. Just go with the narrative flow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:49:21-07:00","id":858039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=857983#post857983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While I like the quote and the description, this seems like it could be fused with the Bloodbrute and/or Soldier Kiths. I mean, isn't an Ogre Soldier already pretty Orc-like? Also, that scene-long bonus to damage is really powerful, even more so if it stacks with normal Damage Bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Maybe, but I really like Orcs! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Besides, the idea of Bloodbrutes is they were used as gladiators, while Soldiers were just that, soldiers. The Orc kith were used as warriors, they <i>enjoyed</i> combat where as the others were forced into it.<br /> <br /> Also, the blessing increases the weapon's base damage, doesn't take additional bonuses into account. Should I decrease the bonus, or is there another suggestion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-02-2016, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:55:03-07:00","id":858044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858039#post858039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe, but I really like Orcs! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Besides, the idea of Bloodbrutes is they were used as gladiators, while Soldiers were just that, soldiers. The Orc kith were used as warriors, they <i>enjoyed</i> combat where as the others were forced into it.<br /> <br /> Also, the blessing increases the weapon's base damage, doesn't take additional bonuses into account. Should I decrease the bonus, or is there another suggestion?</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps their Blessing could make it easier for them to inflict physical Tilts and increase their duration, even against supernaturals who could normally shrug it off or regenerate. Glorious dismemberment, flying viscera and all that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T18:20:09-07:00","id":858058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858044#post858044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Perhaps their Blessing could make it easier for them to inflict physical Tilts and increase their duration, even against supernaturals who could normally shrug it off or regenerate. Glorious dismemberment, flying viscera and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unfortunately I only have the first edition rule book (didn't know they were out of date at the time), so I don't know know what Tilts are. If they're in the book, I can't find them in the index. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just going to edit the blessing so that it increases the next weapon's damage by 3 instead of a scene duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-02-2016, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T19:01:05-07:00","id":858073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858058#post858058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Unfortunately I only have the first edition rule book (didn't know they were out of date at the time), so I don't know know what Tilts are. If they're in the book, I can't find them in the index. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just going to edit the blessing so that it increases the next weapon's damage by 3 instead of a scene duration.</div> </div> </div> </div> Tilts are basically combat-focused Conditions (catch-all term for status effects that generate conflict and give XP). They include broken arm, blinded, poisoned, deafened, erratic/confused, knocked down and stunned, but also extreme temperatures, floods, darkness, heavy winds and earthquakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T19:40:00-07:00","id":858094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858073#post858073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Tilts are basically combat-focused Conditions (catch-all term for status effects that generate conflict and give XP). They include broken arm, blinded, poisoned, deafened, erratic/confused, knocked down and stunned, but also extreme temperatures, floods, darkness, heavy winds and earthquakes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see, thank you for clearing that up for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T20:12:06-07:00","id":858101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858094#post858094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see, thank you for clearing that up for me.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're welcome. Feel free to send me a private message if you have other questions about 2ED.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T20:47:02-07:00","id":858118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=857973#post857973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is an update of the Kith from 1d4chan, right? You should link to the source.<br /> <br /> As it stands, I'd restrict their Blessing a little bit. For example, I don't think that Weaponry rolls for silently assassinating someone in the dark fits their concept very much. My suggestion is to give the 8 Again for duels, competitions, self-defense or just showing off. Actually brutalizing, maiming and killing should be done by Bloodbrutes, Razorhands, Soldiers and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this work better? Also, linked to the source site on the main post.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <u><b>Apollonian</b></u><br /> <i>&quot;Go ahead. Name the challenge. We'll see which of us is better when you don't have any dirty tricks to fall back on&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> These changelings come to embody the physical ideal of perfection rather than the aesthetic, like the heroic athletes of legend. Often fiercely competitive or highly ambitious as mortals, they were taken to excel at all manner of physical contests for their Keepers, whether it's cleaving a block of stone in two with a single blow, running for days on end without so much as losing their breath, or skittering catlike through the most deadly obstacles.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Beast:</b> A man whose features are of an animal that embodies sportsmanship<br /> <b>\u2022 Elemental:</b> A golden Colossus endowed with the strength of ten men.<br /> <b>\u2022 Fairest:</b> An attractive, short-haired woman who can outrun most people with ease.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> An Apollonian gains an extra dot in Strength or Dexterity, which can take her above the usual limitations imposed by her Wyrd. She also benefits from the 8-again rule on all Athletics, Brawl, and Weaponry rolls made during competitions, duels, and self-defense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=857894#post857894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like what you came up with here, especially the Darkling one. It was intended to be part of the gag when I'd gone Fairest only for them, but you do make a good point about the added potential of allowing the other Seemings to be faerysues as well.<br /> <br /> I do hope everyone enjoyed my little joke. I'm slowly working on a more serious 'jack-of-all-trades' flavored kith that would be a bit better balanced than the faerysues.</div> </div> </div> </div>And has a better name, too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That said, might I suggest Fools as a possible name? Referring to the Tarot Card of the same name.<br /> <br /> Also, I've added the Runeskin to the main post, with the Blessing being the second Seeming affinity and additional reflexive activation of Contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-03-2016, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T21:08:13-07:00","id":858127,"title":"","content":"Here's another kith conversion, and a slight revision to the Timekeeper kith. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Lusterlit</u></b> <sup><sub>1E From 1d4chan</sub></sup><br /> Lusterlit were infused with radiant and brilliant light to become shining beacons to hold back the darkness or glittering stars gleaming in the night sky. As mortals, they may have been inquisitive individuals, keen on shedding light upon the truth of things. Others may have looked inward instead, seeking personal enlightenment within themselves. All, however, were, noted for bearing reason, intellect, and inspiration, traits which invariably played a role in their escape.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> An insectoid being that roughly resembles a firefly.<br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling:</b> Bulbous heads, shark-like teeth, and skin that glows electric blue.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> The figure's entire body is suffused with a faint and pulsing luminescence.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Lusterlit can filter their sight through the different spectra of light, and can make vision-based rolls without suffering penalties from darkness or poor lighting. If they spend a point of glamour or Willpower, they may make use of the three-dot version of Psychokinesis (Light).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Timekeeper</u></b> <sup><sub>1E by GibberingEloquence</sub></sup><br /> As mortals, they may have been punctual individuals, mindful of the hours they spent in their daily lives. In Arcadia, they were given the duty to keep track of the strange passage of time, which was not always an easy task. Often immobile, they had to figure out the mad patterns of day and night to remember all the appointments of their Keepers' agendas, although they did not decide how time passed themselves. Some of this power remained even after their escape.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental</b>: A well-chiseled statue bearing a clock upon .<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> A woodland nymph whose leaf-like hair changes with the seasons.<br /> \u2022 <b>Wizened:</b> The figure's body is studded with objects and materials associated with time, such as clocks, hourglasses, sand, water and quicksilver.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Timekeeper has an absolute knowledge of the time, and can count it down to the second like a stopwatch even if he were unconscious in a barren room. He gains the Good Time Management and Patient Merits, and can tell the precise age of any person, object, or place they see (though he may roll a Clash of Wills if this information is supernaturally concealed). If he spends a point of glamour and makes a successful meditation roll, he may make use of the Omen Sensitivity Merit once per dot of Wyrd in a scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-03-2016, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T21:46:50-07:00","id":858138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858118#post858118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And has a better name, too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That said, might I suggest Fools as a possible name? Referring to the Tarot Card of the same name.<br /> <br /> Also, I've added the Runeskin to the main post, with the Blessing being the second Seeming affinity and additional reflexive activation of Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The faerysue name was just a play on the Mary Sue trope. The new ones will have a more serious one.<br /> <br /> As for the Runeskins, I'd recommend going with the revised blessing I gave them in the last post I made about them, given that reflexive Contract activation is already pretty well covered by the basic Contract rules. I'm reposting it here for ease of reference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=857887#post857887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I looked over the draft, and it is actually something that can be done by spending Glamour anyway when fulfilling a Contract's Catch. It is actually something that can be done multiple times per scene anyway, as the limit is based on how much Glamour you can spend and how many Catches you can activate. I've been working on a different version of the blessing, though, and here it is:<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Runeskins are especially adept at acquiring and wielding the magic of Arcadia. Each runeskin has an affinity for a second Seeming, and will gain the favored effect for that Seeming as well as their own when acquiring new Contracts. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, the next Contract that the runeskin activates within the scene will benefit from the 8-Again effect. The changeling may only use this blessing a number of times in a scene equal to their Wyrd, and the Glamour cost to utilize the blessing is not obviated by enacting a Contract's Catch.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T21:56:09-07:00","id":858142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=857963#post857963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Idealy, I was going to give them free Telepathy at character creation, since there are many stories of princesses having prophetic dreams or sending visions to those who would be their heroes. But the point of the Kith was that they learned how to save themselves, instead of waiting for others to come get them. So I designed their blessing to be more self reliant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you were going for and why you would want to do so, but since kith is the aspect of what a character's Keeper did to them, I would think that learning to save themselves would be reflected in their Seeming rather than their kith. That's why I thought that adding some reflection of their original need to be rescued to their blessing would make sense. The Subterfuge benefit you gave them works towards that to some extent, but you could always give them a little bit extra, such as the rote quality on rolls to convince people that they are helpless or an easy victim. Something like that could easily be turned to their advantage when they got bored waiting and decided to rescue themselves.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T22:12:52-07:00","id":858149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858138#post858138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The faerysue name was just a play on the Mary Sue trope. The new ones will have a more serious one.<br /> <br /> As for the Runeskins, I'd recommend going with the revised blessing I gave them in the last post I made about them, given that reflexive Contract activation is already pretty well covered by the basic Contract rules. I'm reposting it here for ease of reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Got it. Thanks for pointing it out to me. Meanwhile, feel free to critique my take on the Lusterlit, as well as the revision I got in mind for the Timekeeper.<br /> <br /> Though I have to ask. How would the Blessing interact with Contracts that somehow benefit from 8-again already? Like Touch of the Workman's Wrath for Renders, and perhaps certain Seeming affinities?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852962#post852962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Omen</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as I mentioned this before. I have an alternative blessing for your Omen Kith. I'm also wondering if we could go for a name change as well. Hmm. How about Portender?<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Omens were strongly tied to luck and fortune during their time in Arcadia, and retain that connection to a lesser extent once they escape. They gain the Changeling Fate Contract for free, but do not suffer from its Ban and need only spend 1 Glamour point to activate it. Furthermore, they add their Wyrd as a dice bonus on all rolls made to detect an impending ambush.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T02:22:47-07:00","id":858237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858149#post858149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. Got it. Thanks for pointing it out to me. Meanwhile, feel free to critique my take on the Lusterlit, as well as the revision I got in mind for the Timekeeper.<br /> <br /> Though I have to ask. How would the Blessing interact with Contracts that somehow benefit from 8-again already? Like Touch of the Workman's Wrath for Renders, and perhaps certain Seeming affinities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that if it is already gaining the 8-Again effect, it would be unaffected by the blessing, but it would not count against the number of times the runeskin could use the blessing in a scene, either. I will need to critique your other kiths later when I'm on an actual computer instead of my phone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T03:06:44-07:00","id":858248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858149#post858149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Seeing as I mentioned this before. I have an alternative blessing for your Omen Kith. I'm also wondering if we could go for a name change as well. Hmm. How about Portender?<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Omens were strongly tied to luck and fortune during their time in Arcadia, and retain that connection to a lesser extent once they escape. They gain the Changeling Fate Contract for free, but do not suffer from its Ban and need only spend 1 Glamour point to activate it. Furthermore, they add their Wyrd as a dice bonus on all rolls made to detect an impending ambush.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I suppose that one works. Portender is also a valid name, though according to the spell check doesn't seem to be a word. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I went and changed them as such. Waaaay back on page 5!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T03:09:40-07:00","id":858250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858142#post858142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand what you were going for and why you would want to do so, but since kith is the aspect of what a character's Keeper did to them, I would think that learning to save themselves would be reflected in their Seeming rather than their kith. That's why I thought that adding some reflection of their original need to be rescued to their blessing would make sense. The Subterfuge benefit you gave them works towards that to some extent, but you could always give them a little bit extra, such as the rote quality on rolls to convince people that they are helpless or an easy victim. Something like that could easily be turned to their advantage when they got bored waiting and decided to rescue themselves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll try to edit that in. One thing I noticed about 2E blessings is they're a hell of a lot more powerful than 1E counterparts. So its difficult to tell when I'm making something over powered or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-03-2016, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T03:15:03-07:00","id":858252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858248#post858248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that one works. Portender is also a valid name, though according to the spell check doesn't seem to be a word. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I went and changed them as such. Waaaay back on page 5!</div> </div> </div> </div>I beg to differ.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.oxforddictionaries.com/us/definition/american_english/portender\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/languages.oup.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/OL-URL-thumbnail.png?fit=1200%2C627&amp;ssl=1\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.oxforddictionaries.com/us/definition/american_english/portender\" target=\"_blank\"> Oxford Languages </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.oxforddictionaries.com/us/definition/american_english/portender\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.oxforddictionaries.com/us/definition/american_english/portender </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The home of language data. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Will be adding it into the main post, then :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T03:22:58-07:00","id":858255,"title":"","content":"Alright, I edited the blessing to the following.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Damsels were made to be rescued until they learned how to rescue themselves. Their blessing gives them the Rote quality on attempts to persuade others that they are weak or foolish. They also add half their Wyrd rounded up on attempts to maintain their Wits during unprovoked confrontations, even if they pretend to have done otherwise. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, they can add +3 to Subterfuge rolls for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> Removed the Composure bonus, since most Damsels are commonly portrayed as screaming for help and flailing about, but kept the Wits bonus to show that this may have just been an act to fool others. Added the Rote quality as a passive action to replace the Composure bonus.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T19:29:47-07:00","id":858680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858118#post858118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does this work better? Also, linked to the source site on the main post.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <u><b>Apollonian</b></u><br /> <i>&quot;Go ahead. Name the challenge. We'll see which of us is better when you don't have any dirty tricks to fall back on&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> These changelings come to embody the physical ideal of perfection rather than the aesthetic, like the heroic athletes of legend. Often fiercely competitive or highly ambitious as mortals, they were taken to excel at all manner of physical contests for their Keepers, whether it's cleaving a block of stone in two with a single blow, running for days on end without so much as losing their breath, or skittering catlike through the most deadly obstacles.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Beast:</b> A man whose features are of an animal that embodies sportsmanship<br /> <b>\u2022 Elemental:</b> A golden Colossus endowed with the strength of ten men.<br /> <b>\u2022 Fairest:</b> An attractive, short-haired woman who can outrun most people with ease.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> An Apollonian gains an extra dot in Strength or Dexterity, which can take her above the usual limitations imposed by her Wyrd. She also benefits from the 8-again rule on all Athletics, Brawl, and Weaponry rolls made during competitions, duels, and self-defense.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like that quote! You forgot to add &quot;and for just showing off&quot; to the list of situations that receive the 8 Again.<br /> <br /> I'd cite the monkey, eagle, tiger, deer and lion as examples of animals that evoke sportsmanship.<br /> <br /> Fairest often manifest floating holograms of colorful light shaped like medals, trophies and heraldic symbols. These holograms usually appear close to the body part used in the sport, like wings on feet for runners and a third eye on the foreheads of archers.<br /> <br /> Ogres might have noticeable muscles that look like stone, steel or bark, and exposed, pointy bones on knuckles, knees and elbows.<br /> <br /> Wizened would have all sorts of cybernetic implants from steampunk to Tron and everything in-between.<br /> <br /> Darklings would be pale or glow with faint moonlight from competing in endless night, and have prominent or alien sensory organs to detect all the dirty tricks their Keeper and other captives played on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-03-2016, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T21:02:38-07:00","id":858748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858680#post858680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like that quote! You forgot to add &amp;quot;and for just showing off&amp;quot; to the list of situations that receive the 8 Again.<br /> <br /> I'd cite the monkey, eagle, tiger, deer and lion as examples of animals that evoke sportsmanship.<br /> <br /> Fairest often manifest floating holograms of colorful light shaped like medals, trophies and heraldic symbols. These holograms usually appear close to the body part used in the sport, like wings on feet for runners and a third eye on the foreheads of archers.<br /> <br /> Ogres might have noticeable muscles that look like stone, steel or bark, and exposed, pointy bones on knuckles, knees and elbows.<br /> <br /> Wizened would have all sorts of cybernetic implants from steampunk to Tron and everything in-between.<br /> <br /> Darklings would be pale or glow with faint moonlight from competing in endless night, and have prominent or alien sensory organs to detect all the dirty tricks their Keeper and other captives played on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll add that last bit in for Beasts. Thanks for giving me some examples. As for the other Seemings, your suggested descriptions are also great. Though my initial description for the Fairest was meant to evoke the myth of Atalanta.<br /> <br /> I kinda wonder if I should add a bit to the Apollonian blessing that helps them detect cheaters. But then, there already might be a few Contracts which can cover that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T21:22:23-07:00","id":858757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858748#post858748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll add that last bit in for Beasts. Thanks for giving me some examples. As for the other Seemings, your suggested descriptions are also great. Though my initial description for the Fairest was meant to evoke the myth of Atalanta.<br /> <br /> I kinda wonder if I should add a bit to the Apollonian blessing that helps them detect cheaters. But then, there already might be a few Contracts which can cover that.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're welcome. As for detecting cheaters, the Perception bonuses of high Clarity, Kenning and 2ED versions of the Contracts of &quot;Oath &amp; Punishment&quot; and &quot;Board&quot; can help a whole lot. Or just use Pledges to enforce the rules (loophole abuse is still a possibility, of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T21:33:35-07:00","id":858762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858757#post858757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're welcome. As for detecting cheaters, the Perception bonuses of high Clarity, Kenning and 2ED versions of the Contracts of &quot;Oath &amp; Punishment&quot; and &quot;Board&quot; can help a whole lot. Or just use Pledges to enforce the rules (loophole abuse is still a possibility, of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course.<br /> <br /> Anyway, any thoughts on this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858127#post858127\">redo</a> of your Timekeeper kith? I revised a bit on how I handled its use of Omen Sensitivity, and added that ability to tell the age of a person/place/object that you wrote down for its 1E version.<br /> <br /> I'd also like some input as well on the Lusterlit kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T22:10:44-07:00","id":858777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858762#post858762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course.<br /> <br /> Anyway, any thoughts on this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858127#post858127\">redo</a> of your Timekeeper kith? I revised a bit on how I handled its use of Omen Sensitivity, and added that ability to tell the age of a person/place/object that you wrote down for its 1E version.<br /> <br /> I'd also like some input as well on the Lusterlit kith.</div> </div> </div> </div> For your redo of Timekeeper, I'd say remove the Omen Sensitivity. That Merit really is more fitting for Tellurics. You could replace that with two free dots in time-related Contracts and/or Tokens. Additionally, they get 1 automatic Success on the activation of time-related Contracts and Tokens, including Clash Of Wills (so you'll see many of them carrying magical time-keeping devices, living up to their name). With ST's permission, they also get this 1 automatic Success when using time-related items of other splats or somehow borrowing their time powers (e.g. a Mage helping them with the Time Arcanum, a Werewolf lending a Fetish containing a Decay spirit).<br /> <br /> For the Lusterlit, I think you meant &quot;through the different wavelengths of the electromagnetic spectrum&quot; (which includes light, radio, X rays and such). This might be too broad, especially in the hands of a physics-savvy player. I'd scratch that. Instead, I suggest giving 8 Again on Contested rolls that would affect their metaphorical sight (e.g. Dominate Discipline, Mind Arcanum), plus immunity to Tilts like Blinded and Darkness. This stacks with the bonuses of high Clarity. If you think that's too much, make the first Contested roll in the scene gain the Blessing for free, but require 1 Glamour for each roll after that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T22:31:56-07:00","id":858782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858777#post858777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For your redo of Timekeeper, I'd say remove the Omen Sensitivity. That Merit really is more fitting for Tellurics. You could replace that with two free dots in time-related Contracts and/or Tokens. Additionally, they get 1 automatic Success on the activation of time-related Contracts and Tokens, including Clash Of Wills (so you'll see many of them carrying magical time-keeping devices, living up to their name). With ST's permission, they also get this 1 automatic Success when using time-related items of other splats or somehow borrowing their time powers (e.g. a Mage helping them with the Time Arcanum, a Werewolf lending a Fetish containing a Decay spirit).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or how about this?<br /> <br /> &quot;If he spends a point of glamour, he can know the Initiative ratings of all participants in a combat scene&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps this?<br /> <br /> &quot;He also gain the Reflections of the Past Contract at three dots, and need not require a reflective surface to activate its effects&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though if I could go with the automatic successes route, I guess I could bump it up from a solid 1 to half the Timekeeper's Wyrd (rounded up).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858777#post858777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Lusterlit, I think you meant &quot;through the different wavelengths of the electromagnetic spectrum&quot; (which includes light, radio, X rays and such). This might be too broad, especially in the hands of a physics-savvy player. I'd scratch that. Instead, I suggest giving 8 Again on Contested rolls that would affect their metaphorical sight (e.g. Dominate Discipline, Mind Arcanum), plus immunity to Tilts like Blinded and Darkness. This stacks with the bonuses of high Clarity. If you think that's too much, make the first Contested roll in the scene gain the Blessing for free, but require 1 Glamour for each roll after that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that first suggestion works. But how's this, then?<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>The Lusterlit can spend a point of glamour or Willpower to use the three-dot version of Psychokinesis (Light). Furthermore, they are immune to any effects which impede their sight, and add their Wyrd when contesting or resisting supernatural powers which affect the mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T02:09:46-07:00","id":858836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858149#post858149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. Got it. Thanks for pointing it out to me. Meanwhile, feel free to critique my take on the Lusterlit, as well as the revision I got in mind for the Timekeeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had every intention of giving you my critique, but GibberingEloquence has already eloquently gibbered most of what I had to say about them! I did wonder, though, what the Psychokinesis (Light) would allow the Lusterlit to do. I'm still getting used to some of the new Merits, and I'm not yet well versed in their capabilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T02:12:34-07:00","id":858837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858255#post858255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I edited the blessing to the following.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Damsels were made to be rescued until they learned how to rescue themselves. Their blessing gives them the Rote quality on attempts to persuade others that they are weak or foolish. They also add half their Wyrd rounded up on attempts to maintain their Wits during unprovoked confrontations, even if they pretend to have done otherwise. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, they can add +3 to Subterfuge rolls for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> Removed the Composure bonus, since most Damsels are commonly portrayed as screaming for help and flailing about, but kept the Wits bonus to show that this may have just been an act to fool others. Added the Rote quality as a passive action to replace the Composure bonus.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think this looks really nice. It is still useful, while keeping the feel of something that was originally intended for a victim. Well done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T02:18:48-07:00","id":858840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858836#post858836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had every intention of giving you my critique, but GibberingEloquence has already eloquently gibbered most of what I had to say about them! I did wonder, though, what the Psychokinesis (Light) would allow the Lusterlit to do. I'm still getting used to some of the new Merits, and I'm not yet well versed in their capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Psychokinesis (Light) would have basically allowed you to manipulate light (even create it at five dots). The Hurt Locker drafts also have Merits which build on Psychokinesis.<br /> <br /> As for how the Lusterlit would have benefited. Well, think Seijins from the Skyland TV series. They'd essentially have a weapon to fall back on a clear sunny day, a full moon's light, and a building that's brightly illuminated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-04-2016, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T06:06:07-07:00","id":858933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858840#post858840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Psychokinesis (Light) would have basically allowed you to manipulate light (even create it at five dots). The Hurt Locker drafts also have Merits which build on Psychokinesis.<br /> <br /> As for how the Lusterlit would have benefited. Well, think Seijins from the Skyland TV series. They'd essentially have a weapon to fall back on a clear sunny day, a full moon's light, and a building that's brightly illuminated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with the series, I'm afraid. Still, the information has given me a bit more to work with, so I thank you for that. I had initially wondered whether it would enable the lusterlit to weave complex visual illusions, but it sounds like it is not quite so potent. This is good, as complex illusions seem like they should be in the realm of Contracts rather than kith blessings. It could still be used quite effectively to illuminate an area or blind an opponent, though, making it seem like a more versatile version of the bright one's blessing. Provided one invested the two Merit dots in bringing it up to five, they'd even be able to create their own light to work to wield. Of course, dual-kithing with bright one could also be an effective combo, allowing the automatic creation of light to work with, or by spending Glamour, cause the blinding light to be inescapable by moving it around anything that a person used in order to break their line of sight with the bright one. I will have to give this one a bit more thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T08:42:27-07:00","id":859033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=858840#post858840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Psychokinesis (Light) would have basically allowed you to manipulate light (even create it at five dots). The Hurt Locker drafts also have Merits which build on Psychokinesis.<br /> <br /> As for how the Lusterlit would have benefited. Well, think Seijins from the Skyland TV series. They'd essentially have a weapon to fall back on a clear sunny day, a full moon's light, and a building that's brightly illuminated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The 3 dot version of Pyschokinesis can be used like a weapon for 1L damage. The 5 dot causes 2L damage. But the 3 dot version can't create light, it can only manipulate it, which means the power would be much weaker at night, unless you hang around a light source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T18:15:14-07:00","id":859363,"title":"","content":"Here's another kith converted from Winter Masques. Critique is appreciated, as well as some Seeming descriptions.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Drudge</u></b> <br /> Even in the enchanted realms of Arcadia, there were tasks reserved for only the most menial of its citizens. Drudges were given the most unpleasant tasks to perform. They were fashioned after house elves, domovoi and other such faeries, and formed the bulk of the workforce in a number of Keepers' domains. However, not all had their spirits broken in Arcadia, and some managed to slip away through the Thorns before their negligent Keepers noticed their absence.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Drudge gains the Brownie's Boon Merit for free, and can benefit from it even if she is being watched. If she isn't, however, she may spend Glamour to further reduce the time between Extended rolls a number of times equal to half her Wyrd (rounded up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T18:18:05-07:00","id":859364,"title":"","content":"And another kith from 1d4chan converted, and one that fills an overlooked role. Again, critique and some Seeming descriptions are welcome.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Chauffeur</u></b> <br /> Tasked with the safe transport of their Fae masters throughout the wild terrain of Arcadia, the Chauffeurs learned to handle all manner of vehicles with aplomb lest the whips be turned on them next. Whether guiding a team of wild fae horses, piloting an impossible clockwork watercraft, or soaring through storm-tossed skies in fantastic balloon, these Lost always arrived safely and on time. Such understanding of all forms of transformation, though, served them well upon taking off in a getaway vehicle. <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Chauffeurs gain the 8-again rule on all Drive rolls, as well as three dots in the Crack Driver Merit. He also benefits from automatic successes in a Drive roll equal to half his Wyrd (rounded up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T18:48:45-07:00","id":859378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=859364#post859364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And another kith from 1d4chan converted, and one that fills an overlooked role. Again, critique and some Seeming descriptions are welcome.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Chauffeur</u></b> <br /> Tasked with the safe transport of their Fae masters throughout the wild terrain of Arcadia, the Chauffeurs learned to handle all manner of vehicles with aplomb lest the whips be turned on them next. Whether guiding a team of wild fae horses, piloting an impossible clockwork watercraft, or soaring through storm-tossed skies in fantastic balloon, these Lost always arrived safely and on time. Such understanding of all forms of transformation, though, served them well upon taking off in a getaway vehicle. <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Chauffeurs gain the 8-again rule on all Drive rolls, as well as three dots in the Crack Driver Merit. He also benefits from automatic successes in a Drive roll equal to half his Wyrd (rounded up).</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol! I've been working on a similar kith (which I was calling coachman). The blessing is pretty similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T18:58:52-07:00","id":859382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=859378#post859378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lol! I've been working on a similar kith (which I was calling coachman). The blessing is pretty similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. Guess we both had similar ideas. Though I gotta admit that Coachman may sound better than Chauffeur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T20:58:47-07:00","id":859443,"title":"","content":"<b>Maenad</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Hah, you call that mind bending pleasure? Come to one of my parties, and bring a trauma kit!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">In the heat of passion, the human mind becomes open to new experiences they would never have condoned while thinking clearly. For the Gentry who fashion themselves upon the dreams and emotions of humanity, some have taken a fascination with this quality and create Maenads as part of a social experiment. Those who were taken to serve this role were subjected to durances that overloaded their emotions, making it nearly impossible for them to slow down and think about what they were doing. They performed sexual acts which no human on earth would dare to attempt outside of the internet, their anger turned into berserker fury, their hunger became ravenous starvation, their sorrow left them wailing on the ground as if the apocalypse had begun. All these and more were what the Maenad experienced while in the service of their Keeper. Miraculously, the Maenad had a moment of clarity one day that allowed them to become self conscious again. It was at that moment, they made their escape amidst the chaos!</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> A beauty like this comes around only once in a generation. Her admirers treat her like a living goddess and cater to her every whim.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> A literal man eater, her body is covered in blood splatters from the lovers she tore appart in a lustful frenzy.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> A disheveled woman who sports the claws and glare of a wild animal, civilized society may describe her as a savage due to her mannerisms.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> The Maenad's durance was spent in excessive self indulgence until they become self conscious of their actions. Now that they are free, they are strongly associated with emotional outbursts. The Maenad regains 2 points of Willpower from indulging in their Vice instead of the usual 1 point. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour and rolling a Wyrd + Manipulation against a target's Wits + Composure, they can give a number of people equal to their Wyrd an additional Vice of the Maenad's choice for the rest of the scene.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">While under the effects of this blessing, the subject (or subjects) receive the Wanton Condition for both of their Vices (the permanent one and the temporary one), as it becomes much more difficult for them to resist the temptation. The temptation only requires 3 successes to be Exceptional instead of the usual 5 for as long as the Maenad's influence has a hold over them.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-05-2016, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T10:48:40-07:00","id":859746,"title":"","content":"Here is the coachman kith. I altered the blessing so that it wouldn't stomp on the toes of the Chauffeur, but would instead synergize with it. Of course, as far as flavor goes, the toe stomping continues, and I apologize for that.<br /> <br /> <b>Coachman</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Relax, Boss. We'll be there in no time.</span><br /> <br /> When the Gentry decide to travel, they choose all manner of fantastic vehicles for their journeys. The coachmen are chosen from mortals with a love of travel or a talent for vehicle operation to pilot these strange conveyances, and sometimes to serve as the means of travel itself. Whether the coachman was lashed to a hollow gourd carriage, pedaling a tiny gnomish airship, or piloting a gigantic walking castle, it was his duty to ensure that his Keeper's journey was both quick and entertaining.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A great yellow cat with many legs, its eyes gleaming like headlights as it runs down hidden roads.<br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A short man with a friendly yet creepily wide grin on his pale face. His eyes are lost in the shadows beneath the visor of his hat.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> It has the chrome grille of an old-fashioned automobile for teeth, headlamps for eyes, and wheels in place of its feet.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> His skin is an intricate parchment navigational map, but the labels are of significant historical events rather than locations.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> She has the head of a frenzied black mare, and her back is a rough network of livid whip scars.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Coachmen gain a bonus equal to their Wyrd on all rolls to operate a conveyance or navigate to a destination. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour while touching the controls of a vehicle, the coachman will gain the Informed Condition related to the specific vehicle that he is currently touching. While this Condition persists, the coachman may spend a second point of Glamour to reduce the travel time required to reach a known destination by half. Such a destination does not need to be one that the coachman has visited previously, but if he hasn't, then the destination does need to be specific enough that a person could realistically navigate to it with the available information. &quot;The city of Seattle&quot;, &quot;the Avalon Restaurant in Gurnee&quot;, or &quot;my childhood home&quot; would all be acceptable destinations, but &quot;the Huntsman's secret lair&quot; would not be, unless the coachman already knew the location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T10:58:25-07:00","id":859754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=859443#post859443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Maenad</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Hah, you call that mind bending pleasure? Come to one of my parties, and bring a trauma kit!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">In the heat of passion, the human mind becomes open to new experiences they would never have condoned while thinking clearly. For the Gentry who fashion themselves upon the dreams and emotions of humanity, some have taken a fascination with this quality and create Maenads as part of a social experiment. Those who were taken to serve this role were subjected to durances that overloaded their emotions, making it nearly impossible for them to slow down and think about what they were doing. They performed sexual acts which no human on earth would dare to attempt outside of the internet, their anger turned into berserker fury, their hunger became ravenous starvation, their sorrow left them wailing on the ground as if the apocalypse had begun. All these and more were what the Maenad experienced while in the service of their Keeper. Miraculously, the Maenad had a moment of clarity one day that allowed them to become self conscious again. It was at that moment, they made their escape amidst the chaos!</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> A beauty like this comes around only once in a generation. Her admirers treat her like a living goddess and cater to her every whim.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> A literal man eater, her body is covered in blood splatters from the lovers she tore appart in a lustful frenzy.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> A disheveled woman who sports the claws and glare of a wild animal, civilized society may describe her as a savage due to her mannerisms.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> The Maenad's durance was spent in excessive self indulgence until they become self conscious of their actions. Now that they are free, they are strongly associated with emotional outbursts. The Maenad regains 2 points of Willpower from indulging in their Vice instead of the usual 1 point. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour and rolling a Wyrd + Manipulation against a target's Wits + Composure, they can give a number of people equal to their Wyrd an additional Vice of the Maenad's choice.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">While under the effects of this blessing, the subject will seek to satisfy both Vices in whatever fashion is available to them and they do not regain willpower for doing so!</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really like this one. The flavor is great, and the blessing is very interesting. The only thing I'd think about changing is the last sentence. Have you considered giving them the Wanton Condition instead? This would allow the Maenads to have an added effect even against beings that usually lack a Vice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T12:00:21-07:00","id":859795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=859363#post859363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another kith converted from Winter Masques. Critique is appreciated, as well as some Seeming descriptions.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Drudge</u></b><br /> Even in the enchanted realms of Arcadia, there were tasks reserved for only the most menial of its citizens. Drudges were given the most unpleasant tasks to perform. They were fashioned after house elves, domovoi and other such faeries, and formed the bulk of the workforce in a number of Keepers' domains. However, not all had their spirits broken in Arcadia, and some managed to slip away through the Thorns before their negligent Keepers noticed their absence.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Drudge gains the Brownie's Boon Merit for free, and can benefit from it even if she is being watched. If she isn't, however, she may spend Glamour to further reduce the time between Extended rolls a number of times equal to half her Wyrd (rounded up).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like what you've come up with here. Here is how I'd add to your description, with your permission:<br /> <br /> <b>Drudge</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">It was the strangest thing. She said it'd take three hours to clean the house, so I said I'd be back then to pay her. I got to the restaurant, and realized I'd left my purse at home, so I went back. I caught her sitting on the couch, watching television. I was so livid! But that's not the weird part. I realized that the whole house was sparkling already. She'd cleaned the whole place in less than 20 minutes. I don't know whether to be mad or keep paying her.</span><br /> <br /> Even in the enchanted realms of Arcadia, there were tasks reserved for only the most menial of its citizens. Drudges were given the most unpleasant tasks to perform, and were expected to do so without drawing attention to themselves. They were fashioned after house elves, domovoi, and other such faeries, and formed the bulk of the workforce in a number of Keepers' domains. However, not all had their spirits broken in Arcadia, and some managed to slip away through the Thorns before their negligent Keepers noticed their absence.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Her mouse-like whiskers quiver as she quietly mends the torn clothing.<br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A pallid man in a dusty suit, silently nodding as he drags the body away.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A shapely and beautiful woman with pointed ears and a maid's outfit that remains pristine regardless of the filth surrounding her.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> Her clothing is permanently ragged and her skin is always covered in dust, but her glass eyes are cleanly polished and striking to behold.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>A Drudge gains the Brownie's Boon Merit for free, and can benefit from it even if she is being watched. If she isn't, however, she may spend Glamour to further reduce the time between Extended rolls a number of times equal to half her Wyrd, rounded up. Additionally, the Drudge benefits from a +2 bonus to rolls to hide or go unnoticed. This benefit stacks with any other bonuses that the Drudge may receive from Contracts or other sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T12:17:45-07:00","id":859806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=859754#post859754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I really like this one. The flavor is great, and the blessing is very interesting. The only thing I'd think about changing is the last sentence. Have you considered giving them the Wanton Condition instead? This would allow the Maenads to have an added effect even against beings that usually lack a Vice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm not familiar with that condition (been trying to quick search the PDF rules update). What does it do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T12:30:59-07:00","id":859811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=859806#post859806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not familiar with that condition (been trying to quick search the PDF rules update). What does it do?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically, it makes it harder for someone to resist temptation and easier for the person who caused the Condition to get them to act on temptation (exceptional success on 3 instead of 5 successes). I know that the full text of the Condition is in Beast, and I believe it's also in Vampire 2ed and the CofD core rulebook, if you have access to any of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T12:34:15-07:00","id":859813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=859811#post859811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Basically, it makes it harder for someone to resist temptation and easier for the person who caused the Condition to get them to act on temptation (exceptional success on 3 instead of 5 successes). I know that the full text of the Condition is in Beast, and I believe it's also in Vampire 2ed and the CofD core rulebook, if you have access to any of those.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sadly, I do not. The only 2nd edition material I have at the moment is the PDF for God Machine rules update, and that's because it was a free download. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll edit the Blessing to include the condition then.<br /> <br /> <br /> How's it look?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-05-2016, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:45:36-07:00","id":859936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=859795#post859795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like what you've come up with here. Here is how I'd add to your description, with your permission:<br /> <br /> <b>Drudge</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">It was the strangest thing. She said it'd take three hours to clean the house, so I said I'd be back then to pay her. I got to the restaurant, and realized I'd left my purse at home, so I went back. I caught her sitting on the couch, watching television. I was so livid! But that's not the weird part. I realized that the whole house was sparkling already. She'd cleaned the whole place in less than 20 minutes. I don't know whether to be mad or keep paying her.</span><br /> <br /> Even in the enchanted realms of Arcadia, there were tasks reserved for only the most menial of its citizens. Drudges were given the most unpleasant tasks to perform, and were expected to do so without drawing attention to themselves. They were fashioned after house elves, domovoi, and other such faeries, and formed the bulk of the workforce in a number of Keepers' domains. However, not all had their spirits broken in Arcadia, and some managed to slip away through the Thorns before their negligent Keepers noticed their absence.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Her mouse-like whiskers quiver as she quietly mends the torn clothing.<br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A pallid man in a dusty suit, silently nodding as he drags the body away.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A shapely and beautiful woman with pointed ears and a maid's outfit that remains pristine regardless of the filth surrounding her.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> Her clothing is permanently ragged and her skin is always covered in dust, but her glass eyes are cleanly polished and striking to behold.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>A Drudge gains the Brownie's Boon Merit for free, and can benefit from it even if she is being watched. If she isn't, however, she may spend Glamour to further reduce the time between Extended rolls a number of times equal to half her Wyrd, rounded up. Additionally, the Drudge benefits from a +2 bonus to rolls to hide or go unnoticed. This benefit stacks with any other bonuses that the Drudge may receive from Contracts or other sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am liking these additions. Thanks, man <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=859813#post859813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, I do not. The only 2nd edition material I have at the moment is the PDF for God Machine rules update, and that's because it was a free download.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want, I could send you some of my 2E stuff to give it a look?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-05-2016, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T20:40:31-07:00","id":860085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=859936#post859936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> If you want, I could send you some of my 2E stuff to give it a look?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No thanks. I'm actually considering buying 2nd edition Changeling once it comes out. I'm also interested in getting Beast. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T03:23:09-07:00","id":860208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=859746#post859746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Coachman</u></b></div> </div> </div> </div>While I like the Seeming descriptions, I'm not sure if the Blessing 'clicks' in terms of mechanics. I do like some elements of it, though, so maybe we can blend the two kiths together somehow? Maybe even find a more universal name than Chauffeur or Coachman?<br /> <br /> Ooh! How does Transporter sound?<br /> <br /> And here's a tentative revision.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Changeling gains the three-dot version of the Crack Driver Merit, and benefits from the 8-again rule on all Drive rolls, as well as any Survival or Streetwise rolls made to navigate towards a destination. If he spends a point of Glamour, he benefits from the Good Time Management Merit and automatic successes equal to half his Wyrd (rounded up) on such rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T06:04:39-07:00","id":860260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=859813#post859813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sadly, I do not. The only 2nd edition material I have at the moment is the PDF for God Machine rules update, and that's because it was a free download. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll edit the Blessing to include the condition then.<br /> <br /> <br /> How's it look?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it looks excellent. Given that your description was showing some of the mechanics of the Condition, and I fully expect that Wanton will be included in Second Edition, you could even shorten the description without losing any of its meaning, like so:<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> The Maenad's durance was spent in excessive self indulgence until they become self conscious of their actions. Now that they are free, they are strongly associated with emotional outbursts. The Maenad regains 2 points of Willpower from indulging in their Vice instead of the usual 1 point. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour and rolling a Wyrd + Manipulation against a target's Wits + Composure, they can give a number of people equal to their Wyrd an additional Vice of the Maenad's choice for the rest of the scene. Those affected by this blessing suffer from the Wanton Condition for as long as the Maenad's influence has a hold over them.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T06:28:09-07:00","id":860267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=860208#post860208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I like the Seeming descriptions, I'm not sure if the Blessing 'clicks' in terms of mechanics. I do like some elements of it, though, so maybe we can blend the two kiths together somehow? Maybe even find a more universal name than Chauffeur or Coachman?<br /> <br /> Ooh! How does Transporter sound?<br /> <br /> And here's a tentative revision.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Changeling gains the three-dot version of the Crack Driver Merit, and benefits from the 8-again rule on all Drive rolls, as well as any Survival or Streetwise rolls made to navigate towards a destination. If he spends a point of Glamour, he benefits from the Good Time Management Merit and automatic successes equal to half his Wyrd (rounded up) on such rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Transporter was one of the ones I'd considered when I was first working on the kith, along with conveyor and, yes, even chauffeur. Transporter had made me think of Star Trek, conveyor made me think of belts. I eventually settled on coachman because I felt like it kind of had an old-fashioned sound to it, much like chirurgeon for the doctor kith, and there are a few magical coachmen in folklore. I could see something like postilion being used for it as well, but personally I liked the feel of coachman even if technically the term is better suited to land vehicles. If it doesn't seem like one that could fit universally, we could always come up with something a bit more 'changelingy' for it, like Thorndriver or Hedgedriver or something similar.<br /> <br /> As for the blessing of the coachman, what was it that seemed off about it? I am willing to poke around at it a bit, but I'd like to know where the blessing falls flat so that I can address it.<br /> <br /> Also, if you'd like the chauffeurs and coachmen to remain separate kiths, I can give some more possible kith descriptions if you were to want them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T09:59:28-07:00","id":860392,"title":"","content":"I personally like Coachman better, as it sounds more fae-like than Transporter. The latter sounds like something from a more urban environment, than a magical land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T11:56:00-07:00","id":860464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=860267#post860267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Transporter was one of the ones I'd considered when I was first working on the kith, along with conveyor and, yes, even chauffeur. Transporter had made me think of Star Trek, conveyor made me think of belts. I eventually settled on coachman because I felt like it kind of had an old-fashioned sound to it, much like chirurgeon for the doctor kith, and there are a few magical coachmen in folklore. I could see something like postilion being used for it as well, but personally I liked the feel of coachman even if technically the term is better suited to land vehicles. If it doesn't seem like one that could fit universally, we could always come up with something a bit more 'changelingy' for it, like Thorndriver or Hedgedriver or something similar.<br /> <br /> As for the blessing of the coachman, what was it that seemed off about it? I am willing to poke around at it a bit, but I'd like to know where the blessing falls flat so that I can address it.<br /> <br /> Also, if you'd like the chauffeurs and coachmen to remain separate kiths, I can give some more possible kith descriptions if you were to want them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it was how you wrote down the Informed Condition? And maybe also the glamour aspect for reducing travel time. The latter I would have reworded as gaining the benefits of the Good Time Management Merit (which could stack with the actual Merit, if already possesses). Plus, the automatic successes equal to Wyrd/2 works much better than Informed in my opinion in terms of roll results.<br /> <br /> And I think we can fold what I got on Chauffeurs into your ideas for the Coachmen. And as Nyrufa said, the term suits them more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T20:50:22-07:00","id":860756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=860464#post860464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe it was how you wrote down the Informed Condition? And maybe also the glamour aspect for reducing travel time. The latter I would have reworded as gaining the benefits of the Good Time Management Merit (which could stack with the actual Merit, if already possesses). Plus, the automatic successes equal to Wyrd/2 works much better than Informed in my opinion in terms of roll results.<br /> <br /> And I think we can fold what I got on Chauffeurs into your ideas for the Coachmen. And as Nyrufa said, the term suits them more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see your point for the automatic successes being a better fit than Informed. I'm not certain that Good Time Management would be an effective replacement for the travel time reduction, though. It seems like it would allow for more frequent rolls, but not necessarily allow for faster travel. I'll have to give that a bit more thought, but I'll try to get another draft of this blessing together tonight or tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T23:43:45-07:00","id":860828,"title":"","content":"I combined the Razorhand and Airtouched blessing to create this Kith.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Harpy</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;It's mine! Get your hands off it!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Sometimes the True Fae want to guard something so strongly, that they need a way to ensure nobody will ever reclaim it again. To fulfill this task, they create the Harpies; vicious thieves who traditionally possess the combined features of humans and birds, although some Keepers have been known to use other flying predators instead of birds to create new types of Harpies. Anyone foolish enough to try and reclaim their stolen possessions would have to not only scale the shear cliffs of the Harpy's nesting ground, but also have to fend off the enraged creature as they defended their hoard. With wsings like razor blades and the ability to soar through the skies, it goes without saying that most did not succeed! But even the Keeper would not be able to keep their avarice in check, and one day the Harpy was lured away from their post by the glittering treasures of the mortal world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> The head of a woman attached to the body of a bird of prey; scaled to human size.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> The head and torso of a beautiful woman with the wings and legs of a majestic bird.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> An ugly hag with the wings and legs of a carrion bird; she has a temper to match her avian features.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Harpies possess the talons of a predator and their wings are said to be as sharp as a razor's edge. When performing unarmed combat, the Harpy inflicts lethal damage instead of bashing. They also gain a +2 bonus on all climbing and grappling rolls, and add their Wyrd to their jumping distance. If they spend a point of Glamour, the Harpy can perform a Reflexive jump, lunge or plunge in any direction without having to pick up speed first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-07-2016, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T02:56:29-07:00","id":860901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=860828#post860828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I combined the Razorhand and Airtouched blessing to create this Kith.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Harpy</b><br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;It's mine! Get your hands off it!&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> Sometimes the True Fae want to guard something so strongly, that they need a way to ensure nobody will ever reclaim it again. To fulfill this task, they create the Harpies; vicious thieves who possess the combined features of humans and birds. Anyone foolish enough to try and reclaim their stolen possessions would have to not only scale the shear cliffs of the Harpy's nesting ground, but also have to fend off the enraged creature as they defended their hoard. With feathers like razor blades and the ability to soar through the skies, it goes without saying that most did not succeed! But even the Keeper would not be able to keep their avarice in check, and one day the Harpy was lured away from their post by the glittering treasures of the mortal world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> The head of a woman attached to the body of a bird of prey; scaled to human size.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> The head and torso of a beautiful woman with the wings and legs of a majestic bird.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> An ugly hag with the wings and legs of a carrion bird; she has a temper to match her avian features.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Harpies possess the talons of a bird and their feathers are said to be as sharp as a razor's edge. When performing unarmed combat, the Harpy inflicts lethal damage instead of bashing. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, the Harpy is able to multiply their jumping distance by 1+ their Wyrd for the rest of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nice one! Might they have features of bats or flying insects despite the name? I know I'd be scared if a wasp-like Harpy dropped their Mask and lunged at me.<br /> <br /> Besides the increased jumping distance, I'd give them bonuses for climbing and grapples. They could also spend 1 glamour to do a reflexive jump, lunge or plunge in any direction without having to pick up speed first, still benefiting from the increased distance. If you want to add a limit to that, Wyrd x 2 or Wyrd x 3 times per scene sounds good to me. <br /> <br /> Dots in Larceny, Investigation, Athletics and Brawl should come separately as a natural consequence of the Durance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T04:54:59-07:00","id":860960,"title":"","content":"@GibberingEloquence<br /> <br /> Well said. Hm. So, would it be worded like this?<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Harpies possess the talons of a bird and their feathers are said to be as sharp as a razor's edge. When performing unarmed combat, the Harpy inflicts lethal damage instead of bashing. They also gain a +2 bonus on all climbing and grappling rolls, and add their Wyrd to their jumping distance. If they spend a point of Glamour, the Harpy can perform a Reflexive jump, lunge or plunge in any direction without having to pick up speed first.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the claws could be given via the Lethal Mien Merit to make the Blessing more mobility-based.<br /> <br /> That said, I am trying to conceive a Siren kith that's music-based and is both aquatic and aerial in nature (to reflect the different depictions of sirens in myth).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-07-2016, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T05:18:42-07:00","id":860974,"title":"","content":"Alright, I replaced the Harpy's blessing with the new worded one. Also changed the description of the Harpy so that other types of flying predators are available.<br /> <br /> I was trying to work on a Kith I like to call <b>Morals</b> who's durance was used to educate others about the error of their ways, but wasn't quite sure how to write up their blessing, unfortunately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T05:28:42-07:00","id":860981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=860974#post860974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was trying to work on a Kith I like to call <b>Morals</b> who's durance was used to educate others about the error of their ways, but wasn't quite sure how to write up their blessing, unfortunately.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am thinking of what I know on the Erinyes/Furies based on this. Perhaps you can use either term in place of Morals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T06:04:36-07:00","id":860995,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Fury</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;They say crime doesn't pay. But that's not quite true. Scum like you pay in blood and tears, sooner or later. Now, give me one reason why I shouldn't make the pain you're feeling last.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The laws of Arcadia are hard, even towards the slightest of infractions. Changelings made into Furies may have already been abusive or abused as mortals. At their Keeper's command, they may have inflicted terrible tortures on fellow captives as punishment for acts of defiance. And while such atrocities tainted their ability to relate to others, they instilled in them a ruthlessness that caused even their Masters to submit.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Furies gain the Air of Menace and Torturer Merits, and can apply the former to supernatural creatures. They also gain a dot of Intimidation, which can take them beyond the limitations imposed by the Wyrd. If a Fury spends a point of Glamour while using Hard Leverage, he opens additional Doors equal to his Wyrd.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> Critique and Seeming descriptions are appreciated.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T08:05:50-07:00","id":861050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=860981#post860981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am thinking of what I know on the Erinyes/Furies based on this. Perhaps you can use either term in place of Morals?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well the idea for the name Morals was inspired by Grimm's fairy tales, which often involved teaching the readers a valuable life lesson. One that ended quite horribly for the main character who didn't heed the advice.<i> &quot;And the moral of the story is...&quot;</i> kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Something along the lines of an avenger and a natural selection process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-07-2016, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T09:21:46-07:00","id":861094,"title":"","content":"At the least, maybe they can spend Glamour and make a roll to give someone the Virtuous Merit keyed to a Virtue of your choice for something like [Wyrd] hours or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T10:53:28-07:00","id":861155,"title":"","content":"Here is another one.<br /> <br /> <b>Deadeye</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">I felt a little embarrassed, losing the contest, being outdone by a girl. She was pretty damned impressive with that rifle, I'll give her that. Didn't miss a single target the whole time. I figured that she must have something hidden under those dark glasses she wore, something to give her an edge. So, when I went to congratulate her, I snatched them right off her face to prove it. That just made it worse. She wasn't cheating at all. She didn't even have any eyes under there. I had been outshot by a blind girl! I'll never live it down.</span><br /> <br /> Sometimes the Gentry wish to deal death to the forces of their enemies from a distance, and the deadeyes are their tools of choice. These eerie changelings are chosen from people who pride themselves on their aim, and made to fight or perform tricks with their weapons for the amusement of their Keepers. Most would have been content with their lot, except that their Keepers preferred servants that could not be blinded, and took their eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> The gunslinger in black always wears a bandanna over his eyes, though tears of blood sometimes seep out from the empty sockets beneath it.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> Her wooden muscles are always as tense as bowstrings, and her eyes are two burnt circles on the wood of her face.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Her body is sleek and graceful, but there is a cold, hard look to the gleaming emeralds in her eyes.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> He watches the world through the crosshairs on the lenses that have replaced his eyes, and his skin is gunmetal gray.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Deadeyes have a talent for ranged combat. When taking an aiming action, the deadeye does not lose her Defense for the turn, and will gain the 8-Again effect on the ranged attack that follows. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, the deadeye can increase the distance of her next ranged attack by her Wyrd * 10 in yards, pushing back range increments accordingly. Attacks that normally aren't ranged can benefit from this effect as well, but the range is only equal to her Wyrd in yards, and these attacks cannot benefit from the aiming action. All deadeyes are also immune to the Blinded Tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T11:21:01-07:00","id":861169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=860995#post860995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Fury</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;They say crime doesn't pay. But that's not quite true. Scum like you pay in blood and tears, sooner or later. Now, give me one reason why I shouldn't make the pain you're feeling last.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The laws of Arcadia are hard, even towards the slightest of infractions. Changelings made into Furies may have already been abusive or abused as mortals. At their Keeper's command, they may have inflicted terrible tortures on fellow captives as punishment for acts of defiance. And while such atrocities tainted their ability to relate to others, they instilled in them a ruthlessness that caused even their Masters to submit.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Furies gain the Air of Menace and Torturer Merits, and can apply the former to supernatural creatures. They also gain a dot of Intimidation, which can take them beyond the limitations imposed by the Wyrd. If a Fury spends a point of Glamour while using Hard Leverage, he opens additional Doors equal to his Wyrd.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> Critique and Seeming descriptions are appreciated.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like what you've come up with so far. Maybe you could add something that allows them to inflict the Guilty Condition somehow?<br /> <br /> As for Seeming descriptions:<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling: </b>She is a vicious crone with bat wings, bloodshot eyes, and serpents for hair. <br /> <b>Elemental: </b>She is a towering figure of dark stone, with flames dancing in her eyes and upon her broad shoulders.<br /> <b>Fairest: </b>He is a handsome older gentleman, but he has a cruel smile and his red eyes seem to penetrate the darkest depths of one's core.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> Observers can always read the litany of their own sins written upon her flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T14:20:06-07:00","id":861293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=861169#post861169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like what you've come up with so far. Maybe you could add something that allows them to inflict the Guilty Condition somehow?<br /> <br /> As for Seeming descriptions:<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling: </b>She is a vicious crone with bat wings, bloodshot eyes, and serpents for hair. <br /> <b>Elemental: </b>She is a towering figure of dark stone, with flames dancing in her eyes and upon her broad shoulders.<br /> <b>Fairest: </b>He is a handsome older gentleman, but he has a cruel smile and his red eyes seem to penetrate the darkest depths of one's core.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> Observers can always read the litany of their own sins written upon her flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I can add that in to the Glamour effect as an option. How's this?<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> &quot;If a Fury spends a point of Glamour while using Hard Leverage, he may choose to open additional Doors equal to his Wyrd, or inflict the Cursed, Guilty, or Frightened Condition&quot;.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> And I do believe that's the first Grimm description I've seen so far, if I may be so kind to point out.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also liking your write-up for the Deadeyes. I have a blind Wizened changeling archer who could work well being of this kith, though I initially conceived him as a Cleareyes with enhanced hearing or a form of seismic sense as his trademark ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-07-2016, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T19:04:53-07:00","id":861518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=861293#post861293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe I can add that in to the Glamour effect as an option. How's this?<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> &quot;If a Fury spends a point of Glamour while using Hard Leverage, he may choose to open additional Doors equal to his Wyrd, or inflict the Cursed, Guilty, or Frightened Condition&quot;.<br /> <br /> -+-</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that. It seems to cover it pretty well, although I'm not entirely certain about the Cursed Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=861293#post861293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I do believe that's the first Grimm description I've seen so far, if I may be so kind to point out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second, actually. The coachman had a Grimm, too. I hope you liked the Seeming descriptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=861293#post861293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also liking your write-up for the Deadeyes. I have a blind Wizened changeling archer who could work well being of this kith, though I initially conceived him as a Cleareyes with enhanced hearing or a form of seismic sense as his trademark ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you liked it. I'm pretty pleased with how they turned out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T19:41:27-07:00","id":861542,"title":"","content":"How does this seem for a revised coachman kith? I've tried to combine your ideas with mine, though I acknowledge that it may yet need more tweaking.<br /> <br /> <b>Coachman</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Relax, Boss. We'll be there in no time.</span><br /> <br /> When the Gentry decide to travel, they choose all manner of fantastic vehicles for their journeys. The coachmen are chosen from mortals with a love of travel or a talent for vehicle operation to pilot these strange conveyances, and sometimes to serve as the means of travel itself. Whether the coachman was lashed to a hollow gourd carriage, pedaling a tiny gnomish airship, or piloting a gigantic walking castle, it was his duty to ensure that his Keeper's journey was both quick and entertaining.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A great yellow cat with many legs, its eyes gleaming like headlights as it runs down hidden roads.<br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A short man with a friendly yet creepily wide grin on his pale face. His eyes are lost in the shadows beneath the visor of his hat.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> It has the chrome grille of an old-fashioned automobile for teeth, headlamps for eyes, and wheels in place of its feet.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> His skin is an intricate parchment navigational map, but the labels are of significant historical events rather than locations.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> She has the head of a frenzied black mare, and her back is a rough network of livid whip scars.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Coachmen inherently understand how to operate any conveyance that they touch, and gain the 8-Again effect on any rolls to do so. Any Streetwise or Survival rolls to navigate to a destination receive a number of bonus dice equal to the coachman's Wyrd. If a coachman has a Specialty in the specific type of vehicle he is operating, he may spend a point of Glamour when travelling to a known destination to reduce his travel time by half. Such a destination does not need to be one that the coachman has visited previously, but if he hasn't, then the destination does need to be specific enough that a person could realistically navigate to it with the available information. &quot;The city of Seattle&quot;, &quot;the Avalon Restaurant in Gurnee&quot;, or &quot;my childhood home&quot; would all be acceptable destinations, but &quot;the Huntsman's secret lair&quot; would not be, unless the coachman already knew the location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T20:26:23-07:00","id":861561,"title":"","content":"@White Oak Dragon<br /> <br /> Might consider trimming the word count and revising the wording, but I like the revisions so far.<br /> <br /> Let's see....<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Coachmen inherently understand how to operate any conveyance that they touch, and gain the 8-Again effect on any Drive rolls to do so. Any Streetwise or Survival rolls to navigate to a destination also receive a number of bonus dice equal to the Coachman's Wyrd. If a Coachman has a Specialty in the specific type of vehicle he is operating, he may spend a point of Glamour when travelling to a known destination to reduce his travel time by half. Such a destination does not need to be one that the Coachman has visited previously, but if he hasn't, then the destination does need to be specific enough that a person could realistically navigate to it with the available information. &quot;The city of Seattle&quot;, &quot;the Avalon Restaurant in Gurnee&quot;, or &quot;my childhood home&quot; would all be acceptable destinations, but &quot;the Huntsman's secret lair&quot; would not be, unless the Coachman already knew the location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T22:46:20-07:00","id":861608,"title":"","content":"I will think of what I might do as far as trimming the word count goes. I deliberately didn't specify the Drive Skill in the description so that the blessing could be used for non-motorized vehicles as well. I know that kayaking fit into the Athletics Skill, and I believe that bicycling probably would as well. I think that sailing might have been Survival, but I'm not certain on that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T23:01:42-07:00","id":861619,"title":"","content":"I see what you mean.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T23:34:47-07:00","id":861639,"title":"","content":"<b>Moral</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;And the moral of the story is... that was a stupid idea!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Human folk lore is cram packed with stories designed to teach people valuable life lessons including how to be a good Samaritan, as well as how to stay alive longer than the other guy. Often, these stories involve humanity coming into contact with magical beings, which just so happen to be the True Fae. Changelings who became Morals were used to educate others about the error of their ways, often teaching them how to survive the dangerous world of the Fey. Perhaps in some way, their durance served a noble function, but the Moral did not see it that way when they were made the subject of demonstration. Eventually, they managed to learn their lesson and escape the narrative forced upon them by their Keepers.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> A lesson in trusting strangers. They are the big bad wolf that leads the naive to certain peril.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> A lesson in humility. They are the beautiful maiden who drives the envious to self destruction.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> A lesson in hard work. Their construction projects are up to code, while their competitors use shoddy materials and cheap labor.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> A lesson in respecting the property of others. They are the angry bear who comes home to find an unwanted house guest.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> The Moral's durance was spent teaching others the error of their ways until they eventually learned the error of their own and managed to correct them. The Moral gains 3 Willpower points for upholding their Virtue instead of the usual 2 points. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, they may curse a subject for a number of days equal to their Wyrd. If the subject indulges in their Vice while under this curse, they gain the <i>Foolish Hubris</i> Tilt, which changes Exceptional Successes on their top priority skills into Dramatic Failures!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-08-2016, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T00:10:49-07:00","id":861653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=861518#post861518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that. It seems to cover it pretty well, although I'm not entirely certain about the Cursed Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I could swap out Cursed for the Paranoid Condition instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T07:15:02-07:00","id":861807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=861653#post861653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps I could swap out Cursed for the Paranoid Condition instead?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What about Shaken? I could even see the possibility of Broken, although I suppose that one's potent enough that it would probably need one of the others first to build upon. Perhaps you could start with Shaken or Spooked, have that upgrade to Frightened, and then Frightened could upgrade to Broken? I think that Guilty should probably be a prerequisite to giving them any others, though, given their flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T08:06:42-07:00","id":861842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=861807#post861807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Shaken? I could even see the possibility of Broken, although I suppose that one's potent enough that it would probably need one of the others first to build upon. Perhaps you could start with Shaken or Spooked, have that upgrade to Frightened, and then Frightened could upgrade to Broken? I think that Guilty should probably be a prerequisite to giving them any others, though, given their flavor.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about now? <hr /><br /> <b><u>Fury</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;They say crime doesn't pay. But that's not quite true. Scum like you pay in blood and tears, sooner or later. Now, give me one reason why I shouldn't make the pain you're feeling last.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The laws of Arcadia are hard, even towards the slightest of infractions. Changelings made into Furies may have already been abusive or abused as mortals. At their Keeper's command, they were made to inflict terrible tortures on fellow captives as punishment for acts of defiance. Wile such atrocities tainted their ability to relate to others, they instilled in them a ruthlessness that caused even their Masters to quaver in fear.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling: </b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">She is a vicious crone with bat wings, bloodshot eyes, and serpents for hair.</span><br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental: </b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">She is a towering figure of dark stone, with flames dancing in her eyes and upon her broad shoulders.</span><br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest: </b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">He is a handsome older gentleman, but he has a cruel smile and his red eyes seem to penetrate the darkest depths of one's core.</span><br /> \u2022 <b>Grimm:</b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Observers can always read the litany of their own sins written upon her flesh.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Furies gain the Air of Menace and Torturer Merits, and can apply the former to supernatural creatures. They also gain a dot of Intimidation, which can take them beyond the limitations imposed by the Wyrd. If a Fury spends a point of Glamour while using Hard Leverage, he may choose to open additional Doors equal to his Wyrd, or inflict the Broken, Guilty, or Fugue Condition. A given victim can only suffer one of these Conditions from a given Fury.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T23:19:59-07:00","id":862468,"title":"","content":"Has anyone tried making a Toon Kith? I'm guessing General Armor and quicker healing somehow based on their Wyrd, downgrading lethal into bashing (maybe aggravated into lethal with Glamour) and 1 automatic Success for any Contract and Token activation in a humorous context. For example: Discrete Conjuration, Hidden Reality and Trivial Reworking for setting up pranks and traps. Changeling Fate for giving someone that extra bit of distraction or bad luck to lead them into danger. This may be too broad, however. Most Toons would invest into Merits for harvesting Glamour from emotions like surprise, shock, joy, anger, shame and confusion.<br /> <br /> I believe dots in Athletics, Expression, Subterfuge, Persuasion, Larceny, Stealth, Weaponry, Firearms and other Skills prominent in cartoon shenanigans should come separately as a part of the &quot;build&quot;. Same goes for Merits. This Kith would go well with Coyote, Flowering, Gremlin, Larcenist, Lurker, Mirrorskin, Muse and Troll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-09-2016, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T23:29:25-07:00","id":862474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=862468#post862468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone tried making a Toon Kith? I'm guessing a free dot of Wits (which also raises this Attribute's cap), General Armor and quicker healing somehow based on their Wyrd, downgrading lethal into bashing (maybe aggravated into lethal with Glamour) and 1 automatic Success for any Contract and Token activation in a humorous context. For example: Discrete Conjuration, Hidden Reality and Trivial Reworking for setting up pranks and traps. Changeling Fate for giving someone that extra bit of distraction or bad luck to lead them into danger. This may be too broad, however. Most Toons would invest into Merits for harvesting Glamour from emotions like surprise, shock, joy, anger, shame and confusion.<br /> <br /> I believe dots in Athletics, Expression, Subterfuge, Persuasion, Larceny, Stealth, Weaponry, Firearms and other Skills prominent in cartoon shenanigans should come separately as a part of the &amp;quot;build&amp;quot;. Same goes for Merits. This Kith would go well with Coyote, Flowering, Gremlin, Larcenist, Lurker, Mirrorskin, Muse and Troll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Nyrufa made one in this thread already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T23:43:17-07:00","id":862478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=862474#post862474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Nyrufa made one in this thread already.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're right, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852478#post852478\"><b>I found it.</b></a><br /> <br /> Nyrufa, what do you think about my suggestions? I mentioned 1 automatic Success on Token activation because a lot of cartoon shenanigans involve slapstick. This wouldn't be about making attacks with weapon Tokens always hit. You can still miss with your attack and apply the Token's effect on someone like your spouse, boss or simply yourself, thus preserving the antics.<br /> <br /> You know what, comedy as a whole relies too much on mistakes for the Blessing to include automatic Success. An Exceptional Success at 3 Successes instead of 5 in Contract and Token activation once per scene sounds good, as long as the context is humorous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-09-2016, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T05:27:04-07:00","id":862559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=853619#post853619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wonderwell</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding the similarities between the Blessing written down and the ideas outlined for Rumpelstiltskin Bargains, I've been trying to think up an alternative write-up to the former. So far, though, the best patch up I could make was this...<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Wonderwells are skilled at granting the desires of others, while at the same time reaping benefits of their own. He gains three dots in the Goblin Vow Merit. And if he initiates a Rumpelstiltskin Bargain, he is considered to have the benefits of an active Goblin Pledge equal in value to the Bargain's Boon. A Wonderwell can only have a number of these Bargains equal to her Wyrd at any given time, and removing an existing one requires the breaking of an existing Bargain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T12:44:54-07:00","id":862705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=861842#post861842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about now? <hr /><br /> <b><u>Fury</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;They say crime doesn't pay. But that's not quite true. Scum like you pay in blood and tears, sooner or later. Now, give me one reason why I shouldn't make the pain you're feeling last.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The laws of Arcadia are hard, even towards the slightest of infractions. Changelings made into Furies may have already been abusive or abused as mortals. At their Keeper's command, they were made to inflict terrible tortures on fellow captives as punishment for acts of defiance. While such atrocities tainted their ability to relate to others, they instilled in them a ruthlessness that caused even their Masters to quaver in fear.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling: </b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">She is a vicious crone with bat wings, bloodshot eyes, and serpents for hair.</span><br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental: </b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">She is a towering figure of dark stone, with flames dancing in her eyes and upon her broad shoulders.</span><br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest: </b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">He is a handsome older gentleman, but he has a cruel smile and his red eyes seem to penetrate the darkest depths of one's core.</span><br /> \u2022 <b>Grimm:</b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Observers can always read the litany of their own sins written upon her flesh.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Furies gain the Air of Menace and Torturer Merits, and can apply the former to supernatural creatures. They also gain a dot of Intimidation, which can take them beyond the limitations imposed by the Wyrd. If a Fury spends a point of Glamour while using Hard Leverage, he may choose to open additional Doors equal to his Wyrd, or inflict the Broken, Guilty, or Fugue Condition. A given victim can only suffer one of these Conditions from a given Fury.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What about rephrasing it like this?<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Furies gain the Air of Menace and Torturer Merits, and can apply the former to supernatural creatures. They also gain a dot of Intimidation, which can take them beyond the limitations imposed by their Wyrd. If a Fury spends a point of Glamour while using Hard Leverage, she may choose to open additional Doors equal to her Wyrd, or inflict the Guilty Condition. If the victim is already suffering the Guilty Condition, the Fury may instead choose to inflict either the Broken or Fugue Condition.<br /> <br /> By the way, where is the Air of Menace Merit? I haven't managed to track it down, so I can't see what it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T12:47:45-07:00","id":862706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=862559#post862559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regarding the similarities between the Blessing written down and the ideas outlined for Rumpelstiltskin Bargains, I've been trying to think up an alternative write-up to the former. So far, though, the best patch up I could make was this...<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Wonderwells are skilled at granting the desires of others, while at the same time reaping benefits of their own. He gains three dots in the Goblin Vow Merit. And if he initiates a Rumpelstiltskin Bargain, he is considered to have the benefits of an active Goblin Pledge equal in value to the Bargain's Boon. A Wonderwell can only have a number of these Bargains equal to her Wyrd at any given time, and removing an existing one requires the breaking of an existing Bargain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would prefer not to make the mechanics of their blessing rely upon any mechanics that aren't self-contained or already present within canon CofD sources. I will need to think a bit more on how to move it further away from the Rumpelstiltskin Bargains without losing the feel of the wish granting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:09:10-07:00","id":862719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=862705#post862705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, where is the Air of Menace Merit? I haven't managed to track it down, so I can't see what it does.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's from the Hurt Locker. It gives a bonus to Intimidation at the cost of increasing the Doors you have to open in Soft Leverage, if I remember correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T17:39:08-07:00","id":862897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=862705#post862705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about rephrasing it like this?<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Furies gain the Air of Menace and Torturer Merits, and can apply the former to supernatural creatures. They also gain a dot of Intimidation, which can take them beyond the limitations imposed by their Wyrd. If a Fury spends a point of Glamour while using Hard Leverage, she may choose to open additional Doors equal to her Wyrd, or inflict the Guilty Condition. If the victim is already suffering the Guilty Condition, the Fury may instead choose to inflict either the Broken or Fugue Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. That actually <i>does</i> work better. Thanks.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the Wonderwell, perhaps giving them Goblin Vows would be a good place to start?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T00:54:31-07:00","id":863065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=862719#post862719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's from the Hurt Locker. It gives a bonus to Intimidation at the cost of increasing the Doors you have to open in Soft Leverage, if I remember correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bAh, thank you. That makes sense. I could definitely see that for Deionscribe's Furies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=862897#post862897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. That actually <i>does</i> work better. Thanks.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the Wonderwell, perhaps giving them Goblin Vows would be a good place to start?</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. I'm glad you liked it.<br /> <br /> I think that Goblin Vows will definitely be involved in the Wonderwell's blessing in some manner, and they'll definitely be able to share the benefits of it with others in some way or another. I'll keep toying with the idea and see what I can come up with.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T00:58:52-07:00","id":863066,"title":"","content":"Here's another one I've been working on. It originally started out as another joke kith, when they would have been called tastytreats and their blessing would have been limited to the benefits others gain from eating them. It's evolved a bit since the beginning.<br /> <br /> <b>Honeysoul</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Look, I'm no happier about this than you are, but you're wounded, and if we're going to have any chance of getting out of here alive, you're going to need to get over it and start eating.</span><br /> <br /> Some Keepers fancy themselves to be gourmets, partaking of exotic fare and hosting great banquets featuring esoteric delicacies. It was the sad lot of the honeysouls to provide the substance for these bizarre repasts. Each night, the honeysoul was devoured by her Keeper or his favored guests and servants, and each morning she was born anew from her bones. Even when a honeysoul has escaped this vicious cycle, it is not uncommon to see her weep in sympathy over her own meals.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> She is a timid rabbit girl, with a bite taken out of one long chocolate ear.<br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Green and red gummy flesh mingle together, covering a visible skeleton of hard black bones.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> His features are lovingly detailed with icing upon his gingerbread flesh.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Her skin is the color of honey, and it is slightly sticky to the touch and sweet to the taste.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> He is a great boar-like creature with slightly burned yet succulent flesh, a tantalizing aroma filling the air around him. <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Each night when the honeysoul sleeps, she heals all bashing and lethal damage she has suffered, or downgrades a single level of aggravated damage to lethal. Additionally, her flesh and blood is mystically potent and especially nourishing. By cannibalizing her own body, the honeysoul may regain a point of Glamour in exchange for a level of lethal damage. Other beings may also benefit from her nourishing flesh by devouring it, regaining a point of Willpower, a point of Glamour, or recovering a single level of bashing or lethal damage for each point of lethal damage inflicted upon the honeysoul. This blessing can only be used a number of times per day equal to the honeysoul's Wyrd. If the honeysoul has cannibalized her own body or been fed upon by others during the day, then she will not benefit from the healing aspect of this blessing when she next sleeps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T01:11:00-07:00","id":863068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=863066#post863066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Honeysoul</u></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Lol. And I was thinking of buying some snacks, just now. Hehe.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, this kinda made me think of the Delicacy kith I found at the 1d4chan wiki. But naturally, this is so much better at handling the concept. Another great work from you.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S: The flavor text was the best point for me. I can even imagine an alternative that incorporates the phrase &quot;enjoy myself&quot;, lol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T09:04:04-07:00","id":863177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=863066#post863066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another one I've been working on. It originally started out as another joke kith, when they would have been called tastytreats and their blessing would have been limited to the benefits others gain from eating them. It's evolved a bit since the beginning.<br /> <br /> <b>Honeysoul</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Look, I'm no happier about this than you are, but you're wounded, and if we're going to have any chance of getting out of here alive, you're going to need to get over it and start eating.</span><br /> <br /> Some Keepers fancy themselves to be gourmets, partaking of exotic fare and hosting great banquets featuring esoteric delicacies. It was the sad lot of the honeysouls to provide the substance for these bizarre repasts. Each night, the honeysoul was devoured by her Keeper or his favored guests and servants, and each morning she was born anew from her bones. Even when a honeysoul has escaped this vicious cycle, it is not uncommon to see her weep in sympathy over her own meals.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> She is a timid rabbit girl, with a bite taken out of one long chocolate ear.<br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Green and red gummy flesh mingle together, covering a visible skeleton of hard black bones.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> His features are lovingly detailed with icing upon his gingerbread flesh.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Her skin is the color of honey, and it is slightly sticky to the touch and sweet to the taste.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> He is a great boar-like creature with slightly burned yet succulent flesh, a tantalizing aroma filling the air around him.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Each night when the honeysoul sleeps, she heals all bashing and lethal damage she has suffered, or downgrades a single level of aggravated damage to lethal. Additionally, her flesh and blood is mystically potent and especially nourishing. By cannibalizing her own body, the honeysoul may regain a point of Glamour in exchange for a level of lethal damage. Other beings may also benefit from her nourishing flesh by devouring it, regaining a point of Willpower, a point of Glamour, or recovering a single level of bashing or lethal damage for each point of lethal damage inflicted upon the honeysoul. This blessing can only be used a number of times per day equal to the honeysoul's Wyrd. If the honeysoul has cannibalized her own body or been fed upon by others during the day, then she will not benefit from the healing aspect of this blessing when she next sleeps.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Personally, I would have suggested a ram for the Beast Seeming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But thank you for writing this up. I've been wanting a chocolate bunny type character!<br /> <br /> Although I would suggest removing the ability to eat themselves for Glamour and making it exclusive towards others. Otherwise you have a Kith who can pretty much supply their own Glamour on a whim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-10-2016, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T09:43:51-07:00","id":863195,"title":"","content":"<b>Kith Deleted:</b> Redundancy compared to Bellower","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-10-2016, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T09:59:29-07:00","id":863200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=863195#post863195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not completely satisfied with the Blessing on this one. I think the sound based attack needs to be better ironed out. Any suggestions?<br /> <br /> <b>Thunder Head</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have anything yet. But you should probably check out my conversion of the Bellower kith for ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T12:07:38-07:00","id":863250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=863200#post863200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have anything yet. But you should probably check out my conversion of the Bellower kith for ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, I did not see that a similar concept was already made. I'm sorry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T08:23:25-07:00","id":863670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=862478#post862478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're right, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=852478#post852478\"><b>I found it.</b></a><br /> <br /> Nyrufa, what do you think about my suggestions? I mentioned 1 automatic Success on Token activation because a lot of cartoon shenanigans involve slapstick. This wouldn't be about making attacks with weapon Tokens always hit. You can still miss with your attack and apply the Token's effect on someone like your spouse, boss or simply yourself, thus preserving the antics.<br /> <br /> You know what, comedy as a whole relies too much on mistakes for the Blessing to include automatic Success. An Exceptional Success at 3 Successes instead of 5 in Contract and Token activation once per scene sounds good, as long as the context is humorous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sorry, I missed this question earlier.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of them getting a bonus to activating Contracts in a comedic manner (via magic satchel type of stuff), but the different Seemings I suggested are based around various types of animation, instead of just loony toon theatrics. You've got Anime, Noir, and even real life conversion (i.e Pagemaster) types available. So making it strictly comedy based seems to limit it's potential, somewhat.<br /> <br /> <br /> Since most Toons seem to be damn near indestructible (Roger Rabbit, not included), I designed them to be massive damage sponges who can take anvils to the head and get right back up again. Of course, I tried not to make them as impervious as Werewolves, as that would have been way too OP compared to the other Kiths. They can still be killed, but it's going to take more effort to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:42:05-07:00","id":863717,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>White Knight</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Evil never dies. Trust me, I tried everything I could to kill that bastard!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> True Fae who like to be the center of attention for their realms often create grand narratives to extol their virtues to others. But some among the Gentry have another idea in mind, and instead of being the hero of their story, they choose to play the villain. It is easy to corrupt the righteous, to cast them down into the dirt. But it is almost impossible to stamp out evil forever. Somehow, it always finds a way to survive and replenish its strength. Changelings who became White Knights were used to play the role of noble hero in these narratives, rising up to a challenge that they could never permanently succeed at. No matter how many times the hero prevailed, the villain would return, gradually sapping the hero's resolve and proving to the realm that the Keeper could not be defied forever. Eventually, the White Knight realized they needed to grow stronger if they were to defeat their enemy once and for all. And so, they made the journey to the distant lands beyond the Hedge where many strong rebels were said to gather.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Their golden armor which once shined like the sun has become dim since it was exposed to human world. Regardless, their posture is still regal and inspiring, with eyes that remain ever vigilant for danger.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> With sloping posture and empty gaze, they realized the futility of their crusade. Their armor is rusty and battle worn from countless battles against the forces of darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A stone sentinel used to guard against the armies of evil. It has fallen into disrepair as moss and vines now grow upon its artistically sculpted armor.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> Like her immortal foe, she too refused to die. Her armor has become a part of her, using mechanical prosthetic to repair her damaged body.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> Once a stalwart champion of justice, now a bitter and disgruntled mercenary. Their bulky armor looks far too heavy for any normal man to wear properly.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A noble savage who protected the forest and its inhabitants from corruption. Their armor is sewn together from leaves and bark<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Ignoring how they escaped Arcadia, the White Knight is a seasoned protector who has many years of experience battling the forces of evil. They start with the Read Lucidity contract for free at character creation and gain exceptional successes on 3 instead of 5 when using it. Additionally, they can spend a point of Glamour to add +2 Melee and half their Wyrd (rounded up) to their armor rating for the rest of the scene.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-12-2016, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T15:16:14-07:00","id":863928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=863068#post863068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lol. And I was thinking of buying some snacks, just now. Hehe.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, this kinda made me think of the Delicacy kith I found at the 1d4chan wiki. But naturally, this is so much better at handling the concept. Another great work from you.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S: The flavor text was the best point for me. I can even imagine an alternative that incorporates the phrase &amp;quot;enjoy myself&amp;quot;, lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you liked it. I was unaware of the delicacy kith, but then, I never go to 1d4chan either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T15:28:23-07:00","id":863936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=863177#post863177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I would have suggested a ram for the Beast Seeming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But thank you for writing this up. I've been wanting a chocolate bunny type character!<br /> <br /> Although I would suggest removing the ability to eat themselves for Glamour and making it exclusive towards others. Otherwise you have a Kith who can pretty much supply their own Glamour on a whim.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had considered a few different animals associated with being devoured and returning afterwards for the Beast description, but in the end, I just couldn't resist the chocolate bunny.<br /> <br /> As for the blessing, you may be right about the ability to eat themselves for Glamour. I had thought that the lethal damage per point coupled with the inability to heal for a day would have been enough of a disincentive to make it an act of last resort, but now that you've said something, I realize that it would mean that a high Wyrd/Health honeysoul could just hole up for a few days and emerge fully healed with a full Glamour pool as well. I'll need to either remove that part or tweak it in some way to make that a less tempting option. Thanks for the feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T15:57:39-07:00","id":863947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=863936#post863936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had considered a few different animals associated with being devoured and returning afterwards for the Beast description, but in the end, I just couldn't resist the chocolate bunny.<br /> <br /> As for the blessing, you may be right about the ability to eat themselves for Glamour. I had thought that the lethal damage per point coupled with the inability to heal for a day would have been enough of a disincentive to make it an act of last resort, but now that you've said something, I realize that it would mean that a high Wyrd/Health honeysoul could just hole up for a few days and emerge fully healed with a full Glamour pool as well. I'll need to either remove that part or tweak it in some way to make that a less tempting option. Thanks for the feedback.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Oh god, the idea of a Changeling <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=erh2ngRZxs0&amp;nohtml5=False\" target=\"_blank\">locked in a room eating themselves!</a></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T05:27:06-07:00","id":864225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=863717#post863717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>White Knight</b><br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;Evil never dies. Trust me, I tried everything I could to kill that bastard!&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> True Fae who like to be the center of attention for their realms often create grand narratives to extol their virtues to others. But some among the Gentry have another idea in mind, and instead of being the hero of their story, they choose to play the villain. It is easy to corrupt the righteous, to cast them down into the dirt. But it is almost impossible to stamp out evil forever. Somehow, it always finds a way to survive and replenish its strength. Changelings who became White Knights were used to play the role of noble hero in these narratives, rising up to a challenge that they could never permanently succeed at. No matter how many times the hero prevailed, the villain would return, gradually sapping the hero's resolve and proving to the realm that the Keeper could not be defied forever. All seemed right with the story until the day the White Knight did something they weren't supposed to do. They ignored the call to arms and left the innocent people to their fate!<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Their golden armor which once shined like the sun has become dim since it was exposed to human world. Regardless, their posture is still regal and inspiring, with eyes that remain ever vigilant for danger.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> With sloping posture and empty gaze, they realized the futility of their crusade. Their armor is rusty and battle worn from countless battles against the forces of darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A stone sentinel used to guard against the armies of evil. It has fallen into disrepair as moss and vines now grow upon its artistically sculpted armor.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> Like her immortal foe, she too refused to die. Her armor has become a part of her, using mechanical prosthetic to repair her damaged body.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> Once a stalwart champion of justice, now a bitter and disgruntled mercenary. Their bulky armor looks far too heavy for any normal man to wear properly.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A noble savage who protected the forest and its inhabitants from corruption. Their armor is sewn together from leaves and bark<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Ignoring how they escaped Arcadia, the White Knight is a seasoned protector who has many years of experience battling the forces of evil. They start with the Read Lucidity contract for free at character creation and gain exceptional successes on 3 instead of 5 when using it. Additionally, they can spend a point of Glamour to add +2 Melee and half their Wyrd (rounded up) to their armor rating for the rest of the scene.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I am liking the write-up, though the last sentence regarding their escape makes me think Darkling more tha any other Seeming. Perhaps you can rephrase it to make the manner of their escape broader somehow? And that said, I do wonder how a Grimm White Knight would have escaped. Also, since Read Lucidity is a one-dot Contract(?), perhaps you could add more to the Kith's bonus for it?<br /> <br /> Anyway, posting up another kith of my own. As always, critique and some Seeming descriptipns are appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T05:29:12-07:00","id":864226,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Sentinel</b></u><br /> <i>&quot;Just so we're clear. If you hurt her in any way, I will hunt you down and make you wish you were never even born!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Lost who were forced to protect what their Keepers judged as most valuable, whether it was a person, place, or thing. Put to task as watchdogs, palace guards, and bridge trolls, they developed both a unique sense of territoriality, as well as a protective instinct to their charges. Needless to say, it was those same qualities that drove them to escape either to protect someone from the wrath of their Keeper, or to seek out what mattered more to him in the world he was taken from.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Sentinels gain three dots in the Defender Merit, and add half their Wyrd (rounded up) to their Initiative when fighting in a Hollow or Safe Place they own. If they spend a point of Glamour while touching someone, they may grant their target a minor blessing which gives +2/+2 Armor. This bonus is doubled if the subject is a Touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T05:58:32-07:00","id":864245,"title":"","content":"And another. Do feel free to write-up Seeming descriptions for this, too.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Blackguard</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;All is fair in love and war. I just ended up having the last laugh in this fight.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> In the Game of Immortals, the rules of engagement allow for more than just 'fair play'. And the Gentry create Blackguards for many of the more shadowy threatres of war. As mortals, they may have been jaded and pragmatic, looking after themselves and willing to get results with whatever tricks they had. Unfortunately, this knack for survival was what aided them when they backstabbed their Keepers and made their escape.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Blackguard gains three dots in the Killer Instinct Merit, and can apply it reflexively on any creature. If he spends a point of Glamour, he may raise his effective dot rating in the Merit by half his Wyrd (rounded up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T06:22:55-07:00","id":864256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=864225#post864225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am liking the write-up, though the last sentence regarding their escape makes me think Darkling more tha any other Seeming. Perhaps you can rephrase it to make the manner of their escape broader somehow? And that said, I do wonder how a Grimm White Knight would have escaped. Also, since Read Lucidity is a one-dot Contract(?), perhaps you could add more to the Kith's bonus for it?<br /> <br /> Anyway, posting up another kith of my own. As always, critique and some Seeming descriptipns are appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I changed the last sentence so it seems more like they were leaving on a journey to improve their skills, rather than abandoning the people. But I couldn't think of any further improvements to their blessing regarding the contract, unfortunately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:16:39-07:00","id":864377,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Sprite</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I didn't want to grow up either. I just wish there had been an easier way to arrange that.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Arcadia is filled with splendor and beauty that would delight any child regardless of gender. But as they grow older, they lose that sense of whimsy and imagination as maturity sets in. Changelings who became Sprites were originally children who feared the idea of growing up and wanted to remain young and carefree. While in Arcadia, these children were notorious pranksters who teased other residents of Arcadia with their games and tricks. But when they finally encountered the horrors that lurked on the other side of the Hedge, they decided that maybe growing up in the human world wasn't such a bad alternative.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> An elven child with pointy ears, cute facial features and hair that comes in any shade of the rainbow. When in the company of friends, they are full of joy and laughter.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A mischievous little imp with devilish horns and tail along with bright red skin and fangs. Their mischievous grin reveals they're up to something.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> The soul of a child inhabiting a wooden puppet or plastic doll, they can almost appear lifeless when they aren't moving.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Dressed in animal themed pajamas, this child looks like they were a member of Neverland's Lost Boys<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Due to their great love for teasing others, Sprites mastered the art of remaining unseen when they didn't want to be. They begin character creation with the Light-Shy contract for free and only needs 3 successes instead of 5 to gain the exceptional success. Furthermore, they may spend a point of Glamour to add their Wyrd to all Crafts and Subterfuge rolls for the scene</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-14-2016, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:30:10-07:00","id":864492,"title":"","content":"<b>Aboleth</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;If you knew the things I knew, you'd want to hide at the bottom of a lake forever too.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Aboleths are a rare kith that first appeared in Faerie about ten years ago. Drawn from stories of ancient, water-dwelling monstrosities, aboleths were often made to terrorize fellow captives in nautical domains. They often found themselves shoved into the role of sinister monsters to be slain by the designated hero in mad fae dramas.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> An amalgamation of eel, cephalopod, and crustacean, three glowing, glowering red eyes, encased in a layer of slimy mucus.<br /> <b>Fairest: </b>A blue-skinned, sinuous being that projects a compelling aura of resolve and wisdom.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> A kraken-esque entity whose body is made from the folded, glossy paper of a modern-day bestiary.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> Cobalt skin joined at non-Euclidean angles, carved with mind-warping runes that encode the language of no human tongue.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Aboleths can breathe underwater, and gain the Indomitable and Eidetic Memory merits for free. With eye or skin-to-skin contact, an aboleth can spend a point of Glamour and roll Intelligence + Wyrd (resisted by Resolve + Wyrd). On a success, the changeling learns one of the victim's personal Breaking Points. If the target doesn't possess Integrity, Clarity, or a similar-enough analogue to warrant personal Breaking Points, the changeling receives a null-result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 04-12-2016, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:53:59-07:00","id":864506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=864492#post864492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Aboleth</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;If you knew the things I knew, you'd want to hide at the bottom of a lake forever too.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Aboleths are a rare kith that first appeared in Faerie about ten years ago. Drawn from stories of ancient, water-dwelling monstrosities, aboleths were often made to terrorize fellow captives in nautical domains. They often found themselves shoved into the role of sinister monsters to be slain by the designated hero in mad fae dramas.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> An amalgamation of eel, cephalopod, and crustacean, three glowing, glowering red eyes, encased in a layer of slimy mucus.<br /> <b>Fairest: </b>A blue-skinned, sinuous being that projects a compelling aura of resolve and wisdom.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> A kraken-esque entity whose body is made from the folded, glossy paper of a modern-day bestiary.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> Cobalt skin joined at non-Euclidean angles, carved with mind-warping runes that encode the language of no human tongue.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Aboleths can breathe underwater, and gain the Indomitable and Eidetic Memory merits for free. With eye or skin-to-skin contact, an aboleth can spend a point of Glamour and roll Intelligence + Wits + Wyrd (resisted by Resolve + Wyrd). On a success, the changeling learns one of the victim's personal Breaking Points. If the target doesn't possess Integrity, Clarity, or a similar-enough analogue to warrant personal Breaking Points, the changeling receives a null-result.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Well, this is an interesting kith. I think I was contemplating making a kith along these lines (or was it a Mind Flayer-based kith?)<br /> <br /> Either way, great job on this one.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Though perhaps you could limit the Glamour-based ability's dice pool to Intelligence + Wyrd or Wits + Wyrd instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:05:11-07:00","id":864513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=864225#post864225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am liking the write-up, though the last sentence regarding their escape makes me think Darkling more tha any other Seeming. Perhaps you can rephrase it to make the manner of their escape broader somehow? And that said, I do wonder how a Grimm White Knight would have escaped. Also, since Read Lucidity is a one-dot Contract(?), perhaps you could add more to the Kith's bonus for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the blessing is fine as it is, given the armor and Weaponry bonus (Nyrufa should probably change Melee to Weaponry). Heck, at high Wyrd, their armor rating can even exceed the Metalflesh, so I think gaining a bonus on a 1 dot Contract actually balances pretty well with other kiths.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Grimm White Knights:<br /> <br /> <br /> Grimm: His white gold armor is etched with an intricate floral pattern, but those who look closely will see that the lines of the etchings are made up of the tales of epic heroism throughout the ages.<br /> <br /> <br /> Durance: The man who calls himself only Sir once denied that heroes from stories could exist. He felt that white knights were merely fantasy, and that nobody would ever rescue anyone without an ulterior motive. The Damsel in Distress heard of this, and decided that it would be entertaining to force such an individual to become the very thing he denied. For countless years, the changeling assumed the identities of various knights as he lived through the endless rescue fantasies of his Keeper. One day, he heard a distant scream, and acting in his assigned role, he went to find the source of peril. The sound led him out into the Hedge, where he found a badly wounded changeling woman being attacked by briarwolves. He rescued the woman, even though she wasn't his Keeper. As he led her to the safety of her home, he gradually remembered his own previous life, and realized that he'd become a storybook hero. Now he collects the stories of other heroes to immortalize their great deeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T18:32:11-07:00","id":864652,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> <br /> <br /> Hmm. You might have a point there on the White Knight Blessing. Nice description for the Grimms among their number, by the wy.<br /> :P<br /> <br /> Any suggestions for covering Seemings with either the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=864245#post864245\">Blackguard</a> or the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=864226#post864226\">Sentinel</a>?<br /> <br /> I got one or two thought up for either kith.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Blackguard</u></b><br /> <b>\u2022 Darkling: </b>The figure is tall and slender, with corpse-like skin and spiked chain mail.<br /> <b>\u2022 Elemental: </b>A living suit of obsidian black armor, with a menacing glow emanating from the visor of its helmet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Sentinel</b></u><br /> <b>\u2022 Ogre:</b> A bodyguard whose tall stature and muscular build intimidates all but the most foolhardy of intruders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T04:36:56-07:00","id":864821,"title":"","content":"Here's another kith from me, folks.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Watcher</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;I saw what you did, back there...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> They say that seeing is believing. And for those made into Watchers, that statement is especially true. Their Keepers made them into spyglasses and telescopes, or imbued their vision with potent magic so that they may extend their sight across long distances.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> A feline huntress whose pupils dilate whenever she prowls through the shadows.<br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling:</b> Despite having spent so long in the darkness, nothing has ever avoided being seen by his wide eyes.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> A man made of finely polished wood, with eyes made of thick, reflective glass.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Watcher can never be permanently blinded, and always benefits from a single automatic success on any vision-based rolls. If he spends a point of Glamour within a scene and take a turn to concentrate, he may extend his telescopic vision to observe anything within a number of kilometers equal to his Wyrd. While this ability is active, he takes a -3 penalty to all other actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T04:47:26-07:00","id":864827,"title":"","content":"And another one, which might require much critique given its potential in a crossover setting.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Spelldrinker</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;That was a neat party trick. Got any more?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> In a land where magic exists in abundance, the Spelldrinkers existed as a means to warn their Keepers of hostile sorcery, as well as ward them from such powers as well. They were essentially arcane lightning rods, painfully conditioned to absorb magic so that they may take their power unto themselves, or turn it back against the offending witch.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling:</b> A dark robed figure with pale skin and discolored eyes. Emulating the code of the Sith, they learned how to usurp the power of their rivals and turn it to their own ends.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> Standing firm in the face of the Gentry's wrath, neither sword nor sorcery can frighten the Freehold's champion as they march into battle.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> An energy being whose body flares up in the presence of magic.<br /> \u2022 <b>Grimm:</b> Lines of runic script are etched upon his skin, a spell of protection in narrative form.<br /> \u2022 <b>Ogre:</b> Raw magic saturates his flesh, and leaks out as wisps of smoke from luminescent scars and bleeding wounds.<br /> \u2022 <b>Wizened:</b> Small, crystal diodes have been grafted to their flesh, generating a protective network when they sense incoming magic.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Spelldrinker benefits from the 8-again rule on all kenning rolls, and rolls them for free as reflexive actions regardless of his Clarity score. If he successfully contests or resists a supernatural power used against him, he may store the power for the remainder of the scene unless he uses it sooner. The Spelldrinker can store a number of such powers equal to his Wyrd for a scene, after which they dissolve into Glamour that is absorbed. The powers of other supernaturals always yield one point of Glamour.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> A Spelldrinker uses his own dots in Attributes, Skills, and Wyrd when rolling for powers acquired by his blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-19-2016, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T23:37:48-07:00","id":865347,"title":"","content":"What about thoughts on my Sprite kith? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Btw, edited the last sentence of their blessing a little bit for those who have already read through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-14-2016, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T00:59:10-07:00","id":865364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=865347#post865347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about thoughts on my Sprite kith? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Btw, edited the last sentence of their blessing a little bit for those who have already read through it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yikes. I completely forgot about them. ^^<br /> <br /> They're a pretty solid kith. Though perhaps you could make their bonus to Craft rolls more versatile? Word it instead as...<br /> <br /> &quot;Furthermore, they may spend a point of Glamour to add their Wyrd to all Crafts and Subterfuge rolls for the scene&quot;.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, any thoughts on the Blackguard, Sentinel, Spellbreaker, and/or Watcher?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T05:40:33-07:00","id":865439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=865364#post865364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yikes. I completely forgot about them. ^^<br /> <br /> They're a pretty solid kith. Though perhaps you could make their bonus to Craft rolls more versatile? Word it instead as...<br /> <br /> &quot;Furthermore, they may spend a point of Glamour to add their Wyrd to all Crafts and Subterfuge rolls for the scene&quot;.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, any thoughts on the Blackguard, Sentinel, Spellbreaker, and/or Watcher?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Changed the last sentence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I think the Sentinel overlaps with the purpose of the Troll Kith. As for the Blackguard, I could have sworn we already had somebody propose a villain themed Kith earlier?<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Spellbreaker, I don't think that name would be appropriate for a creation of the Fae, especially not when they have the power to absorb and digest magic used against them. Maybe call them <b>Spelldrinker</b>, instead?<br /> <br /> <br /> Here are some other Seemings I thought up for them, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> Small, crystal diodes have been grafted to their flesh, generating a protective network when they sense incoming magic.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A dark robed figure with pale skin and discolored eyes. Emulating the code of the Sith, they learned how to usurp the power of their rivals and turn it to their own ends.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Standing firm in the face of the Gentry's wrath, neither sword nor sorcery can frighten the Freehold's champion as they march into battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-14-2016, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T05:55:44-07:00","id":865446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=865439#post865439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changed the last sentence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I think the Sentinel overlaps with the purpose of the Troll Kith. As for the Blackguard, I could have sworn we already had somebody propose a villain themed Kith earlier?<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Spellbreaker, I don't think that name would be appropriate for a creation of the Fae, especially not when they have the power to absorb and digest magic used against them. Maybe call them <b>Spelldrinker</b>, instead?<br /> <br /> <br /> Here are some other Seemings I thought up for them, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> Small, crystal diodes have been grafted to their flesh, generating a protective network when they sense incoming magic.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A dark robed figure with pale skin and discolored eyes. Emulating the code of the Sith, they learned how to usurp the power of their rivals and turn it to their own ends.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Standing firm in the face of the Gentry's wrath, neither sword nor sorcery can frighten the Freehold's champion as they march into battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Well, I'm open to suggestions for revising the Sentinel. And for the Blackguard, I made them with a concept different from the one for the Villain, which I think still needs some more revising before it can be included in the main post.<br /> <br /> Spelldrinker definitely sounds interesting. But I was thinking of the Spellbreakers from Warcraft when I first conceived them. Love the Seeming descriptions you thought up, either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T16:20:15-07:00","id":865741,"title":"","content":"Changed the Spellbreaker's name to Spelldrinker. And working on a more offensive anti-magic kith I might refer to as Hexbanes or Witchslayers, which will likely include two dots of Dark Eras' Contract of Abjuration as part of their blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:40:47-07:00","id":867206,"title":"","content":"Are there any kiths that could work for a character that manipulates the pity and sympathy of others? Like, he looks so pitiable that you just have to help him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:48:41-07:00","id":867217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=867206#post867206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any kiths that could work for a character that manipulates the pity and sympathy of others? Like, he looks so pitiable that you just have to help him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the canon Dearheart already does that? I'm not sure. Do check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:12:45-07:00","id":867241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=867217#post867217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the canon Dearheart already does that? I'm not sure. Do check.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's similar, but the flavor is more of a caretaker and confidant than a ward. I was thinking of a character that looks like an injured child. They both share the idea of convincing people to protect them, but the Dearheart is closer to your lover than your child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236