ner b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=867269#post867269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mZpz1PhV2jzc2ihda1IwHZc_WTrWTv5qbNv4vzcU2-4/edit\" target=\"_blank\">This might help.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. I've seen that before, but I didn't see the stuff on modifying kiths. I could probably just alter the flavor of Dearheart and add a new blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:43:59-07:00","id":867300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=867262#post867262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm trying, but I've never done something like this before. Changeling is basically my first brush with tabletop gaming and definitely my introduction to the World of Darkness. So I'm trying to get some advice on how to go about creating a new kith.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You certainly picked a good choice for introduction into WoD. I think Changeling is my favorite setting of the genre, personally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B9HTbTc08O4IUVp4NjllN2RqUE5fS1h6d1dnUGRUZmlrQXpN/view?pref=2&amp;pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">Also, here's the Playtest version</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-17-2016, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T00:37:50-07:00","id":867414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=867300#post867300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You certainly picked a good choice for introduction into WoD. I think Changeling is my favorite setting of the genre, personally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B9HTbTc08O4IUVp4NjllN2RqUE5fS1h6d1dnUGRUZmlrQXpN/view?pref=2&amp;pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">Also, here's the Playtest version</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you again. It's a nice refresher<br /> <br /> Clarification: I have already played through a few sessions with a character I created myself. He was a Wizened Artist, nothing too special. It's just that I've never screwed around with homebrewing stuff","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T01:10:18-07:00","id":868259,"title":"","content":"Oh, does eating the Honeysoul cause them any pain? I imagine that might make it hard to enjoy kinky sex with them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Suncursed:</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I've been here the whole time. Didn't you notice one of the decorations is missing? &quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> From gargoyles, to garden gnomes, trolls and even some iterations of dwarf. There are many tales of those who transform into inert stone at the touch of sunlight. Changelings who became Suncursed were forced to adapt to a nocturnal life cycle, moving about only at night and taking shelter from the sun, lest they be rendered defenseless. Knowing they could not move during the day, their Keeper never thought to place guards around them during that time. That is until they found a way to break the spell and regain their mobility in daylight!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A wee little man with a big nose, white beard and pointy hat. He loves to tinker with machines as a hobby.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A pale skinned troll with giant muscles and tiny brain, he's lost too many good meals because he wasted the night away conversing with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A fearsome gargoyle who possesses the horns of a goat, wings of a bat, tail of a lizard, face of a demon and claws of a dragon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A Weeping Angel whose hands are placed over her face when she's still, but are capable of snapping a person's neck in an eyeblink.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> While in Arcadia, the Suncursed turned to stone upon exposure to sunlight, but they discovered a way to regain their mobility while in such a state. When exposed to sunlight, the Suncursed gains +3 to their Armor rating as their body hardens like rock. Additionally by spending a point of Glamour, the Suncursed can add their Wyrd to Stealth rolls when attempting to hide in plain view as long as they are remaining still during that time. Even if the room is fully illuminated with a crowd of people, onlookers will simply believe them to be a statue meant for decoration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-21-2016, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T02:57:49-07:00","id":868291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868259#post868259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, does eating the Honeysoul cause them any pain? I imagine that might make it hard to enjoy kinky sex with them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Suncursed:</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. That was rather morbid.<br /> <br /> But I'm definitely liking the write-up for the Suncursed. It reminds me a lot of the Gargoyles from the Gargoyle TV Series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T05:11:33-07:00","id":868327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=867262#post867262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm trying, but I've never done something like this before. Changeling is basically my first brush with tabletop gaming and definitely my introduction to the World of Darkness. So I'm trying to get some advice on how to go about creating a new kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can create such a kith. You've inspired me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The orphanwretches will be on their way before too long.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868259#post868259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, does eating the Honeysoul cause them any pain? I imagine that might make it hard to enjoy kinky sex with them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Suncursed:</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I've been here the whole time. Didn't you notice one of the decorations is missing? &quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> From gargoyles, to garden gnomes, trolls and even some iterations of dwarf. There are many tales of those who transform into inert stone at the touch of sunlight. Changelings who became Suncursed were forced to adapt to a nocturnal life cycle, moving about only at night and taking shelter from the sun, lest they be rendered defenseless. Knowing they could not move during the day, their Keeper never thought to place guards around them during that time. That is until they found a way to break the spell and regain their mobility in daylight!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A wee little man with a big nose, white beard and pointy hat. He loves to tinker with machines as a hobby.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A pale skinned troll with giant muscles and tiny brain, he's lost too many good meals because he wasted the night away conversing with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A fearsome gargoyle who possesses the horns of a goat, wings of a bat, tail of a lizard, face of a demon and claws of a dragon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> While in Arcadia, the Suncursed turned to stone upon exposure to sunlight, but they discovered a way to regain their mobility while in such a state. When exposed to sunlight, the Suncursed gains +3 to their Defense rating as their body hardens like rock. Additionally by spending a point of Glamour, the Suncursed can add their Wyrd to Stealth rolls and is able to use them without penalty for hiding in plain view. Even if the room is fully illuminated with a crowd of people, onlookers will simply believe them to be a statue meant for decoration. This disguise only works if they are remaining still, as people are bound to take notice of a statue walking around the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The honeysouls most definitely feel pain when being eaten. They are still being injured, even if it is done deliberately to give another character a benefit. Of course, they might be more likely than others to develop vorarephilia.<br /> <br /> I like your suncursed, although I would make it Armor instead of Defense given the flavor. I'd also say that their bonus to Stealth rolls should only function when they are holding still to keep the statue theme going. Still, very good job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":". 04-19-2016, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T05:42:42-07:00","id":868344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868327#post868327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can create such a kith. You've inspired me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The orphanwretches will be on their way before too long.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The honeysouls most definitely feel pain when being eaten. They are still being injured, even if it is done deliberately to give another character a benefit. Of course, they might be more likely than others to develop vorarephilia.<br /> <br /> I like your suncursed, although I would make it Armor instead of Defense given the flavor. I'd also say that their bonus to Stealth rolls should only function when they are holding still to keep the statue theme going. Still, very good job.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see a Lurkglider/Suncursed character being a very effective ambusher in a fight.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, any critique for my most recent kiths (Blackguard, Sentinel, Spelldrinker, and Watcher)?<br /> <br /> I'm also trying to look for a suitable name for a more offensive countermagic kith. And so far, I've got Hexenbane and Witchslayer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T06:12:56-07:00","id":868355,"title":"","content":"Here's the kith I was talking about. On a related note, I edited the flavor text and description for the Spelldrinker.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Mageslayer</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;Your magic shall not save you!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Those transformed into Mageslayers were made into weapons against the very magic of Arcadia itself. Their durance saw them destroy enchantments and kill sorcerers with ruthless efficiency. However, when they finally chose to defy their Keepers, they were able to repel whatever magic was used to try and subdue them. <br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> A lambent-eyed owl with bone white feathers.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> Sculpted from mountain ash, this entity's presence causes an adverse reaction to the senses of any unfortunate witch.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest</b> A white-haired warrior with golden .cat's eyes and an intricate array of sigils marked upon his body. <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Mageslayers gain two dots in the Contract of Abjuration, and can always invoke it as a Reflexive action. They also gain a +3 bonus for contesting or resisting any harmful supernatural powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T06:20:27-07:00","id":868362,"title":"","content":"Hey, Nyrufa, I got an idea for a Fairest Suncursed.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A Weeping Angel whose hands are placed over her face when she's still, but are capable of snapping a person's neck in an eyeblink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T08:00:56-07:00","id":868437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868327#post868327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can create such a kith. You've inspired me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The orphanwretches will be on their way before too long.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The honeysouls most definitely feel pain when being eaten. They are still being injured, even if it is done deliberately to give another character a benefit. Of course, they might be more likely than others to develop vorarephilia.<br /> <br /> I like your suncursed, although I would make it Armor instead of Defense given the flavor. I'd also say that their bonus to Stealth rolls should only function when they are holding still to keep the statue theme going. Still, very good job.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I thought it was for standing still. Unless I cut that part out and didn't notice it. if I did then I'm going back to change it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868362#post868362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Nyrufa, I got an idea for a Fairest Suncursed.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A Weeping Angel whose hands are placed over her face when she's still, but are capable of snapping a person's neck in an eyeblink.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> DON'T BLINK!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-19-2016, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T09:27:54-07:00","id":868491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868344#post868344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see a Lurkglider/Suncursed character being a very effective ambusher in a fight.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, any critique for my most recent kiths (Blackguard, Sentinel, Spelldrinker, and Watcher)?<br /> <br /> I'm also trying to look for a suitable name for a more offensive countermagic kith. And so far, I've got Hexenbane and Witchslayer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I apologize for being inactive in the thread for so long. I'd been working on a pet project for Demon: the Descent. I'm back now. Also, Nyrufa, I liked the Sprites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=864226#post864226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Sentinel</b></u><br /> <i>&quot;Just so we're clear. If you hurt her in any way, I will hunt you down and make you wish you were never even born!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Lost who were forced to protect what their Keepers judged as most valuable, whether it was a person, place, or thing. Put to task as watchdogs, palace guards, and bridge trolls, they developed both a unique sense of territoriality, as well as a protective instinct to their charges. Needless to say, it was those same qualities that drove them to escape either to protect someone from the wrath of their Keeper, or to seek out what mattered more to him in the world he was taken from.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Sentinels gain three dots in the Defender Merit, and add half their Wyrd (rounded up) to their Initiative when fighting in a Hollow or Safe Place they own. If they spend a point of Glamour while touching someone, they may grant their target a minor blessing which gives +2/+2 Armor. This bonus is doubled if the subject is a Touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like these guys a lot, although I agree that their flavor is pretty similar to the Troll. The blessing is different enough, though, that they'd synergize well together. Given that the rest of their blessing protects an individual, I could see the bonus to Initiative coming up in a Safe Place owned by their target rather than themselves. I'd also say that the Armor granting portion of their blessing should have a duration, perhaps something like a number of turns equal to their Wyrd? I could also see them gaining the Danger Sense Merit directed towards the object of their defense if they have an active Pledge going to do so. For Seeming descriptions:<br /> <br /> <b>Beast: </b>This canine always wears a spiked collar, and there is a growl to his voice when strangers are near.<br /> <b>Elemental: </b>She is built like a tower, with stone bricks for skin and two flickering flames in the windows of her eyes.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=864245#post864245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And another. Do feel free to write-up Seeming descriptions for this, too.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Blackguard</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;All is fair in love and war. I just ended up having the last laugh in this fight.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> In the Game of Immortals, the rules of engagement allow for more than just 'fair play'. And the Gentry create Blackguards for many of the more shadowy threatres of war. As mortals, they may have been jaded and pragmatic, looking after themselves and willing to get results with whatever tricks they had. Unfortunately, this knack for survival was what aided them when they backstabbed their Keepers and made their escape.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Blackguard gains three dots in the Killer Instinct Merit, and can apply it reflexively on any creature. If he spends a point of Glamour, he may raise his effective dot rating in the Merit by half his Wyrd (rounded up).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would need to track down and read the Merit to be able to give a proper critique of these guys. That said, I like the flavor of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=864827#post864827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And another one, which might require much critique given its potential in a crossover setting.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Spelldrinker</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;That was a neat party trick. Got any more?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> In a land where magic exists in abundance, the Spelldrinkers existed as a means to warn their Keepers of hostile sorcery, as well as ward them from such powers as well. They were essentially arcane lightning rods, painfully conditioned to absorb magic so that they may take their power unto themselves, or turn it back against the offending witch.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling:</b> A dark robed figure with pale skin and discolored eyes. Emulating the code of the Sith, they learned how to usurp the power of their rivals and turn it to their own ends.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> Standing firm in the face of the Gentry's wrath, neither sword nor sorcery can frighten the Freehold's champion as they march into battle.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> An energy being whose body flares up in the presence of magic.<br /> \u2022 <b>Grimm:</b> Lines of runic script are etched upon his skin, a spell of protection in narrative form.<br /> \u2022 <b>Ogre:</b> Raw magic saturates his flesh, and leaks out as wisps of smoke from luminescent scars and bleeding wounds.<br /> \u2022 <b>Wizened:</b> Small, crystal diodes have been grafted to their flesh, generating a protective network when they sense incoming magic.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Spelldrinker benefits from the 8-again rule on all kenning rolls, and rolls them for free as reflexive actions regardless of his Clarity score. If he successfully contests or resists a supernatural power used against him, he may store the power for the remainder of the scene unless he uses it sooner. The Spelldrinker can store a number of such powers equal to his Wyrd for a scene, after which they dissolve into Glamour that is absorbed. The powers of other supernaturals always yield one point of Glamour.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> A Spelldrinker uses his own dots in Attributes, Skills, and Wyrd when rolling for powers acquired by his blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting one. It does seem very powerful, although I can't deny that the concept is cool. I would limit their dice pool to the lower of the original caster or the Spelldrinker's own, possible with an additional penalty to using powers without a fae origin. I'd also make it so that when it dissolves, it is one point of Glamour regardless of which kind of power was used. The kenning rolls benefit is an interesting one, and I like it. I can't remember, was it a reflexive action for regular changelings whenever their Clarity was high enough, or did it take an action? The Seeming descriptions are great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=864821#post864821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another kith from me, folks.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Watcher</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;I saw what you did, back there...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> They say that seeing is believing. And for those made into Watchers, that statement is especially true. Their Keepers made them into spyglasses and telescopes, or imbued their vision with potent magic so that they may extend their sight across long distances.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> A feline huntress whose pupils dilate whenever she prowls through the shadows.<br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling:</b> Despite having spent so long in the darkness, nothing has ever avoided being seen by his wide eyes.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> A man made of finely polished wood, with eyes made of thick, reflective glass.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Watcher can never be permanently blinded, and always benefits from a single automatic success on any vision-based rolls. If he spends a point of Glamour within a scene and take a turn to concentrate, he may extend his telescopic vision to observe anything within a number of kilometers equal to his Wyrd. While this ability is active, he takes a -3 penalty to all other actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting blessing, but it reminds me rather a lot of the cleareyes. I really like the Seeming descriptions you've got for this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T10:15:26-07:00","id":868531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868491#post868491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I apologize for being inactive in the thread for so long. I'd been working on a pet project for Demon: the Descent. I'm back now. Also, Nyrufa, I liked the Sprites.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! I wasn't sure how well received it would be. As I understand it, playing children or child-like character is kind of unpopular among the WoD community. Lots of people were unhappy playing Childlings with Dreaming, from what I heard.<br /> <br /> But I say you can't have a story about fairy tales without the inclusion of children in some way. Hell, the entire concept of fairy tales was created to keep children in line!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T14:34:42-07:00","id":868775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868491#post868491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I apologize for being inactive in the thread for so long. I'd been working on a pet project for Demon: the Descent. I'm back now. </div> </div> </div> </div>Oh? What kind of pet project?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868491#post868491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like these guys a lot, although I agree that their flavor is pretty similar to the Troll. The blessing is different enough, though, that they'd synergize well together. Given that the rest of their blessing protects an individual, I could see the bonus to Initiative coming up in a Safe Place owned by their target rather than themselves. I'd also say that the Armor granting portion of their blessing should have a duration, perhaps something like a number of turns equal to their Wyrd? I could also see them gaining the Danger Sense Merit directed towards the object of their defense if they have an active Pledge going to do so. For Seeming descriptions:<br /> <br /> <b>Beast: </b>This canine always wears a spiked collar, and there is a growl to his voice when strangers are near.<br /> <b>Elemental: </b>She is built like a tower, with stone bricks for skin and two flickering flames in the windows of her eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Liking these additional Seeming descriptions. Now, regarding the Hollow/Safe Place aspect of the blessing, should I reword it to be applied for locations owned by their charges only? I initially wrote it down so that they can also protect locations instead of people.<br /> <br /> As for giving them Danger Sense in relation to their charge if they have a pledge, perhaps they can simply just roll Wits + Composure to sense whenever their wards are in danger? Provided they have an active Bargain or Oath to them? The Armor boon could last a scene, instead of turns in Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868491#post868491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would need to track down and read the Merit to be able to give a proper critique of these guys. That said, I like the flavor of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in Beast: The Primordial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868491#post868491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting one. It does seem very powerful, although I can't deny that the concept is cool. I would limit their dice pool to the lower of the original caster or the Spelldrinker's own, possible with an additional penalty to using powers without a fae origin. I'd also make it so that when it dissolves, it is one point of Glamour regardless of which kind of power was used. The kenning rolls benefit is an interesting one, and I like it. I can't remember, was it a reflexive action for regular changelings whenever their Clarity was high enough, or did it take an action? The Seeming descriptions are great.</div> </div> </div> </div>At Clarity 4, you need to spend Willpower to do a kenning roll as an instant action. That said, the caveat of using the lower of their dice pools or their enemy's makes sense. As is regaining one point of glamour from any power they absorb, regardless of its nature. For penalties, I can just stress that changelings apply half their Wyrd (rounded down) for other Supernatural Advantages and/or power sets like Discipline ratings, Renown, and perhaps even Satiety? Or perhaps it's better to treat them as having <i>no</i> dots whatsoever?<br /> <br /> Now, imagine this paired with Mageslayer via Dual Kith.<br /> <br /> Also, I was thinking of adding this in as part of their blessing.<br /> <br /> &quot;They also gain an Exceptional Success in kenning rolls at three successes so long as they have a Clarity rating of at least five dots&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868491#post868491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting blessing, but it reminds me rather a lot of the cleareyes. I really like the Seeming descriptions you've got for this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit there are similarities to the Cleareyes. And some clarification on vision-based rolls might be needed. If you have any suggestions for this, I'm open to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-19-2016, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T15:45:19-07:00","id":868837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868531#post868531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks! I wasn't sure how well received it would be. As I understand it, playing children or child-like character is kind of unpopular among the WoD community. Lots of people were unhappy playing Childlings with Dreaming, from what I heard.<br /> <br /> But I say you can't have a story about fairy tales without the inclusion of children in some way. Hell, the entire concept of fairy tales was created to keep children in line!</div> </div> </div> </div>Children actually seem to be quite popular, given the popularity of Innocents. I think that the problem most people had with Childlings was that it set a default &quot;growing up is a bad thing&quot; theme to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T15:54:25-07:00","id":868848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868775#post868775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh? What kind of pet project?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Liking these additional Seeming descriptions. Now, regarding the Hollow/Safe Place aspect of the blessing, should I reword it to be applied for locations owned by their charges only? I initially wrote it down so that they can also protect locations instead of people.<br /> <br /> As for giving them Danger Sense in relation to their charge if they have a pledge, perhaps they can simply just roll Wits + Composure to sense whenever their wards are in danger? Provided they have an active Bargain or Oath to them? The Armor boon could last a scene, instead of turns in Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's in Beast: The Primordial.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> At Clarity 4, you need to spend Willpower to do a kenning roll as an instant action. That said, the caveat of using the lower of their dice pools or their enemy's makes sense. As is regaining one point of glamour from any power they absorb, regardless of its nature. For penalties, I can just stress that changelings apply half their Wyrd (rounded down) for other Supernatural Advantages and/or power sets like Discipline ratings, Renown, and perhaps even Satiety? Or perhaps it's better to treat them as having <i>no</i> dots whatsoever?<br /> <br /> Now, imagine this paired with Mageslayer via Dual Kith.<br /> <br /> Also, I was thinking of adding this in as part of their blessing.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;They also gain an Exceptional Success in kenning rolls at three successes so long as they have a Clarity rating of at least five dots&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I admit there are similarities to the Cleareyes. And some clarification on vision-based rolls might be needed. If you have any suggestions for this, I'm open to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Demon project can be found in the Cipher &amp; Sigil thread.<br /> <br /> For the spelldrinkers, I'd say go with half their Wyrd for fae powers (ensuring that it is always better to use Contracts you purchased yourself instead of secondhand ones) and none at all for other supernatural abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T16:13:38-07:00","id":868867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868837#post868837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Children actually seem to be quite popular, given the popularity of Innocents. I think that the problem most people had with Childlings was that it set a default &quot;growing up is a bad thing&quot; theme to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well from a certain point it can be. I looked at Dreaming the same way I looked at Bridge to Terabithia and the plot of the game was like a coming of age ceremony. Forced to discard your childish sense of wonder and creativity to become a cold, empty adult in a soulless world.<br /> <br /> But apparently online reviewers of the game took one look at the art style and thought it was too colorful and whimsy for World of Darkness, completely ignoring how <i>utterly depressing</i> the theme of the game could have been if played right.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm glad the idea of child characters are popular, though. Everybody I saw talking about the game didn't seem pleased by it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T04:52:41-07:00","id":869226,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Siren</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;Come. Join me here while I sing&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> Inspiring the old myths made by sailors in the past, Sirens were made by aquatic Keepers to lure the unwary into the depths of their realms. Few ever turn away once they hear their songs, and the sites where Sirens are known to gather soon become littered with the bones of those who drowned in their efforts to reach them.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> A benevolent rusalka who flies out of the water in the spring to bring rain to the fields.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> A sea nymph with avian and piscine features. The talons and wings of the former, and gills and iridescent scales for the latter.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Siren is able to breathe underwater, and can fly for a number of minutes equal to half her Wyrd (rounded up) before she needs to spend a turn without moving to rest. If she spends Glamour and sings, she can enthrall listeners by rolling Manipulation + Expression vs. Resolve + Wyrd. Enthralled listeners subtract the changeling's Wyrd from all rolls to notice their surroundings and suffer from the Swooning Condition toward the Siren for the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-20-2016, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T05:12:18-07:00","id":869235,"title":"","content":"@White Oak Dragon<br /> <br /> How's this revision for the Sentinel Blessing?<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Sentinels gain three dots in the Defender Merit, and add half their Wyrd (rounded up) to their Initiative when fighting in a Hollow or Safe Place owned by them or their allies. If they spend a point of Glamour while touching someone, they may grant their target a minor blessing which gives +2/+2 Armor for a number of attacks equal to his Wyrd. The Armor's rating is doubled if the subject is a Touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T06:13:46-07:00","id":869261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=869226#post869226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Siren</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;Come. Join me here while I sing&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> Inspiring the old myths made by sailors in the past, Sirens were made by aquatic Keepers to lure the unwary into the depths of their realms. Few ever turn away once they hear their songs, and the sites where Sirens are known to gather soon become littered with the bones of those who drowned in their efforts to reach them.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> A benevolent rusalka who flies out of the water in the spring to bring rain to the fields.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> A sea nymph with avian and piscine features. The talons and wings of the former, and gills and iridescent scales for the latter.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Siren is able to breathe underwater, and can fly for a number of minutes equal to half her Wyrd (rounded up) before she needs to spend a turn without moving to rest. If she spends Glamour and sings, she can enthrall listeners by rolling Manipulation + Expression vs. Resolve + Wyrd. Enthralled listeners subtract the changeling's Wyrd from all rolls to notice their surroundings and suffer from the Swooning Condition toward the Siren for the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think giving a character the ability to fly right out of creation is a little over powered. There are other character splats who deal with aerial creatures that simply have the power to glide instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T07:06:30-07:00","id":869288,"title":"","content":"I think that paradigm is changing; never the less, I do think that this kith might be handled better through a Dual Kith Windwing/Nix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T18:04:48-07:00","id":869781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=869288#post869288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that paradigm is changing; never the less, I do think that this kith might be handled better through a Dual Kith Windwing/Nix.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose.<br /> <br /> It was worth taking a stab at it, though.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T20:36:53-07:00","id":869874,"title":"","content":"Do we have a Kith for those who were forced to count and measure various objects, like the coins of a dragon, the skulls ripped by a black knight or the vials and jars of an alchemist? It would be easy if these collections simply grew, but they often flew about, changed sizes, grew fangs or otherwise changed to make it more complicated. <br /> <br /> The Fireheart Kith represents this pretty well with the bonus to Initiative and rolling for extend mental tasks every turn. I'm wondering if you could make the Kith more general in order to represent Durances where you worked like secretary or accountant. What could replace the ability to start fires? Perhaps they get the Trivial Reworking Contract for free and get Exceptional Success with 3 Successes? My first idea for a name is Number-Watcher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T21:23:54-07:00","id":869913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=869874#post869874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have a Kith for those who were forced to count and measure various objects, like the coins of a dragon, the skulls ripped by a black knight or the vials and jars of an alchemist? It would be easy if these collections simply grew, but they often flew about, changed sizes, grew fangs or otherwise changed to make it more complicated. <br /> <br /> The Fireheart Kith represents this pretty well with the bonus to Initiative and rolling for extend mental tasks every turn. I'm wondering if you could make the Kith more general in order to represent Durances where you worked like secretary or accountant. What could replace the ability to start fires? Perhaps they get the Trivial Reworking Contract for free and get Exceptional Success with 3 Successes? My first idea for a name is Number-Watcher.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a Logician kith here that I'll have to revisit. But your Numberwatcher kith concept is pretty interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T21:35:44-07:00","id":869917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=868867#post868867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well from a certain point it can be. I looked at Dreaming the same way I looked at Bridge to Terabithia and the plot of the game was like a coming of age ceremony. Forced to discard your childish sense of wonder and creativity to become a cold, empty adult in a soulless world.<br /> <br /> But apparently online reviewers of the game took one look at the art style and thought it was too colorful and whimsy for World of Darkness, completely ignoring how <i>utterly depressing</i> the theme of the game could have been if played right.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm glad the idea of child characters are popular, though. Everybody I saw talking about the game didn't seem pleased by it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The theme of discarding the sense of wonder and creativity to become an adult was one of the things that a lot of people didn't like because it implied that all children had it and that the only adults that had a similar sense of wonder were the utterly insane, unless they were a Dreamer. It also made it so that the most powerful characters at character creation had to be children, as adult characters invariably lost more Glamour than they gained in Willpower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=869235#post869235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@White Oak Dragon<br /> <br /> How's this revision for the Sentinel Blessing?<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Sentinels gain three dots in the Defender Merit, and add half their Wyrd (rounded up) to their Initiative when fighting in a Hollow or Safe Place owned by them or their allies. If they spend a point of Glamour while touching someone, they may grant their target a minor blessing which gives +2/+2 Armor for a number of attacks equal to his Wyrd. The Armor's rating is doubled if the subject is a Touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like that. I think that it all flows together quite well now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T22:16:14-07:00","id":869940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=869235#post869235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@White Oak Dragon<br /> <br /> How's this revision for the Sentinel Blessing?<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Sentinels gain three dots in the Defender Merit, and add half their Wyrd (rounded up) to their Initiative when fighting in a Hollow or Safe Place owned by them or their allies. If they spend a point of Glamour while touching someone, they may grant their target a minor blessing which gives +2/+2 Armor for a number of attacks equal to his Wyrd. The Armor's rating is doubled if the subject is a Touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div> Excellent! This stands out from Kiths like Troll and Oni.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T22:26:54-07:00","id":869946,"title":"","content":"Thanks, guys <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I'll be sure to add in the Sentinels to the main post soon... In fact, I may need to set up a GDoc now that it's gotten pretty big as a list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T22:47:12-07:00","id":869958,"title":"","content":"Here is the new one that I promised:<br /> <br /> <b>Orphanwretch</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Look kid, I'm sorry. No, no, don't cry. I shouldn't have said that. Please, don't cry. Come on, I'll buy you dinner.</span><br /> <br /> Pity is an emotion that is alien to most Keepers, but sometimes the Gentry find situations where it can be used to their advantage. Orphanwretches are often selected from the most miserable mortals that a Keeper can find, and are made into small and wretched beings designed to elicit feelings of pity and mercy from other Fae or their servants. While many are left in the Hedge near the lands of a hated rival, some use the opportunities afforded to them by their infiltration to escape.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A diminutive and wrinkled old man with a bent and broken form, a wheezing cough punctuating his every statement.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A tiny tattered teddy bear, forgotten and forlorn.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> From the dust and blood covering his face and the bruises and scratches upon his skin, you can see that the little street kid is tough as nails, but there is a gleam of wonder still lurking in his beautiful blue eyes.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> The young waif in the threadbare rags leans on a crutch and walks with a pronounced limp, a side effect of the weathered peg of cedar that has replaced her missing leg.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The orphanwretch gains the Small-Framed Merit at no cost. Additionally, whenever another character succeeds in a Social roll against the changeling, the orphanwretch may reflexively spend a point of Glamour to inflict either the Guilty or Leveraged Condition on the character. Doing so also gives the orphanwretch a number of bonus dice equal to his Wyrd on his next Empathy, Persuasion, or Subterfuge roll against the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T00:02:35-07:00","id":869994,"title":"","content":"Dang. So even if you win in a Social roll, you <i>still</i> lose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T05:25:18-07:00","id":870104,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Psylocke</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;The mind can be sharper than any mortal sword. Now hold still. This might sting a little.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Assassins of a subtle bent, those made into Psylockes by their Keepers could use their own minds as weapons. While most did not prove hardy in open conflict, they became true threats once they've scattered their foes and single them out, one after the other. A Psylocke who escapes, however, did so after briefly stunning her Keeper with her gift.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> A vaguely humanoid shadow that can manifest curved blades from its forearms with a thought.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> A dark-haired assassin garbed in form-fitting armor, who slowly weakens her foes with each punch and every palm strike.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Psylocke can spend Glamour or Willpower to use any facet of the Numbing Touch Merit, and is considered to have a dot rating in it equal to half her Wyrd (rounded up). Furthermore, when she lashes out at the nervous system of a victim with a Glamour pool, she also gains an amount of Glamour equal to half her Wyrd (rounded up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T06:00:08-07:00","id":870119,"title":"","content":"Revision to the Spelldrinker kith.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Spelldrinker</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;That was a neat party trick. Got any more?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> In a land where magic exists in abundance, the Spelldrinkers existed as a means to warn and ward against hostile sorceries. They were arcane lightning rods, painfully conditioned to absorb magic so they may take it unto themselves, or turn it back against the offending witch. Some were so effective in this purpose, though, that they struck their own Keepers down with their own power.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling:</b> A dark robed figure with pale skin and discolored eyes. Emulating the code of the Sith, they learned how to usurp the power of their rivals and turn it to their own ends.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> Standing firm in the face of the Gentry's wrath, neither sword nor sorcery can frighten the Freehold's champion as they march into battle.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> An energy being whose body flares up in the presence of magic.<br /> \u2022 <b>Grimm:</b> Lines of runic script are etched upon his skin, a spell of protection in narrative form.<br /> \u2022 <b>Ogre:</b> Raw magic saturates his flesh, and leaks out as wisps of smoke from luminescent scars and bleeding wounds.<br /> \u2022 <b>Wizened:</b> Small, crystal diodes have been grafted to their flesh, generating a protective network when they sense incoming magic.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Spelldrinker benefits from the 8-again rule on all kenning rolls, which are always free reflexive actions. If he successfully contests or resists a supernatural power used against him, he may retain it for later use within the scene. The Spelldrinker can store a number of such powers equal to his Wyrd, with any unused each granting one point of Glamour. He uses his own dots in Attributes and Skills when rolling those powers, but does not add his Wyrd for Contracts he doesn't know, as well as the powers of other supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-21-2016, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T06:07:09-07:00","id":870122,"title":"","content":"Has anyone considered making a kith based on either the Fae Mount or Hedgebeast Companion Merits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T06:22:38-07:00","id":870131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=869994#post869994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dang. So even if you win in a Social roll, you <i>still</i> lose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I was trying to go for that sensation where a person totally does or says the right thing to someone, but still feels like shit for doing so afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T06:25:37-07:00","id":870134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870122#post870122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone considered making a kith based on either the Fae Mount or Hedgebeast Companion Merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually had not, though it could certainly be an interesting one. If nobody else does one, I will see what I can come up with. Right now, I'm debating about whether I want to finish up the briarborn or tangletail next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T06:33:43-07:00","id":870138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870131#post870131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. I was trying to go for that sensation where a person totally does or says the right thing to someone, but still feels like shit for doing so afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, congratulations. You pulled it off.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Meantime, any thoughts on the Psylocke and the revisions to the Spelldrinker?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870134#post870134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually had not, though it could certainly be an interesting one. If nobody else does one, I will see what I can come up with. Right now, I'm debating about whether I want to finish up the briarborn or tangletail next.</div> </div> </div> </div>Briarborn and Tangletail? Now, you have me curious. Hmm. For the kith with Hedgebeast Companion for its blessing, perhaps Tamer would be a tentative name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T08:43:05-07:00","id":870235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870138#post870138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, congratulations. You pulled it off.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Meantime, any thoughts on the Psylocke and the revisions to the Spelldrinker?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Briarborn and Tangletail? Now, you have me curious. Hmm. For the kith with Hedgebeast Companion for its blessing, perhaps Tamer would be a tentative name?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spelldrinkers are looking pretty good. I think the only thing I'd take out is the part where any spells absorbed after their limit in a scene are automatically converted to Gkamour. The absorbed ones becoming Glamour makes sense, but allowing the ones beyond the limit to do so as well permits allies to keep a steady supply of low level effects coming for full replenishment. Other than that, it looks great.<br /> <br /> The psylockes are interesting. I appreciate the reference, but I'd consider changing the name and leave the reference in the Fairest description, given Marvel's monopoly on the term. I'd also consider giving a dice pool for Glamour replenishment rather than making it automatic. I do like what you've got so far, though.<br /> <br /> Since you are curious about them, which of the two kiths sounds more intriguing to you? I doubt I'll have time to work on both tonight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T10:31:32-07:00","id":870325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870138#post870138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Meantime, any thoughts on the Psylocke?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Usually when a Kith grants Merit Dots, it appears to grant a fixed three. Any reason you went with what you did?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T11:45:28-07:00","id":870402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=869958#post869958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the new one that I promised:<br /> <br /> <b>Orphanwretch</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Look kid, I'm sorry. No, no, don't cry. I shouldn't have said that. Please, don't cry. Come on, I'll buy you dinner.</span><br /> <br /> Pity is an emotion that is alien to most Keepers, but sometimes the Gentry find situations where it can be used to their advantage. Orphanwretches are often selected from the most miserable mortals that a Keeper can find, and are made into small and wretched beings designed to elicit feelings of pity and mercy from other Fae or their servants. While many are left in the Hedge near the lands of a hated rival, some use the opportunities afforded to them by their infiltration to escape.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A diminutive and wrinkled old man with a bent and broken form, a wheezing cough punctuating his every statement.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A tiny tattered teddy bear, forgotten and forlorn.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> From the dust and blood covering his face and the bruises and scratches upon his skin, you can see that the little street kid is tough as nails, but there is a gleam of wonder still lurking in his beautiful blue eyes.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> The young waif in the threadbare rags leans on a crutch and walks with a pronounced limp, a side effect of the weathered peg of cedar that has replaced her missing leg.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The orphanwretch gains the Small-Framed Merit at no cost. Additionally, whenever another character succeeds in a Social roll against the changeling, the orphanwretch may reflexively spend a point of Glamour to inflict either the Guilty or Leveraged Condition on the character. Doing so also gives the orphanwretch a number of bonus dice equal to his Wyrd on his next Empathy, Persuasion, or Subterfuge roll against the character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh <br /> my <br /> Goddess<br /> <br /> That is amazing. That is exactly what I was looking for. That is just perfect.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'm going to add descriptions from the other seeming<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Saucer-sized, brown eyes that always look to be on the verge of tears. A face that warms the hearts of all with its smile and breaks them to little bits with their frown. To do anything wrong to this perfect little angel would be unthinkable.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> If you look closely, all the dust, dirt and bruises on that weary body are made out of tiny poems about all the people who have used him and left him behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T13:39:43-07:00","id":870570,"title":"","content":"<b>Hivedrone</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Our name is Legion, for we are many</i><br /> <br /> <br /> It doesn't happen often, but sometimes the True Fae come up with a brilliant idea. One of them was that it is much simpler keep your slaves under control when they all think exactly the same! Hivedrones were connected to a vast, mental network designed to monitor and transmit thoughts between each other. What one drone thought, they all thought. What one drone learned, they all learned. Their escape from Arcadia came when they were severed from the collective and regained their sense of individuality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A worker bee who got separated from the others while pollinating the flowers of their Keeper's realm.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A beloved leader who always seems to know what the people expect of their government.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A half shaved head with a surgical scar reveals the location of the transmitter chip in their brain<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Hivedrone's durance left them with a natural talent for the thought processes of other beings. By rolling their Wits + Intelligence, a Hivedrone can detect the presence of any thinking being within ten yards per dot of Wyrd, provided that the being is not hidden by supernatural means. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, they may create a telepathic link with one of their allies within visual range for the duration of the scene. Additional Glamour may be spent to add other allies to this mental network, up to a limit equal to the Hivedrone's Wyrd. While linked into this network, the group may all communicate with each other silently, and none of them shall suffer untrained penalties to Mental Skill rolls, provided at least one member of the network has a dot in the Skill. The characters may also engage in teamwork actions for tasks involving Mental Skills. A character who travels more than Wyrd x 10 yards from the Hivedrone is automatically severed from the link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-22-2016, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T13:42:45-07:00","id":870572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870402#post870402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh<br /> my<br /> Goddess<br /> <br /> That is amazing. That is exactly what I was looking for. That is just perfect.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'm going to add descriptions from the other seeming<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Saucer-sized, brown eyes that always look to be on the verge of tears. A face that warms the hearts of all with its smile and breaks them to little bits with their frown. To do anything wrong to this perfect little angel would be unthinkable.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> If you look closely, all the dust, dirt and bruises on that weary body are made out of tiny poems about all the people who have used him and left him behind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do believe that that's among the most enthusiastic reactions my work has ever received. I am glad that you liked it so much and that it works for what you were seeking. As long as you're looking to have all the Seemings available, let's get a little Beautiful Joe into the mix.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> With his cropped ears and docked tail, you can't help but feel sorry for the poor miserable mongrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T13:49:07-07:00","id":870584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870325#post870325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Usually when a Kith grants Merit Dots, it appears to grant a fixed three. Any reason you went with what you did?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I wasn't sure if that three-dot scheme would work with a Merit like Numbing Touch, so maybe it might work if I handled it like Safe Place for Trolls? Of course, I could probably use the Leechfinger as inspiration instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T13:49:52-07:00","id":870587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870572#post870572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I do believe that that's among the most enthusiastic reactions my work has ever received. I am glad that you liked it so much and that it works for what you were seeking. As long as you're looking to have all the Seemings available, let's get a little Beautiful Joe into the mix.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> With his cropped ears and docked tail, you can't help but feel sorry for the poor miserable mongrel.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* I'm an enthusiastic guy. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T14:00:03-07:00","id":870595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870235#post870235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spelldrinkers are looking pretty good. I think the only thing I'd take out is the part where any spells absorbed after their limit in a scene are automatically converted to Gkamour. The absorbed ones becoming Glamour makes sense, but allowing the ones beyond the limit to do so as well permits allies to keep a steady supply of low level effects coming for full replenishment. Other than that, it looks great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Made that tiny revision to the post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870235#post870235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The psylockes are interesting. I appreciate the reference, but I'd consider changing the name and leave the reference in the Fairest description, given Marvel's monopoly on the term. I'd also consider giving a dice pool for Glamour replenishment rather than making it automatic. I do like what you've got so far, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any suggestions for alternative names? I'm not sure if Psion is apt, and I'm coming up dry on other choices. Also, what kind of dice pool would be good to use?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870235#post870235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you are curious about them, which of the two kiths sounds more intriguing to you? I doubt I'll have time to work on both tonight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Briarborn? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;