 hand,his sking is the color of dirty clothes<br /> Grimm;Slap a winter coat an funny hat,and you have Sherlock holmes,grab the stuff and collar and harry dresden shows up. it is said the line son his skin can tell you all about the maltese falcon....</div> </div> </div> </div> There's already a Kith for detectives called Slewfoot. It even gives 2 dots in the relevant Professional Training Merit as part of the Blessing. There are also the Cleareyes, Whisperwisps and Greys, which are all great for gathering intel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T18:45:11-07:00","id":870833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870828#post870828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's already a Kith for detectives called Slewfoot. It even gives 2 dots in the relevant Professional Training Merit as part of the Blessing. There are also the Cleareyes, Whisperwisps and Greys, which are all great for gathering intel.</div> </div> </div> </div>i think none of those focus enough on the grittiness for my tastes y'know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T18:54:06-07:00","id":870838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870833#post870833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i think none of those focus enough on the grittiness for my tastes y'know?</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough. You can give dots in Merits like Investigative Aide, Investigative Prodigy and Takes One To Know One as part of the blessing of your Detective Kith. Maybe even give them some 2ED Smoke Contracts for free so they can follow suspects and all that jazz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T18:57:19-07:00","id":870839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870838#post870838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Fair enough. You can give dots in Merits like Investigative Aide, Investigative Prodigy and Takes One To Know One as part of the blessing of your Detective Kith. Maybe even give them some 2ED Smoke Contracts for free so they can follow suspects and all that jazz.</div> </div> </div> </div>Smoke contracts!love,those,ill put a merit in the blessing as soon i get the cofd book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T22:35:50-07:00","id":870951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870570#post870570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hivedrone</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Our name is Legion, for we are many</i><br /> <br /> <br /> It doesn't happen often, but sometimes the True Fae come up with a brilliant idea. One of them was that it is much simpler keep your slaves under control when they all think exactly the same! Hivedrones were connected to a vast, mental network designed to monitor and transmit thoughts between each other. What one drone thought, they all thought. What one drone learned, they all learned. Their escape from Arcadia came when they were severed from the collective and regained their sense of individuality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A worker bee who got separated from the others while pollinating the flowers of their Keeper's realm.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A beloved leader who always seems to know what the people expect of their government.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A half shaved head with a surgical scar reveals the location of the transmitter chip in their brain<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Hivedrones begin at character creation with the Telepathy Merit for free and can use it without cost. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, they can form an empathic link with others, combining their Mental Attributes for the rest of the scene. They are capable of forming this link with one person equal to half their Wyrd rounded up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like your concept here, Nyrufa. I agree with Deionscribe that the blessing could use a little polishing, though. The combination of Mental Attributes could rapidly lead to quite massive dice pools for those with high Wyrd and/or Potent Kith. With your permission, I would try something a little different with the blessing.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Their Durances left the hivedrones with a natural talent for the thought processes of other beings. By rolling their Wits + Intelligence + Wyrd, a hivedrone can detect the presence of any thinking being within Wyrd*10 yards, provided that the being is not hidden by supernatural means. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, a hivedrone may create an telepathic link with one of its allies within visual range for the duration of the scene. Additional Glamour may be spent to add other allies to this mental network, up to a limit equal to the hivedrone's Wyrd. While linked into this network, the group may all communicate with each other silently, and none of them shall suffer untrained penalties to Mental Skill rolls, provided at least one member of the network has a dot in the Skill. The characters may also engage in teamwork actions for tasks involving Mental Skills. A character who travels more than a kilometer away from the hivedrone is automatically severed from the mental network.<br /> <br /> That's just my first thought for it. If you can use any of that, feel free to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T22:48:08-07:00","id":870959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870595#post870595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Made that tiny revision to the post.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Any suggestions for alternative names? I'm not sure if Psion is apt, and I'm coming up dry on other choices. Also, what kind of dice pool would be good to use?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Briarborn? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As for the dice pool, perhaps half Wyrd, rounded up? For names, perhaps something like brainblade, mindscythe, or thoughtripper, If I think of something better, I'll let you know.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T22:57:23-07:00","id":870966,"title":"","content":"Here's my own wording of it.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Hivedrone's durance left them with a natural talent for the thought processes of other beings. By rolling their Wits + Intelligence, a Hivedrone can detect the presence of any thinking being within ten yards per dot of Wyrd, provided that the being is not hidden by supernatural means. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, they may create a telepathic link with one of their allies within visual range for the duration of the scene. Additional Glamour may be spent to add other allies to this mental network, up to a limit equal to the Hivedrone's Wyrd. While linked into this network, the group may all communicate with each other silently, and none of them shall suffer untrained penalties to Mental Skill rolls, provided at least one member of the network has a dot in the Skill. The characters may also engage in teamwork actions for tasks involving Mental Skills. A character who travels more than Wyrd x 10 yards from the Hivedrone is automatically severed from the link.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-22-2016, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T23:01:30-07:00","id":870969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870959#post870959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the dice pool, perhaps half Wyrd, rounded up? For names, perhaps something like brainblade, mindscythe, or thoughtripper, If I think of something better, I'll let you know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure there are better names. These ones sound clunky or lacking. But yeah, that dice pool might work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T23:37:20-07:00","id":870994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=870966#post870966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's my own wording of it.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Hivedrone's durance left them with a natural talent for the thought processes of other beings. By rolling their Wits + Intelligence, a Hivedrone can detect the presence of any thinking being within ten yards per dot of Wyrd, provided that the being is not hidden by supernatural means. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, they may create a telepathic link with one of their allies within visual range for the duration of the scene. Additional Glamour may be spent to add other allies to this mental network, up to a limit equal to the Hivedrone's Wyrd. While linked into this network, the group may all communicate with each other silently, and none of them shall suffer untrained penalties to Mental Skill rolls, provided at least one member of the network has a dot in the Skill. The characters may also engage in teamwork actions for tasks involving Mental Skills. A character who travels more than Wyrd x 10 yards from the Hivedrone is automatically severed from the link.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'll go with this version, since I don't know how far a kilometer is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also the increase in distance scaling up with their power.<br /> <br /> So going to copy - paste it once I'm done posting this reply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-22-2016, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T00:37:38-07:00","id":871023,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's the briarborn. Their blessing may still require some tinkering. I'm trying to keep the flavor of the kith being sharp and pointy without making them overpowered.<br /> <br /> <b>Briarborn</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Don't get too close. I don't want to hurt you, but I will.</span><br /> <br /> Before their abductions, the people who would become briarborn tended to keep other people at a safe distance. The Gentry honed these people to a razor's edge and used them as living barriers and obstacles to corral their other servants. Given their intended role, it was often simple for them to abandon their post and slip into the Hedge. Even after escaping, though, the briarborn tend to lead lonely existences bereft of physical intimacy.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> They appear as animals that are covered in protective quills or spines, such as porcupines, hedgehogs, or sea urchins.<br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Razor sharp splinters of bloody broken bone jut out of her grayish skin at odd angles.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> She has beautiful fragrant roses in her hair, but her woody green skin is protected by myriad barbed thorns.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> Ink flows down the sharp black quills covering his body, forming bizarre pictographs upon his skin. <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> His form is drawn and ragged, with metal spikes embedded in his skin and barbed wire coiled around his limbs.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> All briarborn are covered in sharp thorns, spikes, or quills of one sort or another. Any unprotected physical contact with the briarborn more forceful than a gentle touch inflicts 1 Lethal damage on the individual. Especially forceful contact, such as that caused by unarmed attacks, inflicts half the briarborn's Wyrd in Lethal damage, rounded up. This damage increases to an amount equal to the briarborn's Wyrd when large areas of the briarborn's body are contacted, such as during grappling attempts or passionate embraces. Armor protects against this damage as it normally does. The briarborn can withdraw the quills into her body, but this is a painful process. By spending a point of Glamour and suffering a point of Bashing damage, the briarborn's blessing is rendered inactive for the remainder of the scene. Unsheathing the quills again before the end of the scene costs another point of Glamour and inflicts a level of Lethal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T00:46:12-07:00","id":871030,"title":"","content":"Well, this is certainly a kith that really makes the need for personal space go &quot;straight to the point&quot;. And I especially like the Grimm description out of all the Seemings.<br /> <br /> If you don't mind, I'd like to trim the Blessing's word count a bit.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> All Briarborn are covered in sharp thorns, spikes, or quills of one sort or another. Any unprotected physical contact with the briarborn more forceful than a gentle touch inflicts 1 Lethal damage on the individual. Especially forceful contact, such as that caused by unarmed attacks, inflicts half the Briarborn's Wyrd in Lethal damage, rounded up. This damage is doubled when large areas of the Briarborn's body are contacted, such as during grappling attempts or passionate embraces. Armor protects against this damage as it normally does. The Briarborn can withdraw the quills into her body, but this is a painful process. By spending a point of Glamour and suffering a point of Bashing damage, the blessing is rendered inactive for the remainder of the scene. Unsheathing the quills again before the end of the scene costs another point of Glamour and inflicts a level of Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> What if the ability to retract or reactivate the blessing can be done w/ a Glamour <i>or</i> wound cost?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T01:09:17-07:00","id":871040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=871030#post871030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this is certainly a kith that really makes the need for personal space go &quot;straight to the point&quot;. And I especially like the Grimm description out of all the Seemings.<br /> <br /> If you don't mind, I'd like to trim the Blessing's word count a bit.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> All Briarborn are covered in sharp thorns, spikes, or quills of one sort or another. Any unprotected physical contact with the briarborn more forceful than a gentle touch inflicts 1 Lethal damage on the individual. Especially forceful contact, such as that caused by unarmed attacks, inflicts half the Briarborn's Wyrd in Lethal damage, rounded up. This damage is doubled when large areas of the Briarborn's body are contacted, such as during grappling attempts or passionate embraces. Armor protects against this damage as it normally does. The Briarborn can withdraw the quills into her body, but this is a painful process. By spending a point of Glamour and suffering a point of Bashing damage, the blessing is rendered inactive for the remainder of the scene. Unsheathing the quills again before the end of the scene costs another point of Glamour and inflicts a level of Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> What if the ability to retract or reactivate the blessing can be done w/ a Glamour <i>or</i> wound cost?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like how you've trimmed it. It doesn't lose any of the meaning, but it sounds less awkward than my original wording did. Thank you for that.<br /> <br /> The reason I chose to have both a wound and a Glamour cost was to make it so that deactivating their blessing is costly enough to make the briarborn think twice before doing so, reinforcing the distance that the briarborn is forced to maintain in order to keep her loved ones safe from her. I'll need to give it a little thought to decide whether your suggested modification would still keep the same feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T01:55:46-07:00","id":871058,"title":"","content":"Looks like I got to the tangletail after all, even if it's still a little rough. Next up will probably be the venator (I <i>had</i> to do something with those Merits after Deionscribe said something).<br /> <br /> <b>Tangletail</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Don't worry, I can reach it. Why don't you go pick up supper, while I take care of this?</span><br /> <br /> Sometimes the Gentry have tasks that require more than just an extra set of hands. Tangletails were usually skilled at multitasking before their Durances, and the Gentry rewarded them with additional limbs to maximize their utility. Whether a tangletail had a long scaly tail, tentacles stretching from her wrists and shoulders, or long beautiful hair with a mind of its own, she was expected to perform to the highest level in whatever tasks she was assigned.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> They appear as animals with prehensile tails or tentacles, such as monkeys or squids.<br /> <b>Darkling:</b> His heavily wrinkled skin can stretch away from his skeletal frame, operating independently of the muscle and bone beneath it.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> Her eyes stare unblinkingly out of a tangled mass of lianas and moss, and two especially long vines stretch out from her shoulders.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Her shining golden hair is far too long to seem practical, but it is surprisingly strong.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Each tangletail is in possession of one or more prehensile appendages. These appendages can stretch to grapple a single target up to the tangletail's Wyrd in yards away. This distance can be extended further for the scene by spending a point of Glamour for each additional yard. The tangletail may maintain such a grapple as a reflexive action without sacrificing their action or Defense for the turn. The appendage is considered to have a functional Strength equal to half the tangletail's Strength + Wyrd, rounded down, and a functional Dexterity equal to her normal Dexterity. The appendage may also be used to grasp or manipulate objects at the same distance, although it can't manipulate anything that the tangletail would have difficulty wielding without opposable digits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T08:50:59-07:00","id":871298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=871058#post871058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like I got to the tangletail after all, even if it's still a little rough. Next up will probably be the venator (I <i>had</i> to do something with those Merits after Deionscribe said something).<br /> <br /> <b>Tangletail</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Don't worry, I can reach it. Why don't you go pick up supper, while I take care of this?</span><br /> <br /> Sometimes the Gentry have tasks that require more than just an extra set of hands. Tangletails were usually skilled at multitasking before their Durances, and the Gentry rewarded them with additional limbs to maximize their utility. Whether a tangletail had a long scaly tail, tentacles stretching from her wrists and shoulders, or long beautiful hair with a mind of its own, she was expected to perform to the highest level in whatever tasks she was assigned.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> They appear as animals with prehensile tails or tentacles, such as monkeys or squids.<br /> <b>Darkling:</b> His heavily wrinkled skin can stretch away from his skeletal frame, operating independently of the muscle and bone beneath it.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> Her eyes stare unblinkingly out of a tangled mass of lianas and moss, and two especially long vines stretch out from her shoulders.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Her shining golden hair is far too long to seem practical, but it is surprisingly strong.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Each tangletail is in possession of one or more prehensile appendages. These appendages can stretch to grapple a single target up to the tangletail's Wyrd in yards away. This distance can be extended further for the scene by spending a point of Glamour for each additional yard. The tangletail may maintain such a grapple as a reflexive action without sacrificing their action or Defense for the turn. The appendage is considered to have a functional Strength equal to half the tangletail's Strength + Wyrd, rounded down, and a functional Dexterity equal to her normal Dexterity. The appendage may also be used to grasp or manipulate objects at the same distance, although it can't manipulate anything that the tangletail would have difficulty wielding without opposable digits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume the Venators are the kith which use Fae Mount in their Blessing? Either way, nice choice of name.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Onto the Tangletail....<br /> I am liking this concept, too. But I have to ask if the quantity of extra limbs matters here. Does a tentacled octopus man's multiple tentacles get treated no differently from a monkey man's prehensile tail? This may need more brainstorming to iron out.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, a 1E NWoD setting called the Reach had a Merit or two which covered extra limbs, if I recall.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Here it is.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cost: \u2022\u2022 <br /> Prerequisite: Wyrd 5 <br /> <br /> You have an added appendage or multiple appendages over which you have conscious control. This could be a tail, or vines, or shadowy extrusions or any other reasonable thing. The appendage(s) are Str 1, and is nimble enough to open doors and handle objects of reasonable weight. This appendage cannot be used in combat. If you have multiple appendages, like a group of vines, you can only use one of them at a time. The appendage cannot be made stronger with Strength-Boosting Contracts. The appendage is Masked. Non-Changelings cannot see it, and they will rationalize away any oddities caused by it. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-22-2016, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T09:29:29-07:00","id":871357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=871298#post871298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume the Venators are the kith which use Fae Mount in their Blessing? Either way, nice choice of name.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Onto the Tangletail....<br /> I am liking this concept, too. But I have to ask if the quantity of extra limbs matters here. Does a tentacled octopus man's multiple tentacles get treated no differently from a monkey man's prehensile tail? This may need more brainstorming to iron out.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, a 1E NWoD setting called the Reach had a Merit or two which covered extra limbs, if I recall.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Here it is.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, the venatores have a blessing related to the Fae Mount and Hedgebeast Companion Merits. The kith is coming along nicely. If I didn't have to go to work, it would be going up soon. Since I do, it may be awhile yet.<br /> <br /> As for the tangletail, the number of limbs don't really matter. Mechanically they would function the same, even if the description was different. Trying to make each limb able to do its own thing for a tangletail that had more than one would be a mechanical nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T09:34:47-07:00","id":871368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=871357#post871357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, the venatores have a blessing related to the Fae Mount and Hedgebeast Companion Merits. The kith is coming along nicely. If I didn't have to go to work, it would be going up soon. Since I do, it may be awhile yet.<br /> <br /> As for the tangletail, the number of limbs don't really matter. Mechanically they would function the same, even if the description was different. Trying to make each limb able to do its own thing for a tangletail that had more than one would be a mechanical nightmare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two in one? Interesting.<br /> <br /> And yeah, that <i>would</i> be a mechanical nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T02:29:29-07:00","id":872232,"title":"","content":"Here it is:<br /> <br /> <b>Venator</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Shut up! Don't you hear that howl? That's a briarwolf, and they don't travel alone.</span><br /> <br /> The Hedge is a place of great peril as well as wonder, and the odd creatures called hobgoblins are among the greatest dangers a changeling might face, outside of the Gentry and the Huntsmen themselves. Whether he faced them in arenas surrounded by scores of gaping Fae spectators or patrolled the Hedge borders to rid his Keeper's lands of dangerous pests, it was the venator's task to tame or slay these bizarre beasts. An escaped venator often becomes a valued Hedge guide or guardian for the freehold that earns his loyalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A bronze helmet encrusted with verdigris sits atop her body made of thick studded leather.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> The pale scars covering the sun-tanned skin of his muscular body recounts his past victories and the legends of the creatures that he's slain.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> The skull of a great beast sits upon his head, his own tusks barely visible beneath it.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> His oddly formed body has been enhanced with the bones of his previous conquests, with furs stitched over his skin.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Venatores are skilled at the hunting, slaying, and taming of the wild hobgoblins of the Hedge. Every venator gains the Interdisciplinary Specialty (Bestial Hobgoblins) Merit at no cost. By taking a turn to study a hobgoblin in combat, the venator may spend a point of Glamour to add bonus dice equal to his Wyrd to his next attack against the beast. Additionally, if the venator successfully renders a hobgoblin completely helpless without killing it, he may spend a point of Glamour to make the hobgoblin into a temporary Fae Mount or Hedgebeast Companion as per the Merits for a number of days equal to his Wyrd. This can be extended by spending an additional point of Glamour on this blessing for each additional day that he wishes to maintain the bond. If the hobgoblin would fit within the natural limits of one of the two Merits, the venator may spend the necessary Experiences to make the Merit permanent. A venator may only have a number of hobgoblins bonded to him through this blessing equal to the lower of his Presence or Wyrd, although permanent instances of the Merits do not count against this total. No aspect of this blessing functions against the more humanoid hobs of the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T06:38:25-07:00","id":872321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=872232#post872232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here it is:<br /> <br /> <b>Venator</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Shut up! Don't you hear that howl? That's a briarwolf, and they don't travel alone.</span><br /> <br /> The Hedge is a place of great peril as well as wonder, and the odd creatures called hobgoblins are among the greatest dangers a changeling might face, outside of the Gentry and the Huntsmen themselves. Whether he faced them in arenas surrounded by scores of gaping Fae spectators or patrolled the Hedge borders to rid his Keeper's lands of dangerous pests, it was the venator's task to tame or slay these bizarre beasts. An escaped venator often becomes a valued Hedge guide or guardian for the freehold that earns his loyalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A bronze helmet encrusted with verdigris sits atop her body made of thick studded leather.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> The pale scars covering the sun-tanned skin of his muscular body recounts his past victories and the legends of the creatures that he's slain.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> The skull of a great beast sits upon his head, his own tusks barely visible beneath it.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> His oddly formed body has been enhanced with the bones of his previous conquests, with furs stitched over his skin.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Venatores are skilled at the hunting, slaying, and taming of the wild hobgoblins of the Hedge. Every venator gains the Interdisciplinary Specialty (Bestial Hobgoblins) Merit at no cost. By taking a turn to study a hobgoblin in combat, the venator may spend a point of Glamour to add bonus dice equal to his Wyrd to his next attack against the beast. Additionally, if the venator successfully renders a hobgoblin completely helpless without killing it, he may spend a point of Glamour to make the hobgoblin into a temporary Fae Mount or Hedgebeast Companion as per the Merits for a number of days equal to his Wyrd. This can be extended by spending an additional point of Glamour on this blessing for each additional day that he wishes to maintain the bond. If the hobgoblin would fit within the natural limits of one of the two Merits, the venator may spend the necessary Experiences to make the Merit permanent. A venator may only have a number of hobgoblins bonded to him through this blessing equal to the lower of his Presence or Wyrd, although permanent instances of the Merits do not count against this total. No aspect of this blessing functions against the more humanoid hobs of the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>This looks pretty good, though the blessing seems poorly put-together for me. Maybe even a bit too powerful if you count in the Glamour expenditure for an attack bonus. How about something like this instead?<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Venator is skilled at hunting, slaying, and taming the wild beasts of the Hedge. He receives automatic successes equal to half his Wyrd (rounded up) on any Investigation, Survival, or Animal Ken rolls related to Hedgebeasts. If he has rendered one helpless without killing it, he may spend Glamour to make it into a temporary Fae Mount or Hedgebeast Companion as per the Merits for a number of days equal to the points spent. The Venator may be bonded to a number of such creatures equal to the lower of his Presence or Wyrd, though any mounts or companions made permanent with Experience do not count to this limit. This ability does not apply to more intelligent Hobgoblins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-23-2016, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T07:19:03-07:00","id":872343,"title":"","content":"<b>Grendel</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;This is the last time I'm going to ask you to keep it down. You don't want to see what happens when I stop using the broomstick to knock.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Some Keepers like to enjoy peace and quiet in their realms; absolutely, unbroken silence to the point where even footsteps are muted. To ensure the continuation of this silence, they created the Grendel, tortured Changelings who's sense of hearing was so powerful that they could hear a conversation from miles away. If the Grendel detected any noise, it would descend upon the offenders in a murderous rage. Unable to bare the cacophony of rebellion, the Grendel deafened itself just long enough to flee into the Hedge and make their escape.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> a hideously deformed giant who appears to have ripped off its own ears in a fit of agony.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> vaguely resembling a pair of horns, a set of brass trumpets have been permanently lodged in their ear canals.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> An animal who uses sensitive hearing to make up for it's impaired vision<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> While in Arcadia, the Grendel's sense of hearing was so powerful, it was detrimental to their health. Even in its damaged state, the Grendel can still hear far better than most other people. The Grendel is immune to all penalties on sound based Perception rolls As long as they are within earshot, they can listen to it with perfect clarity, ignoring such things like mufflers, frequency, background noise and distance traveled. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, they can multiply their range of hearing by a number of times equal to their Wyrd for the rest of the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-23-2016, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T10:50:39-07:00","id":872501,"title":"","content":"Finally moved the section on Homebrew Kiths into a Google Doc of its own. If there are some kiths still missing, it's likely because they may still need more critiquing before it's to be added.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, made some revisions to the Enchanter and Timekeeper Kiths. And added some flavor texts for those that needed them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T01:33:39-07:00","id":872964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=872321#post872321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This looks pretty good, though the blessing seems poorly put-together for me. Maybe even a bit too powerful if you count in the Glamour expenditure for an attack bonus. How about something like this instead?<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Venator is skilled at hunting, slaying, and taming the wild beasts of the Hedge. He receives automatic successes equal to half his Wyrd (rounded up) on any Investigation, Survival, or Animal Ken rolls related to Hedgebeasts. If he has rendered one helpless without killing it, he may spend Glamour to make it into a temporary Fae Mount or Hedgebeast Companion as per the Merits for a number of days equal to the points spent. The Venator may be bonded to a number of such creatures equal to the lower of his Presence or Wyrd, though any mounts or companions made permanent with Experience do not count to this limit. This ability does not apply to more intelligent Hobgoblins.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make a good point. The attack bonus was a little high, even if it could only be used on a certain type of opponent. I like your idea of giving them a higher bonus specific to those Skills rather than the small bonus to all of them, also. I changed it to bonus dice rather than successes, though, as I'd like them to still have a chance at failure. I did want to give them something that would benefit them in combat against the Hedgebeasts, though, so I gave them the ability to reduce Defense rather than just giving them a bunch of bonus dice. What do you think of this version?<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Venatores are skilled at the hunting, slaying, and taming of the wild hobgoblins of the Hedge. The venator receives bonus dice equal to half his Wyrd, rounded up, on all Animal Ken, Investigation, and Survival rolls related to bestial hobgoblins. Taking a turn to study a hobgoblin in combat and spending a point of Glamour allows the venator to ignore the beast's Defense, up to an amount equal to half the venator's Wyrd, rounded up. Additionally, if the venator successfully renders a hobgoblin completely helpless without killing it, he may spend a point of Glamour to make the hobgoblin into a temporary Fae Mount or Hedgebeast Companion as per the Merits for a number of days equal to his Wyrd. This can be extended by spending an additional point of Glamour on this blessing for each additional day that he wishes to maintain the bond. A venator may only have a number of hobgoblins bonded to him through this blessing equal to the lower of his Presence or Wyrd, although permanent instances of the Merits do not count against this total. No aspect of this blessing functions against the more humanoid hobs of the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T02:13:42-07:00","id":872967,"title":"","content":"I also got around to revising the honeysoul, finally. Let me know what you think.<br /> <br /> <b>Honeysoul</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Look, I'm no happier about this than you are, but you're wounded, and if we're going to have any chance of getting out of here alive, you're going to need to get over it and start eating.</span><br /> <br /> Some Keepers fancy themselves to be gourmets, partaking of exotic fare and hosting great banquets featuring esoteric recipes. It was the sad lot of the honeysouls to provide the substance for these bizarre repasts. Each night, the honeysoul was devoured by her Keeper or his favored guests and servants, and each morning she was born anew from her bones. Even when a honeysoul has escaped this vicious cycle, it is not uncommon to see her weep in sympathy over her own meals.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> She is a timid rabbit girl, with a bite taken out of one long chocolate ear.<br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Green and red gummy flesh mingle together, covering a visible skeleton of hard black bones.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> His features are lovingly detailed with icing upon his gingerbread flesh.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Her skin is the color of honey, and it is slightly sticky to the touch and sweet to the taste.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> He is a great boar-like creature with slightly burned yet succulent flesh, a tantalizing aroma filling the air around him. <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Each night when the honeysoul sleeps, she heals all bashing and lethal damage she has suffered, or downgrades a single level of aggravated damage to lethal. Additionally, her flesh and blood is mystically potent and especially nourishing. A honeysoul will never suffer any negative effects due to starvation. Other beings may also benefit from her nourishing flesh by devouring it, regaining a point of Willpower, a point of Glamour, or recovering a single level of bashing or lethal damage for each point of lethal damage inflicted upon the honeysoul. This blessing can only be used a number of times per day equal to the honeysoul's Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T03:51:31-07:00","id":873005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=872964#post872964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You make a good point. The attack bonus was a little high, even if it could only be used on a certain type of opponent. I like your idea of giving them a higher bonus specific to those Skills rather than the small bonus to all of them, also. I changed it to bonus dice rather than successes, though, as I'd like them to still have a chance at failure. I did want to give them something that would benefit them in combat against the Hedgebeasts, though, so I gave them the ability to reduce Defense rather than just giving them a bunch of bonus dice. What do you think of this version?<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Venatores are skilled at the hunting, slaying, and taming of the wild hobgoblins of the Hedge. The venator receives bonus dice equal to half his Wyrd, rounded up, on all Animal Ken, Investigation, and Survival rolls related to bestial hobgoblins. Taking a turn to study a hobgoblin in combat and spending a point of Glamour allows the venator to ignore the beast's Defense, up to an amount equal to half the venator's Wyrd, rounded up. Additionally, if the venator successfully renders a hobgoblin completely helpless without killing it, he may spend a point of Glamour to make the hobgoblin into a temporary Fae Mount or Hedgebeast Companion as per the Merits for a number of days equal to his Wyrd. This can be extended by spending an additional point of Glamour on this blessing for each additional day that he wishes to maintain the bond. A venator may only have a number of hobgoblins bonded to him through this blessing equal to the lower of his Presence or Wyrd, although permanent instances of the Merits do not count against this total. No aspect of this blessing functions against the more humanoid hobs of the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Apart from some grammatical errors and polishing the mechanics at some points, this is actually much better.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For the Honeysoul, I was thinking of bringing back the Quick Healer Merit and tweak it for 2E to use in place of healing most injuries in an instant with a good night's sleep. Other than that, though, I think their blessing needs little revising. I may have an alternative take on the &quot;eat me&quot; part of it, though.<br /> <br /> P.S: I think you meant gourmand instead of gourmet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-24-2016, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T03:52:17-07:00","id":873006,"title":"","content":"Here's a new one from me. Seeming descriptions are appreciated. As is critique for the kith, in general.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Windwalker</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;I'm a leaf on the wind. Watch me soar&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> Vassals to Lords and Ladies of Arcadia's skies, the Windwalkers were tasked with directing the wind for various tasks. These could be benign like the sculpting of cloud gardens and dispersal of storms. But if given the order, a Windwalker could sweep away armies with a hurricane.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Windwalkers apply the higher of their Wits or Dexterity for Defense, and benefit from the rote quality on all Initiative rolls. They can also spend Glamour or Willpower to use the three-dot version of Psychokinesis to manipulate wind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T08:04:58-07:00","id":873091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=873006#post873006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a new one from me. Seeming descriptions are appreciated. As is critique for the kith, in general.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Windwalker</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;I'm a leaf on the wind. Watch me soar&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> Vassals to Lords and Ladies of Arcadia's skies, the Windwalkers were tasked with directing the wind for various tasks. These could be benign like the sculpting of cloud gardens and dispersal of storms. But if given the order, a Windwalker could sweep away armies with a hurricane.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Windwalkers apply the higher of their Wits or Dexterity for Defense, and benefit from the rote quality on all Initiative rolls. They can also spend Glamour or Willpower to use the three-dot version of Psychokinesis to manipulate wind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, I was trying to come up with a wind walker idea but couldn't think of a good Blessing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though my ideas was going to be more about people who danced through the air. One of the Seemings was going to involve a hanged man. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T08:09:35-07:00","id":873093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=873091#post873091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Ah, I was trying to come up with a wind walker idea but couldn't think of a good Blessing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though my ideas was going to be more about people who danced through the air. One of the Seemings was going to involve a hanged man. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure your ideas might not be mutually exclusive with mine. Still, how does the blessing stand? And you got any Seeming descriptions worked out? Especially the one involving the Hanged Man?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T08:33:07-07:00","id":873102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=873005#post873005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. Apart from some grammatical errors and polishing the mechanics at some points, this is actually much better.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For the Honeysoul, I was thinking of bringing back the Quick Healer Merit and tweak it for 2E to use in place of healing most injuries in an instant with a good night's sleep. Other than that, though, I think their blessing needs little revising. I may have an alternative take on the &quot;eat me&quot; part of it, though.<br /> <br /> P.S: I think you meant gourmand instead of gourmet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not surprised that there may be a few grammar errors and some roughness to it, given how late I was working on it. I'll need to look it again when I've got a bit more time and I'm less tired.<br /> <br /> I'm curious to hear your ideas. Ultimately, I will most likely continue to give them the full heal, although I might make it so that it is all bashing and a number of lethal equal to their Wyrd. I liked the imagery of the ever-renewing creature devoured and reborn from her bones, so I'm not likely to reduce the amount healed by too much.<br /> <br /> No, I meant gourmet. I was going for the &quot;connoisseur of fine delicacies&quot; angle, rather than &quot;gluttonous beast&quot;. That doesn't mean that gourmands wouldn't have also made themselves a brunch of honeysouls to sate their endless hungers. Also, the collective noun for a group of honeysouls is hereby called a &quot;brunch&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T08:33:39-07:00","id":873103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=873093#post873093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure your ideas might not be mutually exclusive with mine. Still, how does the blessing stand? And you got any Seeming descriptions worked out? Especially the one involving the Hanged Man?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The blessing looks appropriate to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> a disheveled figure wearing a black, featureless cowl and a frayed noose around their neck. They were forcibly taught how to dance in the wind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A body comprised of dense, black clouds with sparking eyes and the strength of a storm coursing through their limbs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A graceful, pointy eared sylph who's clothing is fashioned out of thin cloud vapor that never seems to disperse unless she wants it to.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T09:03:33-07:00","id":873121,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> <br /> I am wondering if it's possible to just axe the Defense-lowering aspect of the Venator Blessing, seeing as it could be something that could be better covered with Contracts and Merits (like Killer Instinct and its advanced version for the latter, found in p. 117 of Beast: The Primordial). Furthermore, I imagine that a Venator's methods for handling Hedgebeast would be shaped more by the nature of his Durance instead of an innate quirk to his Kith. One guy could be a skilled ambusher and trapper, while another would exploit openings and weaknesses in a direct confrontation.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, here's a slight revision to the Blessing if we go down this line of thought.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Venator is skilled at hunting, slaying, and taming wild hobgoblins of the Hedge. He receives bonus dice equal to half his Wyrd, rounded up, on all Animal Ken, Investigation, and Survival rolls related to bestial hobgoblins. If the Venator successfully renders one completely helpless without killing it, he may spend a point of Glamour to make it into a temporary Fae Mount or Hedgebeast Companion as per the Merits for a number of days equal to his Wyrd. This can be extended by spending additional points of Glamour for each additional day that he wishes to maintain the bond. The Venator may only have a number of hobgoblins bonded to him this way equal to the lower of his Presence or Wyrd, though permanent instances of the Merits do not count against this total. He also cannot apply this Blessing to the more humanoid hobs.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Noted, as well, on your current thoughts for the Honeysoul. Hehe... Brunch. Great, now I'm getting hungry and it's <i>midnight</i> here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=873103#post873103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The blessing looks appropriate to me.<br /> <br /> Well...<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> a disheveled figure wearing a black, featureless cowl and a frayed noose around their neck. They were forcibly taught how to dance in the wind.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A body comprised of dense, black clouds with sparking eyes and the strength of a storm coursing through their limbs.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A graceful, pointy eared sylph who's clothing is fashioned out of thin cloud vapor that never seems to disperse unless she wants it to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I think these can work well with my write-up. I hope you don't mind if I use these.<br /> <br /> Now. About the Grendel. It seems to overlap a bit too much with the Cleareyes and Whisperwisp kiths of Changeling 2E. But then again, their blessing is entirely oriented towards hearing, as opposed to the former's heightened senses and the latter's emphasis on eavesdropping and remembering what he overheard with perfect clarity. So, I think this can work, provided that some proofreading is done on the mechanics.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me. I have to revisit what I got on the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=844973#post844973\">Logician</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=864821#post864821\">Watcher</a> kiths and see what revisions can be done. Any ideas for either or both are much appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T09:12:17-07:00","id":873126,"title":"","content":"Go ahead and use them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T09:28:27-07:00","id":873132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=873126#post873126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go ahead and use them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Oh, and I did a revision of the Logician Kith. Feel free to compare this with my previous write-up of them. <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Logician</u> </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">By Deionscribe</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>I have already gone through all possible courses of action. Believe me when I say that this is the best one.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some changelings were shaped to be the living beings of pure reason and thought. These Lost served as calculated advisors to their faerie master, while others were given tasks of great magnitude and order. Their heightened thought processes, however, led them to the solution to their plight, and thus made their escape possible. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>\u2022 </b></span><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Beast:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> An animal well-known for its intellect, like a dolphin or an octopus.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Darkling:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A cold-hearted demon whose pupiless eyes gleam with inhuman intellect. </span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Elemental:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shifting fractals of light that cluster together in the shape of a man. </span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wizened:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A human computer, with circuit lines and fiber wires running throughout his body, and a crystalline processor for a brain. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing:</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A Logician gains a dot of Intelligence, which can take him above the usual limitations imposed by his Wyrd. He also does not suffer any penalties to any rolls which use that Attribute, and he may spend a point of Glamour to halve their target number of successes if they are performed as Extended Actions.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T10:28:33-07:00","id":873168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=872967#post872967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also got around to revising the honeysoul, finally. Let me know what you think.<br /> <br /> <b>Honeysoul</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Look, I'm no happier about this than you are, but you're wounded, and if we're going to have any chance of getting out of here alive, you're going to need to get over it and start eating.</span><br /> <br /> Some Keepers fancy themselves to be gourmets, partaking of exotic fare and hosting great banquets featuring esoteric recipes. It was the sad lot of the honeysouls to provide the substance for these bizarre repasts. Each night, the honeysoul was devoured by her Keeper or his favored guests and servants, and each morning she was born anew from her bones. Even when a honeysoul has escaped this vicious cycle, it is not uncommon to see her weep in sympathy over her own meals.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> She is a timid rabbit girl, with a bite taken out of one long chocolate ear.<br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Green and red gummy flesh mingle together, covering a visible skeleton of hard black bones.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> His features are lovingly detailed with icing upon his gingerbread flesh.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Her skin is the color of honey, and it is slightly sticky to the touch and sweet to the taste.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> He is a great boar-like creature with slightly burned yet succulent flesh, a tantalizing aroma filling the air around him.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Each night when the honeysoul sleeps, she heals all bashing and lethal damage she has suffered, or downgrades a single level of aggravated damage to lethal. Additionally, her flesh and blood is mystically potent and especially nourishing. A honeysoul will never suffer any negative effects due to starvation. Other beings may also benefit from her nourishing flesh by devouring it, regaining a point of Willpower, a point of Glamour, or recovering a single level of bashing or lethal damage for each point of lethal damage inflicted upon the honeysoul. This blessing can only be used a number of times per day equal to the honeysoul's Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's an alternative take on the Blessing.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Honeysoul's flesh mends quickly, halving the healing time for all levels of damage. She also naturally heals bashing and lethal damage equal to half her Wyrd (rounded up), and never suffers any negative effects due to starvation. Furthermore, her flesh and blood is mystically potent and especially nourishing, and any being who devours it may regain a point of Willpower or Glamour, or recover a single level of bashing or lethal damage for each point of lethal damage inflicted upon the Honeysoul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T07:59:43-07:00","id":873758,"title":"","content":"Incomplete write-up based on GibberingEloquence's musings on &quot;Number-Watchers&quot;.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Numberwright</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Numberwrights gain the Trivial Reworking Contract, and benefit from the rote quality when invoking it. If they spend Glamour while performing an Extended action that takes an hour or less to do, he may make rolls every turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T10:10:18-07:00","id":873847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=873121#post873121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a><br /> I am wondering if it's possible to just axe the Defense-lowering aspect of the Venator Blessing, seeing as it could be something that could be better covered with Contracts and Merits (like Killer Instinct and its advanced version for the latter, found in p. 117 of Beast: The Primordial). Furthermore, I imagine that a Venator's methods for handling Hedgebeast would be shaped more by the nature of his Durance instead of an innate quirk to his Kith. One guy could be a skilled ambusher and trapper, while another would exploit openings and weaknesses in a direct confrontation.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, here's a slight revision to the Blessing if we go down this line of thought.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Venator is skilled at hunting, slaying, and taming wild hobgoblins of the Hedge. He receives bonus dice equal to half his Wyrd, rounded up, on all Animal Ken, Investigation, and Survival rolls related to bestial hobgoblins. If the Venator successfully renders one completely helpless without killing it, he may spend a point of Glamour to make it into a temporary Fae Mount or Hedgebeast Companion as per the Merits for a number of days equal to his Wyrd. This can be extended by spending additional points of Glamour for each additional day that he wishes to maintain the bond. The Venator may only have a number of hobgoblins bonded to him this way equal to the lower of his Presence or Wyrd, though permanent instances of the Merits do not count against this total. He also cannot apply this Blessing to the more humanoid hobs.</div> </div> </div> </div>The venatores traditionally hunted and killed animals in an arena for spectators, as well as performing tricks with trained ones. I feel that they should have some benefit in combat against them as part of their kith blessing to reflect that, rather than making them just trackers and tamers and saying that any ability to actually deal with them violently stems from the rest of the character's build. It always drove me nuts in first edition that some kiths seemed to need additional points to be spent in order to make them do something they should have had a talent for, such as needing to take Contracts of Elements (Fire) if you wanted a fire elemental to be able to start fires. I think, perhaps, I've been going through too much trouble with it, though. There's an easier way to make them good at all of them. What about this:<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A venator is skilled at hunting, slaying, and taming the wild hobgoblins of the Hedge. The venator gains the Interdisciplinary Specialty (Bestial Hobgoblins) Merit for free, and the venator gains an exceptional success on three successes rather than five on any roll that benefits from it. Additionally, if the venator successfully renders one completely helpless without killing it, he may spend a point of Glamour to make it into a temporary Fae Mount or Hedgebeast Companion as per the Merits for a number of days equal to his Wyrd. This can be extended by spending additional points of Glamour for each additional day that he wishes to maintain the bond. The venator may only have a number of hobgoblins bonded to him in this way equal to the lower of his Presence or Wyrd, although permanent instances of the Merits do not count against this total. He also cannot apply this blessing to the more humanoid hobs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T10:18:33-07:00","id":873852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=873758#post873758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incomplete write-up based on GibberingEloquence's musings on &quot;Number-Watchers&quot;.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Numberwright</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Numberwrights gain the Trivial Reworking Contract, and benefit from the rote quality when invoking it. If they spend Glamour while performing an Extended action that takes an hour or less to do, he may make rolls every turn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not certain how Trivial Reworking relates to the ability to crunch numbers. Perhaps part of their blessing could be Interdisciplinary Specialty (Mathematics) and the ability to instantly count everything within their line of sight, whether it is the coins in a dragon's hoard or the soldiers in an enemy army? Have you considered something like actuary or auditor for the kith name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":". 04-25-2016, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T10:42:31-07:00","id":873867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=873168#post873168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's an alternative take on the Blessing.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Honeysoul's flesh mends quickly, halving the healing time for all levels of damage. She also naturally heals bashing and lethal damage equal to half her Wyrd (rounded up), and never suffers any negative effects due to starvation. Furthermore, her flesh and blood is mystically potent and especially nourishing, and any being who devours it may regain a point of Willpower or Glamour, or recover a single level of bashing or lethal damage for each point of lethal damage inflicted upon the Honeysoul.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had not thought that their healing capability was too potent, given the ease of healing other splats receive and the easy availability of magical healing available to changelings, but I'll tweak it a bit. It makes it so that even at Wyrd 1, they still heal twice as quickly as a normal person, but they can still reach truly impressive levels of healing eventually. I also gave them an ability to benefit more from the magical healing, since they'd be relying upon it a bit more to use the other half of their blessing. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Each night when the honeysoul sleeps, she heals all bashing damage and lethal damage equal to half her Wyrd, rounded up, or she may downgrade a single level of aggravated damage to lethal. If her rest is disturbed to the point where she would not regain Willpower, this magical healing will not function for the night. Her vitality also doubles the benefits of any magical healing she receives, such as that received from devouring goblin fruits. Additionally, her flesh and blood is mystically potent and especially nourishing. A honeysoul will never suffer any negative effects due to starvation. Other beings may also benefit from her nourishing flesh by devouring it, regaining a point of Willpower, a point of Glamour, or recovering a single level of bashing or lethal damage for each point of lethal damage inflicted upon the honeysoul. This blessing can only be used a number of times per day equal to the honeysoul's Wyrd.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T01:33:09-07:00","id":874342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=873847#post873847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The venatores traditionally hunted and killed animals in an arena for spectators, as well as performing tricks with trained ones. I feel that they should have some benefit in combat against them as part of their kith blessing to reflect that, rather than making them just trackers and tamers and saying that any ability to actually deal with them violently stems from the rest of the character's build. It always drove me nuts in first edition that some kiths seemed to need additional points to be spent in order to make them do something they should have had a talent for, such as needing to take Contracts of Elements (Fire) if you wanted a fire elemental to be able to start fires. I think, perhaps, I've been going through too much trouble with it, though. There's an easier way to make them good at all of them. What about this:<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A venator is skilled at hunting, slaying, and taming the wild hobgoblins of the Hedge. The venator gains the Interdisciplinary Specialty (Bestial Hobgoblins) Merit for free, and the venator gains an exceptional success on three successes rather than five on any roll that benefits from it. Additionally, if the venator successfully renders one completely helpless without killing it, he may spend a point of Glamour to make it into a temporary Fae Mount or Hedgebeast Companion as per the Merits for a number of days equal to his Wyrd. This can be extended by spending additional points of Glamour for each additional day that he wishes to maintain the bond. The venator may only have a number of hobgoblins bonded to him in this way equal to the lower of his Presence or Wyrd, although permanent instances of the Merits do not count against this total. He also cannot apply this blessing to the more humanoid hobs.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing left, now, is deciding which Skill actually <i>has</i> that Specialty. Should it be in Occult? Investigation? Animal Ken? But other than that, this looks simpler and better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-26-2016, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T02:08:41-07:00","id":874359,"title":"","content":"Update to the Windwalker kith.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Windwalker</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;I'm a leaf on the wind. Watch me soar&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> Vassals to Lords and Ladies of Arcadia's skies, the Windwalkers were tasked with directing the wind for various tasks. These could be benign like the sculpting clouds and dispersing storms, or as destructive as sweeping away armies with a hurricane. However, a Windwalker's affinity for the winds can quicken him to action once an opportunity for escape is found.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling:</b> A disheveled figure wearing a black, featureless cowl and a frayed noose around his neck, who was forcibly taught how to dance in the wind.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> Formed of thick clouds and mist that darken and lighten according to its mood, this being is a blur of motion with the winds at its beck and call.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> Lithe and graceful, this sylph's clothing is fashioned out of thin cloud vapor that never seems to disperse unless she wants it to. <br /> \u2022 <b>Ogre:</b> A body comprised of dense, black clouds with sparking eyes and the strength of a storm coursing through their limbs.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Windwalkers use the higher of Wits or Dexterity for Defense, and may spend Glamour to apply it against Firearms attacks on a 1-to-1 ratio. They also gain the rote quality on all Initiative rolls, and take no physical penalties from the Heavy Winds Tilt and similar effects. If they spend Glamour or Willpower, they can use the three-dot version of Psychokinesis (Air).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-26-2016, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T07:20:06-07:00","id":874516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=874342#post874342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only thing left, now, is deciding which Skill actually <i>has</i> that Specialty. Should it be in Occult? Investigation? Animal Ken? But other than that, this looks simpler and better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, I would leave that in the player's hands. The Interdisciplinary Specialty Merit seems to negate the need for a specific Skill to be linked to it in my eyes, given its effects. I'm glad that it's looking better, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:56:57-07:00","id":874684,"title":"","content":"<b>Stoutfellow</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Big things come in small packages&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> In Arcadia nothing is ever quite as it seems, as the True Fae have a love for creating mind bending illusions and distorting reality. Changelings who became Stoutfellow were compressed into a fraction of their former size, yet retained all of their physical ability. What resulted was a being who could compete with those several times their size. The Gentry were said to find great amusement in seeing their performance, until even they made the mistake of underestimating their creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> An armored carapace and twitching antennae reveal this Changeling's previous life as an insect.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> Nearly as broad as he is tall and with a beard hanging down to his stomach, this man resembles the dwarf of Norse mythology.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Scrawny and timid from years of public humiliation, they found a strength within themselves they never knew they had.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>When it comes to the Stoutfellow, size isn't everything. They automatically gain the Small-Framed merit at character creation without suffering the reduced health box for their smaller size. Additionally, the Stoutfellow may spend a point of Glamour to add half their Wyrd (rounded up) to their Strength for one action. They may continue to do this as many times in a scene as they have Glamour to spend.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>NOTE:</b> I can't think of a Glamour spending part to their blessing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-27-2016, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T13:22:27-07:00","id":874825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=874684#post874684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>NOTE:</b> I can't think of a Glamour spending part to their blessing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe you could replace the second half of the blessing with a bonus to a single strength-based roll proportionate to the amount of glamour you spend?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:38:57-07:00","id":874898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=873132#post873132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Oh, and I did a revision of the Logician Kith. Feel free to compare this with my previous write-up of them. <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Logician</u> </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">By Deionscribe</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>I have already gone through all possible courses of action. Believe me when I say that this is the best one.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some changelings were shaped to be the living beings of pure reason and thought. These Lost served as calculated advisors to their faerie master, while others were given tasks of great magnitude and order. Their heightened thought processes, however, led them to the solution to their plight, and thus made their escape possible. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>\u2022 </b></span><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Beast:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> An animal well-known for its intellect, like a dolphin or an octopus.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Darkling:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A cold-hearted demon whose pupiless eyes gleam with inhuman intellect. </span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Elemental:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shifting fractals of light that cluster together in the shape of a man. </span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wizened:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A human computer, with circuit lines and fiber wires running throughout his body, and a crystalline processor for a brain. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing:</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A Logician gains a dot of Intelligence, which can take him above the usual limitations imposed by his Wyrd. He also does not suffer any penalties to any rolls which use that Attribute, and he may spend a point of Glamour to halve their target number of successes if they are performed as Extended Actions.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that making them immune to Intelligence penalties might be a bit too potent, as that might give them an inherent immunity to some powers that might attack the mind. What about making them immune to the untrained penalty for Mental Skill rolls and giving them the ability to spend Glamour to gain the Encyclopedic Knowledge Merit for a Mental Skill for the scene? Also, have you considered something like Sage for an alternate name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T15:11:22-07:00","id":874929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=874898#post874898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that making them immune to Intelligence penalties might be a bit too potent, as that might give them an inherent immunity to some powers that might attack the mind. What about making them immune to the untrained penalty for Mental Skill rolls and giving them the ability to spend Glamour to gain the Encyclopedic Knowledge Merit for a Mental Skill for the scene? Also, have you considered something like Sage for an alternate name?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did consider Sage as a name. But it seemed lacking. Moving on...<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Logician gains a dot of Intelligence, which can take him above the usual limitations imposed by his Wyrd. He also does not suffer any untrained penalties to rolls which use Mental skills, and adds his Wyrd to all rolls made to memorize or recall information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:01:15-07:00","id":875105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=874359#post874359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Update to the Windwalker kith.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Windwalker</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;I'm a leaf on the wind. Watch me soar&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> Vassals to Lords and Ladies of Arcadia's skies, the Windwalkers were tasked with directing the wind for various tasks. These could be benign like the sculpting clouds and dispersing storms, or as destructive as sweeping away armies with a hurricane. However, a Windwalker's affinity for the winds can quicken him to action once an opportunity for escape is found.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling:</b> A disheveled figure wearing a black, featureless cowl and a frayed noose around his neck, who was forcibly taught how to dance in the wind.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> Formed of thick clouds and mist that darken and lighten according to its mood, this being is a blur of motion with the winds at its beck and call.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> Lithe and graceful, this sylph's clothing is fashioned out of thin cloud vapor that never seems to disperse unless she wants it to.<br /> \u2022 <b>Ogre:</b> A body comprised of dense, black clouds with sparking eyes and the strength of a storm coursing through their limbs.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Windwalkers use the higher of Wits or Dexterity for Defense, and may spend Glamour to apply it against Firearms attacks on a 1-to-1 ratio. They also gain the rote quality on all Initiative rolls, and take no physical penalties from the Heavy Winds Tilt and similar effects. If they spend Glamour or Willpower, they can use the three-dot version of Psychokinesis (Air).</div> </div> </div> </div>Their blessing seems very potent. They seem to have a better Initiative bonus than the Airtouched and Levinquick, as well as a potentially better Defense bonus. I do like that you made their ability to use their Defense against Firearms a bit more resource intensive than the Levinquick or Windwing's. I really like the resistance to the Heavy Winds Tilt, although I could see it being something where they lose Speed for a turn rather than Health from the damaging aspect of the Tilt, reflecting them dancing around the debris rather than getting hit. Still, it's simpler to just give them the immunity and leave it there. The Psychokinesis (Air) Merit could be very potent, given its ability to suffocate someone by pulling all the air away from them. That said, it makes a lot of sense for them to have something like that, so I'd keep it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=874929#post874929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Logician gains a dot of Intelligence, which can take him above the usual limitations imposed by his Wyrd. He also does not suffer any untrained penalties to rolls which use Mental skills, and adds his Wyrd to all rolls made to memorize or recall information.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:55:55-07:00","id":875161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=875105#post875105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their blessing seems very potent. They seem to have a better Initiative bonus than the Airtouched and Levinquick, as well as a potentially better Defense bonus. I do like that you made their ability to use their Defense against Firearms a bit more resource intensive than the Levinquick or Windwing's. I really like the resistance to the Heavy Winds Tilt, although I could see it being something where they lose Speed for a turn rather than Health from the damaging aspect of the Tilt, reflecting them dancing around the debris rather than getting hit. Still, it's simpler to just give them the immunity and leave it there. The Psychokinesis (Air) Merit could be very potent, given its ability to suffocate someone by pulling all the air away from them. That said, it makes a lot of sense for them to have something like that, so I'd keep it. </div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I went with that Initiative roll bonus to go with the unpredictability of the wind. Sometimes, you're fast enough. Other times, you're not. Still, how would you downgrade it if ever? Personally, I find it apt w/o the Speed bonus of the Levinquick.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I didn't want to complicate things too much with the Heavy Winds Tilt. So I went with full immunity. Also never thought about how Psychokinesis (Air) could be used to suffocate someone that much until you pointed it out. Still, it works if you want to copy LoK's Zaheer.<br /> <br /> And glad you like my change to the Logician.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T01:08:46-07:00","id":875417,"title":"","content":"Another element-using Kith. Do critique.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Wavemaster</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;Do what you want with them. Drown them if you like. I certainly would&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> Anyone who survived a flood knows very well how destructive water can be. Changelings who were remade into Wavemasters spent their durance commanding raging rivers and turbulent seas. More than once, they have used this power to drown any who dared intrude on their Keepers' realms. And they have just as often slain fellow captives who tried to swim for freedom. Those Wavemasters who do escape did so after willing the waters of their prison to hold the Gentry at bay.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> An anthropomorphic shark with sharp teeth and webbed hands and feet.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> A being sculpted wholly from living coral.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> A sea witch with blue skin and silvery hair, with a pair of gills at the sides of her neck.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Wavemaster can breathe underwater, and adds her Wyrd to her Initiative so long as more than half her body is submerged. If she spends Glamour or Willpower, she may use the three-dot version of the Psychokinesis Merit to affect water. All rolls to use the Merit gain the 8-again quality if performed at night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T01:30:16-07:00","id":875428,"title":"","content":"Here's a rewording for the Windwalker Blessing.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Windwalkers use the higher of Wits or Dexterity for Defense, and may spend Glamour to both apply it against Firearms and double their Initiative at a rate of one turn per point. They also take no physical penalties from the Heavy Winds Tilt, and reduce the damage they take from it by half their Wyrd (rounded up). If they spend Glamour or Willpower, they can use the three-dot version of the Psychokinesis Merit to manipulate air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:37:01-07:00","id":875617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=874684#post874684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Stoutfellow</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Big things come in small packages&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> In Arcadia nothing is ever quite as it seems, as the True Fae have a love for creating mind bending illusions and distorting reality. Changelings who became Stoutfellow were compressed into a fraction of their former size, yet retained all of their physical ability. What resulted was a being who could compete with those several times their size. The Gentry were said to find great amusement in seeing their performance, until even they made the mistake of underestimating their creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> An armored carapace and twitching antennae reveal this Changeling's previous life as an insect.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> Nearly as broad as he is tall and with a beard hanging down to his stomach, this man resembles the dwarf of Norse mythology.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Scrawny and timid from years of public humiliation, they found a strength within themselves they never knew they had.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>When it comes to the Stoutfellow, size isn't everything. They automatically gain the Small-Framed merit at character creation without suffering the reduced health box and may purchase physical attributes at a cost of x2 instead of x4.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>NOTE:</b> I can't think of a Glamour spending part to their blessing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that Master Aquatosic's idea of replacing the Experience bonus with the ability to enhance your Strength with Glamour would work well there. That said, this is a pretty interesting kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:45:30-07:00","id":875627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=875417#post875417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another element-using Kith. Do critique.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Wavemaster</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;Do what you want with them. Drown them if you like. I certainly would&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> Anyone who survived a flood knows very well how destructive water can be. Changelings who were remade into Wavemasters spent their durance commanding raging rivers and turbulent seas. More than once, they have used this power to drown any who dared intrude on their Keepers' realms. And they have just as often slain fellow captives who tried to swim for freedom. Those Wavemasters who do escape did so after willing the waters of their prison to hold the Gentry at bay.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> An anthropomorphic shark with sharp teeth and webbed hands and feet.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> A being sculpted wholly from living coral.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> A sea witch with blue skin and silvery hair, with a pair of gills at the sides of her neck.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Wavemaster can breathe underwater, and adds her Wyrd to her Initiative so long as more than half her body is submerged. If she spends Glamour or Willpower, she may use the three-dot version of the Psychokinesis Merit to affect water. All rolls to use the Merit gain the 8-again quality if performed at night.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This one is interesting, but it seems extremely similar to the Waterborn kith. How are you seeing them differ, in terms of flavor? Is it just that they used water as their weapon of choice? When using the Psychokinesis Merit, where does the 8-Again at night come in, flavor-wise? Do you think that it could be used to gain the Speed and grappling advantages that the Waterborn gain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":".  My reading comprehension is great. I forgot that Waterborn get Psychometry rather than Psychokinesis. I apologize for forgetting that. 04-27-2016, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T08:30:51-07:00","id":875670,"title":"","content":"Here is another one. I can't remember whether anyone has tried a 'holy person' kith yet, but here is my take on it.<br /> <br /> <b>Bishop</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">My friends, we cannot simply hide here and wait for mad gods to snatch us away again! Take up your arms, and let us drive this Huntsman from our door!</span><br /> <br /> The Others are not often religious beings, but on occasion, it suits their purposes to play at spirituality to instill such feelings in others. The bishops were often extremely religious before they were taken to act as the Gentry's holy men and women. A bishop may have acted as a spiritual adviser to ensure her Keeper's other servants stayed in line, or she may have been sent out into the world to form bizarre cults in her Keeper's honor. After escaping, most struggle to reconcile their experiences in Arcadia with the faith that they had held before.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> The horned shaman smells of smoke and speaks with a gravelly voice, and there is a vicious scar upon his throat.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A fire and brimstone preacher composed of actual fire and brimstone.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> A handsome man clad in ritual robes sown from the pages of assorted holy texts from around the world.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A savage one-eyed monk with blue skin and a charming voice.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A smiling, squat little man with countless holy relics hung from straps of leather that cross and penetrate his skin.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Bishops were intended to move large groups of people to act in the favor of their Keepers. Each bishop gains the Inspiring Merit free of cost, even if she lacks the prerequisite. When using this Merit, instead of the usual penalties, she suffers a -3 penalty to the roll for a single listener, a -2 penalty for a small clique, a -1 penalty for a small crowd, and no penalty for a large crowd. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, any listeners who have gained the Inspired Condition from the bishop can temporarily gain either the Virtuous or Vice-Ridden Merit with a Virtue or Vice of the bishop's choice. The temporary Merit persists until it is used to regain Willpower or for a number of days equal to the bishop's Wyrd, whichever comes first. All affected listeners receive the same Virtue or Vice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:23:31-07:00","id":876050,"title":"","content":"I just imagined the Elemental Bishop pointing at a Gentry and preparing to rave about divine judgement just as the camera goes into a freeze frame with an Arcadian backdrop like they do for epic cliffhangers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, that's two suggestions for what to do with the Stourfellow, so I'll see about editing it here in a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:31:14-07:00","id":876055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=874825#post874825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe you could replace the second half of the blessing with a bonus to a single strength-based roll proportionate to the amount of glamour you spend?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright, here's the revised version. I altered it a bit because I felt 1 Glamour for 1 Strength would have been massively broken late game when you can spend like 20 Glamour at a time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Blessing:</b> When it comes to the Stoutfellow, size isn't everything. They automatically gain the Small-Framed merit at character creation without suffering the reduced health box for their smaller size. Additionally, the Stoutfellow may spend a point of Glamour to add half their Wyrd (rounded up) to their Strength for one action. They may continue to do this as many times in a scene as they have Glamour to spend</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:39:28-07:00","id":876059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=876055#post876055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Alright, here's the revised version. I altered it a bit because I felt 1 Glamour for 1 Strength would have been massively broken late game when you can spend like 20 Glamour at a time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Blessing:</b> When it comes to the Stoutfellow, size isn't everything. They automatically gain the Small-Framed merit at character creation without suffering the reduced health box for their smaller size. Additionally, the Stoutfellow may spend a point of Glamour to add half their Wyrd (rounded up) to their Strength for one action. They may continue to do this as many times in a scene as they have Glamour to spend</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is much better. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=875627#post875627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one is interesting, but it seems extremely similar to the Waterborn kith. How are you seeing them differ, in terms of flavor? Is it just that they used water as their weapon of choice? When using the Psychokinesis Merit, where does the 8-Again at night come in, flavor-wise? Do you think that it could be used to gain the Speed and grappling advantages that the Waterborn gain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's the Initiative bonus (which I'm still open to tweaking). And I've been thinking of removing the 8-again rule because it doesn't fit. Also, I can probably see a Wavemaster using Psychokinesis to grapple others from afar, rather than getting the bonuses of the Waterborn. And if you happen to be grappling someone with water, and hold him below the surface.... Well, you get the idea.<br /> <br /> Also, imagine this. What is 70% of the human body comprised of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:43:01-07:00","id":876063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=876059#post876059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, imagine this. What is 70% of the human body comprised of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood and meat and skin and bone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:57:15-07:00","id":876071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=876063#post876063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood and meat and skin and bone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was hoping for water as an answer. But I suppose it wouldn't be covered by Psychokinesis (Water), yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T16:24:15-07:00","id":876103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=875670#post875670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is another one. I can't remember whether anyone has tried a 'holy person' kith yet, but here is my take on it.<br /> <br /> <b>Bishop</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">My friends, we cannot simply hide here and wait for mad gods to snatch us away again! Take up your arms, and let us drive this Huntsman from our door!</span><br /> <br /> The Others are not often religious beings, but on occasion, it suits their purposes to play at spirituality to instill such feelings in others. The bishops were often extremely religious before they were taken to act as the Gentry's holy men and women. A bishop may have acted as a spiritual adviser to ensure her Keeper's other servants stayed in line, or she may have been sent out into the world to form bizarre cults in her Keeper's honor. After escaping, most struggle to reconcile their experiences in Arcadia with the faith that they had held before.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> The horned shaman smells of smoke and speaks with a gravelly voice, and there is a vicious scar upon his throat.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A fire and brimstone preacher composed of actual fire and brimstone.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> A handsome man clad in ritual robes sown from the pages of assorted holy texts from around the world.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A savage one-eyed monk with blue skin and a charming voice.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A smiling, squat little man with countless holy relics hung from straps of leather that cross and penetrate his skin.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Bishops were intended to move large groups of people to act in the favor of their Keepers. Each bishop gains the Inspiring Merit free of cost, even if she lacks the prerequisite. When using this Merit, instead of the usual penalties, she suffers a -3 penalty to the roll for a single listener, a -2 penalty for a small clique, a -1 penalty for a small crowd, and no penalty for a large crowd. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, any listeners who have gained the Inspired Condition from the bishop can temporarily gain either the Virtuous or Vice-Ridden Merit with a Virtue or Vice of the bishop's choice. The temporary Merit persists until it is used to regain Willpower or for a number of days equal to the bishop's Wyrd, whichever comes first. All affected listeners receive the same Virtue or Vice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still thinking up my thoughts on this kith. But so far, it provides a different flavor from that of the Truefriend. One thing, though. Is there a more neutral term you could use for the kith?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T20:35:22-07:00","id":876225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=876103#post876103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still thinking up my thoughts on this kith. But so far, it provides a different flavor from that of the Truefriend. One thing, though. Is there a more neutral term you could use for the kith?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My original working title for the kith had been shepherd, but I thought that that one might bug people. I had considered priest, but I just didn't like the way it sounded in the description. If you have any ideas, I'd love to hear them. I'll try to come up with something different. I look forward to hearing your thoughts on the rest of the kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T21:20:21-07:00","id":876252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=876225#post876225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My original working title for the kith had been shepherd, but I thought that that one might bug people. I had considered priest, but I just didn't like the way it sounded in the description. If you have any ideas, I'd love to hear them. I'll try to come up with something different. I look forward to hearing your thoughts on the rest of the kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about Orator?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T21:32:20-07:00","id":876259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=876252#post876252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about Orator?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Orator just means you're good at speech; doesn't really have anything to do with faith.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Could try:</b><br /> <br /> Inquisitor<br /> <br /> Exorcist<br /> <br /> Shepherd<br /> <br /> Purifier","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T02:54:24-07:00","id":876409,"title":"","content":"I'd take Purifier as the new name for the Bishop. Or even Shepherd. I'd also put Emissary as an option.<br /> <br /> That said, here's my update on the Wavemaster Blessing.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Wavemaster can breathe underwater, and halves all healing times so long as she is fully submerged. She also benefits from the rote quality on all swimming rolls. If she spends Glamour or Willpower, she may use the three-dot version of the Psychokinesis Merit to affect water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-28-2016, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T04:29:48-07:00","id":876470,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Iceborn</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;Don't worry. A little cold isn't going to stop me&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Taken by Keepers who made their homes in realms of endless winter, Iceborn were kept as sentries who roamed under the cover of blizzards. Their touch is imbued with biting cold, and many intruders who crossed their paths more often than not ended up as stiff corpses. Yet while most were numbed by the cold they now embodied, some manage to flee when memories of a warmer time thawed their hearts and urged them to flee.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> A white wolf whose howl echoes with those of the winter winds.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> A living snowman with glistening patterns of ice instead of veins.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> A platinum-haired woman garbed in a translucent blue gown.<br /> \u2022 <b>Grimm:</b> Snowflakes decorate his flesh, their kaleidoscopic forms shaping lines of text which speak of cold, lonely tales.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Iceborn are immune to any penalties from cold weather, and can walk on ice without difficulty. If they spend a point of Glamour in a scene, they may cause anyone they touch to suffer the Extreme Cold Tilt at a starting penalty equal to their Wyrd. This Tilt lasts for a number of hours equal to successes on a Resolve + Occult roll. And if the victim is already suffering the Tilt, he adds to its existing penalty, and takes any dots in excess of 5 as lethal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-28-2016, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T06:18:08-07:00","id":876554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=876409#post876409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd take Purifier as the new name for the Bishop. Or even Shepherd. I'd also put Emissary as an option.<br /> <br /> That said, here's my update on the Wavemaster Blessing.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Wavemaster can breathe underwater, and halves all healing times so long as she is fully submerged. She also benefits from the rote quality on all swimming rolls. If she spends Glamour or Willpower, she may use the three-dot version of the Psychokinesis Merit to affect water.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I will go with shepherd. It's come up a couple times, and it was the name I'd originally had for the kith. Besides, it gets across the intended purpose of herding groups of people rather well. Thank you, Deionscribe and Nyrufa, for the feedback.<br /> <br /> I like this version of the Wavemaster blessing better. Good job on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T08:12:41-07:00","id":876647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=876259#post876259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Orator just means you're good at speech; doesn't really have anything to do with faith.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Could try:</b><br /> <br /> Inquisitor<br /> <br /> Exorcist<br /> <br /> Shepherd<br /> <br /> Purifier</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But outside the flavor text, the blessing itself does not have anything to do with religion. I think it could just as easily be a generic speech-making kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T17:23:19-07:00","id":877142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=876554#post876554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I will go with shepherd. It's come up a couple times, and it was the name I'd originally had for the kith. Besides, it gets across the intended purpose of herding groups of people rather well. Thank you, Deionscribe and Nyrufa, for the feedback.<br /> <br /> I like this version of the Wavemaster blessing better. Good job on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. And glad you like the new revisions.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on the Iceborn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T17:54:42-07:00","id":877167,"title":"","content":"Kittens are ass holes. Screwed up the computer and had to reinstall the whole thing.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T21:09:24-07:00","id":877297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=877167#post877167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kittens are ass holes. Screwed up the computer and had to reinstall the whole thing.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least you still have it. Had <i>really</i> bad luck last night with my phone getting stolen while I wasn't looking.<br /> <br /> Luckily, most of the stuff I had on it was either backed up or is replaceable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T21:27:41-07:00","id":877311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=877297#post877297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, at least you still have it. Had <i>really</i> bad luck last night with my phone getting stolen while I wasn't looking.<br /> <br /> Luckily, most of the stuff I had on it was either backed up or is replaceable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Still, lost a bunch of home brew content I was still tweaking before posting it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T06:22:56-07:00","id":877625,"title":"","content":"That sucks. I'm sorry your phone got snatched, Deionscribe. And I'm sorry you lost so much homebrew stuff, Nyrufa.<br /> <br /> Hmmm.... New kith idea: Asscat - blessing enables one to disrupt electronic memory, entangle strings or cords, and get in the way at critical moments...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T11:34:53-07:00","id":877925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=877311#post877311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, lost a bunch of home brew content I was still tweaking before posting it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Dang... Hope you can still piece it back together from memory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=877625#post877625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm.... New kith idea: Asscat - blessing enables one to disrupt electronic memory, entangle strings or cords, and get in the way at critical moments...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll wait for mechanics before I comment more on this.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, thoughts on the Iceborn kith?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T13:57:26-07:00","id":878071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=877925#post877925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dang... Hope you can still piece it back together from memory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'll wait for mechanics before I comment more on this.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, thoughts on the Iceborn kith?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What differentiates it from the snowskin flavorwise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T15:06:34-07:00","id":878139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=878071#post878071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What differentiates it from the snowskin flavorwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Snowskins are a Social-oriented kith with their Subterfuge dice bonus, and extra dot in Presence or Wyrd. What I'm going for with the Iceborn is something more offensive. For reference purposes, here is the Snowskin Blessing.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blessing:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A snowskin knows how to mask her emotions and make her voice carry a chilling terror. She can add her Wyrd to Subterfuge rolls to hide her feelings, and she gains a dot in Presence or Manipulation (your choice) which can bring her above her normal limit based on her Wyrd.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T16:06:40-07:00","id":878198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=876470#post876470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Iceborn</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;Don't worry. A little cold isn't going to stop me&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Taken by Keepers who made their homes in realms of endless winter, Iceborn were kept as sentries who roamed under the cover of blizzards. Their touch is imbued with biting cold, and many intruders who crossed their paths more often than not ended up as stiff corpses. Yet while most were numbed by the cold they now embodied, some manage to flee when memories of a warmer time thawed their hearts and urged them to flee.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> A white wolf whose howl echoes with those of the winter winds.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> A living snowman with glistening patterns of ice instead of veins.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> A platinum-haired woman garbed in a translucent blue gown.<br /> \u2022 <b>Grimm:</b> Snowflakes decorate his flesh, their kaleidoscopic forms shaping lines of text which speak of cold, lonely tales.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Iceborn are immune to any penalties from cold weather, and can walk on ice without difficulty. If they spend a point of Glamour in a scene, they may cause anyone they touch to suffer the Extreme Cold Tilt at a starting penalty equal to their Wyrd. This Tilt lasts for a number of hours equal to successes on a Resolve + Occult roll. And if the victim is already suffering the Tilt, he adds to its existing penalty, and takes any dots in excess of 5 as lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is awesome. I like this kith a lot. I do think that the blessing could use a little tweaking, though. First, the ability to inflict such a potent Tilt seems like it should either cost a point of Glamour for each person touched (if the character is playing freeze tag with her enemies, and the Tilt will linger), or one point of Glamour to create an area of effect with the Tilt centered around the iceborn (affecting all within the range, but easily escaped by fleeing the presence of the iceborn), rather than one point of Glamour to play freeze tag for the duration of the scene. If going the route with the lingering Tilt, there also needs to be some thought given as to what will happen if the victim tries to warm up to end the Tilt. I'd also say that, given how quickly the effective Wyrd could exceed 5 with Potent Kith, that you may want to consider the starting penalty of the Tilt to be half Wyrd rather than full Wyrd. As the blessing currently stands, an especially potent iceborn could walk into a crowded place, spend a point of Glamour, and then go on to slay every normal human that could be caught with a single touch.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T16:11:55-07:00","id":878209,"title":"","content":"Okay, here is the revised shepherd kith. Thank you to everyone who gave me name suggestions for this kith. In fact, the purifier name has made me begin toying with an idea for a new kith, tentatively called a hallowheart. We'll see how that goes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shepherd</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">My friends, we cannot simply hide here and wait for mad gods to snatch us away again! Take up your arms, and let us drive this Huntsman from our door!</span><br /> <br /> The Others are not often religious beings, but on occasion, the trappings of religion suit their purposes, either to play at spirituality or to instill such feelings in others. The shepherds were often extremely religious before they were taken to act as the Gentry's holy men and women. A shepherd may have acted as a spiritual adviser, herding her Keeper's other servants with her words, or she may have been sent out into the world to form bizarre cults in her Keeper's honor. After escaping, most struggle to reconcile their experiences in Arcadia with the faith that they had held before.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> The horned shaman smells of smoke and speaks with a gravelly voice, and there is a vicious scar upon his throat.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A fire and brimstone preacher composed of actual fire and brimstone.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> A handsome man clad in ritual robes sown from the pages of assorted holy texts from around the world.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A savage one-eyed monk with blue skin and a charming voice.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A smiling, squat little man with countless holy relics hung from straps of leather that cross and penetrate his skin.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Shepherds were intended to move large groups of people to act in the favor of their Keepers. Each shepherd gains the Inspiring Merit free of cost, even if she lacks the prerequisite. When using this Merit, instead of the usual penalties, she suffers a -3 penalty to the roll for a single listener, a -2 penalty for a small clique, a -1 penalty for a small crowd, and no penalty for a large crowd. When utilizing the trappings of a religion that the majority of listeners believe in, the shepherd may add her Wyrd to this roll. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, any listeners who have gained the Inspired Condition from the shepherd's speech temporarily gains either the Virtuous or Vice-Ridden Merit with a Virtue or Vice of the shepherd's choice. The temporary Merit persists until it is used to regain Willpower or for a number of days equal to the shepherd's Wyrd, whichever comes first. All affected listeners receive the same Virtue or Vice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T16:17:18-07:00","id":878217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=877925#post877925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll wait for mechanics before I comment more on this.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's unlikely to be any forthcoming any time soon. Ultimately, the Asscat is intended as a rather horrible joke kith. Of course, I might actually make it anyway. The faerysue shows that I'm quite willing to do a full write-up for a joke kith. Hmmm... I can see the quote already: &quot;He was just standing there, in the wreckage of my apartment, smiling innocently up at me. Then he had the audacity to ask me for a cheeseburger!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T19:40:17-07:00","id":878361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=878217#post878217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's unlikely to be any forthcoming any time soon. Ultimately, the Asscat is intended as a rather horrible joke kith. Of course, I might actually make it anyway. The faerysue shows that I'm quite willing to do a full write-up for a joke kith. Hmmm... I can see the quote already: &quot;He was just standing there, in the wreckage of my apartment, smiling innocently up at me. Then he had the audacity to ask me for a cheeseburger!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That does sound like some warped thing the True Fae would make. What if you made it into a hobgoblin instead of a kith?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:02:04-07:00","id":878371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=878361#post878361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That does sound like some warped thing the True Fae would make. What if you made it into a hobgoblin instead of a kith?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could actually see that. Once we get a good look at the 2nd edition hobgoblins, I might just do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T21:14:43-07:00","id":878428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=878371#post878371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could actually see that. Once we get a good look at the 2nd edition hobgoblins, I might just do that.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Always happy to help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T22:45:21-07:00","id":878485,"title":"","content":"By the way, does anybody have the link to the play test document? Need to add it to bookmarks again.<br /> <br /> Working on a Minotaur Kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T22:54:12-07:00","id":878505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=878485#post878485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, does anybody have the link to the play test document? Need to add it to bookmarks again.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a thread with the link stickied to the top of this forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T23:03:43-07:00","id":878514,"title":"","content":"<b>Minotaur:</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Never quite understood why we call ourselves the Lost. I know exactly where we are, and it's up shit's creek!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Some Keepers design realms that are so complex in layout that friends and enemies alike are prone to getting hopelessly turned around walking from point A to point B. Those who became Minotaur were forced to patrol these labyrinths as added security measures. Escorting those who had permission to travel and disposing of those who did not. For reasons unclear, all Minotaur resemble a cross between a human and a bovine of some kind, most commonly that of a bull. Eventually the warden of the labyrinth managed to find the exit and started running like hell!<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> The head and legs of a bovine, dressed in little more than tattered rags.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A muscle packed giant with a bovine's head, sharp claws and fangs.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A bronze bull mask has been permanently welded shut around their head, forever concealing the wearer's true identity.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Minotaur have a keen sense of direction and quickly adapt to any structural layout regardless of how complex it may be. The Minotaur begins with both the Direction Sense and the Trained Observer merits for free at character creation. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour and walking from room to room, the Minotaur can commit to memory a recorded map of the layout. As a result, the Minotaur always succeeds on attempts to navigate places they have previously been to before. The minotaur is capable of memorizing one location equal to their Wyrd. If they reach their limit, they must allow themselves to forget a previous location in order to record a new one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-30-2016, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T08:56:35-07:00","id":878768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=878198#post878198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is awesome. I like this kith a lot. I do think that the blessing could use a little tweaking, though. First, the ability to inflict such a potent Tilt seems like it should either cost a point of Glamour for each person touched (if the character is playing freeze tag with her enemies, and the Tilt will linger), or one point of Glamour to create an area of effect with the Tilt centered around the iceborn (affecting all within the range, but easily escaped by fleeing the presence of the iceborn), rather than one point of Glamour to play freeze tag for the duration of the scene. If going the route with the lingering Tilt, there also needs to be some thought given as to what will happen if the victim tries to warm up to end the Tilt. I'd also say that, given how quickly the effective Wyrd could exceed 5 with Potent Kith, that you may want to consider the starting penalty of the Tilt to be half Wyrd rather than full Wyrd. As the blessing currently stands, an especially potent iceborn could walk into a crowded place, spend a point of Glamour, and then go on to slay every normal human that could be caught with a single touch.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about this, then?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing</b>: Iceborn are immune to any penalties from cold weather, and can walk on ice without difficulty. If they spend a point of Glamour after a successful touch action, they may inflict the Extreme Cold Tilt on a target. This Tilt lasts for a number of hours equal to successes on a Resolve + Occult roll, and has an initial penalty equal to half the changeling's Wyrd, rounded up. If the victim is already suffering the Tilt, he adds to its penalty, and takes any dots in excess of 5 as lethal damage.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> As for warming up, I say treat it as normal, which definitely means an Iceborn has the biggest advantage against his opponent if he can deprive him of any source of heart. Easy enough with Contracts and whatever other tricks happen to be up the changeling's sleeves. It's a slow death for the victim, if that's the case. And <i>that</i> is what I was aiming for with the blessing. On the other hand, I am curious to see how an area of effect version would go down. I didn't go down that route because I didn't want to make a copy of the Vulcanalis kith, for all intents and purposes.<br /> <br /> Regarding your Shepherd kith, I really like the Blessing. I can definitely see how one dual-kithed as a Truefriend or Playmate would be a very effective team leader. Looking forward to seeing what you cook up for the Hallowheart.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T09:15:19-07:00","id":878788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=878514#post878514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Minotaur:</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Never quite understood why we call ourselves the Lost. I know exactly where we are, and it's up shit's creek!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Some Keepers design realms that are so complex in layout that friends and enemies alike are prone to getting hopelessly turned around walking from point A to point B. Those who became Minotaur were forced to patrol these labyrinths as added security measures. Escorting those who had permission to travel and disposing of those who did not. For reasons unclear, all Minotaur resemble a cross between a human and a bovine of some kind, most commonly that of a bull. Eventually the warden of the labyrinth managed to find the exit and started running like hell!<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> The head and legs of a bovine, dressed in little more than tattered rags.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A muscle packed giant with a bovine's head, sharp claws and fangs.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A bronze bull mask has been permanently welded shut around their head, forever concealing the wearer's true identity.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Minotaur have a keen sense of direction and quickly adapt to any structural layout regardless of how complex it may be. The Minotaur begins with both the Direction Sense and the Trained Observer merits for free at character creation. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour and walking from room to room, the Minotaur can permanently record a mental map of whatever layout they happen to be exploring. As a result, the Minotaur always succeeds at attempts to navigate places they have previously visited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Interesting concept, but I'm thinking the Blessing could use a bit more work. At the very least, I'd retain the Glamour aspect, though limit it to a number of such locations equal to Wyrd?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T11:09:09-07:00","id":878876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=878788#post878788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. Interesting concept, but I'm thinking the Blessing could use a bit more work. At the very least, I'd retain the Glamour aspect, though limit it to a number of such locations equal to Wyrd?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Edited it a bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------<br /> <br /> I'm really tempted to create Kiths for Changeling Dreaming too. Unfortunately, I don't know crap about how the setting works, so it would probably be a disaster.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://changelingthedreaming.wikia.com/wiki/The_Kith_List\" target=\"_blank\">Some Dreaming Kiths I Found.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-30-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T12:14:04-07:00","id":878914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=878768#post878768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about this, then?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing</b>: Iceborn are immune to any penalties from cold weather, and can walk on ice without difficulty. If they spend a point of Glamour after a successful touch action, they may inflict the Extreme Cold Tilt on a target. This Tilt lasts for a number of hours equal to successes on a Resolve + Occult roll, and has an initial penalty equal to half the changeling's Wyrd, rounded up. If the victim is already suffering the Tilt, he adds to its penalty, and takes any dots in excess of 5 as lethal damage.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> As for warming up, I say treat it as normal, which definitely means an Iceborn has the biggest advantage against his opponent if he can deprive him of any source of heart. Easy enough with Contracts and whatever other tricks happen to be up the changeling's sleeves. It's a slow death for the victim, if that's the case. And <i>that</i> is what I was aiming for with the blessing. On the other hand, I am curious to see how an area of effect version would go down. I didn't go down that route because I didn't want to make a copy of the Vulcanalis kith, for all intents and purposes.<br /> <br /> Regarding your Shepherd kith, I really like the Blessing. I can definitely see how one dual-kithed as a Truefriend or Playmate would be a very effective team leader. Looking forward to seeing what you cook up for the Hallowheart.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the new version of the blessing. I'm glad you liked the revised shepherd, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T12:18:41-07:00","id":878920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=878876#post878876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Edited it a bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------<br /> <br /> I'm really tempted to create Kiths for Changeling Dreaming too. Unfortunately, I don't know crap about how the setting works, so it would probably be a disaster.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://changelingthedreaming.wikia.com/wiki/The_Kith_List&amp;quot;]Some</a> Dreaming Kiths I Found.[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dreaming kiths can be fun. I created one called the Powries, which were Thallain redcaps. I've actually contemplated creating a Minotaur kith for that game as well, with a blessing that allows them to find their way and a frailty of agoraphobia. I like your Minotaur kith for Lost. Excellent job on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T04:32:03-07:00","id":879437,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a>, here's an alternative write-up for the Minotaur Blessing. <hr /><br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Minotaurs have a keen sense of direction and quickly adapt to any structural layout regardless of how complex it may be. A Minotaur gains the Direction Sense Merit, and cannot be affected by powers that would cause him to be lost. If he spends a point of Glamour while walking from room to room, he can commit to memory a recorded map of a given location. In such places, he benefits from a single automatic success to all navigation rolls. The Minotaur is capable of memorizing a number of locations equal to his Wyrd. If he reaches this limit, he must allow himself to forget a previous location in order to record a new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T03:40:52-07:00","id":880019,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a>. I also decided to do an alternative version of the Moral, with a different name and Blessing. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Fabulist</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;And the moral of the story is... that was a stupid idea!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Human folklore is cram packed with stories designed to teach people valuable life lessons including how to be a good Samaritan, as well as how to stay alive longer than the other guy. Often, these stories involve Humanity coming into contact with magical beings, which just so happen to be the True Fae. Changelings who became Fabulists were used to educate others about the error of their ways, often teaching them how to survive the dangers of Faerie. Perhaps in some way, their durance served a noble function, but they did not see it that way when they were made the subject of demonstration. Eventually, though, a Fabulist manages to learn his lesson and escape the narrative forced upon him by his Keeper.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> A lesson in trusting strangers. They are the big bad wolf that leads the naive to certain peril.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> A lesson in humility. They are the beautiful maiden who drives the envious to self destruction.<br /> \u2022 <b>Ogre:</b> A lesson in respecting the property of others. They are the angry bear who comes home to find an unwanted house guest.<br /> \u2022 <b>Wizened:</b> A lesson in hard work. Their construction projects are up to code, while their competitors use shoddy materials and cheap labor.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Fabulist's durance was spent teaching others the error of their ways until they eventually learned and corrected themselves. Upon escaping, however, they become highly attuned to circumstances which would bring about their own personal growth. Whenever the Fabulist would receive the Acuity Condition, he doubles its duration, and gains an additional dot of Clarity if he manages to resolve it. If he spends a point of Glamour and successfully touches a subject, he may inflict the Delusional Condition on him for a number of days equal to his Wyrd.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> For trivia purposes, the term Fabulist refers to someone who writes Fables.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T03:55:57-07:00","id":880026,"title":"","content":"Tentative tweak to the Spelldrinker Blessing. Comments? <hr /><br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Spelldrinker benefits from the 8-again rule on all kenning rolls, which are always free reflexive actions. If he successfully contests or resists a supernatural power used against him, he may retain it for later use within the scene, or dissolve it in an Instant action for one point of Glamour. The Spelldrinker can store a number of such powers equal to his Wyrd, with any unused automatically converted to Glamour. When using an absorbed power, he uses his own dots in Attributes and Skills, but does not add his Wyrd for both Contracts he doesn't know, and the powers of other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> I'm mentioning this because I realized there would be some supernatural powers that the kith would be unable to use, like the spells of an Awakened character. Not sure whether it's a good or bad thing. But if anyone has alternative ideas for handling it, I'm open to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T16:56:16-07:00","id":881362,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> Made a slight addition to the Sentinel Blessing based on your 1E version. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Sentinels gain three dots in the Defender Merit, and add half their Wyrd (rounded up) to their Initiative when fighting in a Hollow or Safe Place owned by them or their allies. If they spend a point of Glamour while touching someone, they may grant their target a minor blessing which gives +2/+2 Armor for a number of attacks equal to his Wyrd. The Armor's rating is doubled if the subject is a Touchstone, and a Sentinel can also tell how much and what kind of damage she suffers if he shares an active pledge with her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-03-2016, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T22:03:23-07:00","id":881497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=880026#post880026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tentative tweak to the Spelldrinker Blessing. Comments? <hr /><br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Spelldrinker benefits from the 8-again rule on all kenning rolls, which are always free reflexive actions. If he successfully contests or resists a supernatural power used against him, he may retain it for later use within the scene, or dissolve it in an Instant action for one point of Glamour. The Spelldrinker can store a number of such powers equal to his Wyrd, with any unused automatically converted to Glamour. When using an absorbed power, he uses his own dots in Attributes and Skills, but does not add his Wyrd for both Contracts he doesn't know, and the powers of other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> I'm mentioning this because I realized there would be some supernatural powers that the kith would be unable to use, like the spells of an Awakened character. Not sure whether it's a good or bad thing. But if anyone has alternative ideas for handling it, I'm open to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the version you've got in the existing doc a bit better. Dissolving the effect for a point of Glamour before the scene ends brings back the problem of low level spell spamming to recharge the spelldrinker's batteries, without diminishing how many effects could actually be stored when the action gets underway. As for how to handle other effects, I'd say that it would ultimately function as though he was reflecting the power back at the desired moment. For instance, if a mage was to target him with a spell to disorient him and he resisted it, he would be able to disorient someone else. He wouldn't understand the Supernal symbols that made it possible, but he would be able to understand that he had an effect that could disorient at his disposal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T22:11:24-07:00","id":881502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=881362#post881362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> Made a slight addition to the Sentinel Blessing based on your 1E version. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Sentinels gain three dots in the Defender Merit, and add half their Wyrd (rounded up) to their Initiative when fighting in a Hollow or Safe Place owned by them or their allies. If they spend a point of Glamour while touching someone, they may grant their target a minor blessing which gives +2/+2 Armor for a number of attacks equal to his Wyrd. The Armor's rating is doubled if the subject is a Touchstone, and a Sentinel can also tell how much and what kind of damage she suffers if he shares an active pledge with her.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that addition. I think it adds a nice bit of flavor. One thing I hadn't thought of before, though, is that the blessing seems like it could be used to give all of the Sentinel's friends the Armor bonus by touching each of them and spending the Glamour before combat begins. Is that something you had intended, or is it something unexpected that could be exploited?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T01:26:17-07:00","id":881591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=881497#post881497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the version you've got in the existing doc a bit better. Dissolving the effect for a point of Glamour before the scene ends brings back the problem of low level spell spamming to recharge the spelldrinker's batteries, without diminishing how many effects could actually be stored when the action gets underway. As for how to handle other effects, I'd say that it would ultimately function as though he was reflecting the power back at the desired moment. For instance, if a mage was to target him with a spell to disorient him and he resisted it, he would be able to disorient someone else. He wouldn't understand the Supernal symbols that made it possible, but he would be able to understand that he had an effect that could disorient at his disposal.</div> </div> </div> </div>So perhaps instead of having to roll the power himself, he instead uses an alternative dice pool or even just readily use it? Let me see if this version works better.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing:</b> A Spelldrinker benefits from the 8-again rule on all kenning rolls, which are always free reflexive actions. If he successfully contests or resists a supernatural power used against him, he may retain it for later use within the scene. The Spelldrinker can store a number of such powers equal to his Wyrd, with any unused each granting one point of Glamour. He uses his own dots in Attributes and Skills when rolling those powers, but does not add his Wyrd for Contracts he doesn't know. With the powers from other supernaturals, he instead rolls Wits + Occult.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> That way, the kith is still best effective against fae magic, but his ability to manipulate the powers of other supernaturals requires further refinement and training. And that's not counting in the fact that it'd make an effective combination for Chimeras or Mageslayers.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=881502#post881502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that addition. I think it adds a nice bit of flavor. One thing I hadn't thought of before, though, is that the blessing seems like it could be used to give all of the Sentinel's friends the Armor bonus by touching each of them and spending the Glamour before combat begins. Is that something you had intended, or is it something unexpected that could be exploited?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I intended it, for the most part. Anyway, polishing the wording a little more.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Sentinels gain three dots in the Defender Merit, and add half their Wyrd (rounded up) to their Initiative when fighting in a Hollow or Safe Place owned by them or their allies. They are also aware of the well-being of anyone they have an active pledge with, and can tell how much and what kind of harm they suffer. If they spend Glamour while touching someone, they may grant their target a minor blessing which gives +2/+2 Armor. Each point empowers the blessing to last for a number of attacks equal to his Wyrd within the scene. The Armor's rating is doubled if the subject is a Touchstone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=873852#post873852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not certain how Trivial Reworking relates to the ability to crunch numbers. Perhaps part of their blessing could be Interdisciplinary Specialty (Mathematics) and the ability to instantly count everything within their line of sight, whether it is the coins in a dragon's hoard or the soldiers in an enemy army? Have you considered something like actuary or auditor for the kith name?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I think that's a good place to start. And I'm having a hard time deciding which of the two terms I should pick for the kith name.<br /> <br /> Also...<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Windwalkers use the higher of Wits or Dexterity for Defense, and <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">benefit from the rote quality on all Initiative rolls</span>. They also take no physical penalties from the Heavy Winds Tilt, and reduce the damage they take from it by half their Wyrd (rounded up). If they spend Glamour or Willpower, they can use the three-dot version of the Psychokinesis Merit to manipulate air.<br /> -=-<br /> <br /> I'm going with this version of the Windwalker Blessing for the time being, since I find that allowing them to apply their (augmented) Defense against Firearms in any way might be a bit too much. Besides, having the Levinquick or Windwing via Dual Kith should satisfy those who want that advantage. Not to mention I remember an Advanced or Epic Merit that also granted it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-04-2016, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T01:58:08-07:00","id":881601,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> <br /> Also. Not sure if you guys saw this revision to the Enchanter kith in the doc, so posting it here. Critique is appreciated.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blessing</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Enchanter gains the Gentrified Bearing Merit for free, and benefits from the 8-again rule on all rolls made to perform Sealings on Huntsmen. Furthermore, Hobgoblins who interact with her in person must roll Wits + Composure with a target number equal to half her Wyrd (rounded up) to expose her as a fraud.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T04:15:30-07:00","id":881650,"title":"","content":"Revisited my &quot;Psylocke&quot; kith and decided to try a different direction. <hr /><br /> <u><b>Psyblade</b></u><br /> <i>&quot;The mind can be a delicate thing. But mine is as sharp as any blade.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Assassins of a subtle bent, those made into Psyblades by their Keepers could use their own minds as weapons. While most did not prove hardy in open conflict, they became true threats once they've scattered their foes and single them out, one after the other. A Psyblades who escapes, however, managed to do so after briefly stunning her Keeper with her gift.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Elemental:</b> A vaguely humanoid shadow whose hands light up with ethereal flame when it strikes.<br /> <b>\u2022 Fairest:</b> A dark-haired assassin garbed in form-fitting armor, who slowly weakens her foes with each punch and every palm strike.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>A Psyblade can spend Glamour or Willpower to use the Aura Reading Merit without any drawbacks, and is immune to any supernatural powers which would detect, influence, or read her thoughts. Additionally, her unarmed attacks inflict lethal damage, and can inflict the Stunned Tilt for a number of turns equal to her Wyrd on an Exceptional Success. Any victims of her attack must succeed on a Resolve + Composure roll in addition to spending Willpower if they wish to end the Tilt sooner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T03:25:44-07:00","id":882727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=881591#post881591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So perhaps instead of having to roll the power himself, he instead uses an alternative dice pool or even just readily use it? Let me see if this version works better.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing:</b> A Spelldrinker benefits from the 8-again rule on all kenning rolls, which are always free reflexive actions. If he successfully contests or resists a supernatural power used against him, he may retain it for later use within the scene. The Spelldrinker can store a number of such powers equal to his Wyrd, with any unused each granting one point of Glamour. He uses his own dots in Attributes and Skills when rolling those powers, but does not add his Wyrd for Contracts he doesn't know. With the powers from other supernaturals, he instead rolls Wits + Occult.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> That way, the kith is still best effective against fae magic, but his ability to manipulate the powers of other supernaturals requires further refinement and training. And that's not counting in the fact that it'd make an effective combination for Chimeras or Mageslayers.</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about the alternative dice pool. It brings back the problem of the spelldrinker becoming being better at wielding the power than the original user. In fact, it could even make the problem worse, as they'd only need to focus on raising a single dice pool with Experiences. Perhaps powers that require something other than an Attribute + Skill to use would just need to be ones that sat there until they were digested into Glamour. That wouldn't necessarily be a bad thing, though. Gaining the Glamour from the effects fits the 'drinking' imagery a bit better anyway, so having some effects that can only be digested isn't inherently a problem. If you really want an alternative dice pool, though, you could always have it default to Wits alone (to reflect the quickness of thought necessary to wield the effect) or Resolve alone (to reflect the tenacity of will required to redirect the energies of another), which would likely be a smaller pool than the original user for most changelings. Another thought that occurred to me is that if you wanted to give the ability to use the other powers more of a &quot;catching the power and redirecting it&quot; sort of feel, you could require them to utilize the power within a number of turns equal to their Wyrd or have it automatically convert to Glamour at that time. You'd still need to limit the number of times that the spelldrinker could do it in order to prevent power spamming for easy Glamour recharge, but it would give a bit more of a sense of urgency to the blessing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=881591#post881591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I intended it, for the most part. Anyway, polishing the wording a little more.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Sentinels gain three dots in the Defender Merit, and add half their Wyrd (rounded up) to their Initiative when fighting in a Hollow or Safe Place owned by them or their allies. They are also aware of the well-being of anyone they have an active pledge with, and can tell how much and what kind of harm they suffer. If they spend Glamour while touching someone, they may grant their target a minor blessing which gives +2/+2 Armor. Each point empowers the blessing to last for a number of attacks equal to his Wyrd within the scene. The Armor's rating is doubled if the subject is a Touchstone.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the way this sounds. I could see limiting the ability to bestow Armor to being one target at a time, given the potency of Armor in 2E.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=881591#post881591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. I think that's a good place to start. And I'm having a hard time deciding which of the two terms I should pick for the kith name.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Let's go with auditor, for now, if that's helpful to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=881591#post881591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Windwalkers use the higher of Wits or Dexterity for Defense, and <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">benefit from the rote quality on all Initiative rolls</span>. They also take no physical penalties from the Heavy Winds Tilt, and reduce the damage they take from it by half their Wyrd (rounded up). If they spend Glamour or Willpower, they can use the three-dot version of the Psychokinesis Merit to manipulate air.<br /> -=-<br /> <br /> I'm going with this version of the Windwalker Blessing for the time being, since I find that allowing them to apply their (augmented) Defense against Firearms in any way might be a bit too much. Besides, having the Levinquick or Windwing via Dual Kith should satisfy those who want that advantage. Not to mention I remember an Advanced or Epic Merit that also granted it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this version better. I would change the Psychokinesis Merit from air to wind, though, as the ability to just stop the air getting into someone's lungs is a pretty quick victory and, coupled with a higher Defense and rote Initiative, could make a Windwalker more or less unstoppable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T03:45:50-07:00","id":882736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=881650#post881650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revisited my &quot;Psylocke&quot; kith and decided to try a different direction. <hr /><br /> <u><b>Psyblade</b></u><br /> <i>&quot;The mind can be a delicate thing. But mine is as sharp as any blade.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Assassins of a subtle bent, those made into Psyblades by their Keepers could use their own minds as weapons. While most did not prove hardy in open conflict, they became true threats once they've scattered their foes and single them out, one after the other. A Psyblades who escapes, however, managed to do so after briefly stunning her Keeper with her gift.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Elemental:</b> A vaguely humanoid shadow whose hands light up with ethereal flame when it strikes.<br /> <b>\u2022 Fairest:</b> A dark-haired assassin garbed in form-fitting armor, who slowly weakens her foes with each punch and every palm strike.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>A Psyblade can spend Glamour or Willpower to use the Aura Reading Merit without any drawbacks, and is immune to any supernatural powers which would detect, influence, or read her thoughts. Additionally, her unarmed attacks inflict lethal damage, and can inflict the Stunned Tilt for a number of turns equal to her Wyrd on an Exceptional Success. Any victims of her attack must succeed on a Resolve + Composure roll in addition to spending Willpower if they wish to end the Tilt sooner.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Looking better. A complete blanket immunity to all thought detecting or influencing powers seems pretty potent, especially coupled with some of the other capabilities. Perhaps it could be something like doubling her Wyrd for purposes of resisting such effects, rather than automatic immunity? I could see the Stunned effect requiring Glamour to activate, as well, especially if it is going to require a Resolve + Composure roll in order to have the ability to end the Tilt. I like the new name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T16:31:13-07:00","id":883285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=882727#post882727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about the alternative dice pool. It brings back the problem of the Spelldrinker becoming being better at wielding the power than the original user. In fact, it could even make the problem worse, as they'd only need to focus on raising a single dice pool with Experiences. Perhaps powers that require something other than an Attribute + Skill to use would just need to be ones that sat there until they were digested into Glamour. That wouldn't necessarily be a bad thing, though. Gaining the Glamour from the effects fits the 'drinking' imagery a bit better anyway, so having some effects that can only be digested isn't inherently a problem. If you really want an alternative dice pool, though, you could always have it default to Wits alone (to reflect the quickness of thought necessary to wield the effect) or Resolve alone (to reflect the tenacity of will required to redirect the energies of another), which would likely be a smaller pool than the original user for most changelings. Another thought that occurred to me is that if you wanted to give the ability to use the other powers more of a &quot;catching the power and redirecting it&quot; sort of feel, you could require them to utilize the power within a number of turns equal to their Wyrd or have it automatically convert to Glamour at that time. You'd still need to limit the number of times that the spelldrinker could do it in order to prevent power spamming for easy Glamour recharge, but it would give a bit more of a sense of urgency to the blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. Why not both Attributes? It'd still be very heavy investment, considering how each Attribute dot costs 4 Experience to purchase.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing:</b> A Spelldrinker benefits from the 8-again rule on all kenning rolls, which are always free reflexive actions. If he successfully contests or resists a supernatural power used against him, he may retain it for later use within the scene. The Spelldrinker can store a number of such powers equal to his Wyrd, with any unused each granting one point of Glamour. He uses his own dots in Attributes and Skills when rolling Contracts, but does not roll his Wyrd for those he does not possess. When wielding t</span>he powers of other supernaturals (such as a Mage's spells or Kindred Disciplines), the Spelldrinker rolls Wits + Resolve instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=882727#post882727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this version better. I would change the Psychokinesis Merit from air to wind, though, as the ability to just stop the air getting into someone's lungs is a pretty quick victory and, coupled with a higher Defense and rote Initiative, could make a Windwalker more or less unstoppable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edited. Though that does make me wonder if the element is still readily available for Windwalkers to use. I'm going to say yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=882736#post882736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking better. A complete blanket immunity to all thought detecting or influencing powers seems pretty potent, especially coupled with some of the other capabilities. Perhaps it could be something like doubling her Wyrd for purposes of resisting such effects, rather than automatic immunity? I could see the Stunned effect requiring Glamour to activate, as well, especially if it is going to require a Resolve + Composure roll in order to have the ability to end the Tilt. I like the new name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like the name. Now, how's this revision?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>A Psyblade can spend Glamour or Willpower to use the Aura Reading Merit without any drawbacks, and doubles her effective Wyrd rating when contesting or resisting any supernatural powers which would detect, influence, or read her thoughts. Additionally, her unarmed attacks inflict lethal damage, and she can spend Glamour to have an unarmed attack inflict the Stunned Tilt for a number of turns equal to her Wyrd. Her victims must succeed on a Resolve + Composure roll in addition to spending Willpower if they wish to end the Tilt sooner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-05-2016, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T18:38:29-07:00","id":883370,"title":"","content":"Here is a new one, up for critique:<br /> <br /> <b>Coveted</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Tell me that you don't love me, and I promise that I'll go. Tell me you that you do, and we can figure out what to do about my husband.</span><br /> <br /> Often beautiful and always desirable, the coveted were created to be gifts for the Gentry's rivals or to disrupt the unity of changeling freeholds. These living apples of discord were intended to utilize their inherent desirability to sow envy and jealousy among all, causing instability among their victims that their Keepers could then exploit. While one of the coveted may be able to free herself from her Keeper's influence, she will inevitably find herself dragged back into the same petty rivalries that she had hoped to escape.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> The skin of her delicate body is the color of beautifully polished opal, but her eyes glow a sickly green and her smile seems unnatural.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> She is a beautiful and baroque golden statue, with silvered angelic wings and two gleaming emeralds for eyes.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> His penetrating green eyes sit within features that subtly alter to be pleasing to the individual viewer.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> Her skin is composed of illuminated manuscripts, promising ancient and forgotten wisdom, with intricate patterns of silver and gold highlighting her forest green eyes.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> His haggard body is held together with loops of the purest silver and gold, and there is sadness lurking in his weary jade eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The coveted gains the Apple of Discord Contract for free, and she gains the 8-Again quality when rolling for the Contract's activation. Additionally, the coveted may spend a point of Glamour to add her Wyrd to her Manipulation rolls for the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>New Contract<br /> <br /> Apple of Discord (..)<br /> </b><br /> The character makes herself or an object that she is carrying into something greatly desirable to all who see it, sowing discord wherever the object of desire goes.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Glamour<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Persuasion + Wyrd vs. Composure + Wyrd<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant and Contested<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Everyone who would have been affected by the power realize that the changeling had sought to turn them against each other.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The object of the Contract is no more desirable than it was before.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The object of the Contract becomes highly desirable to everyone who looks at it. For the duration of the scene, anyone who looks at the object of the Contract gains the Obsession Condition related to gaining possession of the object. The Contract's effects automatically end if anyone engages in behavior that would constitute a Breaking Point for the individual in order to gain possession of the object.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The effects of the Contract last for a number of days equal to the changeling's Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <b>-Darkling:</b> The Contract's effects will not automatically end if one of the affected targets engages in behavior that constitutes a Breaking Point.<br /> <b>-Fairest:</b> By touching another person, the Fairest may make that target the object of the Obsession Condition.<br /> <b>-Grimm:</b> By writing down an idea, the Grimm may then use this Contract to make this idea disruptive to a group discussing it, giving the participants the Obsession Condition related to proving the superiority of their own ideas.<br /> <br /> <b>Catch:</b> Someone has previously killed another person to gain ownership of the object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T19:17:21-07:00","id":883394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883285#post883285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm. Why not both Attributes? It'd still be very heavy investment, considering how each Attribute dot costs 4 Experience to purchase.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing:</b> A Spelldrinker benefits from the 8-again rule on all kenning rolls, which are always free reflexive actions. If he successfully contests or resists a supernatural power used against him, he may retain it for later use within the scene. The Spelldrinker can store a number of such powers equal to his Wyrd, with any unused each granting one point of Glamour. He uses his own dots in Attributes and Skills when rolling Contracts, but does not roll his Wyrd for those he does not possess. When wielding t</span>he powers of other supernaturals (such as a Mage's spells or Kindred Disciplines), the Spelldrinker rolls Wits + Resolve instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still gives a fairly large potential pool for wielding other supernatural creatures' effects, even if it is a bit more expensive to raise two Attributes instead of an Attribute and a Skill. You could always go with something like &quot;half the original user's dicepool, rounded up&quot; for it, giving more potent effects a higher potency when wielded by the spelldrinker while still ensuring that the spelldrinker's ability to wield the secondhand powers would never outpace the original user's capabilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883285#post883285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edited. Though that does make me wonder if the element is still readily available for Windwalkers to use. I'm going to say yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that if you're outside, most likely the element would be present, unless you were in a truly dead area. If you were inside, though, I could see you needing either an open window or a fan of some sort to get things moving.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883285#post883285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad you like the name. Now, how's this revision?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>A Psyblade can spend Glamour or Willpower to use the Aura Reading Merit without any drawbacks, and doubles her effective Wyrd rating when contesting or resisting any supernatural powers which would detect, influence, or read her thoughts. Additionally, her unarmed attacks inflict lethal damage, and she can spend Glamour to have an unarmed attack inflict the Stunned Tilt for a number of turns equal to her Wyrd. Her victims must succeed on a Resolve + Composure roll in addition to spending Willpower if they wish to end the Tilt sooner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that giving the ability to inflict the Stunned Tilt so easily should not be coupled with the ability to make it harder to shrug off. A psyblade with enough Wyrd or Potent Kith could potentially keep an unlucky character Stunned until said character runs out of Willpower to even make the attempt to break free. It seemed more reasonable in the previous version, where it required the exceptional success in order to manage the feat. Hmmm... Have you considered making it that the psyblade can make an unarmed attack and spend Glamour to inflict the Tilt instead of doing damage with the attack, forcing the psyblade to choose between going for the kill and going for mind disruption in a given turn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T20:49:44-07:00","id":883442,"title":"","content":"I am liking your write-up for the Coveted. And the Contract you thought up for them.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T21:03:52-07:00","id":883454,"title":"","content":"Five more pages already? Let's see if I can offer some feedback without getting confused. If anyone would like feedback directed at other Kiths I missed, please mention me in your post with @ like I did below.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a>: First off, the quote for the Minotaurs is freaking <i>priceless</i>. It reminded me of that quote from Full Metal Jacket: &quot;I am...in a world...of shit&quot;. My only issue with this Kith is that it's based on a specific creature that doesn't offer a lot of room for different takes on the concept, or Miens. I think you could have something similar to the Minotaur as an Ogre or Beast with the Troll + Gargantuan Kiths. The Direction Sense and Trained Observer Merits wouldn't come free in that case, I know, and not every monstrous guardian will use Fast Talker 3 very often. But the combination of +1 to Presence, +[Wyrd/2] to Size with 1 glamour for the scene, +[Wyrd/2]L natural weapons and the generation of Safe Places with [Wyrd/2]L traps is impressive, and that's without going into Contracts.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a>: The Venator Kith is just awesome. It reminded me of Chris Pratt with the velociraptors in Jurassic World. I was going to suggest bonuses for Survival and Investigation, but dots in those Skills should be bought separately as part of the character's build. To get <i><b>really</b></i> good at dealing with animalistic hobgoblins and the Hedge in general, Professional Training (Outdoors-Man) is an excellent choice, as is Woodwalker/Woodblood/Farwalker/Roteater/Skogsra as a secondary Kith. I also like the Shepherd and Coveted Kiths (the latter is a different take on the Treasured Kith for the Fairest in 1ED, right?).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a>: White Oak Dragon has a point about Trivial Reworking not really fitting into Number-Watcher. I much prefer your Logician Kith. I would keep the +1 dot and raised cap for Intelligence, the instant calculations of quantities within line-of-sight and Interdisciplinary Specialty + Area Of Expertise (Mathematics). I would add the following to the Blessing: for 1 Glamour, they can roll for an Extended Action that is mostly Mental as an Instant Action if the Specialty Of Mathematics could apply (no use in combat or most social interactions). That's already a mighty Blessing right there. As I usually say, Skill Dots and Merits that fit the concept can usually be bought separately to leave room for more impressive things in the Blessings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-06-2016, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T21:12:40-07:00","id":883461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883394#post883394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That still gives a fairly large potential pool for wielding other supernatural creatures' effects, even if it is a bit more expensive to raise two Attributes instead of an Attribute and a Skill. You could always go with something like &quot;half the original user's dicepool, rounded up&quot; for it, giving more potent effects a higher potency when wielded by the spelldrinker while still ensuring that the spelldrinker's ability to wield the secondhand powers would never outpace the original user's capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is quite a challenging endeavor, alright. But the more this is done, the better the Kith will turn out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Anyway, I took your suggestion for rolling a single Attribute as the dice pool, and I struck a compromise. Regardless of the Attribute rolled, though, a Spelldrinker <i>still</i> has the option of spending Willpower to get a +3 dice bonus. That way, you still end up with a sizable dice pool if you have at least Wits or Resolve at 3 dots.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing:</b> A Spelldrinker benefits from the 8-again rule on all kenning rolls, which are always free reflexive actions. If he successfully contests or resists a supernatural power used against him, he may retain it for later use within the scene. The Spelldrinker can store a number of such powers equal to his Wyrd, with any unused each granting one point of Glamour. He uses his own dots in Attributes and Skills when rolling Contracts, but does not roll his Wyrd for those he does not possess. When wielding t</span>he powers of other supernaturals (such as a Mage's spells or Kindred Disciplines), the Spelldrinker instead rolls the higher of his Wits or Resolve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883394#post883394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that if you're outside, most likely the element would be present, unless you were in a truly dead area. If you were inside, though, I could see you needing either an open window or a fan of some sort to get things moving.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883394#post883394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that giving the ability to inflict the Stunned Tilt so easily should not be coupled with the ability to make it harder to shrug off. A psyblade with enough Wyrd or Potent Kith could potentially keep an unlucky character Stunned until said character runs out of Willpower to even make the attempt to break free. It seemed more reasonable in the previous version, where it required the exceptional success in order to manage the feat. Hmmm... Have you considered making it that the psyblade can make an unarmed attack and spend Glamour to inflict the Tilt instead of doing damage with the attack, forcing the psyblade to choose between going for the kill and going for mind disruption in a given turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>How about this one, instead?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>A Psyblade can spend Glamour or Willpower to use the Aura Reading Merit without any drawbacks, and doubles her effective Wyrd rating when contesting or resisting any supernatural powers which would detect, influence, or read her thoughts. Her unarmed attacks also inflict lethal damage, and she may spend Glamour during a successful Brawl attack to inflict the Stunned Tilt. If the attack roll scores an Exceptional Success, the attack also inflicts the Disoriented Condition for the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T21:23:48-07:00","id":883468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883454#post883454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Five more pages already? Let's see if I can offer some feedback without getting confused. If anyone would like feedback directed at other Kiths I missed, please mention me in your post with @ like I did below.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. A lot can happen, given time.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Also. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a>, you missed the Iceborn, Psyblade, Wavemaster, and Windwalker kiths from me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883454#post883454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a>: White Oak Dragon has a point about Trivial Reworking not really fitting into Number-Watcher. I much prefer your Logician Kith. I would keep the +1 dot and raised cap for Intelligence, the instant calculations of quantities within line-of-sight and Interdisciplinary Specialty + Area Of Expertise (Mathematics). I would add the following to the Blessing: for 1 Glamour, they can roll for an Extended Action that is mostly Mental as an Instant Action if the Specialty Of Mathematics could apply (no use in combat or most social interactions). That's already a mighty Blessing right there. As I usually say, Skill Dots and Merits that fit the concept can usually be bought separately to leave room for more impressive things in the Blessings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, all I'm missing is a Glamour expenditure aspect to the Logician blessing. So I'll probably revisit that later. Your suggestions, though, can definitely fit for a separate Auditor Kith. Let me see if I can put a Blessing write-up together....<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing:</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Auditors gain a free Academics or Science Specialty in Mathematics, as well as the Area of Expertise and Interdisciplinary Specialty Merits tied to it. They can also instantly count anything within their line of sight, and benefit from the 8-again rule on all Intelligence rolls. If they spend a point of Glamour while rolling for an Extended Mental Action, he may make rolls at a rate of one per turn if the Mathematics Specialty would apply. This power cannot be used in combat, though may apply in social interactions at the Storyteller's discretion.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-06-2016, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T21:37:33-07:00","id":883478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883442#post883442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am liking your write-up for the Coveted. And the Contract you thought up for them.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad that you liked them. My wife came up with the original idea for them a few weeks back, and I've spent the last couple weeks trying to come up with a name for them. Today, she gave me that as well, so I was finally able to write them up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883454#post883454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a>: The Venator Kith is just awesome. It reminded me of Chris Pratt with the velociraptors in Jurassic World. I was going to suggest bonuses for Survival and Investigation, but dots in those Skills should be bought separately as part of the character's build. To get <i><b>really</b></i> good at dealing with animalistic hobgoblins and the Hedge in general, Professional Training (Outdoors-Man) is an excellent choice, as is Woodwalker/Woodblood/Farwalker/Roteater/Skogsra as a secondary Kith. I also like the Shepherd and Coveted Kiths (the latter is a different take on the Treasured Kith for the Fairest in 1ED, right?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the Coveted are intended to be the changeling equivalent of Helen of Troy crossed with a bit of Andvaranaut with just a dash of the One Ring, although I'd have considered Treasured as a name for them if they hadn't already been an official kith. I'm glad that you liked them, and the Venator and Shepherd as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T21:54:12-07:00","id":883485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883461#post883461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is quite a challenging endeavor, alright. But the more this is done, the better the Kith will turn out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Anyway, I took your suggestion for rolling a single Attribute as the dice pool, and I struck a compromise. Regardless of the Attribute rolled, though, a Spelldrinker <i>still</i> has the option of spending Willpower to get a +3 dice bonus. That way, you still end up with a sizable dice pool if you have at least Wits or Resolve at 3 dots.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing:</b> A Spelldrinker benefits from the 8-again rule on all kenning rolls, which are always free reflexive actions. If he successfully contests or resists a supernatural power used against him, he may retain it for later use within the scene. The Spelldrinker can store a number of such powers equal to his Wyrd, with any unused each granting one point of Glamour. He uses his own dots in Attributes and Skills when rolling Contracts, but does not roll his Wyrd for those he does not possess. When wielding t</span>he powers of other supernaturals (such as a Mage's spells or Kindred Disciplines), the Spelldrinker instead rolls the higher of his Wits or Resolve.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one has, indeed, been a challenge. I think that it has come along quite nicely, though. If I might attempt a slight rewording of your blessing:<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Spelldrinker may make reflexive kenning rolls without spending Willpower regardless of his Clarity, and benefits from the 8-Again quality on these rolls. If he successfully contests or resists a supernatural power used against him, he may retain it for later use within the scene. The Spelldrinker can store a number of such powers equal to his Wyrd, with unused effects dissolving into one point of Glamour each at the end of the scene. He uses his own dots in Attributes and Skills when rolling for Contracts, but does not add his Wyrd for Contracts that he does not possess. The Spelldrinker's dice pool when wielding the powers of other supernaturals (such as a Mage's spells or Kindred Disciplines) is equal to the higher of his Wits or Resolve.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883461#post883461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about this one, instead?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>A Psyblade can spend Glamour or Willpower to use the Aura Reading Merit without any drawbacks, and doubles her effective Wyrd rating when contesting or resisting any supernatural powers which would detect, influence, or read her thoughts. Her unarmed attacks also inflict lethal damage, and she may spend Glamour during a successful Brawl attack to inflict the Stunned Tilt. If the attack roll scores an Exceptional Success, the attack also inflicts the Disoriented Condition for the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is the Disoriented Condition found? I didn't see it in the CofD core rulebook or BtP, which were the sources I immediately had on hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T22:07:09-07:00","id":883487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883454#post883454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Five more pages already? Let's see if I can offer some feedback without getting confused. If anyone would like feedback directed at other Kiths I missed, please mention me in your post with @ like I did below.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a>: First off, the quote for the Minotaurs is freaking <i>priceless</i>. It reminded me of that quote from Full Metal Jacket: &quot;I am...in a world...of shit&quot;. My only issue with this Kith is that it's based on a specific creature that doesn't offer a lot of room for different takes on the concept, or Miens. I think you could have something similar to the Minotaur as an Ogre or Beast with the Troll + Gargantuan Kiths. The Direction Sense and Trained Observer Merits wouldn't come free in that case, I know, and not every monstrous guardian will use Fast Talker 3 very often. But the combination of +1 to Presence, +[Wyrd/2] to Size with 1 glamour for the scene, +[Wyrd/2]L natural weapons and the generation of Safe Places with [Wyrd/2]L traps is impressive, and that's without going into Contracts.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a>: The Venator Kith is just awesome. It reminded me of Chris Pratt with the velociraptors in Jurassic World. I was going to suggest bonuses for Survival and Investigation, but dots in those Skills should be bought separately as part of the character's build. To get <i><b>really</b></i> good at dealing with animalistic hobgoblins and the Hedge in general, Professional Training (Outdoors-Man) is an excellent choice, as is Woodwalker/Woodblood/Farwalker/Roteater/Skogsra as a secondary Kith. I also like the Shepherd and Coveted Kiths (the latter is a different take on the Treasured Kith for the Fairest in 1ED, right?).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a>: White Oak Dragon has a point about Trivial Reworking not really fitting into Number-Watcher. I much prefer your Logician Kith. I would keep the +1 dot and raised cap for Intelligence, the instant calculations of quantities within line-of-sight and Interdisciplinary Specialty + Area Of Expertise (Mathematics). I would add the following to the Blessing: for 1 Glamour, they can roll for an Extended Action that is mostly Mental as an Instant Action if the Specialty Of Mathematics could apply (no use in combat or most social interactions). That's already a mighty Blessing right there. As I usually say, Skill Dots and Merits that fit the concept can usually be bought separately to leave room for more impressive things in the Blessings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mmm, true, it's kind of hard to come up with Miens, but not completely impossible. I went with some ideas for Minotaur that I've seen over the years. Some are just a simple half man / half bull. Others display such features but are distinctly carnivorous such as having claws and fangs. There was also this one movie that I forgot the name of (Immortals, I think?) Where the minotaur was just this psychopath who dressed like a bull in order to scare his enemies in battle.<br /> <br /> I decided to use all three interpretations for the Seemings that I listed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-06-2016, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T00:42:55-07:00","id":883552,"title":"","content":"Here is a new attempt at the wonderwell. I took away the ability to gain temporary Goblin Vows and replaced it with the ability to go into Experience debt in order to gain a new one, so that the wonderwell would still need to purchase any new capabilities gained through the pledge.<br /> <br /> <b>Wonderwell</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">I can make your fondest wish come true. There's just one tiny little favor you need to do for me in exchange.</span><br /> <br /> Arcadia is a place of beauty as well as terror, and all too often a desperate or greedy mortal is seduced into the waiting arms of the Gentry by the promise of untold power and riches. Some Keepers delight in the corruption of mortal wishes, while others feel that granting wishes is a fair bargain for a mortal's freedom. Wonderwells are often chosen to lure such mortals, granting their hearts' desires while slowly drawing them deeper into the Gentry's influence. Her close interactions with humanity makes it difficult for a wonderwell to forget her previous life, leading many to perpetual sorrow. Mortals who are moved to pity for their plight should be wary, though, as a wish for a wonderwell's freedom often comes at the price of their own.<br /> <br /> <b>-Beast:</b> They are covered in shimmering fish scales, with small fins at their joints.<br /> <b>-Darkling:</b> Attractive yet sinister figures, with small horns upon their heads and warm smiles upon their lips as their offer hangs in the air.<br /> <b>-Elemental:</b> Skin composed of gray bricks, with water pouring out from between the stones, and eyes that gleam like two silver coins.<br /> <b>-Fairest:</b> Beautiful men and women, clothed in nothing but beautiful jewels and sheer fabrics, with legs fading into mist.<br /> <b>-Ogre:</b> Huge and intimidating figures composed of smokeless fire, their colorful eyes promising reward and punishment alike.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Wonderwells are masters at navigating the tortuous network of obligations of the Wyrd in order to grant the desires of others. Each wonderwell gains two dots of the Goblin Vow Merit at character creation, and may choose to spend Glamour instead of Willpower when crafting a pledge with an aspect of the Wyrd. When entering into a pledge, the wonderwell may enter into Experience debt in order to gain a new Goblin Vow related to upholding her end of the pledge. The wonderwell may acquire more Goblin Vows than other changelings, up to a maximum of 5 + Wyrd. Additionally, whenever a wonderwell succeeds on a Social Skill roll against a character, she may spend a point of Glamour for an attempt to uncover the target's true desires. Roll the wonderwell's Wyrd contested by the target's Composure. On a success, the wonderwell learns whichever Aspiration that the target would most want known. On an exceptional success, the wonderwell learns all of the target's current Aspirations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T01:23:02-07:00","id":883568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883485#post883485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This one has, indeed, been a challenge. I think that it has come along quite nicely, though. If I might attempt a slight rewording of your blessing:<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Spelldrinker may make reflexive kenning rolls without spending Willpower regardless of his Clarity, and benefits from the 8-Again quality on these rolls. If he successfully contests or resists a supernatural power used against him, he may retain it for later use within the scene. The Spelldrinker can store a number of such powers equal to his Wyrd, with unused effects dissolving into one point of Glamour each at the end of the scene. He uses his own dots in Attributes and Skills when rolling for Contracts, but does not add his Wyrd for Contracts that he does not possess. The Spelldrinker's dice pool when wielding the powers of other supernaturals (such as a Mage's spells or Kindred Disciplines) is equal to the higher of his Wits or Resolve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely liking this. Thanks for the rewording, man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883485#post883485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is the Disoriented Condition found? I didn't see it in the CofD core rulebook or BtP, which were the sources I immediately had on hand.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#9EA0B1\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Disoriented </span></span><i>[ Demon: The Descent -- Page 211 ]</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Your character cannot get her bearings and dealing with simple tasks is daunting. The character is at a -2 penalty to any Physical action. She can defend herself normally, but her disorientation prevents her from making ranged attacks at all.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> The character finds something to help her orient herself to her surroundings, such as a familiar landmark or a friend. If a supernatural power caused this Condition, then it resolves when the power ends.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T07:38:04-07:00","id":883757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883568#post883568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely liking this. Thanks for the rewording, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. I'm glad you liked it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883568#post883568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#9EA0B1\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Disoriented </span></span><i>[ Demon: The Descent -- Page 211 ]</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Your character cannot get her bearings and dealing with simple tasks is daunting. The character is at a -2 penalty to any Physical action. She can defend herself normally, but her disorientation prevents her from making ranged attacks at all.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> The character finds something to help her orient herself to her surroundings, such as a familiar landmark or a friend. If a supernatural power caused this Condition, then it resolves when the power ends.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. It seems like a pretty potent effect. As the kith stands, I think that the flavor text of them not being hardy in open combat probably doesn't fit so well, as they are more potent than some of the other lethal damage dealing kiths that are supposed to excel at such things, like the Bloodbrute. They aren't weaker than the other combat kiths, they are equal to or better in open combat, with further benefits against psychic or ranged attack-specializing opponents. Perhaps making the Disoriented Condition last for a number of turns equal to her Wyrd on an exceptional success might help to balance it a bit. With it lasting for the scene, if she can manage to inflict Stunned with a single success on her first attack, she can go for an all-out attack with her second and effectively take out any ranged combatant for good, such as a deadeye, a fae sorceress with an affinity for fireballs or lightning bolts, or a fire-breathing dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:00:01-07:00","id":884160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=883757#post883757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. It seems like a pretty potent effect. As the kith stands, I think that the flavor text of them not being hardy in open combat probably doesn't fit so well, as they are more potent than some of the other lethal damage dealing kiths that are supposed to excel at such things, like the Bloodbrute. They aren't weaker than the other combat kiths, they are equal to or better in open combat, with further benefits against psychic or ranged attack-specializing opponents. Perhaps making the Disoriented Condition last for a number of turns equal to her Wyrd on an exceptional success might help to balance it a bit. With it lasting for the scene, if she can manage to inflict Stunned with a single success on her first attack, she can go for an all-out attack with her second and effectively take out any ranged combatant for good, such as a deadeye, a fae sorceress with an affinity for fireballs or lightning bolts, or a fire-breathing dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this work better?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <u><b>Psyblade</b></u><br /> <i>&quot;The mind can be a delicate thing. But mine is as sharp as any blade.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Assassins and precision fighters, those made into Psyblades by their Keepers were charged with cutting down key targets in order to sow chaos among enemy forces. Their hands and feet were weapons in themselves, and their strikes could cripple an opponent by disrupting the balance of his energies. A Psyblade who escapes, however, did so by briefly stunning her Keeper. But even after emerging through the Thorns, there are many who would covet her talents.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Beast:</b> A humanoid eel whose veins and arteries pulse with electricity.<br /> <b>\u2022 Elemental:</b> A vaguely humanoid shadow whose hands light up with ethereal flame when it strikes.<br /> <b>\u2022 Fairest:</b> A dark-haired woman garbed in form-fitting armor, who slowly weakens her foes with each punch and every palm strike.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>Blessing: </b>A Psyblade can spend Glamour or Willpower to use the Aura Reading Merit without any drawbacks, and doubles her effective Wyrd rating when contesting or resisting any supernatural powers which would detect, influence, or read her thoughts. Her unarmed attacks also inflict lethal damage, and she may spend Glamour during a successful Brawl attack to inflict the Stunned Tilt. If the attack roll scores an Exceptional Success, the attack also inflicts the Disoriented Condition for a number of turns equal to 1 + half her Wyrd, rounded up.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:37:12-07:00","id":884180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=884160#post884160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does this work better?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <u><b>Psyblade</b></u><br /> <i>&amp;quot;The mind can be a delicate thing. But mine is as sharp as any blade.&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> Assassins and precision fighters, those made into Psyblades by their Keepers were charged with cutting down key targets in order to sow chaos among enemy forces. Their hands and feet were weapons in themselves, and their strikes could cripple an opponent by disrupting the balance of his energies. A Psyblade who escapes, however, did so by briefly stunning her Keeper. But even after emerging through the Thorns, there are many who would covet her talents.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Beast:</b> A humanoid eel whose veins and arteries pulse with electricity.<br /> <b>\u2022 Elemental:</b> A vaguely humanoid shadow whose hands light up with ethereal flame when it strikes.<br /> <b>\u2022 Fairest:</b> A dark-haired woman garbed in form-fitting armor, who slowly weakens her foes with each punch and every palm strike.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>Blessing: </b>A Psyblade can spend Glamour or Willpower to use the Aura Reading Merit without any drawbacks, and doubles her effective Wyrd rating when contesting or resisting any supernatural powers which would detect, influence, or read her thoughts. Her unarmed attacks also inflict lethal damage, and she may spend Glamour during a successful Brawl attack to inflict the Stunned Tilt. If the attack roll scores an Exceptional Success, the attack also inflicts the Disoriented Condition for a number of turns equal to 1 + half her Wyrd, rounded up.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>That works much better, both mechanically and flavor-wise. Well done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T00:25:12-07:00","id":884435,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> <br /> Made some updates to the Logician kith blessing. And I also reworded the Doppleganger Blessing somewhat. Critique is appreciated, as always. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Doppleganger</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> By spending a point of Glamour, a Doppelganger can create a duplicate of himself. Each duplicate has a number of Health dots equal to the changeling's Wyrd, and will persist for the duration of the scene unless dismissed sooner. They also act instinctively to assist the changeling, functioning as secondary actors in teamwork actions involving a Physical Skill. The Doppelganger may also take full control of a single duplicate by spending another point of Glamour. While controlling the duplicate, he cannot engage in any strenuous activities with his own body, and will suffer a -3 distraction penalty on all other actions. The Doppelganger may only control one duplicate in this manner at a time, and have up to a number of active duplicates in a scene equal to half his Wyrd, rounded up. Each duplicate after the first incurs a -1 distraction penalty on all actions (which stacks with the penalty for taking full control), and causes a point of lethal damage to the original if killed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Logician</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Logician gains the Common Sense Merit, and a dot of Intelligence which can take him above the usual limitations imposed by his Wyrd. He may also apply the benefits of Common Sense once per scene, and takes no penalties to rolls which use Mental skills. If he spends a point of Glamour, he may add his Wyrd as a dice bonus to all rolls for memorizing or recalling information for a scene.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> I proposed the lethal damage per duplicate killed for the Doppleganger as an additional deterrent against overusing the kith's blessing. For the changeling, this isn't some expendable tool at his disposal. It's a copy that is, for most intents and purposes, him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-07-2016, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T07:29:14-07:00","id":884603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=884435#post884435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a><br /> Made some updates to the Logician kith blessing. And I also reworded the Doppleganger Blessing somewhat. Critique is appreciated, as always. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Doppleganger</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> By spending a point of Glamour, a Doppelganger can create a duplicate of himself. Each duplicate has a number of Health dots equal to the changeling's Wyrd, and will persist for the duration of the scene unless dismissed sooner. They also act instinctively to assist the changeling, functioning as secondary actors in teamwork actions involving a Physical Skill. The Doppelganger may also take full control of a single duplicate by spending another point of Glamour. While controlling the duplicate, he cannot engage in any strenuous activities with his own body, and will suffer a -3 distraction penalty on all other actions. The Doppelganger may only control one duplicate in this manner at a time, and have up to a number of active duplicates in a scene equal to half his Wyrd, rounded up. Each duplicate after the first incurs a -1 distraction penalty on all actions (which stacks with the penalty for taking full control), and causes a point of lethal damage to the original if killed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Logician</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Logician gains the Common Sense Merit, and a dot of Intelligence which can take him above the usual limitations imposed by his Wyrd. He may also apply the benefits of Common Sense once per scene, and takes no penalties to rolls which use Mental skills. If he spends a point of Glamour, he may add his Wyrd as a dice bonus to all rolls for memorizing or recalling information for a scene.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> I proposed the lethal damage per duplicate killed for the Doppleganger as an additional deterrent against overusing the kith's blessing. For the changeling, this isn't some expendable tool at his disposal. It's a copy that is, for most intents and purposes, him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your addition of the lethal damage for a duplicate being killed. I had worried before that the kith might have been a bit too powerful, and that is actually a pretty good way to balance it a bit. Allow me to take your suggestion and reword it a bit:<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> By spending a point of Glamour, a Doppelganger is able to create a duplicate of himself. Each duplicate has a number of Health levels equal to the changeling's Wyrd, and will persist for the duration of the scene unless dismissed sooner. The Doppelganger may create up to half his Wyrd in duplicates, and each will instinctively act to assist the changeling, functioning as secondary actors in teamwork actions involving a Physical Skill. Each duplicate created after the first will impose a -1 distraction penalty on all actions, which is cumulative with any other distraction penalties. The Doppelganger may also take full control of a single duplicate by spending another point of Glamour. While actively controlling the duplicate, he cannot engage in any strenuous activities with his own body, and will suffer a -3 distraction penalty on all other actions. Only one duplicate may be controlled in this manner at a time. If a duplicate is killed, the Doppelganger suffers a point of lethal damage from the shock. If the Doppelganger is rendered unconscious, all duplicates that are not being actively controlled are automatically dismissed.<br /> <br /> The changes you made to the Logician make sense, although allowing Common Sense to be used once per scene could make it pretty potent for cutting through any mysteries. What if it was something like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Logician gains a dot of Intelligence, which can take him above the usual limitations imposed by his Wyrd. He also gains the Common Sense Merit, and may use it a number of times per chapter equal to his Wyrd, although never more than once in a scene. The Logician does not suffer untrained penalties for the use of Mental Skills, and by spending a point of Glamour, he may add his Wyrd as bonus dice to all rolls for memorizing or recalling information for the duration of the scene.<br /> <br /> This would make a Wyrd 1 Logician have the Merit as it usually functions, but a second dot of Wyrd or even a single dot of Potent Kith would double his capabilities with it compared to anyone else, and it would only go up from there.<br /> <br /> What did you think of my new version of the Wonderwell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T08:04:01-07:00","id":884631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=884603#post884603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your addition of the lethal damage for a duplicate being killed. I had worried before that the kith might have been a bit too powerful, and that is actually a pretty good way to balance it a bit. Allow me to take your suggestion and reword it a bit:<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> By spending a point of Glamour, a Doppelganger is able to create a duplicate of himself. Each duplicate has a number of Health levels equal to the changeling's Wyrd, and will persist for the duration of the scene unless dismissed sooner. The Doppelganger may create up to half his Wyrd in duplicates, and each will instinctively act to assist the changeling, functioning as secondary actors in teamwork actions involving a Physical Skill. Each duplicate created after the first will impose a -1 distraction penalty on all actions, which is cumulative with any other distraction penalties. The Doppelganger may also take full control of a single duplicate by spending another point of Glamour. While actively controlling the duplicate, he cannot engage in any strenuous activities with his own body, and will suffer a -3 distraction penalty on all other actions. Only one duplicate may be controlled in this manner at a time. If a duplicate is killed, the Doppelganger suffers a point of lethal damage from the shock. If the Doppelganger is rendered unconscious, all duplicates that are not being actively controlled are automatically dismissed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. We can definitely go with this, and I'm liking the addition of a Doppelganger's duplicates fading should he fall unconscious. It definitely adds another weakness that adds depth to a character concept that allows one to be like Flash's Multiplex, or the Inhuman, Alisha, from Agents of SHIELD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=884603#post884603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The changes you made to the Logician make sense, although allowing Common Sense to be used once per scene could make it pretty potent for cutting through any mysteries. What if it was something like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Logician gains a dot of Intelligence, which can take him above the usual limitations imposed by his Wyrd. He also gains the Common Sense Merit, and may use it a number of times per chapter equal to his Wyrd, although never more than once in a scene. The Logician does not suffer untrained penalties for the use of Mental Skills, and by spending a point of Glamour, he may add his Wyrd as bonus dice to all rolls for memorizing or recalling information for the duration of the scene.<br /> <br /> This would make a Wyrd 1 Logician have the Merit as it usually functions, but a second dot of Wyrd or even a single dot of Potent Kith would double his capabilities with it compared to anyone else, and it would only go up from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I should have probably gone with the more uses in a chapter route in the first place. Again, thanks for the revision. I'll paste them on the Doc as soon as I can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=884603#post884603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did you think of my new version of the Wonderwell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely liking parts of the revised Blessing, but I may have a few alternative write-ups for it. I'll post them here once I've worked them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:42:11-07:00","id":885005,"title":"","content":"<b>Baalor:</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I'm warning you, inspector. Abandon this investigation. If you keep digging, you're not going to like what you uncover!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> In the Arcadian realm of dreams, sometimes people get the brilliant idea to dig their way under places they weren't supposed to gain access to. From impenetrable vaults, to the roots of the Hedge itself. Changelings who became Baalor were used as subterranean guardians for these ancient tunnel systems. With the countenance of Biblical demons, they terrorized any who dug too deeply beneath Arcadia's soil. One day, the Baalor chased its prey all the way back to the surface, where it soon managed to escape its underground imprisonment!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Cloven hooves, bright red fur, curling horns, monstrous claws and the wings of a dragon. This creature resembles the traditional portrayal of a devil.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Bright red skin, black horns and claws, a prehensile tail, handsome features and a gaunt physique. He has all the charismatic charm of Satan himself, right up to when he screws you over for personal benefit!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> Skin of brimstone and muscles of fire, their roar is filled with the screams of hell itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Baalor was the last thing anybody wanted to encounter underground with perhaps the True Fae being the only exception. Their unarmed attacks inflict Lethal damage and they gain access to two dots in Cloak of the Elements (Fire) for free at character creation. Additionally, they only need 3 successes to gain the exceptional benefit, instead of the usual 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-10-2016, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:36:19-07:00","id":885427,"title":"","content":"I am finally making the attempt to update one of my first edition kiths. Critique is welcome.<br /> <br /> <b>Stitchborn</b><br /> <br /> Don't worry about me! It's just a scratch! Keep going!<br /> <br /> Before their Durances, most stitchborn had either a soft and comforting personality or a keen fashion sense. These hapless changelings were taken to be made into the bizarre fripperies of the Gentry or plush accessories to decorate their luxurious palaces. Despite the torments they suffered, most stitchborn are able to maintain their original personality traits upon their escape.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Burlap skin covers a thin frame, with stalks of straw jutting out of his raw wounds.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Her skin is made of the finest black silk, stitched together with beautiful gold and silver threads.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> His linen skin is covered with colorful embroidered images of wondrous tales.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> Beige mohair fur has been stitched and restitched to the ragged overstuffed figure, and one button eye is missing.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A stitchborn gains the Raiment of Moon and Stars Contract for free, and may ignore a number of points of bashing damage equal to his Wyrd each turn. Additionally, the stichborn may make attempts to repair damage to his flesh once per day. The changeling may sew or direct another to sew any rips in his flesh, rolling Dexterity + Crafts + Wyrd. Each success on this roll downgrades one level of lethal damage to bashing or repairs one level of bashing damage. This action requires a minimum of three turns for each wound that the character is currently suffering to complete, and suffers normal penalties for lack of proper equipment if the stichborn does not have a sewing kit available.<br /> <br /> <b>New Contract</b><br /> <br /> <b>Raiment of Moon and Stars (..)</b><br /> <br /> By transforming ordinary clothing into a Hedgespun raiment of impossible beauty, the changeling ensures that the wearer will be the belle of the ball.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Glamour<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Crafts + Wyrd<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The clothing created is completely inappropriate, and the changeling will be unable to remove it until the sun next rises.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> No new article of clothing is created.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The changeling transforms an ordinary set of clothing into a wondrously beautiful set of finery, seemingly composed of impossible materials such as gemstones or the sky at twilight. The outfit gives the wearer an equipment bonus equal to the changeling's Wyrd for Social rolls intending to gain or keep attention. The outfit remains until the sun next rises, at which point it reverts to tattered rags.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The finery created is especially durable, remaining for a number of days equal to the changeling's Wyrd. Additionally, for the first night, the finery will give a single point of Armor to the wearer.<br /> <br /> <b>-Darkling:</b> The Darkling may create an outfit that blends into the crowd, giving the wearer a bonus to avoid attention rather than gain it.<br /> <b>-Fairest:</b> The Fairest uses the higher of her Presence or her Wyrd for the bonus granted by this Contract.<br /> <b>-Wizened:</b> By spending a point of Willpower, the industrious Wizened may create one outfit for each success rolled on the Contract's activation.<br /> <br /> <b>Catch:</b> The changeling is bestowing the outfit as a gift within an unusual container that the recipient has never seen opened. The outfit persist within until it is opened, at which point its duration begins as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:50:15-07:00","id":887217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=885005#post885005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Baalor:</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I'm warning you, inspector. Abandon this investigation. If you keep digging, you're not going to like what you uncover!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> In the Arcadian realm of dreams, sometimes people get the brilliant idea to dig their way under places they weren't supposed to gain access to. From impenetrable vaults, to the roots of the Hedge itself. Changelings who became Baalor were used as subterranean guardians for these ancient tunnel systems. With the countenance of Biblical demons, they terrorized any who dug too deeply beneath Arcadia's soil. One day, the Baalor chased its prey all the way back to the surface, where it soon managed to escape its underground imprisonment!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Cloven hooves, bright red fur, curling horns, monstrous claws and the wings of a dragon. This creature resembles the traditional portrayal of a devil.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Bright red skin, black horns and claws, a prehensile tail, handsome features and a gaunt physique. He has all the charismatic charm of Satan himself, right up to when he screws you over for personal benefit!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> Skin of brimstone and muscles of fire, their roar is filled with the screams of hell itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Baalor was the last thing anybody wanted to encounter underground with perhaps the True Fae being the only exception. Their unarmed attacks inflict Lethal damage and they gain access to a dot of Cloak of the Elements (Fire) for free at character creation. Additionally, they may use Cloak of the Elements (Fire) for free as opposed to spending a point of Glamour!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is an interesting idea. Where did you get the name for these guys? It sounds very similar to Balor, but it doesn't have the same sort of flavor. Have you considered tying it in to other dangerous fire creatures, such as the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherufe\" target=\"_blank\">Cherufe</a>? On the blessing, I think that giving them the ability to use the Contract for free is a bit potent. Perhaps giving them double duration or exceptional success on 3 instead of 5 successes instead would work well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:14:49-07:00","id":887271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=887217#post887217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is an interesting idea. Where did you get the name for these guys? It sounds very similar to Balor, but it doesn't have the same sort of flavor. Have you considered tying it in to other dangerous fire creatures, such as the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherufe\" target=\"_blank\">Cherufe</a>? On the blessing, I think that giving them the ability to use the Contract for free is a bit potent. Perhaps giving them double duration or exceptional success on 3 instead of 5 successes instead would work well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also. Maybe you could give two dots in the Contract for free. I might go for the double duration benefit, too, to differentiate it somewhat from other Kiths whose blessings lower the Exceptional threshold of certain Contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T12:01:50-07:00","id":887365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=887217#post887217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It is an interesting idea. Where did you get the name for these guys? It sounds very similar to Balor, but it doesn't have the same sort of flavor. Have you considered tying it in to other dangerous fire creatures, such as the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherufe\" target=\"_blank\">Cherufe</a>? On the blessing, I think that giving them the ability to use the Contract for free is a bit potent. Perhaps giving them double duration or exceptional success on 3 instead of 5 successes instead would work well?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It can be spelled either way, Balor or Baalor. An alternate name is also Balar.<br /> <br /> It's appeared in both Lord of the Rings (under the name Balrog), as well as Dungeons and Dragons, and is actually associated with Irish mythology. Apparently, Balor was known as king among the Fomorians.<br /> <br /> As for the blessing, I'll go with the 2 free dots + exceptional success idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-10-2016, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:21:40-07:00","id":888277,"title":"","content":"Here is my attempt at a kith that calls upon the &quot;Devil at the Crossroads&quot; archetype that is sometimes found in fairy tales:<br /> <br /> <b>Oathdevil</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Silence! I don't want to hear your protests or excuses. You agreed to our bargain. I'm just here to collect.</span><br /> <br /> Woe be to those who encounter the oathdevil at the crossroads, for his friendly demeanor obscures the hidden barbs of his agreements. These changelings, chosen for their literal minds and attention to detail, were often employed by their Keepers to track and punish their wayward servants. Upon escape, an oathdevil is likely to weave himself an intricate web of influence and owed favors in whichever freehold he claims as home.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> She is inhumanly beautiful, with a lovely voice and seductive mannerisms that distract from the dainty horns upon her head and the fire in her eyes.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> His vellum skin is covered in minute contractual language, with larger signatures inked in blood foreshadowing the fates of those who would cross him.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A large and menacing figure, with two spiraling horns and three golden hairs upon his head.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> His fiber optic tail twitches of its own accord, and his horns are constructed from the bones of an oathbreaker.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> An oathdevil is a dangerous changeling to cross, as the pledges that he creates carry severe consequences. When sealing a statement, the sealing is automatically considered strengthened. By spending Willpower to strengthen it further, the oathdevil may impose the Leveraged Condition on the subject. This Condition only lasts for the duration of the sealing, but will become Persistent if the pledge is broken. While the subject is Leveraged, the subject's resistance to the oathdevil's Contracts suffers a -3 penalty. Additionally, the oathdevil may track the subject as though they shared a personal oath together. By spending a point of Glamour in the presence of someone with the Oathbreaker Condition, the oathdevil may apply the Leveraged Condition, which persists until the Oathbreaker Condition is resolved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":".  Edited the blessing to make the penalty against Contracts have a set penalty rather than a variable one. 05-29-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T16:54:19-07:00","id":888657,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=888277#post888277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is my attempt at a kith that calls upon the &quot;Devil at the Crossroads&quot; archetype that is sometimes found in fairy tales:<br /> <br /> <b>Oathdevil</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Silence! I don't want to hear your protests or excuses. You agreed to our bargain. I'm just here to collect.</span><br /> <br /> Woe be to those who encounter the oathdevil at the crossroads, for his friendly demeanor obscures the hidden barbs of his agreements. These changelings, chosen for their literal minds and attention to detail, were often employed by their Keepers to track and punish their wayward servants. Upon escape, an oathdevil is likely to weave himself an intricate web of influence and owed favors in whichever freehold he claims as home.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> She is inhumanly beautiful, with a lovely voice and seductive mannerisms that distract from the dainty horns upon her head and the fire in her eyes.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> His vellum skin is covered in minute contractual language, with larger signatures inked in blood foreshadowing the fates of those who would cross him.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A large and menacing figure, with two spiraling horns and three golden hairs upon his head.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> His fiber optic tail twitches of its own accord, and his horns are constructed from the bones of an oathbreaker.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> An oathdevil is a dangerous changeling to cross, as the pledges that he creates carry severe consequences. When sealing a statement, the sealing is automatically considered strengthened. By spending Willpower to strengthen it further, the oathdevil may impose the Leveraged Condition on the subject. This Condition only lasts for the duration of the sealing, but will become Persistent if the pledge is broken. While the subject is Leveraged, the subject's resistance to the oathdevil's Contracts suffers a penalty equal to half the oathdevil's Wyrd, rounded up. Additionally, the oathdevil may track the subject as though they shared a personal oath together. By spending a point of Glamour in the presence of someone with the Oathbreaker Condition, the oathdevil may apply the Leveraged Condition, which persists until the Oathbreaker Condition is resolved.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dang. I'll have to come back to this later, but imagine how effective a pledgesmith the Oathdevil could be if Dual-Kith'd with the Lionheart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T17:57:41-07:00","id":888707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=888657#post888657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Dang. I'll have to come back to this later, but imagine how effective a pledgesmith the Oathdevil could be if Dual-Kith'd with the Lionheart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a good dang or a bad dang? Yeah, coupled with Lionheart, it could be pretty effective. It would also pair quite nicely with the Wonderwell, to maximize that &quot;deal with the devil&quot; flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T21:02:16-07:00","id":888817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=888707#post888707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that a good dang or a bad dang? Yeah, coupled with Lionheart, it could be pretty effective. It would also pair quite nicely with the Wonderwell, to maximize that &quot;deal with the devil&quot; flavor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good dang. And the Oathdevil's blessing makes me think of a partial conversion of the Nemesis Pledges from 1E, given how it lowers one's Resistance to the changeling's Contracts so long as he suffers the Leveraged Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:30:50-07:00","id":889184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=888817#post888817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good dang. And the Oathdevil's blessing makes me think of a partial conversion of the Nemesis Pledges from 1E, given how it lowers one's Resistance to the changeling's Contracts so long as he suffers the Leveraged Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm glad to hear it. The Nemesis Pledges were one of the things I'd been thinking about when I was designing their blessing. I wanted to make it so that the Oathdevil's blessing would encourage subjects to actually carry through with their agreements rather than breaking their word to the Oathdevil, given how frequently fairy tale characters weep even as they hand over a loved one to uphold a deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:17:28-07:00","id":891402,"title":"","content":"<b>Windrider:</b><br /> <br /> <i>You don't have the balls to tame me!</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Long seen as a symbol of nobility and pride by magical and mundane parties alike, those who became Windriders were used as mounts to carry their masters across sky and sea. Most of them were created by combining the features of a predatory bird with some other type of animal. Both parts blending seamlessly together and being fully functional as if such hybrids were natural creatures. Only the most regal were permitted to harness them, while anyone undeserving was gored in the attempt. Their escape came on the day when their esteemed masters were judged unworthy to saddle them, thus prompting the Windrider to rebel! Although they value their new freedom, they still offer rides to those who have earned their trust.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A gryphon fit for a king. From the torso upwards is the body of a giant eagle, but from the waist down they have the legs and tail of a lion.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre: </b>The wings of a dragon and the body of a lion, this manticore tragically lost its scorpion's tail during aerial combat.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Angelic wings attached to the body of a horse, they now run wild and free across the sky, forever denying the bridle of their captors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Windrider often bare the features of two or more dangerous animals. Their unarmed attacks inflict Lethal damage due to their savage claws and fangs. Additionally, their time spent as airborne steeds allows to fly at twice their normal movement speed for six times their Wyrd in minutes. Spending a point of Glamour will double this duration. While flying, they may carry a passenger who is within their capacity to lift, but suffer -1 speed for each size rating of the passenger in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-18-2016, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T13:42:42-07:00","id":891975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=891402#post891402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Windrider:</b><br /> <br /> <i>You don't have the balls to tame me!</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Long seen as a symbol of nobility and pride by magical and mundane parties alike, those who became Windriders were used as mounts to carry their masters across sky and sea. Most of them were created by combining the features of a predatory bird with some other type of animal. Both parts being scaled to compatible size, of course. Only the most regal were permitted to harness them, while anyone undeserving was gored in the attempt. Their escape came on the day when their esteemed masters were judged unworthy to saddle them, thus prompting the Windrider to rebel!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A gryphon fit for a king. From the torso upwards is the body of a giant eagle, but from the waist down they have the legs and tail of a lion.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre: </b>The wings of a dragon and the body of a lion, this manticore tragically lost its scorpion's tail during aerial combat.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Angelic wings attached to the body of a horse, they now run wild and free across the sky, forever denying the bridle of their captors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Windrider often bare the features of two or more dangerous animals. Their unarmed attacks inflict Lethal damage due to their savage claws and fangs. Additionally, their time spent as airborne steeds allows to spend a point of Glamour to fly at a speed in yards equal to x3 their Wyrd for the rest of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is an interesting concept. I don't think that you need to specify that the multiple animal parts are scaled, as I think that that would be assumed. A gryphon that only had the wings of an ordinary eagle on a full-sized lion body would look pretty ridiculous, after all. Perhaps instead, refer to the perfect grace with which the parts seamlessly meld? The idea that they were a noble kith that only allowed the worthy to ride is a fascinating one. The blessing comes across as a more potent version of the windwing's blessing. For endurance, the windrider wins hands down, getting an entire scene for a single point of Glamour as opposed to a few minutes. At their lowest level, a windwing can win at speed (minimum 7 with 1 Strength, 1 Dexterity, and no Fleet of Foot) against the windrider (minimum 3 at Wyrd 1 with Potent Kith 0), but even with that in mind, at Wyrd 1 with Potent Kith 5 the windrider (Speed 18) can match or exceed any windwing below Wyrd 6 (Speed 18 at Strength 5, Dexterity 5, and Fleet of Foot 3). At the highest level, for considerably less Experience investment, windriders (Speed 45 at Wyrd 10, Potent Kith 5) easily exceed the windwing (Speed 38 at Wyrd 10, Strength 10, Dexterity 10, Fleet of Foot 3). Looking at the rest of the blessings, windriders gain Lethal damage on attacks, compared to perching on things that could hold a small child and the ability to fly for a couple turns without Glamour. I think perhaps the blessing needs a bit more refining in order to balance it with the others. Still, I think this has a lot of potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T15:05:12-07:00","id":892044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=891975#post891975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It is an interesting concept. I don't think that you need to specify that the multiple animal parts are scaled, as I think that that would be assumed. A gryphon that only had the wings of an ordinary eagle on a full-sized lion body would look pretty ridiculous, after all. Perhaps instead, refer to the perfect grace with which the parts seamlessly meld? The idea that they were a noble kith that only allowed the worthy to ride is a fascinating one. The blessing comes across as a more potent version of the windwing's blessing. For endurance, the windrider wins hands down, getting an entire scene for a single point of Glamour as opposed to a few minutes. At their lowest level, a windwing can win at speed (minimum 7 with 1 Strength, 1 Dexterity, and no Fleet of Foot) against the windrider (minimum 3 at Wyrd 1 with Potent Kith 0), but even with that in mind, at Wyrd 1 with Potent Kith 5 the windrider (Speed 18) can match or exceed any windwing below Wyrd 6 (Speed 18 at Strength 5, Dexterity 5, and Fleet of Foot 3). At the highest level, for considerably less Experience investment, windriders (Speed 45 at Wyrd 10, Potent Kith 5) easily exceed the windwing (Speed 38 at Wyrd 10, Strength 10, Dexterity 10, Fleet of Foot 3). Looking at the rest of the blessings, windriders gain Lethal damage on attacks, compared to perching on things that could hold a small child and the ability to fly for a couple turns without Glamour. I think perhaps the blessing needs a bit more refining in order to balance it with the others. Still, I think this has a lot of potential.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What would you suggest scaling the speed down to (terrible at calculations)? I'm thinking of tweaking it so that they can carry another person with them during flight, as that would fit their Kith.<br /> <br /> As for the needing to be worthy part, that came inspired by Harry Potter and other tales of majestic beasts who only allowed a chosen few to mount them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T01:02:04-07:00","id":893112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=892044#post892044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What would you suggest scaling the speed down to (terrible at calculations)? I'm thinking of tweaking it so that they can carry another person with them during flight, as that would fit their Kith.<br /> <br /> As for the needing to be worthy part, that came inspired by Harry Potter and other tales of majestic beasts who only allowed a chosen few to mount them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll need to give that a little bit of thought. Ultimately, I think that the kith should pair well with windwing or lurkglider for Dual-Kith purposes, so the blessing for the windriders should synergize well with it. Perhaps start it off at a speed equal to their normal speed, and reduce it by the size of a passenger from there? Then they could gain a speed boost and improved Defense by pairing it with windwing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T06:50:56-07:00","id":893260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=893112#post893112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll need to give that a little bit of thought. Ultimately, I think that the kith should pair well with windwing or lurkglider for Dual-Kith purposes, so the blessing for the windriders should synergize well with it. Perhaps start it off at a speed equal to their normal speed, and reduce it by the size of a passenger from there? Then they could gain a speed boost and improved Defense by pairing it with windwing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright, I edited the flying description. Reduced the speed to twice their normal movement and included the part about lowering the speed further based on the passenger's size. How's that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T09:37:02-07:00","id":893389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=893260#post893260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Alright, I edited the flying description. Reduced the speed to twice their normal movement and included the part about lowering the speed further based on the passenger's size. How's that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's an improvement. This makes them the equals to windwings in speed while still maintaining the windriders' superior endurance, rather than simply superior over all. Superior endurance makes sense, given that they were aerial mounts. The windwings aren't any faster than the windriders, but they are still more maneuverable, which does give them a small benefit that Dual-Kith could still grant to a windrider that wanted to maximize flight capabilities. Effectively, the difference between them is that the windriders are long-range battle flyers (enhanced endurance, Lethal damage, passenger option), while windwings are short-range defensive flyers (low endurance, improved Defense, light weight perching). Twice the movement rate does make the loss of speed from a passenger largely negligible, though. Still, it is a definite improvement over the previous version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T10:02:37-07:00","id":893401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=893389#post893389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's an improvement. This makes them the equals to windwings in speed while still maintaining the windriders' superior endurance, rather than simply superior over all. Superior endurance makes sense, given that they were aerial mounts. The windwings aren't any faster than the windriders, but they are still more maneuverable, which does give them a small benefit that Dual-Kith could still grant to a windrider that wanted to maximize flight capabilities. Effectively, the difference between them is that the windriders are long-range battle flyers (enhanced endurance, Lethal damage, passenger option), while windwings are short-range defensive flyers (low endurance, improved Defense, light weight perching). Twice the movement rate does make the loss of speed from a passenger largely negligible, though. Still, it is a definite improvement over the previous version.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Glad to hear it. I thought giving them double flight speed was appropriate because flying should be faster than running; at least the way I understand it. And it makes me smile imagining one of these guys carrying a motley member into battle during a Hedge raid. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-18-2016, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T16:19:19-07:00","id":893711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=891402#post891402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Windrider:</b><br /> <i>You don't have the balls to tame me!</i><br /> <br /> Long seen as a symbol of nobility and pride by magical and mundane parties alike, those who became Windriders were used as mounts to carry their masters across sky and sea. Most of them were created by combining the features of a predatory bird with some other type of animal. Both parts blending seamlessly together and being fully functional as if such hybrids were natural creatures. Only the most regal were permitted to harness them, while anyone undeserving was gored in the attempt. Their escape came on the day when their esteemed masters were judged unworthy to saddle them, thus prompting the Windrider to rebel!<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A gryphon fit for a king. From the torso upwards is the body of a giant eagle, but from the waist down they have the legs and tail of a lion.<br /> <b>Ogre: </b>The wings of a dragon and the body of a lion, this manticore tragically lost its scorpion's tail during aerial combat.<br /> <b>Beast:</b> Angelic wings attached to the body of a horse, they now run wild and free across the sky, forever denying the bridle of their captors.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Windrider often bare the features of two or more dangerous animals. Their unarmed attacks inflict Lethal damage due to their savage claws and fangs. Additionally, their time spent as airborne steeds allows to spend a point of Glamour to fly at twice their normal movement speed. While flying, they may carry a passenger who is within their capacity to lift, but suffer -1 speed for each size rating of the passenger in question.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am <i>definitely</i> liking this revision. Would you mind if I polish the write-up a little further?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Windrider:</b><br /> <i>You don't have the balls to tame me!</i><br /> <br /> Long seen as a symbol of nobility and pride by magical and mundane parties alike, those who became Windriders were used as mounts to carry their masters across sky and sea. Most owere created by combining the features of a predatory bird with some other type of animal, with noth parts blending seamlessly together and being fully functional. Only the most regal were permitted to harness them, while anyone undeserving was gored in the attempt. Their escape came on the day when their esteemed masters were judged unworthy to saddle them, thus prompting the Windrider to rebel. Yet even though they value their freedom, they are still willing to let others ride should they earn the privilege.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 </span> <b>Beast:</b> Angelic wings attached to the body of a horse, they now run wild and free across the sky, forever denying the bridle of their captors.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 </span> <b>Fairest:</b> A gryphon fit for a king. From the torso upwards is the body of a giant eagle, but from the waist down they have the legs and tail of a lion.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 </span> <b>Ogre: </b>The wings of a dragon and the body of a lion, this manticore tragically lost its scorpion's tail during aerial combat.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Windrider often bears the features of two or more dangerous animals. Their unarmed attacks inflict Lethal damage due to their savage claws and fangs., and their time spent as airborne steeds allows them to fly at twice their Speed for a number of minutes equal to half their Wyrd, rounded up. If they spend a point of Glamour, they double the duration of their flight. While flying, they may carry a passenger who is within their capacity to lift, but reduce their Speed by the Size rating of the passenger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-18-2016, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T17:23:10-07:00","id":893738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=893711#post893711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am <i>definitely</i> liking this revision. Would you mind if I polish the write-up a little further?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Windrider:</b><br /> <i>You don't have the balls to tame me!</i><br /> <br /> Long seen as a symbol of nobility and pride by magical and mundane parties alike, those who became Windriders were used as mounts to carry their masters across sky and sea. Most owere created by combining the features of a predatory bird with some other type of animal, with noth parts blending seamlessly together and being fully functional. Only the most regal were permitted to harness them, while anyone undeserving was gored in the attempt. Their escape came on the day when their esteemed masters were judged unworthy to saddle them, thus prompting the Windrider to rebel. Yet even though they value their freedom, they are still willing to let others ride should they earn the privilege.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 </span> <b>Beast:</b> Angelic wings attached to the body of a horse, they now run wild and free across the sky, forever denying the bridle of their captors.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 </span> <b>Fairest:</b> A gryphon fit for a king. From the torso upwards is the body of a giant eagle, but from the waist down they have the legs and tail of a lion.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 </span> <b>Ogre: </b>The wings of a dragon and the body of a lion, this manticore tragically lost its scorpion's tail during aerial combat.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A Windrider often bears the features of two or more dangerous animals. Their unarmed attacks inflict Lethal damage due to their savage claws and fangs., and their time spent as airborne steeds allows them to fly at twice their Speed for a number of minutes equal to half their Wyrd, rounded up. If they spend a point of Glamour, they double the duration of their flight. While flying, they may carry a passenger who is within their capacity to lift, but reduce their Speed by the Size rating of the passenger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've spotted a few typos in the description. But now that I think about it, putting a time limit on their flight seems to make sense as their wings are bound to get tired after a while. Still being able to maintain flight for only minutes at a time seems <i>way too small</i>. These guys were used as mounts in battle and even the strongest among them would only be able to maintain flight for 10 minutes. That's not exactly impressive.<br /> <br /> Maybe increase it to six minutes per Wyrd. That way at level 10, they can maintain flight for an hour before needing to rest?<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Here's my newest version of it<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Windrider:</b><br /> <br /> <i>You don't have the balls to tame me!</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Long seen as a symbol of nobility and pride by magical and mundane parties alike, those who became Windriders were used as mounts to carry their masters across sky and sea. Most of them were created by combining the features of a predatory bird with some other type of animal. Both parts blending seamlessly together and being fully functional as if such hybrids were natural creatures. Only the most regal were permitted to harness them, while anyone undeserving was gored in the attempt. Their escape came on the day when their esteemed masters were judged unworthy to saddle them, thus prompting the Windrider to rebel! Although they value their new freedom, they still offer rides to those who have earned their trust.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A gryphon fit for a king. From the torso upwards is the body of a giant eagle, but from the waist down they have the legs and tail of a lion.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre: </b>The wings of a dragon and the body of a lion, this manticore tragically lost its scorpion's tail during aerial combat.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Angelic wings attached to the body of a horse, they now run wild and free across the sky, forever denying the bridle of their captors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Windrider often bare the features of two or more dangerous animals. Their unarmed attacks inflict Lethal damage due to their savage claws and fangs. Additionally, their time spent as airborne steeds allows them to fly at twice their normal movement speed for six times their Wyrd in minutes. Spending a point of Glamour will double this duration. While flying, they may carry a passenger who is within their capacity to lift, but suffer -1 speed for each size rating of the passenger in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-18-2016, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T18:18:47-07:00","id":893766,"title":"","content":"<b>Basilisk</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;No, my gaze won't turn you to stone. But you'll wish it did... at least your death would be less painful that way.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> One of the most deadly creatures in mythology, the Basilisk was created to destroy any life that crossed its path, sentient or otherwise. So virulent were they, that merely breathing was enough to kill the environment in which they lived! Their durances were tragic existences of complete isolation, for none would dare approach them, lest they begin convulsing in agony. Eventually, the Basilisk realized they could use this to their advantage and escaped the prisons that held them! Known to some as the &quot;king of reptiles,&quot; many Basilisks exhibit a reptilian motif in their design.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A freakishly large snake, far more massive than any natural species found on earth.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> The body of a lizard, the head of a rooster, and a crest shaped like a royal crown.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A near sighted crocodile who exhibits an additional pair of limbs between the first four!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Basilisk gains the Evil Eye Merit, and can use it without any drawback with the 8-again benefit to its roll. Additionally, its scaled hide serves as extra protection against those who would see them harmed. They automatically gain 3/1 Armor, which stacks with any other armor they might be wearing over their body. If they spend a point of Glamour, the Basilisk is able to exhale a cloud of deadly poison with a Toxicity level equal to half their Wyrd, rounded up. This cloud has an effective range of 3 yards equal to their Wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-19-2016, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T19:24:51-07:00","id":893805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=893766#post893766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Basilisk</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;No, my gaze won't turn you to stone. But you'll wish it did... at least your death would be less painful that way.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> One of the most deadly creatures in mythology, the Basilisk was created to destroy any life that crossed its path, sentient or otherwise. So virulent were they, that merely breathing was enough to kill the environment in which they lived! Their durances were tragic existences of complete isolation, for none would dare approach them, lest they begin convulsing in agony. Eventually, the Basilisk realized they could use this to their advantage and escaped the prisons that held them! Known to some as the &quot;king of reptiles,&quot; many Basilisks exhibit a reptilian motif in their design.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A freakishly large snake, far more massive than any natural species found on earth.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> The body of a lizard, the head of a rooster, and a crest shaped like a royal crown.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A near sighted crocodile who exhibits an additional pair of limbs between the first four!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The scaley hide of a Basilisk serves as extra protection against those who would see them harmed. They automatically gain 3/1 armor rating in addition to any other armor they might be wearing over their body . Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, the Basilisk is able to exhale a cloud of deadly poison with a toxicity level equal to half their Wyrd rounded up. This cloud has an effective range of 3 yards equal to their Wyrd</div> </div> </div> </div>Added in the Windrider kith to the GDoc.<br /> <br /> Moving onto the basilisk, I am liking their concept. But perhaps you can add another effect to that poison cloud besides it being toxic? Let me see if I can give some additions and polish up the write-up.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Basilisk gains the Evil Eye Merit, and can use it without any drawback with the 8-again benefit to its roll. Additionally, its scaled hide serves as extra protection against those who would see them harmed. They automatically gain 3/1 Armor, which stacks with any other armor they might be wearing over their body. If they spend a point of Glamour, the Basilisk is able to exhale a cloud of deadly poison with a Toxicity level equal to half their Wyrd, rounded up. This cloud has an effective range of 3 yards equal to their Wyrd. <hr /><br /> For the Evil Eye Merit, see <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jM_bpQHo-dM4yop592S09y4AjQGLLTNhK5_0-5_85kg/edit\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T19:43:18-07:00","id":893813,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> <br /> Added your Baalor (renamed it to Balaur, after the Romanian monster of the same name) and Stitchborn Kiths respectively to the GDoc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T22:49:27-07:00","id":893868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=893805#post893805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Added in the Windrider kith to the GDoc.<br /> <br /> Moving onto the basilisk, I am liking their concept. But perhaps you can add another effect to that poison cloud besides it being toxic? Let me see if I can give some additions and polish up the write-up.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Basilisk gains the Evil Eye Merit, and can use it without any drawback with the 8-again benefit to its roll. Additionally, its scaled hide serves as extra protection against those who would see them harmed. They automatically gain 3/1 Armor, which stacks with any other armor they might be wearing over their body. If they spend a point of Glamour, the Basilisk is able to exhale a cloud of deadly poison with a Toxicity level equal to half their Wyrd, rounded up. This cloud has an effective range of 3 yards equal to their Wyrd. <hr /><br /> For the Evil Eye Merit, see <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jM_bpQHo-dM4yop592S09y4AjQGLLTNhK5_0-5_85kg/edit\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, well the Basilisk that I used was its original interpretation. Baslisks today are depicted as being able to petrify people with a glare, similar to Gorgons. But the original Basilisks were depicted as being extremely poisonous creatures. A single drop of their blood leaking from one's spear was enough to kill both a rider and his horse. I didn't see any toxic related Kiths in the draft write up, so figured it was a good time to implement one.<br /> <br /> Strangely enough, the stench of weasel urine was toxic to the Basilisk.<br /> <br /> Anyways, added the new Blessing description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T02:35:09-07:00","id":893919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=893868#post893868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, well the Basilisk that I used was its original interpretation. Baslisks today are depicted as being able to petrify people with a glare, similar to Gorgons. But the original Basilisks were depicted as being extremely poisonous creatures. A single drop of their blood leaking from one's spear was enough to kill both a rider and his horse. I didn't see any toxic related Kiths in the draft write up, so figured it was a good time to implement one.<br /> <br /> Strangely enough, the stench of weasel urine was toxic to the Basilisk.<br /> <br /> Anyways, added the new Blessing description.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, nothing wrong with drawing on both depictions of the Basilisk for this kith, right? Anyway, I am wondering though if the 8-again rule is a good idea on top of the fact that they can use Evil Eye as an Instant action without any drawbacks. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a>, what do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:01:36-07:00","id":894062,"title":"","content":"<b>Will-O-the-Wisp</b><br /> <br /> &quot;<i>I told you not to trust her!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Not every abduction the Fae perform is an obvious one. Sometimes, they like to make it seem like an accident so that it people don't go asking too many questions. To conduct these abductions, they create Will-O-the-Wisps, ephemeral beings who appear in the mist at night and entrance mortals with their hypnotic allure. The hapless victim would then proceed to chase after the wisp, leading them straight into the clutches of their new masters! One night, the Will-O-the-Wisp decided to change things around and chase after the mortal instead, eventually following them back through the Hedge!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> An entity composed of ghostly flames. It produces no heat, but wavers enticingly before your eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A beautiful maiden with a miniature sun shining around her head. Her presences fills you with a sense of security.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling: </b>A mysterious figure, wrapped in a tight cloud of luminescent mist. The cloud blinks hypnotically when your eyes try to follow their movements.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Will-O-the-Wisps spent their durances leading people into danger and have become quite proficient at tricking others as a result. They begin with the Nevertread contract for free at character creation and gain exceptional successes on 3 instead of 5. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour and rolling a contested Wyrd + Manipulation against Willpower + Composure, they can force a subject to devote their attention on the Will-O-the-Wisp, causing them to momentarily forget about what they were doing. If the Will-O-the-Wisp leaves the area, and the victim has not overcome the effect, they will feel compelled to track them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:33:45-07:00","id":894093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=893919#post893919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, nothing wrong with drawing on both depictions of the Basilisk for this kith, right? Anyway, I am wondering though if the 8-again rule is a good idea on top of the fact that they can use Evil Eye as an Instant action without any drawbacks. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a>, what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that 8-Again without drawbacks is way too potent for something that can apply such a brutal Tilt. I'd say having the Merit is great as is, given how effectively it could take someone out of a fight. I'd add their Wyrd to the activation roll for it instead of the loss of drawback or the 8-Again effect. As an aside, great idea with the Evil Eye Merit being used for this. A similar kith that I'd been working on (diregaze) had simply reduced Speed and Initiative with a look, and could sacrifice Defense to lock eyes and inflict the Stunned Tilt. The Merit actually reflects a petrifying stare a lot better. I also think that the Armor is a bit potent, given that it is superior to any other kith's armor out of the box, though admittedly the metalflesh can become superior by spending Glamour and the earthbones manages it by increasing Wyrd or Potent Kith. Given the potency of the rest of the blessing, giving 1/1 Armor for the scales like the draconic and coldscale get wouldn't be bad. The poison cloud seems like it could use a bit of work, as well. A brewer creates poison of the same Toxicity, but requires someone to ingest it to be effective, while the blightbent creates a more potent cloud, but a potentially much smaller one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:37:21-07:00","id":894327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One night, the Will-O-the-Wisp decided to change things around and chase after the mortal instead, eventually following them back through the Hedge! </div> </div> </div>Kiths don't normally have the escape as part of them, the escape is part of the seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T15:14:26-07:00","id":894350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=894093#post894093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think that 8-Again without drawbacks is way too potent for something that can apply such a brutal Tilt. I'd say having the Merit is great as is, given how effectively it could take someone out of a fight. I'd add their Wyrd to the activation roll for it instead of the loss of drawback or the 8-Again effect. As an aside, great idea with the Evil Eye Merit being used for this. A similar kith that I'd been working on (diregaze) had simply reduced Speed and Initiative with a look, and could sacrifice Defense to lock eyes and inflict the Stunned Tilt. The Merit actually reflects a petrifying stare a lot better. I also think that the Armor is a bit potent, given that it is superior to any other kith's armor out of the box, though admittedly the metalflesh can become superior by spending Glamour and the earthbones manages it by increasing Wyrd or Potent Kith. Given the potency of the rest of the blessing, giving 1/1 Armor for the scales like the draconic and coldscale get wouldn't be bad. The poison cloud seems like it could use a bit of work, as well. A brewer creates poison of the same Toxicity, but requires someone to ingest it to be effective, while the blightbent creates a more potent cloud, but a potentially much smaller one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, as I said, I couldn't find a toxic based Kith in <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/16XgmK7x1ZfRWF4cs-Ayw-Ih1YLgBmkFEs6klD81AfPY/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">the draft</a>, so I didn't have anything to compare it to.<br /> <br /> The 3/1 armor is about the same as chain mail, according to the armor chart. I thought it fit in theme with their scales. I was also juggling with the idea of making it 2/1, but wasn't sure if that would have even been worth it or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> The basilisk was already able to function as a poisonous tank without the stun lock power. And like I said, it wasn't part of the original interpretation. Giving them armor, paralysis and poison makes them seem a little bit too OP, even by second edition standards.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think we could sacrifice either the Armor bonus or the Evil Eye and keep the poison. Either version would work for a Basilisk without making it unfair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T15:16:58-07:00","id":894353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=894327#post894327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kiths don't normally have the escape as part of them, the escape is part of the seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well all I said was they chased the human, I didn't say how they did so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T15:45:42-07:00","id":894373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=894350#post894350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, as I said, I couldn't find a toxic based Kith in <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/16XgmK7x1ZfRWF4cs-Ayw-Ih1YLgBmkFEs6klD81AfPY/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1&amp;quot;]the</a> draft[/URL], so I didn't have anything to compare it to.<br /> <br /> The 3/1 armor is about the same as chain mail, according to the armor chart. I thought it fit in theme with their scales. I was also juggling with the idea of making it 2/1, but wasn't sure if that would have even been worth it or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> The basilisk was already able to function as a poisonous tank without the stun lock power. And like I said, it wasn't part of the original interpretation. Giving them armor, paralysis and poison makes them seem a little bit too OP, even by second edition standards.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think we could sacrifice either the Armor bonus or the Evil Eye and keep the poison. Either version would work for a Basilisk without making it unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are using an older draft of the kiths. I'll try to find the links to the newer ones once I get home tonight. <br /> <br /> If you are wishing to remove one of the blessing's aspects, oddly enough, I would say that the paralysis would be better to remove than the armor, mostly because a paralyzed foe cannot leave the cloud of poison. As for the poison cloud, it will need a duration added to it, at least. The size may need adjustment as well, given how quickly it could overtake everything with Potent Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:01:13-07:00","id":894751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=894350#post894350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, as I said, I couldn't find a toxic based Kith in <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/16XgmK7x1ZfRWF4cs-Ayw-Ih1YLgBmkFEs6klD81AfPY/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">the draft</a>, so I didn't have anything to compare it to.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the link to the more <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mZpz1PhV2jzc2ihda1IwHZc_WTrWTv5qbNv4vzcU2-4/edit\" target=\"_blank\">complete document</a>, and a <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoeDVLclY0SW1hWm8/view\" target=\"_blank\">couple more</a>, too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:14:58-07:00","id":894757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=894327#post894327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kiths don't normally have the escape as part of them, the escape is part of the seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is some precedent, though. For example, the dearheart kith speaks of how their Durances often end with another changeling standing between dearheart and Keeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T11:58:38-07:00","id":894866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=894757#post894757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There is some precedent, though. For example, the dearheart kith speaks of how their Durances often end with another changeling standing between dearheart and Keeper.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fox and the Hound. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T09:07:58-07:00","id":896863,"title":"","content":"Computer messed up again. Found out it wasn't the cats, but some kind of glitch on Windows 8 that causes it to get stuck in auto repair loop. Had to reinstall the computer <i><b>again</b></i> and switch to windows 10....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T04:17:14-07:00","id":897682,"title":"","content":"Here's a new Kith from me. Seeming descriptions are welcome. As is critique.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr /><br /> <u><b>Stormtouched</b></u><br /> <i>You thought you had me cornered? Out here in the open with a storm brewing? Well, I'm about to prove you wrong.</i><br /> <br /> Imbued with all the fury and power of their namesake, Stormtouched already embodied it in some way as mortals. Some may have been prone to violent mood swings, while others had a certain relentlessness in their actions. A few may have even taken because of their fascination with storms. In any case, their Keepers had them exposed repeatedly to waves of lightning until they filled every fiber of their being. Yet while this transformation made them into living weapons, many were also made more empowered by the experience. This sparked defiance against their captors, and eventually culminated with their flight through the Thorns.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Stormtouched have three dots in the Psychokinesis Merit, and can spend Glamour or Willpower to manipulate electricity with it. They may also heal any damage they suffered by exposing themselves to electrical currents. If a Stormtouched is outdoors during suitable weather conditions, he may spend Glamour and roll Resolve + Occult to call down a bolt of lightning. If used as an attack, the roll is penalized by the target's Defense, and deals bashing damage equal to half the Changeling's Wyrd, rounded up, plus successes in the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-24-2016, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T09:57:07-07:00","id":897910,"title":"","content":"I like the basic idea. I'm not sure about the healing aspect. You'd need to add more to it in order to make it clear how it works before I can give a good review. The rest of it seems promising, though. For seemings:<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> These changelings seem to be raptors, with lightning clutched in their talons and thunder echoing from their flapping wings.<br /> <b>Fairest: </b>Her flesh is made from the peaceful blue sky, but when angered, the lightning flickering in her gray eyes dances throughout her body.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> Electricity continually crackles over his cloud-gray skin, causing the faint text to illuminate briefly for seconds at a time.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> He is tall and thin, his lower half narrower than his top. His eyes have been replaced with plasma globes, and his spine is a Jacob's ladder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T16:19:34-07:00","id":898338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=897910#post897910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the basic idea. I'm not sure about the healing aspect. You'd need to add more to it in order to make it clear how it works before I can give a good review. The rest of it seems promising, though. For seemings:<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> These changelings seem to be raptors, with lightning clutched in their talons and thunder echoing from their flapping wings.<br /> <b>Fairest: </b>Her flesh is made from the peaceful blue sky, but when angered, the lightning flickering in her gray eyes dances throughout her body.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> Electricity continually crackles over his cloud-gray skin, causing the faint text to illuminate briefly for seconds at a time.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> He is tall and thin, his lower half narrower than his top. His eyes have been replaced with plasma globes, and his spine is a Jacob's ladder.</div> </div> </div> </div>The healing aspect is supposed to be similar to the <a href=\"http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/cod/ptc/CreationBen.html\" target=\"_blank\">Electroshock Therapy of Prometheans</a>.<br /> <br /> Also, I am liking these Seeming descriptions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks a bunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T18:17:55-07:00","id":898457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=898338#post898338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The healing aspect is supposed to be similar to the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/cod/ptc/CreationBen.html&amp;quot;]Electroshock</a> Therapy of Prometheans[/URL].<br /> <br /> Also, I am liking these Seeming descriptions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks a bunch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed that it was based on Promethean healing. I think that simply being immune to harmful effects could work pretty well, given that Promethean healing is one of the most potent healing systems in the CofD. I'm glad that you liked the Seeming descriptions. You're quite welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T18:22:13-07:00","id":898461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=898457#post898457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed that it was based on Promethean healing. I think that simply being immune to harmful effects could work pretty well, given that Promethean healing is one of the most potent healing systems in the CofD. I'm glad that you liked the Seeming descriptions. You're quite welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this better, then?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Stormtouched have three dots in the Psychokinesis Merit, and can spend Glamour or Willpower to manipulate electricity with it. They also take no damage from electrical sources. If a Stormtouched is outdoors during suitable weather conditions, he may spend Glamour and roll Resolve + Occult to call down a bolt of lightning. If used as an attack, the roll is penalized by the target's Defense, and deals bashing damage equal to half the Changeling's Wyrd, rounded up, plus successes in the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-25-2016, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T02:10:25-07:00","id":898765,"title":"","content":"Get rid of the &quot;may also&quot; from that sentence, and I think you're good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T16:08:53-07:00","id":899504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=898765#post898765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get rid of the &quot;may also&quot; from that sentence, and I think you're good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Noted and done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:16:58-07:00","id":901537,"title":"","content":"Here's a beastmaster-type kith that's got a different flavor to the Skogsra. Critique, flavor text, and Seeming Descriptions are welcome.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr /><br /> <b><u>Wildling</u></b><br /> <i>Look, I know rats are smart, okay? I'm telling you, though, this one was reading through my emails! That ain't natural!</i><br /> <br /> Holding an affinity to animals as mortals, Wildlings were taken to assist in the assembly and caring of great menageries. Some used their heightened talent to lure beasts into the Hedge in attempts to produce new species for their Keepers. Others, however, were taught how to act through the bodies of their animal companions in order to serve as scouts and sentries. Most Gentry, however, underestimate how deeply a Wildling bonds with his charges. And in nurturing those bonds, he finds the means to bring about their freedom.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling:</b> Slender and covered in fine gray fur, her eyes are beady like those of a rat.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> With a goatskin stitched over his legs and the eyes of a goat staring wildly at the world around him, this changeling seems to be a satyr composed of solid bone.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> He is a handsome savage, with long flowing hair and the gleaming eyes of a raptor.<br /> \u2022 <b>Wizened:</b> She seems to be a shriveled old woman, but the canine eye in her right socket and the feline eye in her left both shine brightly.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Wildling benefits from the 8-Again rule on all Animal Ken rolls, and can spend Glamour or Willpower to use the Animal Possession Merit on any animal he established the Bonded Condition with. If he is made to roll Resolve + Animal Ken to maintain control of the animal when it's injured, reduce the penalty to the dice pool by his Wyrd.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> The Animal Possession Merit can be found in <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jM_bpQHo-dM4yop592S09y4AjQGLLTNhK5_0-5_85kg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":".  Added the flavor text and Seeming descriptions given by White Oak Dragon, and tweaked the benefit to rolling to maintain control. 06-02-2016, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T09:04:08-07:00","id":904989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=901537#post901537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a beastmaster-type kith that's got a different flavor to the Skogsra. Critique, flavor text, and Seeming Descriptions are welcome.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr /><br /> <b><u>Wildling</u></b><br /> <br /> Holding an affinity to animals as mortals, Wildlings were taken to assist in the assembly and caring of great menageries. Some used their heightened talent to lure beasts into the Hedge in attempts to produce new species for their Keepers. Others, however, were taught how to act through the bodies of their animal companions in order to serve as scouts and sentries. Most Gentry, however, underestimate how deeply a Wildling bonds with his charges. And in nurturing those bonds, he finds the means to bring about their freedom.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Wildling benefits from the 8-Again rule on all Animal Ken rolls, and can spend Glamour or Willpower to use the Animal Possession Merit on any animal he established the Bonded Condition with. If the animal sustains any damage while he is controlling its mind, he reflexively rolls Resolve + Animal Ken to maintain control at no penalty.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> The Animal Possession Merit can be found in <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jM_bpQHo-dM4yop592S09y4AjQGLLTNhK5_0-5_85kg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, this one will be a tricky one. Okay, here goes:<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Slender and covered in fine gray fur, her eyes are beady like those of a rat.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> With a goatskin stitched over his legs and the eyes of a goat staring wildly at the world around him, this changeling seems to be a satyr composed of solid bone.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> He is a handsome savage, with long flowing hair and the gleaming eyes of a raptor.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> She seems to be a shriveled old woman, but the canine eye in her right socket and the feline eye in her left both shine brightly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T09:25:10-07:00","id":905005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=904989#post904989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, this one will be a tricky one. Okay, here goes:<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Slender and covered in fine gray fur, her eyes are beady like those of a rat.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> With a goatskin stitched over his legs and the eyes of a goat staring wildly at the world around him, this changeling seems to be a satyr composed of solid bone.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> He is a handsome savage, with long flowing hair and the gleaming eyes of a raptor.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> She seems to be a shriveled old woman, but the canine eye in her right socket and the feline eye in her left both shine brightly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loving them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Now, I just need a good flavor text for them and I'm set. What do you think of the kith blessing, by the way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T13:45:52-07:00","id":905150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=905005#post905005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Loving them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Now, I just need a good flavor text for them and I'm set. What do you think of the kith blessing, by the way?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking that there should be some penalty for having the animal that they are controlling injured (or at least one if the animal dies while/because they are controlling them). Otherwise, I think it looks pretty good. For flavor text:<br /> <br /> Look, I know rats are smart, okay? I'm telling you, though, this one was reading through my emails! That ain't natural!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T23:07:22-07:00","id":905419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=905150#post905150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm thinking that there should be some penalty for having the animal that they are controlling injured (or at least one if the animal dies while/because they are controlling them). Otherwise, I think it looks pretty good. For flavor text:<br /> <br /> Look, I know rats are smart, okay? I'm telling you, though, this one was reading through my emails! That ain't natural!</div> </div> </div> </div>Added the text in. Definitely liking it.<br /> As for your suggestion on the penalty, I tweaked the blessing as follows....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=901537#post901537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blessing:</b> The Wildling benefits from the 8-Again rule on all Animal Ken rolls, and can spend Glamour or Willpower to use the Animal Possession Merit on any animal he established the Bonded Condition with. If he is made to roll Resolve + Animal Ken to maintain control of the animal when it's injured, reduce the penalty to the dice pool by his Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T07:18:51-07:00","id":905606,"title":"","content":"That is better. A high Wyrd or Potent Kith Wildling would be able to keep going without penalty, but an inexperienced one can still lose his grip on the animal. I do think that there should be consequences for the changeling if the animal dies. Perhaps suffering a Health Level of damage, or the loss of a Willpower point, or even suffering a Clarity breaking point could all be potential options. I'm just thinking something that would ultimately discourage the Wildlings from being cavalier with the lives of their animal friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T13:50:48-07:00","id":905925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=905606#post905606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is better. A high Wyrd or Potent Kith Wildling would be able to keep going without penalty, but an inexperienced one can still lose his grip on the animal. I do think that there should be consequences for the changeling if the animal dies. Perhaps suffering a Health Level of damage, or the loss of a Willpower point, or even suffering a Clarity breaking point could all be potential options. I'm just thinking something that would ultimately discourage the Wildlings from being cavalier with the lives of their animal friends.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Clarity breaking point could be covered as a trigger, which is almost certainly a given seeing as the kith's durance deals with animals and Hedgebeasts. The same could apply with the curses of the Darkling, Fairest, and perhaps even the Elemental. Alternatively, the Animal Possession Merit could be house-ruled to inflict the Soul Shocked Condition if the animal dies. The draft doc <i>did</i> come out before Beast, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T02:37:50-07:00","id":910653,"title":"","content":"I actually like that idea of house-ruling the Soul Shocked Condition to apply to someone who controls an animal that dies during the possession.<br /> <br /> Here is a draft for one of the kiths I've been working on for quite a while. Feedback is welcome.<br /> <br /> <b>Jester</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">I am beside myself with amazement! Here I am, carefully forged, trained, and perfected to be exactly what I am, and yet, here I find a greater fool before me!</span><br /> <br /> Wise fools and masters of mockery, the jesters were kept for both comedy and candor. Jesters were expected to keep the courts and banquets of the Gentry echoing with laughter, often at the expense of guest and host alike. While most changelings wouldn't dare to question their Keepers, a jester could often get away with it, provided that he could do so in an amusing manner. Jesters who escape always hope that they have gotten the last laugh, but most secretly fear that their freedom is part of a larger cruel joke.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> The brightly colored cockscomb on the head of this rooster-like changeling is not a hat.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> The porcelain fool in faded motley, the points of her hat tipped with jingling brass bells, appears to have been shattered and repaired countless times.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> The dour man's patchwork skin records countless tales that illustrate the ultimate absurdity of life itself.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> The misshapen hunchbacked dwarf grits his teeth and walks with a frog-like gait. The smell of smoke and charred flesh follows him everywhere.<br /> <b>Wizened:</b> Greasepaint oozes from her pores, and tarnished silver hooks pull at the corners of her mouth, twisting her face into an eternal grin.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Jesters add their Wyrd to any Wits or Social rolls intended for amusement or mockery, and gain an exceptional success on three successes rather than five on such rolls. An exceptional success on such a roll allows the changeling to inflict his choice of the Admonished, Amused, or Humiliated Condition upon the target. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour when placing the Condition on the target, any other listeners with a lower Composure score than his successes will be overcome with laughter at his jest, suffering the Insensate Tilt for a number of turns equal to the jester's Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <b>New Conditions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Admonished</b><br /> Your character has been gently warned about a foolish course of action that she was about to take, and now she is reevaluating her plans. Your character's newfound hesitancy about her actions inflicts a -1 penalty to Wits and Manipulation rolls, but she may resolve this Condition at any time to gain a +3 bonus on a roll related to abandoning her previous course of action.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> The advice of a wise mentor, an observant or cutting remark about one's actions.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Your character gains confidence in a new course of action, changing her tactics and resolving the Condition as described above.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Your character meets with disaster and regret by holding to her original course of action.<br /> <br /> <b>Amused</b><br /> That was hilarious! Your character's mood has been greatly improved, and that has given him a bit more heart to face the challenges before him. When spending a point of Willpower to add dice to a roll, if the roll is successful, the character may choose to resolve this Condition instead of spending the Willpower point.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Witnessing something that gave a good laugh.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Resolving the Condition as described above, suffering damage, or gaining another Condition that ruins your character's good mood.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a<br /> <br /> <b>Humiliated</b><br /> Your character has been deeply embarrassed, causing her to become frustrated and stumble through social situations. Her Composure score is treated as though it was 2 lower, which also affects all derived traits. She also loses the 10-Again effect on all Social rolls while the Condition persists.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Vicious mockery, a dramatic failure on a roll in front of numerous witnesses.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Facing the source of the Condition and emerging victorious, gaining an exceptional success on a roll, or inflicting the Humiliated Condition on another character.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Your character suffers a dramatic failure on a Social roll.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T02:50:47-07:00","id":910658,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> <br /> <br /> Well, look what we have here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Another great kith from you. Really loving the write-up for the Blessing. Woe to anyone who's on the tail end of the Jester's humor. Especially if you end up Humiliated <i>and</i> the laughingstock of everyone around you. Bravo, man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T08:59:29-07:00","id":911694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=910658#post910658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <br /> <br /> Well, look what we have here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Another great kith from you. Really loving the write-up for the Blessing. Woe to anyone who's on the tail end of the Jester's humor. Especially if you end up Humiliated <i>and</i> the laughingstock of everyone around you. Bravo, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you liked it. This kith is one that I've been working on for a while, and it's nice to see it finally completed, even if it may need some alterations somewhere down the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T06:12:10-07:00","id":914775,"title":"","content":"This kith is one that I've been trying to figure out ever since I started creating kiths for First Edition. While it may yet require some tweaking, I am still quite pleased to finally have something for it. <br /> <br /> <b>Sorrowscent</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">It was like nothing that I'd ever smelled before. By the time I managed to get my eyes to stop watering, he was gone.</span><br /> <br /> Rejected by others prior to their Durances, the malodorous sorrowscents tend to be desperately lonely. Sorrowscents were most often used to ward remote areas against unwanted intruders, although some Gentry with odd tastes used them as living censers, filling areas with a scent that the Keeper alone would favor. Even after escaping, a sorrowscent often leads a lonesome existence, shunned by his peers for the stench forced upon him.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> His charming mannerisms and exotic accent do nothing to disguise the fact that this changeling is a skunk.<br /> <b>Darkling:</b> The revolting stench of putrid garbage and body odor emanates from the squat goblin with a bulbous eye in the palm of each hand.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> There is never a strand of her perfect green hair out of place, but the heavy perfume surrounding her is cloyingly sweet.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> The script on her wrinkled paper flesh is almost illegible, and the miasma of mildew and moldering manuscripts is inescapable.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> This ape-like changeling is covered in shaggy gray fur, the stench of rotten cabbage following in his wake.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> A sorrowscent emits a powerful odor that disrupts the concentration of those around them. Provided that their olfactory capabilities are functioning, anybody coming within two meters of a sorrowscent will suffer from the Distracted Condition due to the overpowering smell. The sorrowscent may extend this radius by his Wyrd in meters as a reflexive action. By spending a point of Glamour, the sorrowscent may intensify his disgusting odor. Any characters affected by the stench must roll their Stamina, penalized by half the sorrowscent's Wyrd, rounded up. Failure on this roll inflicts the Sick Tilt at moderate severity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T07:07:00-07:00","id":914808,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a><br /> <br /> Ooh. This is an interesting one. And perfect for a Pepe Le Pew type character.<br /> :3<br /> I assume there's no way for this Blessing to be rendered inert, like with the Briarborn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T07:59:32-07:00","id":914830,"title":"","content":"Need some help with the kith and seeming descriptions. But I definitely am liking how this concept turned out. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Mentalist</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;Fine. Let me rephrase that. Drop the gun. </i>Now<i>.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Mentalist gains the three-dot version of the Mind Control Merit, and can spend Glamour or Willpower to activate it. Anyone influenced by her command suffer a penalty equal to her Wyrd + 1 for the rest of the scene or until it is completed. If the command is not something they could conceivably do in that time and place, then the effect lasts for a number of turns equal to half the Mentalist's Wyrd, rounded up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 06-15-2016, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T09:23:40-07:00","id":914867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=914808#post914808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span><br /> <br /> Ooh. This is an interesting one. And perfect for a Pepe Le Pew type character.<br /> :3<br /> I assume there's no way for this Blessing to be rendered inert, like with the Briarborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly the type I'd been envisioning when I first got the idea. I had thought it odd that there wasn't really a kith appropriate for the odor defense exhibited by some animals. It has taken a long time to finally get a name and description that I liked.<br /> <br /> As for rendering the blessing inert, I've actually been debating that. I can't make up my mind, yet, but if I decide to be kind to them, I would make it cost a point of Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T11:55:38-07:00","id":914957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=914830#post914830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Need some help with the kith and seeming descriptions. But I definitely am liking how this concept turned out. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Mentalist</u></b><br /> <i>&amp;quot;Fine. Let me rephrase that. Drop the gun. </i>Now<i>.&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Mentalist gains the three-dot version of the Mind Control Merit, and can spend Glamour or Willpower to activate it. Anyone influenced by her command suffer a penalty equal to her Wyrd + 1 for the rest of the scene or until it is completed. If the command is not something they could conceivably do in that time and place, then the effect lasts for a number of turns equal to half the Mentalist's Wyrd, rounded up.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one has a lot of potential. I'll try to help out with the descriptions when I get home tonight. I was wondering, though, what led you to choose Mentalist as the name? When I hear mentalist, my thoughts first go to telepathy and precognition, rather than mind control. Have you considered a name with more connotations of command, such as Sovereign?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T12:08:36-07:00","id":914966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=914957#post914957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This one has a lot of potential. I'll try to help out with the descriptions when I get home tonight. I was wondering, though, what led you to choose Mentalist as the name? When I hear mentalist, my thoughts first go to telepathy and precognition, rather than mind control. Have you considered a name with more connotations of command, such as Sovereign?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From this.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Mentalist, noun. Someone who uses mental acuity, hypnosis and/or suggestion. A master manipulator of thoughts and behavior.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> I am open to alternative choices for names, though Sovereign is a bit too fancy for my taste. And I'm not sure if I want to go with Influencer, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:12:31-07:00","id":915066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=914966#post914966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> From this.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Mentalist, noun. Someone who uses mental acuity, hypnosis and/or suggestion. A master manipulator of thoughts and behavior.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> I am open to alternative choices for names, though Sovereign is a bit too fancy for my taste. And I'm not sure if I want to go with Influencer, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about something like Enforcer, Slave Driver, Taskmaster, or Overseer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":". 06-15-2016, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T19:11:30-07:00","id":915275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=915066#post915066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about something like Enforcer, Slave Driver, Taskmaster, or Overseer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Taskmaster sounds like a good name for the kith, especially since I'm reminded of the subtype of Formian from Dungeons and Dragons. Speaking of which....<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast: </b>An ant man with twitching antennae, and mandibles capable of human speech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T10:03:27-07:00","id":915678,"title":"","content":"Okay, I've added some descriptions to what you already had, and changed the name:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Taskmaster</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;Fine. Let me rephrase that. Drop the gun. </i>Now<i>.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Not every Keeper wishes to keep a constant eye on his changelings. A Taskmaster is appointed to watch over the other servants, ensuring that her Keeper's will is upheld even in his absence. While Taskmasters are usually chosen for their leadership capabilities, their roles as slave drivers often alienate them from other changelings.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast: </b>An ant man with twitching antennae, and mandibles capable of human speech.<br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling</b><b>: </b> A cruel sneer permanently twists the face of the pale woman, a livid scar stretching from her forehead to her cheek.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental</b><b>: </b>This changeling appears to be an imperious queen painted in bold watercolors.<br /> \u2022 <b>Wizened</b><b>: </b>The changeling's eyes have been replaced with swirling black and white disks, and phantom whips extend from the back of each hand.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Taskmaster gains the three-dot version of the Mind Control Merit, and can spend Glamour or Willpower to activate it. Anyone influenced by her command suffers a penalty equal to her Wyrd + 1 for the rest of the scene or until it is completed. If the command is not something they could conceivably do in that time and place, then the effect lasts for a number of turns equal to half the Taskmaster's Wyrd, rounded up.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do think that the penalty for refusing the command being Wyrd + 1 might be a little high, given how easily that can be boosted with Potent Kith. Maybe half Wyrd? Have you considered allowing them to open an additional Door when using Hard Leverage as well?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T10:26:40-07:00","id":915696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=915678#post915678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I've added some descriptions to what you already had, and changed the name:<br /> <br /> I do think that the penalty for refusing the command being Wyrd + 1 might be a little high, given how easily that can be boosted with Potent Kith. Maybe half Wyrd? Have you considered allowing them to open an additional Door when using Hard Leverage as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. That was my original idea, actually. I'll probably revert that. And maybe add the Additional Door bit as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:19:28-07:00","id":915799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=915696#post915696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. That was my original idea, actually. I'll probably revert that. And maybe add the Additional Door bit as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good to me. Did the descriptions work for what you were envisioning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T19:53:57-07:00","id":915986,"title":"","content":"Yes. Yes, they did. :3 Anyway, here's the revised entry. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Taskmaster</u> </b><sup>By Deionscribe</sup><br /> <i>&quot;Fine. Let me rephrase that. Drop the gun. </i>Now<i>.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Not every Keeper wishes to keep a constant eye on his changelings. Taskmasters are appointed to watch their captor's servants, ensuring that her will is upheld even in her absence. While Taskmasters were natural leaders before their abduction, their roles as slave drivers often alienate them from other changelings. Most of those who escaped, though, either earned at least the respect of their fellow captives, or had no qualms about using them as puppets in order to save themselves.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast: </b>A tall and imposing ant man, with large, sharp mandibles and ever twitching antennae.<br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling</b><b>: </b>A cruel sneer permanently twists the face of the pale woman, a livid scar stretching from her forehead to her cheek.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental</b><b>: </b>This changeling appears to be an imperious queen painted in bold watercolors.<br /> \u2022 <b>Wizened</b><b>: </b>The changeling's eyes have been replaced with swirling black and white disks, and phantom whips extend from the back of each hand.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Taskmaster opens one additional Door when employing Hard Leverage, and can spend Glamour or Willpower to use the three-dot version of the Mind Control Merit. Anyone influenced by her command suffers a penalty equal to 1 + half her Wyrd, rounded up, for the rest of the scene or until it is completed. The effect lasts for a number of turns equal to the Taskmaster's Wyrd if the command cannot be done at the time and place it is given.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 06-20-2016, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T09:25:43-07:00","id":916266,"title":"","content":"It looks pretty good. I would lose the &quot;at least&quot; from the last sentence in the description, since it feels a bit clunky there. I'd also drop the +1 from the penalty for refusing the order, and possibly revert the number of turns back to half Wyrd as well. This is mostly because of the ease with which even a starting character could place a -4 penalty on someone for the scene by spending a point of Glamour and saying &quot;Shoot yourself in the head&quot;. That's just my thoughts, though, and ultimately they are minor enough alterations that I'd probably still consider them for my games as is. Good job on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T10:29:03-07:00","id":916308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=916266#post916266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks pretty good. I would lose the &quot;at least&quot; from the last sentence in the description, since it feels a bit clunky there. I'd also drop the +1 from the penalty for refusing the order, and possibly revert the number of turns back to half Wyrd as well. This is mostly because of the ease with which even a starting character could place a -4 penalty on someone for the scene by spending a point of Glamour and saying &quot;Shoot yourself in the head&quot;. That's just my thoughts, though, and ultimately they are minor enough alterations that I'd probably still consider them for my games as is. Good job on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like it.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Hmmm. How about this tweak? <hr /><br /> <b><u>Taskmaster</u> </b><sup>By Deionscribe</sup><br /> <i>&quot;Fine. Let me rephrase that. Drop the gun. </i>Now<i>.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Not every Keeper wishes to keep a constant eye on his changelings. Taskmasters are appointed to watch their captor's servants, ensuring that her will is upheld even in her absence. Though they were natural leaders before their abduction, their roles as slave drivers often alienate them from other changelings. Most of those who escaped, though, either earned the respect of their fellow captives, or had no qualms about using them as puppets in order to save themselves.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast: </b>An ant man with twitching antennae, and mandibles capable of human speech.<br /> \u2022 <b>Darkling</b><b>: </b>A cruel sneer permanently twists the face of the pale woman, a livid scar stretching from her forehead to her cheek.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental</b><b>: </b>This changeling appears to be an imperious queen painted in bold watercolors.<br /> \u2022 <b>Wizened</b><b>: </b>The changeling's eyes have been replaced with swirling black and white disks, and phantom whips extend from the back of each hand.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Taskmaster opens one additional Door when employing Hard Leverage, and can spend Glamour or Willpower to use the three-dot version of the Mind Control Merit. Anyone influenced by her command suffers a penalty equal to 1 + half the changeling's Wyrd, rounded down, to all other actions for the rest of the scene or until it is completed. Furthermore, if the command can't be fulfilled within the scene, it instead lasts for a number of turns equal to half the Taskmaster's Wyrd, rounded up","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":".  Tweaked the Blessing. 06-18-2016, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T15:43:47-07:00","id":916464,"title":"","content":"I'm glad that you reduced the duration, although the way it is worded sounds like the penalty itself has increased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T19:57:12-07:00","id":916574,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=916464#post916464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad that you reduced the duration, although the way it is worded sounds like the penalty itself has increased.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think that's the last point I need to work out, since Mind Control as is imposes a &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\">a -2 penalty to all actions for the rest of the scene or until the command is completed&quot;. I was wondering whether or not it should have some more force to it. Hence why I set it at &quot;1 + half the changeling's Wyrd, rounded up&quot;. Hmm. How about rounded <i>down</i> instead?</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T21:07:07-07:00","id":916621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=916574#post916574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> <br /> Well, I think that's the last point I need to work out, since Mind Control as is imposes a &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\">a -2 penalty to all actions for the rest of the scene or until the command is completed&quot;. I was wondering whether or not it should have some more force to it. Hence why I set it at &quot;1 + half the changeling's Wyrd, rounded up&quot;. Hmm. How about rounded <i>down</i> instead?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What about -2 or half Wyrd, whichever is higher? Rounded down, as you suggested, would also work well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T21:22:51-07:00","id":916632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=916621#post916621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about -2 or half Wyrd, whichever is higher? Rounded down, as you suggested, would also work well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went with the rounded down one. Edited the write-up to reflect it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/>