strong>hyperspacewizard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=936794#post936794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone think a kith that interacts with spirits like the gravewright kith would be a good ideal or is the changeling setting not a good one for including spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>There had been someone who had suggested such a kith earlier in the thread, but I can't remember if that ever went anywhere. I see no problem with such a kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T17:42:57-07:00","id":937843,"title":"","content":"I was thinking spirits are to much outside of the wryds paradigm maybe a kith that instead of talking to spirits could talk to inanimate objects and ask them favors like make it a social role. Like a kith with a similar power to the fan made The Office of the Lord Stewards \u2013 Arrangements specifically the Loqui ad Terram power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T19:27:31-07:00","id":937876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hyperspacewizard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=937843#post937843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking spirits are to much outside of the wryds paradigm maybe a kith that instead of talking to spirits could talk to inanimate objects and ask them favors like make it a social role.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like it'd give the changeling a free goblin vow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T20:47:22-07:00","id":938560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hyperspacewizard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=937843#post937843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking spirits are to much outside of the wryds paradigm maybe a kith that instead of talking to spirits could talk to inanimate objects and ask them favors like make it a social role. Like a kith with a similar power to the fan made The Office of the Lord Stewards \u2013 Arrangements specifically the Loqui ad Terram power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've always had a question of what exactly the Fae made Contracts with-- say, the infamous agreement they broke with Iron. What is Iron in this case? Possibly a powerful spirit, maybe in the time before the Sundering? Maybe even before Arcadia broke away from the Fallen world... Just speculation, of course, but I imagine the Fae once had a much closer relationship with the spirit world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T21:57:09-07:00","id":938592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=938560#post938560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always had a question of what exactly the Fae made Contracts with</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyrd.<br /> <br /> The Fae make Contracts with reality through the interface of the Wyrd, which is to be expected on account of how it's what they're made of and where they get the authority to make the kind of exchanges that the legendary word-bond enforces.<br /> <br /> Why Iron is treated so favorably by the Wyrd is a different question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T22:11:14-07:00","id":938603,"title":"","content":"One might not unreasonably consider Iron the Wyrd's equal and opposite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T11:08:15-07:00","id":940150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=938603#post938603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One might not unreasonably consider Iron the Wyrd's equal and opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking along the same lines. Iron in mythology seems to have associations of stability, something relatively fixed and immutable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T21:39:06-07:00","id":966038,"title":"","content":"I've had a fascination with the idea of Kiths that could weave temporary mental conditions into the minds of others. Moonborn looked like an interesting kith although I haven't seen the Lunacy Condition defined in any preview drafts. Although 2E went away from the Derangement style of mental afflictions I've kind of missed that classification in my own games, for characters with the ability to work madness into the minds of others.<br /> <br /> I've been running a game for almost a year now with two Changeling NPCs that fit in this concept. One took up residency as a psychology professor at a midwestern campus and the other is a transplanted brooding-beau who runs about in a dream protecting motley on the west coast. The verse originally had a shared setting to it before the second group of players collapsed. Both of the Changelings I've mentioned were Darklings that shared a Durance from a Keeper's realm of razor mirrors and deeply psychological horrors.<br /> <br /> Given that they were NPCs I played fast and loose with their innate capabilities from their Dual Kiths. Professor Thatcher (as in Margaret Thatcher, very low key name) was a Razohand/Moonborn and Smythe the other changeling was a Pischa/Moonborn (Pisacha comes fromWinter Masques). Although I've been thinking of switching out their shared Kith for a home-brewed idea matching the style of their powers I wanted to convey. Thatcher, also being a Razorhand, could reap the 'derangement' out of a target to transfer it to someone else. And Smythe could use his madness inducing kiss from the Pisacha Kith to inflict a negative mental condition he had endured within the past month.<br /> <br /> <br /> At the moment I don't have a coherent draft for what this custom kith should be called and how the Blessing would be worded. The idea is that the Changeling could receive and instill negative mental conditions in others, suffering from the Condition as persistent when they house it or recalling a Condition they've endured in the past month. Wyrd would likely play a part for the number of days they could inflict the Condition on another target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T21:59:19-07:00","id":966045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=966038#post966038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the moment I don't have a coherent draft for what this custom kith should be called and how the Blessing would be worded. The idea is that the Changeling could receive and instill negative mental conditions in others, suffering from the Condition as persistent when they house it or recalling a Condition they've endured in the past month. Wyrd would likely play a part for the number of days they could inflict the Condition on another target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps a number of days equal to half the changeling's Wyrd, rounded up? And as for a name, how does Psyker sound? Granted, the term was taken from Warhammer 40K but it sounds apt nonetheless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T02:33:18-07:00","id":971219,"title":"","content":"What would be a good replacement for the ability to switch fighting styles and ignore preregs for the soldier kith I like the theme and the last bit with the weapons and armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T09:18:08-07:00","id":971352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=915066#post915066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about something like Enforcer, Slave Driver, Taskmaster, or Overseer?</div> </div> </div> </div> I like Overseer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T09:32:51-07:00","id":971359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=857675#post857675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Damsel</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;If you expect me to put out just because you saved me, I'll show you what happened to the last guy who made assumptions about me.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Some Fae like to play the hero in their realm, defeating the forces of evil and saving the people while being showered with praise. Unfortunately their alien mindset is unable to distinguish genuine acts of heroism from a common PR stunt. Changelings who became Damsels were taken from women who lead abusive or dangerous lives for the soul purpose of being rescued over and over again. During their time in Arcadia, they were constantly kidnapped, threatened, assaulted, or imprisoned from the world, only to have their Keeper come to their rescue. After being celebrated for their heroic deed, the Keeper would take the Damsel to his bed and the cycle would repeat again. One day, they decided to save themselves instead of waiting around for others to do it for them!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Her perfect beauty attracted the scorn of those vying for her Keeper's affections. One day, she took advantage of her position and staged a preemptive strike on the evil queen, denying the Keeper his chance to save the day.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> She was told that only true love's kiss would break the spell that turned her into a hideous monster. But now she's done looking for romance, she just wants revenge on the one who cursed her.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A beautiful nature spirit kidnapped by evil wizards who desired her power for their own. One day, she decided to show them what happens when you antagonize mother nature.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> Isolated from social contact, she often found that animals were her only companions in life. One day she used her connection to them and became the savage princess of the wild that she is now.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Her Keeper trapped her in a continuous loop of watching her friends and family slaughtered by a tyrant who claimed her as his bride, only to have the Keeper avenge their deaths and free her from the unwanted marriage. That kind of trauma can do terrible things to a young girl's soul, like giving her the strength to murder her husband who was still exhausted from sex.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> A life sized toy brought to life, she was the key piece of a play set orchestrated by her Keeper. Before her escape, she showed the puppet master why men often have a psychological fear of dolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Damsels were made to be rescued until they learned how to rescue themselves. Their blessing gives them the Rote quality on attempts to persuade others that they are weak or foolish. They also add half their Wyrd rounded up on attempts to maintain their Wits during unprovoked confrontations, even if they pretend to have done otherwise. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, they can add +3 to Subterfuge rolls for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> As the name implies, Damsels are stereotypically female characters. However, there have cases where eccentric or female oriented Keepers have chosen male Damsels as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think Nighting Gale Syndrome is kind of the female verison of treating males as damsels, its just less actiony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:36:14-07:00","id":971390,"title":"","content":"Mastermind <br /> <br /> Update to my Villian Kith. Just a new name.<br /> <br /> Masochists.<br /> <br /> The Masochists and Sadists are the Gentry's attempt at understanding human pain.<br /> <br /> Masochists: The Masochists gain pleasure for pain, but also power. They bounce back from a beating faster then other Changelings.<br /> <br /> Fairest: Golden Piecings, and glowing whip marks in gorgeous, erotic patterns that change often.<br /> <br /> Beast: Feline features, with a collar and cuffs, purrs when hurt.<br /> <br /> Elemental: Skin is one giant scar, cracked and bleeding.<br /> <br /> Blessing: Any time the Masochist takes 3 bashing or 1 lethal damage they gain a point of glammer. By spending a point of Glamour they can regenerate like a werewolf for a scene.<br /> <br /> Sadists: Generally unpopular with other Changeling except those with gruesome Kiths and oddly Masochists who are drawn to Sadists like moths to flames.<br /> <br /> Orgers: Covered in blood splatter that never washes off and surrounded by the screams of their victims at all times.<br /> <br /> Darkling: Skin like supple black leather, eyes that sparkling and glow then they cause pain.<br /> <br /> Wizened: Shaped like a mobile ironmaiden with arms and legs, some always seems to be someone struggling and crying within the Wizened.<br /> <br /> Blessing. You can summon a whip or riding crop by spending a point of Glamour. You have a free speciality in whips and riding crops. A Changeling has to spend twice as much glamour to get free if you tie them up or imprison them.<br /> <br /> Heirophants<br /> <br /> True Fae often loved to be worshipped. All Heirophants have the symbol of their Keepers on their foreheads, but in none Loyalists that Symbol is upside down to express they're rebellion.<br /> <br /> Fairest: WIngs of Light and glowing eyes, with a glowing the symbol of their Keeper on their forheads.<br /> <br /> Darkling: Batwing made of Shadow, red skin, and massive horns, and their Keepers symbol on their foreheads written in shadows and flame.<br /> <br /> Wizened: Flesh like parchment with the holy words of their Keeper written on their skin in blood, and a metal holy symbol embedded in their forehead.<br /> <br /> Blessing: You gain the Lay on Hands Merit, you have a free occult specialty in your Keeper.<br /> <br /> Grim Reapers: Some Changeling refuse to make a deal with death in Arcadia, the True Fae used the Grim Reapers to convince those Changelings to make deals with death.<br /> <br /> Darkling: Fact like a skull and robes of shadows.<br /> <br /> Beasts: Jackle headed Anubis like Grim Reapers, with Heiroglyph tattoos expressing great truths about dying.<br /> <br /> Fairest: Looking like a beautiful corpse straight from the Morturary's makeup artist, they don't appear to breath and when cut, they bleed perservatives, not blood.<br /> <br /> Blessings: Spend a point of glamour and touch a target to block them from magical healing during the scene. If the target dies during that scene they can choose not to come back if they have a resurrection power.<br /> <br /> Slob: Why the True Fae choose some people to become Slobs is unknown.<br /> <br /> Elemental: A pile of debris in human form, they keep dropping random peices of debris all over the place, which disppears when they get to far from it.<br /> <br /> Orger: Overweight with poor hygine, and a noise that always seems to be dripping with snot.<br /> <br /> Beast: A dirty Racoon, Rat, or Pigeon, with animal droppings scatter all around them.<br /> <br /> Blessings: Spend a Glamour and have someone of your choice within 30 feet trip on a discarded piece of your mien. With a touch learn any taboos they might have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-17-2016, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:45:16-07:00","id":971399,"title":"","content":"Hologram:<br /> <br /> Fairest: You look like an exotic fantasy, but you shimmer everyonce in a while as your light pattern is disturbed.<br /> <br /> Elemental: Glowing, nearly transparent light of a single colour, thst occassional shimmers.<br /> <br /> Wizened: You look like a robot with a projector. Instead of a shadow, your projector projects a semitransparent hologram of your Mask.<br /> <br /> Blessing: For a point of Glamour you create a hologram.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:53:43-07:00","id":971435,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Paleos</b></span><br /> <i>Time ain't what you think it is, kid. Not in There. I walked an ancient world. All the stuff you ever learned in school is the stripped-down 'kids' movie fairy tale' version of it. Monsters that shook the earth. Screeching not-birds wheeling in the sky. Deserts so vast they are oceans, oceans so vast whole worlds could swim between 'em. I was a monster there, too. And I liked it.</i><br /> <br /> The True Fae weren't always &quot;the Gentry.&quot; They're prehistoric, haunting the dreams of mortals since the days of Paleolithic hunters and perhaps before. The scariest stories tell that the Fae intentionally spurred the dreams that inspired humans to grow, that they might have more interesting playthings. Even in those ancient days the True Fae captured mortals and took them to impossibly vast wildernesses born of primal nightmares. The Paleos are just that: remnants of the creatures and powerful elemental forces that raged so fiercely in this prehistoric paradise. More than most other changelings they return to a time far removed from the world they knew. How they can return when this is the case is a matter of endless debate, but the echoing laughter of now-refined Gentry follows these living fossils out of their lost world.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Beast: </b>Armored skin, spikes, fangs, glowing reptilian eyes. A Beast that would give dinosaurs nightmares.<br /> \u2022 <b>Elemental:</b> Craggy skin like igneous rock, emitting noxious volcanic fumes with every breath.<br /> \u2022 <b>Fairest:</b> Tall, Amazonian in build, clad in a raiment of glittering fronds and animal hides that move as though alive.<br /> \u2022 <b>Ogre:</b> A saurian behemoth, its hide pitted and scarred with murals that depict her many battles.<br /> \u2022 <b>Wizened:</b> This creature is swift, short, and covered in fur, with wide yellow eyes that let its clever fingers work in the dark.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>Hailing from the savage primordial Faerie, Paleos are rugged in a way that few modern changelings can match. Scaled armor or thick fur grant the changeling 1/1 armor. The character gains a +3 bonus to Speed and perception rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T14:12:17-07:00","id":971519,"title":"","content":"I like the Paleos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T17:01:19-07:00","id":971584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=971519#post971519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Paleos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second that. It's a pretty good kith write-up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T04:16:50-07:00","id":971869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=971584#post971584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I second that. It's a pretty good kith write-up.</div> </div> </div> </div> Motion passed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T21:33:33-07:00","id":974225,"title":"","content":"Here is my first attempt at a kith. <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Banshee</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Don\u2019t ever laugh as a hearse goes by, for you may be the next to die.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Being immortals the True Fae are fascinated by death. Not just the concept of being extinguished/ceasing to be, but the emotions surrounding death. All Banshee\u2019s are created from mortals touched by death in some way; the grief a mortal feels when losing a loved one, the guilt a soldier feels when they survived, but their unit did not, the horror of someone who has cancer growing in them. The True Fae took this connection to death and made it part of the changeling\u2019s kith.</span></span></span><br /> <b><i>Banshee\u2019s Lament:</i></b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Banshee\u2019s can feel death around them. They see the death marks on mortals and feel/experience a death that is currently happening near by. Finally, by spending a point of glamour, they can give a target, usually a mortal, a vision of their death.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><i>Darkling:</i></b> Ghostly apparitions whose wail </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">foretells your coming death.<br /> <i><b>Fairest: </b></i>Beautiful Maidens of the Sidhe<br /> <i><b>Wizened: </b></i>The Washer Woman who cleans your blood stained clothes.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T22:02:58-07:00","id":974230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=974225#post974225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is my first attempt at a kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not bad for a first attempt <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But I do wonder if there is a way to give their Blessing more potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T22:11:35-07:00","id":974234,"title":"","content":"Previously, I started a post wondering about a changeling crossover chronicle. Does anyone have ideas for a kith that was originally a mage, werewolf, or even vampire? While Witch tooth's can arguably be a mage type kith, my understanding is that you don't originally have to be one to be converted to this kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T22:18:49-07:00","id":974238,"title":"","content":"Deviant sounds like it might be changing it up, but generally none of the types of protagonist groups can be/have been a member of another of the splats previously. If memory serves, the metaphysical mojo would just cause the death of the individual. Individual STs could of course change this up for their table, but by the books, it's not an available option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:06:59-07:00","id":974575,"title":"","content":"Right, I was wondering something. I know the main benefit of a Kith roughly works out as equivalent to a 3 dot Merit, but has anyone figured out a pattern for the minor benefit that acompanies these Kiths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T11:41:01-07:00","id":975625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=974225#post974225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Fairest: </b></i>Beautiful Maidens of the Sidhe</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to give this a bit of flavour there is the stock phrase &quot;Na mn\u00e1 fionna&quot;, it basically refers to beautiful fairy women who used to kidnap young girls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T21:46:13-07:00","id":975826,"title":"","content":"If you want to give this a bit of flavour there is the stock phrase &quot;Na mn\u00e1 fionna&quot;, it basically refers to beautiful fairy women who used to kidnap young girls.<br /> <br /> Thanks<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T21:47:25-07:00","id":975827,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Having discussed Changeling crossover chronicles in another thread, I thought I would try my hand at a crossover kith. I shared some of my thoughts on Changeling vampires so here is my attempt at that.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><i>Red Stained</i></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There are many legends that link Fairies to vampires. The Baobhan sith lured unwary travelers with their charming looks to feast on their blood, the Glaistig, and the Red Caps who stained their hat\u2019s in the blood of their victims. The revelation of the existence of vampires has led some of the Lost to believe that these legends are about vampires who were turned into Changelings. This is partly incorrect. Because the Kindred gave up their souls, the Gentry tend to regards vampires the way humans regard rats or cockroaches. Many True, however, are curious about their ghoul servants and half-damned offspring, the Dhampires. The Red Stained are created from former ghouls and dhampires to explore the vampire curse\u2019 connection to life and the underworld.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Darklings: </i>Red Caps, Venezuelan La Sayona, The One Legged South American Patasola.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Elementals:</i> Slavic Samodiva</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Fairiest: Scottish </i>Baobahan sith, Indonesian Sundal Bolong, Russian Rusalka,</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>The Hunger:</i> The Red Stained blessing mimics the powers of vampires to a certain degree. They can harvest glamor by drinking blood, and have retractable fangs, and a healing saliva to leave no traces of a wound. Their ability to smell blood is as keen as a sharks and they gain +4 to all perception roles in an area where blood has been spilled. Finally, when they taste a victims vitae, they gain a great deal of genetic information on the victim.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T15:08:07-07:00","id":976745,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><i>The Daemonic</i></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Some legends about the Fae claim that they are demons or fallen angels. These changelings and their Keepers are a manifestation of this belief. Ironically, they were not demon worshipers or occult scholars as mortals. They tend to be men and women of great Christian faith or innocence; pious priests, strict and severe nuns, innocent and chaste catholic school girls. The True Fae tried to corrupt/destroy their Christian faith by turning them into demons and forcing them to participate in some of the most depraved acts.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>The Devils Tongue:</i> The Daemonic possess one permanent demonic feature to better represent their infernal masters. They also have the 4 dot fame merit, in that mortals feel comfortable sharing their darkest secrets/desires with them. Finally, by spend a dot a glamor they can force a mortal to give in to their darkest desires.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Elementals: Namaru, Asharu, Annunaki,and Lammasu.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Fairiest: Lucifer</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Wiziened: Goblins and imps</i></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T19:19:06-07:00","id":978137,"title":"","content":"I've taken a shot at drafting out my mental afflicting kith idea mentioned earlier. The Blessing is a bit wordy, requiring a means of compact, but it hopefully brings out the intent of the Kith.<br /> <br /> Since this draft is several degrees removed from the Moonborn Kith, does anyone know if the mechanics of the Lunacy Condition are part of any current previews?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Corsiva\"><u>Psychsemy</u></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From what little the True Fae know of psychology, the effect is more like having the lunatic in charge of the asylum. These changelings both endured and help perpetuate a variety of derangements or psychoses in their Keeper\u2019s realms. Instilled to the very core with the concept of madness, the remain well aware of the mental states of others upon their escape.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Darkling</u>: he is a shriveled figure born from primordial nightmares with a maddening grin and diseased brain</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Elemental</u>: a chaotic swirl of pneuma, nigh invisible, with each wisp carrying an air of dark secrets</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Grimm</u>: she is a living Rorschach blot, her pattern meaning something different every time you look at it</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Fairest</u>: as beautifully disheveled as Ophelia within Hamlet, each slight a sign of what she is working through</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blessing: for the purposes of this kith the changeling can affect Conditions depicting mental state, not physical ones. When touching a target the Psychsemy can transfer such a Condition for 1 Glamour, housing it for the scene and transferring it to another with another touch and Glamour. For targets with a Persistent or inherent Condition it is instead muted for a number of hours equal to the Psychsemy\u2019s Wyrd before coming back. The Psychsemy can house stolen Conditions after the seen by making it Persistent. Persistant Conditions the Changeling suffers can be resolved normally, although they do not need to spend Glamour to distill that Condition in another. Alternatively, the Psychsemy can spend 2 Glamour to inflict a Condition they had within the last month. Also, when achieving an exceptional success when attacking a target the Psychsemy can inflict the Insane Tilt, changing it to an applicable Condition in the target after combat. New Conditions last for a number of hours equal to the Psychsemy\u2019s Wyrd, although they can make it Persistent by spending additional Glamour equal to the target\u2019s Willpower score.<br /> </span></span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"h