of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 10-01-2016, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:01:29-07:00","id":980023,"title":"","content":"I don't know. Which link has the most recent update?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:06:21-07:00","id":980028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=980023#post980023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. Which link has the most recent update?</div> </div> </div> </div>Edited the post to include the link.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:09:22-07:00","id":980029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=980028#post980028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edited the post to include the link.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you. And nothing particularly comes to mind right now. If I come up with any ideas, though, I'll let you know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T06:07:15-07:00","id":980207,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the link. I'll need to look it over after work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T12:36:22-07:00","id":980382,"title":"","content":"Regarding the <b><u>Homebrew Changeling Kiths (2E)</u></b> google document, which I believe has many of the Kiths created in this thread, a quick search-and-fine reveals that these Kiths have no current Wyrd based benefit:<br /> <br /> <b>Babelfish, Balaur, Executioner, Huckster, Oathdevil, Orc, Timekeeper, Treasured, Wavemaster</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1elqCKhNJweqnLuUy8Rbh2PiZSsnccnXQWrNy8cPf5o4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1elqCKhNJweqnLuUy8Rbh2PiZSsnccnXQWrNy8cPf5o4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1elqCKhNJweqnLuUy8Rbh2PiZSsnccnXQWrNy8cPf5o4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1elqCKhNJweqnLuUy8Rbh2PiZSsnccnXQWrNy8cPf5o4/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> --------------------------------------<br /> <br /> While I'm here, I wanted to toss out a Winter Masques revision, one of my favorites:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Corsiva\"><u>Pamarindo</u></span></span></b><br /><br /><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First appearing in Italian folklore, the Pamarindo were master butchers and chefs in their Keepers banquet halls, needing to hunt and prepare all manner of strange game. Out of the Hedge their methods and recipes may look gruesome yet are oddly satisfying.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Beast:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> a stately bloodstained carnivore, well worked claws as their cooking utensils</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Fairest:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> shapely and well fed with the aromatic smell of cooking meat, yet harsh taskmasters in the kitchen</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Ogre:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> built as if hammocks and other appropriated meat make up their muscles</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Grimm:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> unread recipe cards along his back, with naught but an apron and knife he\u2019s worked his way through every use of cuisine in a tale</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Wizened:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> shriveled potbellied folk like a dried carcass, deftly arranging cuts of meat</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing:</b> the Changeling gains a +2 bonus when appropriate to finding food or staving off their own deprivation. Gain a free Weaponry specialty in Knives and the Interdisciplinary merit for this specialty regardless of prerequisite. For 1 Glamour with a pound of meat or flesh available (other ingredients optional) the Pamarindo can whip up a meal within a minute to feed a number of people equal to their Wyrd. The dish nourishes for a full 24 hours.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T18:57:41-07:00","id":980515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=980382#post980382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the <b><u>Homebrew Changeling Kiths (2E)</u></b> google document, which I believe has many of the Kiths created in this thread, a quick search-and-fine reveals that these Kiths have no current Wyrd based benefit:<br /> <br /> <b>Babelfish, Balaur, Executioner, Huckster, Oathdevil, Orc, Timekeeper, Treasured, Wavemaster</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1elqCKhNJweqnLuUy8Rbh2PiZSsnccnXQWrNy8cPf5o4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Here's my revisions for some of those Kiths.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Huckster</u></b><br /> Hucksters are skilled brokers and businessmen, able to land good bargains (and weed out bad ones) with ruthless efficiency. They gain the Market Sense Merit for free, and may apply the latter to deals and transactions made outside the Goblin Market a number of times equal to their Wyrd in a day. They may also perform Bargains without shedding the Mask.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Timekeeper</u></b><br /> The Timekeeper has an absolute knowledge of the time, and can count it down to the second like a stopwatch even if he were unconscious in a barren room. He gains the Good Time Management and Patient Merits, and can tell the precise age of any person, object, or place they see. If this knowledge is supernaturally concealed, he may roll Wits + Wyrd in a Clash of Wills. If he spends a point of Glamour, he may also know the Defense, Initiative, and Speed of any people encountered in the scene.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Treasured</u></b><br /> Treasured gain the Vainglory clause, Splendor of the Envoy's Protection, for free, and benefit from the 8-again rule when invoking its effect. They also acquire the three-dot version of the Iron Stamina Merit, and lower the effects of any Extreme Environment on them by half their Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Wavemaster</u></b><br /> A Wavemaster can breathe underwater, and halves all healing times so long as she is fully submerged. She also benefits from the rote quality on all swimming rolls. If she spends Glamour or Willpower, she may use the three-dot version of the Psychokinesis Merit to affect water, and may use Wyrd instead of the normal dice pool.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Hmm. The Pamarindo doesn't seem too unchanged from its 1E version, but I'll wait to hear from the other people who follow this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 10-02-2016, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T20:53:50-07:00","id":980560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=980515#post980515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. The Pamarindo doesn't seem too unchanged from its 1E version, but I'll wait to hear from the other people who follow this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>The meat cooking is unchanged, I merely added a set time to how long the cooking takes (since no roll is involved). In 1E the kith also granted the Iron Stomach merit but that hasn't carried over, so it become the bonus for foraging, hunting for food, resisting starvation and food poisoning as well. The Knives Specialty used to be 1E Razorhand I believe, although I find that to be more suitable for the &quot;butcher kith&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T06:11:22-07:00","id":982087,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's an update (and minor nerf) for the oathdevils.<br /> <br /> <b>Oathdevil</b><br /> <br /> <i>Silence! I don't want to hear your protests or excuses. You agreed to our bargain. I'm just here to collect.</i><br /> <br /> Woe be to those who encounter the oathdevil at the crossroads, for his friendly demeanor obscures the hidden barbs of his agreements. These changelings, chosen for their literal minds and attention to detail, were often employed by their Keepers to track and punish their wayward servants. Upon escape, an oathdevil is likely to weave himself an intricate web of influence and owed favors in whichever freehold he claims as home.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> She is inhumanly beautiful, with a lovely voice and seductive mannerisms that distract from the dainty horns upon her head and the fire in her eyes.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> His vellum skin is covered in minute contractual language, with larger signatures inked in blood foreshadowing the fates of those who would cross him.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A large and menacing figure, with two spiraling horns and three golden hairs upon his head. <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> His fiber optic tail twitches of its own accord, and his horns are constructed from the bones of an oathbreaker.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> An oathdevil is a dangerous changeling to cross, as the pledges that he creates carry severe consequences. When sealing a statement, the sealing is automatically considered strengthened. By spending Willpower to strengthen it further, the oathdevil may impose either the Leveraged or Ensnared Condition on the subject. The Ensnared Condition functions identically to Leveraged, except that the subject also suffers a -3 penalty to contest or resist the oathdevil's Contracts. These Conditions last for the duration of the sealing, but become Persistent if the pledge is broken. Additionally, the oathdevil may track the subject as though they shared a personal oath together. By spending a point of Glamour in the presence of someone with the Oathbreaker Condition, the oathdevil may apply the Ensnared Condition, which persists until the Oathbreaker Condition is resolved. The oathdevil may only have a number of subjects Ensnared equal to his Wyrd at any time, although he may remove the Ensnared Condition and apply Leveraged instead for a point of Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T08:34:40-07:00","id":982140,"title":"","content":"Having Wyrd as a cap works well as a 'nerf' in regards to not making the Kith overpowered. Better want to think twice if you take Oathdevil along with Dual Kith.<br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> Any general feedback on wordsmithing for the Psychsemy Kith I wrote a few posts back?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T06:23:09-07:00","id":982654,"title":"","content":"A new kith-in-progress from me. I'm still not sure if the name I picked is the right one, and I'm having trouble working out a description. Anyone mind giving me a hand? <hr /><br /> <u><b>Bareface</b></u><br /> <i>&quot;I hope you know what you're getting into, buddy. I have a very good poker face.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Changeling gains the Rigid Mask Merit with no drawback, and applies 1 + half his Wyrd as a penalty to characters who can perceive his Mien. He also gains an automatic success on all Subterfuge rolls, in addition to the roll results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 10-06-2016, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T07:09:11-07:00","id":982675,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> <br /> Based on the latest revisions on the 2E kiths, what do you think of of the changes to these two? Also, the Wyrdo might also need some tweaking to make use of Wyrd. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Babelfish</u></b><br /> When speaking to a Babelfish, you may as well be talking in their native language as far as they're concerned. He is automatically fluent in all forms of spoken language, even if it is the first time hearing it. If he spends a point of Glamour while performing a touch action, he can share this knowledge to someone else for the scene. A Babelfish can apply his blessing in this manner to a number of people equal to his Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Executioner</u></b><br /> Masters of death and destruction, the Executioner gains the benefit of the 8-Again rule when attempting to use any weapon type they have a Specialty in. Additionally, when attacking, they may spend a point of Glamour to upgrade an amount of damage equal to half their Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T07:48:04-07:00","id":982688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=982654#post982654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A new kith-in-progress from me. I'm still not sure if the name I picked is the right one, and I'm having trouble working out a description. Anyone mind giving me a hand? <hr /><br /> <u><b>Bareface</b></u><br /> <i>&amp;quot;I hope you know what you're getting into, buddy. I have a very good poker face.&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Changeling gains the Rigid Mask Merit with no drawback, and applies 1 + half his Wyrd as a penalty to characters who can perceive his Mien. He also gains an automatic success on all Subterfuge rolls, in addition to the roll results.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about simply going for Deceiver? Or Inveigler for a more obscure term. You could have them as changelings that were used to lure people in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T10:45:54-07:00","id":982788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=982688#post982688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about simply going for Deceiver? Or Inveigler for a more obscure term. You could have them as changelings that were used to lure people in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Inveigler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:26:22-07:00","id":982930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=982675#post982675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a><br /> Based on the latest revisions on the 2E kiths, what do you think of of the changes to these two? Also, the Wyrdo might also need some tweaking to make use of Wyrd. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Babelfish</u></b><br /> When speaking to a Babelfish, you may as well be talking in their native language as far as they're concerned. He is automatically fluent in all forms of spoken language, even if it is the first time hearing it. If he spends a point of Glamour while performing a touch action, he can share this knowledge to someone else for the scene. A Babelfish can apply his blessing in this manner to a number of people equal to his Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Executioner</u></b><br /> Masters of death and destruction, the Executioner gains the benefit of the 8-Again rule when attempting to use any weapon type they have a Specialty in. Additionally, when attacking, they may spend a point of Glamour to upgrade an amount of damage equal to half their Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, those look good to me, and I don't think they're too dissimilar from their original versions, if I remember correctly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:56:12-07:00","id":983740,"title":"","content":"Finally worked out my new Kith. Behold the Grifter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Grifter</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;Trust me on this. I haven't let you down, yet.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Many True Fae spirit their victims away through proxies, and those changed into Grifters were counted among such tools. Chronic liars and silvertongued rogues, many were tasked with luring unsuspecting mortals into the waiting arms of their masters, or sowing dissent within a Freehold. Those who do defy their Keepers did so after the lies become too much to bear, or they came to see their deceptions as the truth.<br /> <br /> \u25cf<b> Darkling:</b> A demonic figure garbed in a trenchcoat, whose red eyes glow in the shade of his fedora.<br /> \u25cf <b>Elemental:</b> The white mist that is her body greatly obscures the expressions of her face.<br /> \u25cf <b>Grimm:</b> Lines of encrypted text adorn his skin, and his eyes adjust and focus like camera lenses.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Grifter gains the Rigid Mask Merit, and does not take lethal damage whenever he sheds his mask. Furthermore, changelings and other creatures that can perceive his Mien suffer a penalty equal to 1 + Wyrd on rolls made to tell either if he's lying or what he is thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T04:23:24-07:00","id":984344,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a><br /> <br /> Any suggestions and additions for expanding this latest kith of mine? You can find the Master Shaper Merit <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K8R3qXyDyoY0lxSjZQZXhyNGc\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, and look at the rules for the Hedge in <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyocUNHbEc0T1RQYVU/view?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> for additional reference. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Bramblewright</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;You're realizing it, now, aren't you? Why I agreed to the duel? This is </i>my <i>turf. And we play by</i> my<i> rules</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Bramblewright gains the Master Shaper Merit at three dots, and a dot of Empathy that can take her beyond the limits of her Wyrd. She also takes no penalties to rolls for warping the Hedge, and may spend Glamour to add her Wyrd as successes to such rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 10-09-2016, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:16:43-07:00","id":984412,"title":"","content":"Maybe give it a background description? From the looks of it, it seems like they just pop in and start running the Hedge. Why would the True Fae create somebody like that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:48:20-07:00","id":984438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=984412#post984412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe give it a background description? From the looks of it, it seems like they just pop in and start running the Hedge. Why would the True Fae create somebody like that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually having a bit of trouble working out the description. But the basic idea for changelings of the Kith is that the Gentry use them to shape the Hedge to their liking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T09:11:32-07:00","id":984453,"title":"","content":"Update on the Kith, this time with description. Some ideas for Seemings would be nice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr /><br /> <b><u>Bramblewright</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;It's been quiet, so far. But my friends in the trods are on the lookout, just in case.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> While all changelings make use of the Hedge to varying degrees, those made into Bramblewrights had a special affinity for it. These Lost were made to impose their Keepers' will upon the Hedge which bordered their realms, warping it according to their ever-changing desires. Upon choosing to escape, though, their ability to shape this psychoreactive realm proved crucial to their success.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Bramblewright gains the Master Shaper Merit at three dots, and a dot of Empathy that can take her beyond the limits of her Wyrd. She also takes no penalties to rolls for warping the Hedge, and reduces the target number of successes for warping the Hedge by her Wyrd, to a minimum of one. When she chooses to infuse objects or spaces with emotion, she needs to have invested at least [25 - Wyrd] successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T06:26:04-07:00","id":984846,"title":"","content":"It looks like it's coming along pretty well. I'll need to look over the Merit and the Hedge shaping rules again, but it looks promising. For Seemings:<br /> <br /> Elemental: Twisting coils of thorny vines compose her body, but a small horror nesting in the hollow of her heart is unique to each observer.<br /> Fairest: The androgynous figure is unquestionably beautiful, but his or her features are an amalgam of everyone who ever broke your heart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T06:53:52-07:00","id":984862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=984846#post984846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like it's coming along pretty well. I'll need to look over the Merit and the Hedge shaping rules again, but it looks promising. For Seemings:<br /> <br /> Elemental: Twisting coils of thorny vines compose her body, but a small horror nesting in the hollow of her heart is unique to each observer.<br /> Fairest: The androgynous figure is unquestionably beautiful, but his or her features are an amalgam of everyone who ever broke your heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are great descriptions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Here's one for Grimms.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Grimm:</b> Everchanging lines of text on his skin recount to onlookers the most painful moments in their lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T10:01:49-07:00","id":984925,"title":"","content":"Say, does anyone have suggestions for naming a kith with this blessing? I'm also wondering how to expand it beyond the Merit.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Found a name.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Mender</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The changeling gains the Faerie Healing Merit, and heals lethal damage or downgrades aggravated damage equal to half her Wyrd for each Goblin Fruit consumed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 10-11-2016, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T20:36:08-07:00","id":988097,"title":"","content":"Update to the Apollonian kith x3<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> An Apollonian gains an extra dot in Strength or Dexterity, which can take her above the usual limitations imposed by her Wyrd. She also benefits from the 8-again rule on all Athletics, Brawl, Firearms, and Weaponry rolls made during competitions, duels, self-defense, and showing off, and may roll her Wyrd in place of her normal dice pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 10-15-2016, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T09:33:38-07:00","id":988278,"title":"","content":"That seems quite potent, especially when paired with Potent Kith. Someone who maxed it out at character creation would have a minimum of 6 dice with the 8-again effect on virtually every combat dice pool regardless of opponent Defense, as well as a majority of Athletics rolls. They're ineffective as stealthy assassins, but pretty much any other combat situation they will own easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T10:07:10-07:00","id":988295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=988278#post988278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems quite potent, especially when paired with Potent Kith. Someone who maxed it out at character creation would have a minimum of 6 dice with the 8-again effect on virtually every combat dice pool regardless of opponent Defense, as well as a majority of Athletics rolls. They're ineffective as stealthy assassins, but pretty much any other combat situation they will own easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a good thing or a bad thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:13:32-07:00","id":988386,"title":"","content":"A bad thing. It ensures that in the majority of situations involving one of those four skills the character will have 8-Again and six dice minimum (provided the character invested heavily in Potent Kith, and with benefits like that, who wouldn't?). It puts the other combat oriented kiths to shame, and gives them a boost to most athletic endeavors as well. Really good armor and tactics would be required to even stand a chance against one, and even then a Soldier or Razorhand would be praying for the dice gods to hate the Apollonian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:02:34-07:00","id":988635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=988386#post988386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bad thing. It ensures that in the majority of situations involving one of those four skills the character will have 8-Again and six dice minimum (provided the character invested heavily in Potent Kith, and with benefits like that, who wouldn't?). It puts the other combat oriented kiths to shame, and gives them a boost to most athletic endeavors as well. Really good armor and tactics would be required to even stand a chance against one, and even then a Soldier or Razorhand would be praying for the dice gods to hate the Apollonian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. So, reverting it back to its original version (no Firearms dice trick and no Wyrd benefit), how would you apply Wyrd in a balanced manner?<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a>, how about this?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Apollonian:</b><br /> The Apollonian embodies the physical ideal of perfection rather than the aesthetic. She gains a dot of Strength or Dexterity, which can bring her above her normal limit based on her Wyrd, and benefits from the 8-again rule on all Athletics rolls. If she makes an Athletics, Brawl, or Weaponry roll for a competition, duel, self-defense, or showing off, she may use her Wyrd instead of her normal dice pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 10-17-2016, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T23:04:31-07:00","id":989229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=988635#post988635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. So, reverting it back to its original version (no Firearms dice trick and no Wyrd benefit), how would you apply Wyrd in a balanced manner?<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, how about this?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Apollonian:</b><br /> The Apollonian embodies the physical ideal of perfection rather than the aesthetic. She gains a dot of Strength or Dexterity, which can bring her above her normal limit based on her Wyrd, and benefits from the 8-again rule on all Athletics rolls. If she makes an Athletics, Brawl, or Weaponry roll for a competition, duel, self-defense, or showing off, she may use her Wyrd instead of her normal dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to need to give this a bit of thought. As it stands, it was an extremely potent blessing in the first place. They gained a dot in an Attribute, 8-Again on 3 different skills under most circumstances (as opposed to 8-Again on a single skill regardless of circumstances), and adding the current Wyrd benefit makes it so that even a starting character can ensure a decent dice pool to take full advantage of said 8-Again effect. The change to only Athletics gaining 8-Again was a good one, and is definitely a step in the right direction. I'd be reluctant to allow the Wyrd benefit to cover as many circumstances as it does, though. Especially for combat rolls. It leads to &quot;My character is throwing a knife. My base dice pool is 6. He had a four Defense, bringing me down to 2. I'll switch to Wyrd, which brings me back to 6. I'm also going to target his eye to blind him and bypass his armor. Still at 6 dice with the 8-Again effect.&quot; Allowing the Wyrd benefit to function that way effectively allows the character to bypass Defense, most Armor, and penalties for called shots and environmental difficulties, with 8-Again if it's Athletics based. I'll need to compare it to some of the other physically focused kiths, but it might work as simply as having a Glamour or Willpower cost in order to use the suggested Wyrd benefit for a turn. I'll give it a bit of thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T03:55:15-07:00","id":989283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=989229#post989229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to need to give this a bit of thought. As it stands, it was an extremely potent blessing in the first place. They gained a dot in an Attribute, 8-Again on 3 different skills under most circumstances (as opposed to 8-Again on a single skill regardless of circumstances), and adding the current Wyrd benefit makes it so that even a starting character can ensure a decent dice pool to take full advantage of said 8-Again effect.<br /> <br /> The change to only Athletics gaining 8-Again was a good one, and is definitely a step in the right direction. I'd be reluctant to allow the Wyrd benefit to cover as many circumstances as it does, though. Especially for combat rolls. It leads to &quot;My character is throwing a knife. My base dice pool is 6. He had a four Defense, bringing me down to 2. I'll switch to Wyrd, which brings me back to 6. I'm also going to target his eye to blind him and bypass his armor. Still at 6 dice with the 8-Again effect.&quot; Allowing the Wyrd benefit to function that way effectively allows the character to bypass Defense, most Armor, and penalties for called shots and environmental difficulties, with 8-Again if it's Athletics based. I'll need to compare it to some of the other physically focused kiths, but it might work as simply as having a Glamour or Willpower cost in order to use the suggested Wyrd benefit for a turn. I'll give it a bit of thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is another revision to the Apollonian.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Apollonian</u><br /> <br /> Blessing:</b> She gains the 8-again quality on all Athletics rolls, and a dot of Strength or Dexterity which can bring her beyond the limit of her Wyrd. Furthermore, when making a Brawl or Weaponry attack, she may choose to use her Wyrd in place of her normal dice pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:28:49-07:00","id":989458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=989283#post989283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here is another revision to the Apollonian.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Apollonian</u><br /> <br /> Blessing:</b> She gains the 8-again quality on all Athletics rolls, and a dot of Strength or Dexterity which can bring her beyond the limit of her Wyrd. Furthermore, when making a Brawl or Weaponry attack, she may choose to use her Wyrd in place of her normal dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is much better, as it keeps the character from coupling the 8-Again effect with the ability to ignore all penalties when attacking. That said, the ability to ignore all penalties when attacking is still pretty powerful. I'll use a couple examples, assuming 3 in each Attribute (4 for Apollonian, to reflect an extra dot of Strength being chosen) and Skill and Potent Kith 5 for each comparison.<br /> <br /> Let's start with improvised weapons. Bloodbrute gets to ignore the -1 penalty to attack with an improvised weapon, and gets to keep using it. The Apollonian gets to ignore the penalty as well, and also gets to ignore Defense, potentially ignore Armor (using a called shot is made to strike a vulnerable spot), and also make a called shot without any added difficulty. In effect, the Apollonian is more skilled at wielding improvised weapons, but the Bloodbrute gets to keep using them for longer.<br /> <br /> Looking at called shots, a Hunterheart can ignore penalties for a called shot equal to Wyrd. In this situation, both the Hunterheart and Apollonian will be able to ignore most penalties for called shots, and both will be able to bypass some worn Armor. An Apollonian will also ignore Defense, however. This is a much closer match, though, because while the Apollonian wins on called shots, the Hunterheart's got some goodies to help even the odds. It's debatable whether innate lethal damage and the ability to cause fear by locking eyes would be greater or less than 8-Again on Athletics, a bonus Attribute dot, and the ability to ignore Defense and environmental penalties during attacks, though I think I'd give the win to the Apollonian there.<br /> <br /> Now, on to inflicting Tilts. A Razorhand can spend a point of Glamour to make the next successful attack inflict one of four Tilts without needing to make a called shot. Assuming that they are facing an opponent with a Defense of 4, this will put the Razorhand at 2 dice on his attack roll. If he hits, he'll do a lot of damage with his attack and inflict the Tilt, but the odds aren't in his favor unless he spends Willpower. The Apollonian needs to make a called shot to be able to inflict one of those Tilts, but doing so doesn't penalize him and he's able to ignore Defense as well, giving him a base dice pool of six thanks to the Wyrd effect. This makes the Apollonian more skilled at applying the Tilts, but requires that he bring a weapon along to the fight if he wants to match the Razorhand in damage during successful attacks.<br /> <br /> On the whole, it seems to me that the Wyrd benefit in combat places the Apollonian on stronger ground than some of the other kiths that specialize in that arena, and that's before figuring in the 8-Again effect on Athletics and the bonus Attribute dot. That said, while potent, your current version isn't completely unreasonable. Back when it gave 8-Again to all of the above rolls, though... I'm glad that you changed that.<br /> <br /> Here's my thoughts on some potential Blessings:<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Apollonian was intended to be a model of physical perfection, and as such, gains an additional dot to either Strength or Dexterity, even if this takes him above the limit imposed by his Wyrd. Additionally, the character gains the 8-Again effect on Atheletics rolls involving his enhanced Attribute. When in situations intended to demonstrate his prowess to onlookers, such as during duels or competitions, the Apollonian ignores penalties to all Physical Skill dice-pools equal to half his Wyrd. He may increase this to his full Wyrd for a single action by spending a point of Glamour. If the Apollonian spends Glamour in this manner outside of such situations, the benefit is only equal to half his Wyrd for a single action.<br /> <br /> The above enables the character to excel physically wherever they go, but to truly shine in front of an audience. It also means that the character will be able to compete using Skills besides the combat ones, such as a Drive challenge for a chariot race or Larceny to reflect impressive feats of manual dexterity. It also means that a character with impressive Defense, such as a Skitterskulk (whose tripled Defense would just be outright ignored using the originally suggested Wyrd benefit) could continue to be more of a challenge to take down than an ordinary opponent, while still giving the Apollonian a greater chance of managing it than most others.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:00:03-07:00","id":989588,"title":"","content":"I like the revisions you're proposing xD And I agree on all those points. I'll be making the changes to the doc with a few tweaks soon, as written below.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Apollonian was intended to be a model of physical perfection. He gains an additional dot to either Strength or Dexterity, which may bring him above the limit imposed by his Wyrd, as well as the 8-Again quality on Athletics rolls which use his enhanced Attribute. In situations intended to demonstrate his prowess to onlookers, such as during duels or competitions, the character ignores penalties to all Physical Skill dice pools equal to half his Wyrd. He may increase this to his full Wyrd for a single action by spending a point of Glamour. If the Apollonian spends Glamour in this manner outside of such situations, the benefit is only equal to half his Wyrd for a single action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T00:15:12-07:00","id":989760,"title":"","content":"I'm glad that you liked them, Deionscribe.<br /> <br /> So, on another thread, people have been saying that they'd like to see a hacker kith in the future. Here's my attempt at such a thing:<br /> <br /> <b>Cybersage</b><br /> <br /> She's so weird. Yeah, she's smart, but she always seems distracted, and sometimes, she just starts laughing for no reason in the middle of class. <br /> <br /> The rapid rise of technology in mortal society has not gone unnoticed by the Others, and some have chosen to embrace the new toys that the mortals have created. Cybersages are the tools of choice for these Gentry, who use them as espionage agents or soldiers on the field of cyberwarfare. Tasked with undermining the efforts of other technologically savvy Fae, Cybersages frequently burn out from the constant need for their talents.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> This adorable kitten is always laughing about something.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> She resembles a video game avatar, beautiful to behold, but firmly in the uncanny valley.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> Glowing lines of binary code flow constantly beneath her glass skin.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> This ill-tempered troll has a foul mouth, thick glasses, and surprisingly dexterous fingers.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Cybersages add their Wyrd to dice pools using the Computer Skill. A Cybersage may also interface with any electronic device she can physically touch, bypassing mundane security measures like passwords or firewalls, although supernatural protection provokes a Clash of Wills. Additionally, by spending a point of Glamour, a Cybersage may mentally access the Internet for the scene as though she had a smartphone or laptop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:43:59-07:00","id":989798,"title":"","content":"This looks promising as a concept, but perhaps you can try incorporating the Technopathy Merit from the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jM_bpQHo-dM4yop592S09y4AjQGLLTNhK5_0-5_85kg/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\">Hurt Locker drafts</a>?<br /> <br /> Here's an alternative take on the Blessing.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Cybersages add their Wyrd to dice pools using the Computer Skill, and can spend Glamour or Willpower to use the Technopathy Merit at three dots. She may also use it on a target a number of times equal to half her Wyrd without its drawback, and ignores penalties from mundane security measures like passwords or firewalls, although supernatural protection provokes a Clash of Wills. If she spends a point of Glamour, a Cybersage may mentally access the Internet for the scene as though she had a smartphone or laptop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 10-19-2016, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T04:36:11-07:00","id":989826,"title":"","content":"Here's another kith which uses a Merit from the Hurt Locker drafts.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Spellbinder</u></b><br /> <i>You tore my life apart. Now, I'll do the same to yours.</i><br /> <br /> There is power found in one's image, and those who subvert it can hold great power over him. Changelings transformed into Spellbinders were made to punish their Keepers' captives enemies with equal measure. They wove charms bearing pieces of their victims, and used them to inflict all manner of harm. Some were brutal and powerful in their curses that they would often leave a trail of death in their wake..<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Whenever she makes an Occult roll, the changeling receives an exceptional success at three instead of five. She also can spend Glamour or Willpower to invoke the Curse Effigy Merit, and has automatic successes equal to half her Wyrd in addition to the roll results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:26:55-07:00","id":989891,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a>, another proposed revision for a kith of yours based on recent material.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <u><b>Babelfish</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> When speaking to a Babelfish, you may as well be talking in their native language as far as they're concerned. He gains the Legendary Language Merit for free, and may spend a point of Glamour to confer its effects to another for the scene. The character may bless up to a number of individuals equal to his Wyrd, and may remove this gift at any time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:54:00-07:00","id":989901,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing the Legendary Language allows them to speak all languages? In which case it works for what I based their idea on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:58:01-07:00","id":989904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=989901#post989901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing the Legendary Language allows them to speak all languages? In which case it works for what I based their idea on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. It does. And I remember someone on this thread mentioning it after you first posted the kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T09:07:33-07:00","id":989906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=989904#post989904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. It does. And I remember someone on this thread mentioning it after you first posted the kith.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was unaware of its existence at the time when I made them. But that makes them much easier to handle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Babelfish</i> is a popular story telling trope in which the characters are actually speaking their own languages, but we hear them speaking our own. It's supposed to explain why thousands of different races all over the world / galaxy appear to be perfectly fluent in one language. It also eliminates the need to translate or design multiple foreign languages.<br /> <br /> The famous <i>universal translator</i> <i>technology</i> is a popular example of Babelfish","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:13:15-07:00","id":989942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=989906#post989906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was unaware of its existence at the time when I made them. But that makes them much easier to handle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially since virtually every culture in the world has myths on fae beings, one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:05:17-07:00","id":990057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=989826#post989826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another kith which uses a Merit from the Hurt Locker drafts.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Spellbinder</u></b><br /> <i>You tore my life apart. Now, I'll do the same to yours.</i><br /> <br /> There is power found in one's image, and those who subvert it can hold great power over him. Changelings transformed into Spellbinders were made to punish their Keepers' captives enemies with equal measure. They wove charms bearing pieces of their victims, and used them to inflict all manner of harm. Some were brutal and powerful in their curses that they would often leave a trail of death in their wake..<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Whenever she makes an Occult roll, the changeling receives an exceptional success at three instead of five. She also can spend Glamour or Willpower to invoke the Curse Effigy Merit, and has automatic successes equal to half her Wyrd in addition to the roll results.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this kith, assuming that it still requires the construction of the effigy as part of it. I'd also suggest that the bonus successes only apply if the initial roll is successful.<br /> <br /> As far as Technopathy goes for the cybersages, I'll need to give that some thought. I could see going either way on that, and need to weigh the pros and cons a bit more. It is a good idea, though, so thanks for pointing it out to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:44:29-07:00","id":990342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=990057#post990057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this kith, assuming that it still requires the construction of the effigy as part of it. I'd also suggest that the bonus successes only apply if the initial roll is successful.<br /> <br /> As far as Technopathy goes for the cybersages, I'll need to give that some thought. I could see going either way on that, and need to weigh the pros and cons a bit more. It is a good idea, though, so thanks for pointing it out to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For the Spellbinder, the need to make an effigy is still there. Also, would your suggestion be worded as something like this?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Whenever she makes an Occult roll, the changeling receives an exceptional success at three instead of five. She also can spend Glamour or Willpower to invoke the Curse Effigy Merit. If the roll succeeds, it has automatic successes equal to half her Wyrd in addition to the roll results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 10-20-2016, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T02:18:47-07:00","id":990350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=990342#post990342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're welcome.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For the Spellbinder, the need to make an effigy is still there. Also, would your suggestion be worded as something like this?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Whenever she makes an Occult roll, the changeling receives an exceptional success at three instead of five. She also can spend Glamour or Willpower to invoke the Curse Effigy Merit. If the roll succeeds, it has automatic successes equal to half her Wyrd in addition to the roll results.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would phrase it as &quot;gains automatic successes&quot; rather than has, but otherwise that's exactly how I'd phrase it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T02:32:41-07:00","id":990352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=990350#post990350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would phrase it as &amp;quot;gains automatic successes&amp;quot; rather than has, but otherwise that's exactly how I'd phrase it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. That makes more sense. That just leaves Seeming descriptions to work out.<br /> <br /> Also, what would you call a Kith that has Faerie Healing as part of its Blessing? Mender is my placeholder until I find the right name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T05:47:38-07:00","id":997097,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Mirrorshade</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;Magic mirror on the wall, who shall be the next to fall?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Every mirror can be a looking glass for the Gentry, and Mirrorshades were blessed with this same power for their durance. Some served as observers and spies, peering through a myriad of mirrors in search of new knowledge for their Keepers to use. Others, however, became guards and assassins, hiding wherever one can see his reflection until they emerge to deal the killing blow.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Mirrorshade gains the Glimpse of a Distant Mirror Contract, and gains an Exceptional Success on it at three instead of five. If he is touching a reflective surface that is either as tall and wide as he or as wide as he is tall in both dimensions, any roll made to find him suffers his Wyrd as a penalty.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Critique and ideas for Seeming descriptions are appreciated, as are Seeming ideas for the Spellbinder kith I posted a few days back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-02-2016, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T06:23:17-07:00","id":997103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=997097#post997097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Mirrorshade</u></b><br /> <i>&amp;quot;Magic mirror on the wall, who shall be the next to fall?&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> Every mirror can be a looking glass for the Gentry, and Mirrorshades were blessed with this same power for their durance. Some served as observers and spies, peering through a myriad of mirrors in search of new knowledge for their Keepers to use. Others, however, became guards and assassins, hiding wherever one can see his reflection until they emerge to deal the killing blow.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Mirrorshade gains the Glimpse of a Distant Mirror Contract, and gains an Exceptional Success on it at three instead of five. If he is touching a reflective surface that is either as tall and wide as he or as wide as he is tall in both dimensions, any roll made to find him suffers his Wyrd as a penalty.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Critique and ideas for Seeming descriptions are appreciated, as are Seeming ideas for the Spellbinder kith I posted a few days back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll need to give the seeming descriptions some thought. Here's one:<br /> <br /> Grimm: Words of flickering flame drift through his polished bronze skin.<br /> <br /> I like where you're going with this kith. Is the difficulty to find the kith increased for any type of attempt to find him (ie: high Wyrd mirrorshade gains huge stealth bonus against mundane security guards and scrying attempts from a Mage if he can trail his fingers along a clean shiny window) or is it only certain types of attempts to find the changeling? Also, since most people are taller than they are wide, I don't think that you need both of the descriptions for the size of the reflective surfaces. I've got a couple other thoughts too, but I'll address them when I've got a bit more time. Overall, great idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T06:36:43-07:00","id":997109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=997103#post997103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll need to give the seeming descriptions some thought. Here's one:<br /> <br /> Grimm: Words of flickering flame drift through his polished bronze skin.<br /> <br /> I like where you're going with this kith. Is the difficulty to find the kith increased for any type of attempt to find him (ie: high Wyrd mirrorshade gains huge stealth bonus against mundane security guards and scrying attempts from a Mage if he can trail his fingers along a clean shiny window) or is it only certain types of attempts to find the changeling? Also, since most people are taller than they are wide, I don't think that you need both of the descriptions for the size of the reflective surfaces. I've got a couple other thoughts too, but I'll address them when I've got a bit more time. Overall, great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nicely done on the Grimm Seeming. How about this for an Elemental?<br /> <br /> <b>\u00b0 Elemental:</b> Skin as clear as water or as smooth as glass.<br /> <br /> For the Stealth aspect of the Mirrorshade, which is based off of the Woodblood's, I think it should be limited to mundane attempts. So the scrying attempt of a Mage (and other supernatural methods) might see through the disguise or prompt a Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:59:16-07:00","id":997176,"title":"","content":"Update on the Seeming descriptions.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Mirrorshade</u></b> <br /> <i>&quot;Magic mirror on the wall, who shall be the next to fall?&quot;</i> <br /> <br /> The Gentry can make a looking glass out of any mirror, and Mirrorshades are capable of the same feat with their power. Some served as observers and spies, peering through a myriad of mirrors in search of new knowledge for their Keepers to use. Others, however, became guards and assassins, hiding wherever one can see his reflection until they emerge to deal the killing blow. <br /> <br /> \u00b0 <b>Beast:</b> A piscine being with glittering translucent scales. <br /> \u00b0 <b>Elemental:</b> His body glistens like the clear waters of a lake. <br /> \u00b0 <b>Grimm:</b> Words of flickering flame drift through his polished bronze skin. <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Mirrorshade gains the Glimpse of a Distant Mirror Contract, and gains an Exceptional Success on it at three instead of five. If he touches a reflective surface that is at least as tall and wide as he, any roll made to find him by mundane means suffers his Wyrd as a penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-02-2016, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:42:32-07:00","id":997207,"title":"","content":"Not saying it's a problem, but it seems like a lot of these kiths are ways to get a free Contract. Almost like they're well-suited to be more secondary kiths you get from the Dual Kith merit than primary, character-defining kiths","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:43:56-07:00","id":997312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=997207#post997207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not saying it's a problem, but it seems like a lot of these kiths are ways to get a free Contract. Almost like they're well-suited to be more secondary kiths you get from the Dual Kith merit than primary, character-defining kiths</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it has less to do with getting a Contract and more to do with the Contract covering the ability that the writer wants them to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:51:03-07:00","id":997317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=997176#post997176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Update on the Seeming descriptions.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Mirrorshade</u></b> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;Magic mirror on the wall, who shall be the next to fall?&amp;quot;</i> <br /> <br /> The Gentry can make a looking glass out of any mirror, and Mirrorshades are capable of the same feat with their power. Some served as observers and spies, peering through a myriad of mirrors in search of new knowledge for their Keepers to use. Others, however, became guards and assassins, hiding wherever one can see his reflection until they emerge to deal the killing blow. <br /> <br /> \u00b0 <b>Beast:</b> A piscine being with glittering translucent scales. <br /> \u00b0 <b>Elemental:</b> His body glistens like the clear waters of a lake. <br /> \u00b0 <b>Grimm:</b> Words of flickering flame drift through his polished bronze skin. <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Mirrorshade gains the Glimpse of a Distant Mirror Contract, and gains an Exceptional Success on it at three instead of five. If he touches a reflective surface that is at least as tall and wide as he, any roll made to find him by mundane means suffers his Wyrd as a penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things I considered was possibly replacing the stealth effect with the ability to spend a point of Glamour to physically hide within such a surface for a number of minutes equal to Wyrd. Basically they'd get to observe the area they were in as though they were using the Contract from another area (complete with any indication of their presence that they'd have when spying on someone from a distant mirror). The surface would still need to be big enough to step through, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T16:39:08-07:00","id":997429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=997317#post997317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things I considered was possibly replacing the stealth effect with the ability to spend a point of Glamour to physically hide within such a surface for a number of minutes equal to Wyrd. Basically they'd get to observe the area they were in as though they were using the Contract from another area (complete with any indication of their presence that they'd have when spying on someone from a distant mirror). The surface would still need to be big enough to step through, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this in addition to the Contract itself? But yeah, that idea also came to mind when I was making the Kith. The only reason I didn't go with it was because it might mix a bit with that Mirror walking Contract. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I revised it based on your suggestions.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Mirrorshade</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;Magic mirror on the wall, who shall be the next to fall?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The Gentry can make a looking glass out of any mirror, and Mirrorshades are capable of the same feat with their power. Some served as observers and spies, peering through a myriad of mirrors in search of new knowledge for their Keepers to use. Others, however, became guards and assassins, hiding wherever one can see his reflection until they emerge to deal the killing blow. <br /> <br /> <b>\u00b0 Beast:</b> A piscine being with glittering translucent scales. <br /> <b>\u00b0 Elemental:</b> His body glistens like the clear waters of a lake. <br /> <b>\u00b0 Grimm:</b> Words of flickering flame drift through his polished bronze skin. <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Mirrorshade gains the Glimpse of a Distant Mirror Contract, and gains an Exceptional Success on it at three instead of five. If he touches a reflective surface that is at least as tall and wide as he, he may hide within it for a number of minutes equal to his Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-02-2016, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T17:07:59-07:00","id":997444,"title":"","content":"Spellbinder Seemings.<br /> <br /> \u00b0 <b>Beast:</b> This spidery figure weaves her effigies with ease using her slender fingers. <br /> \u00b0 <b>Darkling:</b> A tall and gaunt woman with paper white skin and long, thin fingers. <br /> \u00b0 <b>Wizened:</b> The front half of her face is replaced with a mask, while her fingers are metal and needle-like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:36:30-07:00","id":997721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=997429#post997429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this in addition to the Contract itself? But yeah, that idea also came to mind when I was making the Kith. The only reason I didn't go with it was because it might mix a bit with that Mirror walking Contract. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I revised it based on your suggestions.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Mirrorshade</u></b><br /> <i>&amp;quot;Magic mirror on the wall, who shall be the next to fall?&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> The Gentry can make a looking glass out of any mirror, and Mirrorshades are capable of the same feat with their power. Some served as observers and spies, peering through a myriad of mirrors in search of new knowledge for their Keepers to use. Others, however, became guards and assassins, hiding wherever one can see his reflection until they emerge to deal the killing blow. <br /> <br /> <b>\u00b0 Beast:</b> A piscine being with glittering translucent scales. <br /> <b>\u00b0 Elemental:</b> His body glistens like the clear waters of a lake. <br /> <b>\u00b0 Grimm:</b> Words of flickering flame drift through his polished bronze skin. <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Mirrorshade gains the Glimpse of a Distant Mirror Contract, and gains an Exceptional Success on it at three instead of five. If he touches a reflective surface that is at least as tall and wide as he, he may hide within it for a number of minutes equal to his Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. I don't think that it tramples the toes of the Contract at all, given that all the blessing offers is an extra type of hiding place. I do think that hiding in the mirror should cost a point of Glamour, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:45:46-07:00","id":997726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=997721#post997721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. I don't think that it tramples the toes of the Contract at all, given that all the blessing offers is an extra type of hiding place. I do think that hiding in the mirror should cost a point of Glamour, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edited and added to the Doc.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> On a different note, I'm trying to revisit the Treasured kith and see if I can improve upon or otherwise revise its Blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-03-2016, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T22:33:42-07:00","id":999075,"title":"","content":"Tentative revision to the Treasured.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Treasured's beauty was not only enhanced, but endowed with greater resilience. She receives the Iron Stamina Merit at three dots, and adds half her Wyrd on all rolls to resist fatigue, poison, and disease. In addition, she may spend Glamour once per dot of Wyrd in a day to apply the rote quality to any Presence or Manipulation roll made using her looks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T03:49:14-08:00","id":999145,"title":"","content":"Another WIP from me. Still missing the description and Seemings. Critique is welcome, as always.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Mistwalker</u></b> <br /> <i>&quot;Hit them fast and hard. They won't be able to put up a good defense while this fog is up&quot;</i> <br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Mistwalker's movements are faster when she is unseen. She gains the Nevertread Contract, and benefits from the 8-again rule when rolling for it. If she is in a location where dim light, fog, or other conditions inflict at least a -1 penalty on rolls involving vision, she adds half her Wyrd to her Speed and Initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T19:45:34-08:00","id":1002056,"title":"","content":"<br /> I've been collecting custom Kith examples from across the web, the majority written during 1E Changeling so in need of revisions. I also need to have a second pass over the list to note how Wyrd is utilized so I won't post many at a time.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>(from </i></span></span><a href=\"http://qsf-changeling.wikidot.com/custom-kiths\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>QSF Changeling</u></i></span></span></a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>)</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><u>Hollowmade</u></b><br /> Not every Changeling can recall a durance spent being the building, place or structure within Arcadia. Shaped into extensions of their Keeper's realms, there were nothing but the platform on which others went about. Since that them some have become architects or builders, holding appreciation for well made structures. Others considered themselves blessed to finally be able to move and not be spread out over square acreage.<ul><li><b>Beast:</b> like a great crustacean, on the back of its shell a multitude of housing coral</li> <li><b>Darkling:</b> preforated, pierced and zippered across gaping wounds leading to internal cavities</li> <li><b>Elemental:</b> twisty Hedge growths, alien fae structures or golems of brick and motar</li> </ul><br /> <u>Blessing:</u> Within them is a closet sized space only they can access, storing and retrieving items for 1 Glamour each. The total combined volume of objects, by Size, cannot exceed the Changeling's Size + Wyrd. Once stored the objects (at Storyteller's discretion) are unreachable for anyone else yet age and decay at their normal rate. Additionally, any Hollow merit the Changeling owns gains 2 free dots of features when they reside in it, or 1 free dot of features when given permission when guest to another's Hollow. Different features can be selected at each visit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T20:45:52-08:00","id":1002074,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Merchant</b></u> (From Angelus Morningstar's Kith Compendium)<ul><li><b>Beast:</b> A maneki-neko, tanuki, magpie, pig or another animal associated with good fortune or greed.</li> <li><b>Wizened:</b> Eyes that can expand into telescopes to appraise items and weird calculators built into their arms.</li> <li><b>Elemental:</b> A living abbacus made of levitating gems and coins that constantly move from one spot to the other as they crunch numbers in their mind.</li> </ul><u>Blessing:</u> Merchants gain the 8 Again rule for all trade negotiations, the Market Sense Merit, and a free Interdisciplinary Specialty with Area Of Expertise for Goblin Markets. By spending 1 point of Glamour when touching an object, they may use the the Psychometry Merit, adding her Wyrd to the roll and suffering no penalties. The questions must be focused on the object's potential uses or drawbacks in trade negotiations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T21:03:44-08:00","id":1002094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1002056#post1002056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been collecting custom Kith examples from across the web, the majority written during 1E Changeling so in need of revisions. I also need to have a second pass over the list to note how Wyrd is utilized so I won't post many at a time.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>(from </i></span></span><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://qsf-changeling.wikidot.com/custom-kiths&amp;quot;]</a><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>QSF Changeling</u></i></span></span>[/URL]<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>)</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><u>Hollowmade</u></b></div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting concept for a kith, and one not explored by any in the docs at that. The write-up could use some revisions, and I'm not sure if using character Size is a good idea (alternatively, I could make it 5 per dot of Wyrd). But other than that, it looks good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1002074#post1002074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Merchant</b></u> (From Angelus Morningstar's Kith Compendium)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Interesting, but I can't help but think that there's a lot crammed into the Blessing. Feel free to look at the Huckster and Tradesman kiths for comparison, though. Some of the stuff in the write-up looks like it can be folded over to either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T21:24:42-08:00","id":1002106,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Shadowcaster</u></b><br /> <i>&quot;What's the matter? Afraid of the dark?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The darkness is a common fear, representing the menacing unknown to the mortal world. More specific is mankind's fear of having the light stolen from them, the sudden rush of terror a dropped flashlight or power outage can cause. Shadowcasters are often those who found this fear realized, forced to run through nightmares where the lights always went out, and when they did, terrible things would happen. Others were those who used the darkness to protect themselves, shattering lights or otherwise engendering an absence of illumination.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Shadowcaster gains three dots in the Psychokinesis Merit, and can spend Glamour or Willpower to manipulate shadows. If he spends a point of Glamour, he may drain all light within a radius of ten yards per dot of Wyrd, inflicting penalties on all visual rolls as if they were made in complete darkness, except those made by the changeling himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T15:44:25-08:00","id":1010373,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1002094#post1002094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting concept for a kith, and one not explored by any in the docs at that. The write-up could use some revisions, and I'm not sure if using character Size is a good idea (alternatively, I could make it 5 per dot of Wyrd). But other than that, it looks good.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to remember a Kith is only a fraction of what a Changeling was able to do in Arcadia, where they were empowered by the Gentry's whims and the raw Wyrd beyond the Hedge. There should be a limit of some kind and I considered Size to be the best qualifier as it's universally used for people and objects. Instead of volumetric math you compare the total Size of a collection to the Changeling's maximum. Their own Size (because the objects are housed within) and Wyrd are a suitable maximum, and Size 0 objects can be stored limitlessly if you wanted to spend the Glamour. It's true that while in their Keeper's realms the Hollowmade could be a tower or a palace, back on earth you need to pick up Potent Kith if you want to be the walking garage with a fleet of vehicles and tools.<br /> <br /> The most I would consider expanding the limit is twice the character Size + Wyrd. Anything greater and it would just be silly as a Kith, chucking cars and dumpsters out of your body, although that would be an entertaining high rating Contract. <br /> <br /> --------------------------<br /> <br /> This Kith never had a previous writeup as it was only a musing. My interest in developing the Kith has spiked since the revised Dual Kith reduces your effective Wyrd for multiple Kith benefits. This custom Kith emulates other abilities for a different cost<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><b>Assemblyman</b></u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>(from </i></span></span><a href=\"http://ageofravens.blogspot.com/2011/05/more-kith-and-kind-continued.html\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>AgeOfRavens</u></i></span></span></a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> blog)</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> What if you were never abducted from Earth to begin with? It's true that every Changeling is not the same when they escape Arcadia, with a Fetch in the place of the person that was taken. Although you were never a single person to begin with. Especially bizarre and morbid Keepers that has fashioned themselves as sewers of flesh, cobblers of discorporate parts or swapping minds and bodies of their captives indiscriminately often 'unintentionally' create this Kith pulled together from scraps and failed projects. What emerges from Arcadia as living hodgepodges find themselves a mess of memories, bodies and durances from beings that no longer exist. Or perhaps the Assemblyman is the result of a fierce sense of desperation pulled together from the bodies of several fallen escapees.<ul><li><u>Fairest:</u> a horrid yet pleasing appearance masking distinctive and contrasting attitudes</li> <li><u>Grimm:</u> like a bad fan fiction, several characters compiled together</li> <li><u>Darkling:</u> each of their personalities has retained a frighting feature</li> </ul><b>Blessing:</b> The Assemblyman selects 4 Skills to gain the benefits of this Kith. Each day they have a pool of dice that can be spent on any of these skills, although no more than half their Wyrd for a single roll. Additionally the Assemblyman selects three other Kiths that they can emulate, using the lowest of their Wyrd or their lowest Resistance Attribute in place of Wyrd for these Kiths. Unlocking the benefits of these other Kiths requires taking a level of damage resistant to supernatural healing that cannot be mitigated in any way. It costs 1 Bashing for the first Kith, 1 Lethal for the second Kith, and 1 Aggravated damage for the third Kith in the same scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T19:37:47-08:00","id":1012932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1002056#post1002056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been collecting custom Kith examples from across the web, the majority written during 1E Changeling so in need of revisions. I also need to have a second pass over the list to note how Wyrd is utilized so I won't post many at a time.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>(from </i></span></span><a href=\"http://qsf-changeling.wikidot.com/custom-kiths\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>QSF Changeling</u></i></span></span></a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>)</i></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh hey, that's my wiki page. &gt;.&gt; Glad to see it's still getting some use by someone other than me!<br /> <br /> Also, very nice rewrite for the Hollowmade.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T20:20:42-08:00","id":1014120,"title":"","content":"Here's one I've been working on for a bit. Not sure if this sort of idea has been covered or not.<br /> <br /> <b>Hearth Heart</b><br /> <i>I know I have some with me. Hold on, let me check my pockets...my sleeves...my shadow maybe...ah, there it is! Weird at how hard it is to keep track of loose change. Worse than socks in that regard.</i><br /> <br /> Even with the vast space their realms can grant, even the Gentry need something, or someone, to keep track of things. Whether it's a treasured token, bric a brac or even just themselves, sometimes there's nothing safer than hiding something inside of someone. Hearth Hearts are those who were hollowed out in some way, making their bodies, minds and even their shadows storage. Some Keepers even make their Changelings into fashion statements, transformed into a coat that bares the winter instead of the wearer.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> Her shadows teem with hands that grasp and pull at anything close, and her mouth unzips to reveal a massive space.<br /> <b>Elemental:</b> Once an armoire, his front has a split down the middle, and hinges sit at his sides, ready to open at a thought.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> Her sleeves store anything and everything, and her eyes have an impossible sense of depth to them.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Changeling always has a space with them they may store items in, invisible and inaccessible to anyone without permission. This space is capable of holding items with a size up and equal to their Wyrd. Time is arrested in this space - anything within will not degrade or age, but anything living will be conscious and able to make a Perception roll (penalized by your character's Wyrd) to listen outside. The Changeling feels the weight of anything within the space, but everything within them is considered half as heavy as it normally is. By expending a Glamour, this space may be tripled for the remainder of the scene at the risk of the Changeling over encumbering themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T20:25:30-08:00","id":1014124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1014120#post1014120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's one I've been working on for a bit. Not sure if this sort of idea has been covered or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was with the Hollowmade. Still, this looks interesting, so I'll give it a good look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T20:33:44-08:00","id":1014126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1014124#post1014124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was with the Hollowmade. Still, this looks interesting, so I'll give it a good look.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so I see. It's interesting at how certain concepts are gotten by many, and different aspects become focused on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T04:28:50-08:00","id":1014243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1014126#post1014126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, so I see. It's interesting at how certain concepts are gotten by many, and different aspects become focused on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> <br /> Still, between it and the Hollowmade, which works better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T11:41:12-08:00","id":1014395,"title":"","content":"Hard to say. Hollowmade certainly has more rules set in place regarding the actual dimensions the Changeling has on offer, but I'm not that on board with how it grants temporary dots of Hollow benefits when you visit one. It feels too random, particularly since additions to a Hollow are considerable and take time. The difference between one and two dots of Size Matters is the difference between a townhouse and an entire town, and yet a Hollowmade visiting it could inspire such a change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T19:59:43-08:00","id":1017455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caelene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1012932#post1012932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh hey, that's my wiki page. &gt;.&gt; Glad to see it's still getting some use by someone other than me!<br /> <br /> Also, very nice rewrite for the Hollowmade.</div> </div> </div> </div>So that was yours? That link ended up being one of the larger list of Kith concepts I had come across. Lots of fund ideas there.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------<br /> <br /> As mentioned above, Hollowmade was a revision of a previously written custom Kith. This was the blessing of the 1E version to be updated for 2E:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Hollowmade are </span></span></span><b>Empty Inside</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">; their bodies invariably contain an entrance of some sort that can expand to create a special Hollow usable only by the Hollowmade, into which various objects can be placed for storage at the cost of Glamour. This Hollow is about the size of a large closet (5' by 5' by 10'), and cannot store living beings (or undead). Inserting or removing an object is an instant action; the changeling never has to search for an item, it always comes to hand immediately. When placing an item inside, the Hollowmade's true nature is fully visible for a turn. Note that for every day this Blessing in use (that is, the changeling contains one or more objects), the changeling must spend a point of Glamour to avoid taking a level of aggravated damage. In addition, Hollowmade add a dot to any Hollow which they have already purchased at least a dot of; this dot can be in any category.</span></span></span></i> </div> </div> </div>Much like your Hearth Heart, Taidragon, there should be some kind of consistent mechanic and limitation to what the Changeling can store. There's also a slight difference of theme, as your kith outlines Changelings used as storage like a chest or a pocket vest and Hollowmade is indicative of structures, buildings, or Hedge border growths. A lot of the crunch in the first half of both Kiths cover similar strata.<br /> <br /> Towards the end, I still wanted to retain the Hollowmade notion that they are 'living dwellings' and how that influences their connection with a Hollow. Also, this will very greatly on how the Hollow merit is done in 2E. From the early looks, I was operating under the assumption that the Hollow merit is one that unlocks additional features depending on how many dots you have. Those 2 or 3 dot Escape Routes and Long Roads and such.<br /> <br /> Keeping the first half of the Kith writeup the same, here's a new draft for the ancillary blessing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the duration of their visit the Hollowmade can enhance a Hollow they own and upkeep, receiving 2 free dots of features. If they are given permission from the owner of another Hollow they visit, they may grant that Hollow an additional dot of features for the duration of their stay. Different features can be selected each visit. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T09:18:54-08:00","id":1019287,"title":"","content":"You make a fair argument -metablender (cool name, by the way), and after thinking on it I have come to appreciate the idea of a Changeling who was a building being able to expand on a building within the Hedge. It does make sense, all things considered, and your revised edit does sit with me better (thank you for taking the critique in good standing).<br /> <br /> However, now I feel I should rework Hearth Heart a bit so that it is more clear on its bonus, particularly the capacity they have beyond what size of items they can hold (quantity would be good, for a start). As I said before, you better defined the carrying capacity of a Hollowmade in fewer words, and its hard to compare between the two Kiths. Hollowmade can straight up hold more within them, and dots of free Hollow is nothing to sneeze at, but Hearth Heart can store living beings away and store and access their hold more easily, plus the ability to temporarily expand that storage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T09:21:02-08:00","id":1019288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1019287#post1019287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You make a fair argument -metablender (cool name, by the way), and after thinking on it I have come to appreciate the idea of a Changeling who was a building being able to expand on a building within the Hedge. It does make sense, all things considered, and your revised edit does sit with me better (thank you for taking the critique in good standing).<br /> <br /> However, now I feel I should rework Hearth Heart a bit so that it is more clear on its bonus, particularly the capacity they have beyond what size of items they can hold (quantity would be good, for a start). As I said before, you better defined the carrying capacity of a Hollowmade in fewer words, and its hard to compare between the two Kiths. Hollowmade can straight up hold more within them, and dots of free Hollow is nothing to sneeze at, but Hearth Heart can store living beings away and store and access their hold more easily, plus the ability to temporarily expand that storage.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a Demon Form ability that did something similar. Maybe you can look at it for inspiration?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T19:57:28-08:00","id":1026829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1019287#post1019287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You make a fair argument -metablender (cool name, by the way), and after thinking on it I have come to appreciate the idea of a Changeling who was a building being able to expand on a building within the Hedge. It does make sense, all things considered, and your revised edit does sit with me better (thank you for taking the critique in good standing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the critique, Taidragon. Even what is considered a good idea by one should have some kind of soundboard with somebody else, to get that perspective outside of your own.<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Before my Sunday game went on hiatus for the holidays, I was struck with an interesting challenge. Basically I needed to populate a local chapter of the Margravate of the Brim quickly. The non-Court Hedge marchers and ragtag militia. So I asked each of the players to pick a letter from the alphabet, from the letter I would pick an official or fan made kith that sounded interesting for an NPC.<br /> <br /> And then we came to the letter Z where no kiths had existed to my knowledge. Since I like to improvise I skimmed down a list of odd words beginning with the letter Z and found an intriguing word to build a kith from:<br /> <br /> Zek: an inmate of a prison labor camp<br /> <br /> We know that most Changelings were taken as slaves of the Gentry yet I hadn't seen a specific prisoner kith before. The Brim marcher I came up with is a chain gang escapee named Zacchaeus, likely Wizened, all that's left is his tattered uniform, shackles and a hard look to his eye. So I was looking to expand the concept some more with a kith writeup, Seemings and blessing.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of some remainder of their bondage being present in this kith, like a chain or leash or rope. And that they have toughened internally even if not physically. This grants the Indomitable Merit without prerequisite. As for utilizing the shackle that would be a length of 5' for each dot of Wyrd, allowing for grapples and similar Dexterity + Athletics tricks at range.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T20:07:57-08:00","id":1026832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1026829#post1026829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before my Sunday game went on hiatus for the holidays, I was struck with an interesting challenge. Basically I needed to populate a local chapter of the Margravate of the Brim quickly. The non-Court Hedge marchers and ragtag militia. So I asked each of the players to pick a letter from the alphabet, from the letter I would pick an official or fan made kith that sounded interesting for an NPC.<br /> <br /> And then we came to the letter Z where no kiths had existed to my knowledge. Since I like to improvise I skimmed down a list of odd words beginning with the letter Z and found an intriguing word to build a kith from:<br /> <br /> Zek: an inmate of a prison labor camp<br /> <br /> We know that most Changelings were taken as slaves of the Gentry yet I hadn't seen a specific prisoner kith before. The Brim marcher I came up with is a chain gang escapee named Zacchaeus, likely Wizened, all that's left is his tattered uniform, shackles and a hard look to his eye. So I was looking to expand the concept some more with a kith writeup, Seemings and blessing.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of some remainder of their bondage being present in this kith, like a chain or leash or rope. And that they have toughened internally even if not physically. This grants the Indomitable Merit without prerequisite. As for utilizing the shackle that would be a length of 5' for each dot of Wyrd, allowing for grapples and similar Dexterity + Athletics tricks at range.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me somewhat of the Mauler from Battle Realms. That aside, I am liking the idea you have there for the Zek.<br /> <br /> For an Elemental of this kith, I can picture something like a D&amp;D Chain Golem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.fantasylands.net/varie-cose/ChainGolem.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.fantasylands.net/varie-cose/ChainGolem.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.fantasylands.net/varie-cose/ChainGolem.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.fantasylands.net/varie-cose/ChainGolem.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, what sort of roster did you put together for the Margravate in your chronicle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T01:10:08-08:00","id":1026911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1026829#post1026829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for the critique, Taidragon. Even what is considered a good idea by one should have some kind of soundboard with somebody else, to get that perspective outside of your own.<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Before my Sunday game went on hiatus for the holidays, I was struck with an interesting challenge. Basically I needed to populate a local chapter of the Margravate of the Brim quickly. The non-Court Hedge marchers and ragtag militia. So I asked each of the players to pick a letter from the alphabet, from the letter I would pick an official or fan made kith that sounded interesting for an NPC.<br /> <br /> And then we came to the letter Z where no kiths had existed to my knowledge. Since I like to improvise I skimmed down a list of odd words beginning with the letter Z and found an intriguing word to build a kith from:<br /> <br /> Zek: an inmate of a prison labor camp<br /> <br /> We know that most Changelings were taken as slaves of the Gentry yet I hadn't seen a specific prisoner kith before. The Brim marcher I came up with is a chain gang escapee named Zacchaeus, likely Wizened, all that's left is his tattered uniform, shackles and a hard look to his eye. So I was looking to expand the concept some more with a kith writeup, Seemings and blessing.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of some remainder of their bondage being present in this kith, like a chain or leash or rope. And that they have toughened internally even if not physically. This grants the Indomitable Merit without prerequisite. As for utilizing the shackle that would be a length of 5' for each dot of Wyrd, allowing for grapples and similar Dexterity + Athletics tricks at range.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be more fitting to give them an extra dot of Resolve or Composure, which can take the Attribute beyond the normal limit imposed by Wyrd. The Indomitable Merit is more about resisting supernatural powers, and the horrors of prison are a lot more mundane, even in Arcadian prisons. As for their chains or leashes, they could also have some dots in either version of the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bH4XMrM7iovLQGBLJGVXHDTGXUrNc0JMy22wc-5MxZ8/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chain Weapons Style</b></a>, ignoring prerequisites. Since changelings can escape from bindings automatically by spending 1 glamour, I think you should allow a Clash Of Wills if the Zek is using his chains on another changelings or some other supernatural with escapism powers.<br /> <br /> By the way, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a>, I just realized something about your Toon Kith. They could also gain the Discreet Conjuration Contract for free, with the Wizened clause and Exceptional Success with 3 Successes. This would represent how cartoon characters pull objects out of Hammerspace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-05-2017, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T06:20:07-08:00","id":1028522,"title":"","content":"Here's one I promised some time ago.<br /> <br /> <b>Cursed One</b><br /> <br /> No, please, not now... Get away from me! I don't need any of you!<br /> <br /> Most changelings are taken because the Gentry have a use for them, but sometimes a person is taken merely as punishment. A cursed one has been punished by his Keeper with a dual nature, torn between a savage monster and a noble hero. Every time he thinks he has finally triumphed, the cursed one finds himself descending into savagery once more.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> The man has the smooth, slimy green skin of a frog, but a shining bejeweled crown sits upon his brow.<br /> <b>Fairest:</b> This swan wears a lovely crown, but her feathers darken with her mood.<br /> <b>Grimm:</b> Sorrowful tales of dark enchantments are embossed with gold upon his mottled scales.<br /> <b>Ogre:</b> The muscular shaggy body and raging temper are barely contained within the immaculate clothing of a nobleman.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> While afflicted with the Delusional or Warped Condition, the cursed one becomes more bestial, gaining a bonus to Physical and Intimidation rolls equal to half of his Wyrd. In this state, he also suffers an additional -2 penalty to other Social Skill rolls and loses the 10-Again effect for Composure rolls. The changeling may force one of these Conditions to manifest in himself by spending a point of Glamour and Willpower, but doing so causes the Condition to persist for its usual duration without a Beat gained for resolution. While benefiting from the Acuity Condition, the character seems more noble, gaining a +2 bonus on all Social Skill rolls. The changeling cannot force this Condition to manifest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T08:48:25-08:00","id":1028562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1026832#post1026832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a semi-related note, what sort of roster did you put together for the Margravate in your chronicle?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Margravate, or Squatters of the Brim as I've been calling them, are small 'chapter' of the Entitlement headquartered in their eponymous Squatters Roadhouse. A dive that's been cobbled together from whatever is salvageable. Long story short is that my players (who aren't actually Changelings but are pretending to be such) are helping an allied motley clear their name of an assassination attempt of the King of Thrilling Autumn; with his Queen, the Homeless Hag, mobilizing the entire Freehold to hunt them down. Including their very lethal liaison into Changeling matters of the local Psychology Dept. Professor, one of my examples from several posts ago about the Moonborn or Psychsemy kith. Who did offer a heads up, although she and others are obliged to attack on sight.<br /> <br /> Currently there is Fiddy, an alien Grey Elemental as the team telepath; Edith Lot, a Fairest Sandharrowed who is a pillar of salt, fresh off a change of her Seeming from Elemental to Fairest; Zaccheaus the aforementioned Wizened Zek, a gaunt brackish skinned escaped prisoner, and Vivip Phrynos, the defacto leader and Beast Coldscales who is a horned toad. In both the amphibious and reptilian sense. There's a mention of one or two others, as I had a player miss last session so I may grant her suggestion for a member currently patrolling the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Vivip, the horned toad, is tangentially related to my first ever Changeling character I reused as an NPC. Based on a shared 'brood' of Changelings, commonly Beasts, that take after the fauna of a bizarre bog garden from their slurry mixing Keeper, these surviving Changelings ('scumlings') consider licking each others backs to be a greeting and sign of alliance. Since the PC-now-NPC was killed in the assassination attempt, and she was Brimmer as well, Vivip is agreeing to help out of vengeful feelings.<br /> <br /> The other main motley allies accused of this assassination included the (deceased) Anura Spongely, froggy Beast Steepscrambler and Swimmerskin; Smog Eve, a hazy night Elemental Palewraith and Ask-we-da-eed whose Mask is the exact doppleganger of one of my players, Smythe, a punkish Darkling Pisacha Moonborn; and Chester Lockley a shriveled old toymaker (in appearance, not age) Wizened Artist and Gameplayer.<br /> <br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> Back to blessings of the Zek Kith, I'll play around with the suggestions during tonight's session to see what fits most for the Kith. I do want to keep it as general or vanilla as possible (where you have only the core rulebook and C:tL as references) in contrast to the common trend I've been seeing with home-brew of late using Hurt Locker material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T10:25:15-08:00","id":1028604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1028522#post1028522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's one I promised some time ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Another interesting kith.<br /> <br /> Not sure if the name's fine, but the mechanics are solid in my opinion. It's actually a good base for a character akin to the Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T12:33:00-08:00","id":1028651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1028604#post1028604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. Another interesting kith.<br /> <br /> Not sure if the name's fine, but the mechanics are solid in my opinion. It's actually a good base for a character akin to the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast was exactly the archetype I'd been envisioning when I created them. I'm glad you liked it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T18:29:12-08:00","id":1028814,"title":"","content":"I think your Kith is really cool<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just a thought, why don't you also give them the feature or the ability to gain one of the traits of the monster they are associated with? Also, how are your Cu Sith going?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T05:56:51-08:00","id":1028990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1028814#post1028814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your Kith is really cool<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just a thought, why don't you also give them the feature or the ability to gain one of the traits of the monster they are associated with? Also, how are your Cu Sith going?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I figured that anybody looking for something extra in a cursed one can always use Dual Kith or Contracts to expand the character's capabilities. I don't want to load too much into a single blessing, and they've got a lot already.<br /> <br /> As for the Cu Sith, I've still got my notes for them, but I ended up setting them aside to work on... something else. Between that, work, and the holidays, I haven't had a chance to go back to them yet. I still intend to do so, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T18:25:57-07:00","id":1107471,"title":"","content":"<b>Superhero</b><br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m telling you, he showed up out of nowhere and saved me from that thing! I asked who he was and he said \u2018just a guy with great responsibilities\u2019.\u201d<br /> <br /> The True Fae are partial to the popular stories of the zeitgeist, and fashion their Realms and captives accordingly. And few tales have taken the world by storm like those of the costumed crime fighters and justice bringers known as Superheroes. In Arcadia, they were shining beacons of hope for metropolises caught within the dastardly plans of other changelings cast in the role of supervillains, while their Keepers joined in the action as one or the other depending on their mood. Despite the immense glory, these changelings grew tired of their make believe worlds and strove toward a greater purpose. This desire to make a real difference allowed them to escape their Keepers\u2019 Realms, and now they protect people for real in the Ironside, regardless of the danger or the fear people might have of them.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A wild animal man, embodying the symbolic abilities of his chosen animal and righting wrongs even if it means breaking rules.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A cunning anti-hero who prowls the dark underbelly of the city and is not afraid of getting blood and dirt on their hands. Their faces seem perpetually framed in shadows, their voices serious and their steps are as silent as can be.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A survivor of harsh environments clad in the elements like a living cloak, he explores the furthest reaches of the world where no one else will go in search of those who need help.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A striking paragon with noble features and athletic build, his very presence is followed by a glowing aura of righteousness and determination.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A hulking barge of a man covered in proud scars and tattoos, with a menacing glare and an even more menacing knuckle crack. When they chase an evil doer, the pavement cracks under their mighty feet.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened: </b>A brilliant inventor and investigator wearing the most sophisticated Hedgespun gadgets for solving crimes, often incorporated into his body.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Superheroes receive an extra dot of Presence or Resolve, which may take them beyond their normal limits. They may roll Presence + Wyrd vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance a number of times per scene equal to Wyrd. Success changes one of the target\u2019s Aspirations, which must be turned into something related to improving themselves or fighting for justice in some way. Should the Superhero succeed, he may spend 1 Glamour to also give the target the Inspired Condition or Beaten Down Tilt. Lastly, he may roll Resolve + Wyrd to give the Steadfast Condition to any one of his allies a number of times per story equal to Wyrd. An Exceptional Success on this roll gives the Steadfast Condition to Wyrd + 1 individuals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-24-2017, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T12:46:40-07:00","id":1107714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=1107471#post1107471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Superhero</b><br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m telling you, he showed up out of nowhere and saved me from that thing! I asked who he was and he said \u2018just a guy with great responsibilities\u2019.\u201d<br /> <br /> The True Fae are partial to the popular stories of the zeitgeist, and fashion their Realms and captives accordingly. And few tales have taken the world by storm like those of the costumed crime fighters and justice bringers known as Superheroes. In Arcadia, they were shining beacons of hope for metropolises caught within the dastardly plans of other changelings cast in the role of supervillains, while their Keepers joined in the action as one or the other depending on their mood. Despite the immense glory, these changelings grew tired of their make believe worlds and strove toward a greater purpose. This desire to make a real difference allowed them to escape their Keepers\u2019 Realms, and now they protect people for real in the Ironside, regardless of the danger or the fear people might have of them.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> A wild animal man, embodying the symbolic abilities of his chosen animal and righting wrongs even if it means breaking rules.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkling:</b> A cunning anti-hero who prowls the dark underbelly of the city and is not afraid of getting blood and dirt on their hands. Their faces seem perpetually framed in shadows, their voices serious and their steps are as silent as can be.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental:</b> A survivor of harsh environments clad in the elements like a living cloak, he explores the furthest reaches of the world where no one else will go in search of those who need help.<br /> <br /> <b>Fairest:</b> A striking paragon with noble features and athletic build, his very presence is followed by a glowing aura of righteousness and determination.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogre:</b> A hulking barge of a man covered in proud scars and tattoos, with a menacing glare and an even more menacing knuckle crack. When they chase an evil doer, the pavement cracks under their mighty feet.<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened: </b>A brilliant inventor and investigator wearing the most sophisticated Hedgespun gadgets for solving crimes, often incorporated into his body.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Superheroes receive an extra dot of Presence or Resolve, which may take them beyond their normal limits. They may roll Presence + Wyrd vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance a number of times per scene equal to Wyrd. Success changes one of the target\u2019s Aspirations, which must be turned into something related to improving themselves or fighting for justice in some way. Should the Superhero succeed, he may spend 1 Glamour to also give the target the Inspired Condition or Beaten Down Tilt. Lastly, he may roll Resolve + Wyrd to give the Steadfast Condition to any one of his allies a number of times per story equal to Wyrd. An Exceptional Success on this roll gives the Steadfast Condition to Wyrd + 1 individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div> Perfect in honour of the late Adam West.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}